PVD("pakistan_ndp_2024-2029",{"docs":["","PK NDP 2024 29"],"s":{"1":[[1,"67","18","Innovative PPP/BOT Project Financing","Explore innovative modes of financing of projects on PPP/BOT basis",""],[1,"71","13","PPP Project Prioritization for PSDP Funding Support","Priority will be given to PPP projects, where PSDP funding is either used as equity or as viability gap.",""],[1,"73","4","Public-Private Partnership Authority Advisory and Approval Mechanism","P3A is a focal entity at Federal Level to approve all qualified projects through Public Private Partnership Working Party and its Board.",""],[1,"73","5","Public-Private Partnership Regulatory Framework","The regulatory framework devised by P3A provides effective, timely and transparent project approval processes to boost the private investors' confidence in taking informed investment decisions for infrastructure development.",""],[1,"74","9","National PPP Pipeline and Ecosystem Advancement","Proactively advance the national PPP Pipeline and ecosystem",""],[1,"74","15","PPP Option Sensitization for Implementing Agencies","P3A during the implementation framework shall sensitize the implementing agencies to explore PPP options first and if it is concluded that a given project is not a viable option for PPP only than government funding options should be explored as an alternate option for implementation of a given development project.",""],[1,"74","17","PPP Project Pipeline Development and Screening","The critical aspect is the development of PPP project pipeline.",""],[1,"74","18","Project Development Facility for Feasibility Studies","The identified projects shall further undergo detailed feasibility studies for which P3A may provide Project Development Facility to an implementing agency subject to the approval of its Board.",""],[1,"74","18","Viability Gap Funding for PPP Projects","Once operationalized and capitalized, P3A shall also provide viability gap funding to appropriate PPP projects in accordance with its applicable regulations.",""],[1,"74","18","Annual Viability Gap Funding Allocation","Depending upon the size of viability gap fund, P3A foresees to provide VGF to atleast two projects in a given financial year to make such projects bankable and financially feasible.",""],[1,"74","19","P3A Advisory Services for Non-Qualified Projects","P3A shall also provide advisory services to implementing agencies for their non-qualified projects.",""],[1,"319","3","Public Private Partnership Authority","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""],[1,"321","14","Institutional Collaboration Enhancement for Best Practices","Enhance institutional collaborations to promote best practices",""],[1,"322","3","Civil Society and Private Sector Policy Collaboration Framework","Collaboration and partnerships with civil society and private sector will be pursued in decision making process and policy implementation.",""],[1,"322","4","Multi-Stakeholder Collaboration for Academic Excellence and Skills","Collaboration among policymakers, academia and other stakeholders will be ensured for fostering academic excellence, producing skilled human resources, and contributing to the country's socio-economic development.",""],[1,"339","3","Public-Private Partnership Funding Promotion","Promoting Public-Private Partnership mode of funding in infrastructure and social sector projects will be promoted.",""],[1,"339","5","Public-Private Partnership Authority Strengthening and PPP Rule Revision","Strengthening Public-Private Partnership Authorities and revisiting rules on PPP at the federal level to enhance ease of doing business.",""],[1,"339","8","Public Investment Project Monitoring, Evaluation, and Risk Management Mechanism","Strengthening of mechanisms for project monitoring, evaluation, and risk management for effective utilization of public investment.",""],[1,"339","10","Contract Management Capacity Enhancement","Enhancing capacity for contract management, including transparency in contract documents, greater professionalism and adequate delegation of authority.",""],[1,"339","12","Strengthening the Result-Based Monitoring System in Project Management","Strengthening Result Based Monitoring System (RBMS) in project management",""],[1,"339","15","Legal and Regulatory Regime Strengthening for Public Property Protection","Strengthening of legal and regulatory regime to protect public properties and interests through institutional integrity, separation of institutional power, consistent and coordinated regulations, transparency, predictability of policies and rule of law",""]],"2":[[1,"324","6","Public Sector Capacity Enhancement and Civil Service Induction","Public sector capacity will be enhanced through inducting skilled, accessible, and motivated civil service at federal, provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"325","1","Public Service Training Regime Review","relevant cadres and groups with review of training regime based on a comprehensive training needs assessment will be focused.",""],[1,"325","1","Competitive Public Servant Remuneration Alignment","To attract and retain top talent, remuneration of public servants will be aligned with competitive market-based salaries.",""],[1,"325","2","Performance Management System and Annual Performance Agreements","Performance Management System including annual performance agreements at ministerial, departmental and individual levels will be implemented to foster accountability and effective dispensation of departmental functions aligned with job descriptions based on quantifiable KPI's.",""],[1,"325","2","Revival of the PM Committee for Performance Contract Evaluation","Efforts will be made for revival of the PM Committee for performance contract evaluation through periodic ministerial review while incentivizing performance score.",""],[1,"325","2","Strengthening of the Secretariat of Council of Common Interest and Training Institutions","The Secretariat of Council of Common Interest and training institutions including Pakistan Planning and Management Institute (PPMI) will be strengthened.",""],[1,"325","2","Civil Servant Training and Performance-Based Career Progression","Post-induction, in-service and on-the-job training with due weightage in career progression will be imparted to all Civil Servants and their future appointments will be linked with their performance.",""],[1,"325","3","Comprehensive Review of Government Structure","A comprehensive review of entire government structure will be conducted to address emerging national and international challenges while optimizing delivery of public services.",""],[1,"325","4","Public Sector Service Outsourcing and Regulatory Streamlining","The Plan prioritizes to outsource maximum services of public sector organization by limiting the role of public sector as regulator.",""],[1,"325","4","Workload Reassessment and Resource Redistribution","Workload re-assessments will be carried out at every level for optimal redistribution of financial and human resources.",""],[1,"325","4","Government Employee Performance Rules Review","Rules governing performance of government employees will be reviewed with a focus on rationalizing discretionary powers.",""],[1,"325","4","Public Administration Organization Strengthening","The role of PAO will be strengthened in alignment with Public Finance Management Act.",""],[1,"325","4","Public Sector Functional Review and Rationalization","To streamline and modernize public sector, organizations functions will be reviewed and redundant organizations will be abolished.",""],[1,"325","4","Smart Innovative Governance System","Smart innovative governance will be introduced for open, transparent, and merit-based processes in public sector.",""],[1,"325","4","Public Institution Impact and Satisfaction Assessment Framework","A framework will be developed for impact assessment and measuring satisfaction level of general public on performance and role of public intuitions.",""],[1,"327","3","Federal Government Right-Sizing and Institutional Reform Programme","Institutional Reforms Cell (IRC) has been mandated to undertake a comprehensive exercise for right sizing of Government to ensure productive and allocative efficiency in accordance with assigned functions of federal government.",""],[1,"336","3","Public Sector Capacity Enhancement through Training and Career Development","Enhancing the capacity of public sector through training, skill development, career progression",""],[1,"336","5","Civil Service Reform and Market-Based Incentives","Introduction and Implementation of civil service reforms and provision of market- based incentives to civil servants",""],[1,"336","9","Strengthening the Council of Common Interest Secretariat","Strengthening the Council of Common Interest (CCI) Secretariat",""]],"3":[[1,"21","2","Public Sector Enterprises Reform Programme","Fiscal policy involves intensive Public Sector Enterprises (PSEs) / State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) reforms, public financial management reforms and debt management reforms besides tax policy reforms.",""],[1,"60","10","State-Owned Enterprise Privatization and Restructuring","Privatize/restructure SOEs to decrease burden on the national exchequer.",""],[1,"61","10","SOE Privatization and Restructuring","Privatization / restructuring of SOEs to increase their efficiency and reduce their losses; 2",""],[1,"325","3","State-Owned Enterprises Governance and Operations Reform","Corporate governance in PSEs will be ensured by implementing the State-Owned Enterprises (governance and operations) Act, 2023 and State-Owned Enterprises (Ownership and Management) Policy, 2023.",""],[1,"325","5","Institutional Restructuring and Privatization Measures","To further strengthen institutional landscape focus will be on transformation of Pakistan Railways, restructuring PIA through outsourcing of management, outsourcing and privatization in road and motorways governance, development and privatization of water channels, privatization of urban public transport, streamlining national traffic challan system, Islamabad safe city project optimization, institutional setup for freshwater fish export, maximizing earnings from Afghan visit visa fees and forestation through private sector.",""],[1,"336","10","State-Owned Enterprises Governance and Operations Act Implementation","Effective implementation of the State-Owned Enterprises (governance and operations) Act,2023 and State-Owned Enterprises (Ownership and Management) Policy, 2023 for corporate governance in Public Sector Enterprises (PSEs)",""]],"4":[[1,"11","7","Digital Governance for Transparency and Service Delivery","Digital governance will enhance transparency and service delivery.",""],[1,"23","3","Digital Infrastructure and E-Pakistan Transformation Programme","Efforts are focused on building robust digital infrastructure, expanding broadband and 5G services, supporting startups and tech innovation, and integrating digital services like e-governance, telemedicine, and fintech.",""],[1,"23","4","Digital Economy and Connectivity Enhancement Initiatives","The ICT initiatives are enhancing Pakistan's digital economy through improved mobile and broadband penetration, especially in underserved areas like Gilgit-Baltistan and AJK.",""],[1,"23","4","National Cybersecurity and Digital Policy Programs","National programs such as the National CERT (Cybersecurity), Cloud First Policy, and the National Artificial Intelligence Policy are advancing Pakistan's capabilities in cybersecurity, digital infrastructure, and emerging technologies.",""],[1,"40","5","Digital Economy and FinTech Ecosystem Development","Special emphasis is also being placed on developing the IT and freelancing ecosystem, which includes establishing a Cloud Procurement Framework for government e- services, expanding 5G rollout and broadband penetration in rural and peri-urban areas, and advancing the FinTech ecosystem.",""],[1,"40","6","IT Parks and Digital Literacy Promotion","Additionally, the establishment of IT parks, coupled with the government's emphasis on enhancing computer and IT literacy, will help position Pakistan as an emerging hub for both software and hardware development.",""],[1,"97","1","Digital Economy Development Initiatives","The Plan focuses on a series of initiatives to shape the digital economy eco-system.",""],[1,"97","1","Inclusive E-Services and Capacity-Building Initiative","The core priorities are to build a robust digital economy and empower citizens through inclusive e-services and capacity-building initiatives.",""],[1,"97","1","Digital Skills Development and Research Programmes","Key federal and provincial stakeholders, will spearhead major skills-development and research programs.",""],[1,"98","16","e-Office Suite Deployment","The flagship e-Office Suite has been deployed in all federal Ministries/Divisions and their attached departments.",""],[1,"98","16","e-Government Digitalization Initiative","e-Government initiatives across federal and provincial ministries are driving improvements in efficiency, transparency, and responsiveness in public service delivery.",""],[1,"98","16","Public Sector Digitalization of Service Departments","These digitalization efforts have brought various federal and provincial departments including health, education, revenue, police, and judiciary partially or fully online, thereby improving efficiency, transparency, and service delivery",""],[1,"99","5","Federal E-Government Infrastructure Strengthening","There is a need to significantly strengthen the e-Government infrastructure at the Federal level.",""],[1,"99","5","Federal ICT Capacity Building for Service Delivery","Through building critical capacity in several domains of ICT delivering high quality services to various entities of the federal government at a commercial (or near-commercial) rate.",""],[1,"99","5","National Citizen Feedback and Government Interface Program","Also, a national program to enable citizen feedback and citizen-government interface needs to be created.",""],[1,"99","5","National Data Backbone Development","Furthermore, focused effort is needed at the national level to create a National Data Backbone (Open Data platform as well as National Spatial Data Infrastructure).",""],[1,"100","4","Digital Technology Adoption and E-Governance Capacity Building","Leverage productivity improvements in government, business, and society through rapid adoption of digital technologies.",""],[1,"100","9","Inter-Agency Digital Coordination for Uraan Pakistan","The Plan focuses on synergies to be developed among various executing agencies including PSEB, IGNITE, PTA, NTC, USF, SCO, and NITB.",""],[1,"100","9","Digital Government Services Expansion","Digitalize government services including taxation, registrations, land records, and FIRs to reduce inefficiencies, improve transparency, and eliminate corruption.",""],[1,"100","9","National Data Backbone and Open Data Platform","Create National Data Backbone (Open Data platform and National Spatial Data Infrastructure) for government and private sector innovators.",""],[1,"100","9","NITB Capacity Building for Real-Time Geo-Tagged Data Access","Build NITB capacity and collaborate with SUPARCO, Survey of Pakistan, NADRA, and Planning Commission to provide real-time geo-tagged government data access from citizens to senior policymakers for intelligent policymaking.",""],[1,"103","3","Government Function and Citizen Interface Automation and Digitization","Automation and digitization of at least 75 percent of the government's functions and citizen interface to lead to quantifiable improvements in efficiency and performance on a year-on-year basis.",""],[1,"103","5","Digital Content and Interface Localization for Citizen Services","Indigenization of digital content and user interfaces to Urdu and other major regional languages for on line citizen services by the government.",""],[1,"103","6","Government Data Backbone for APIs and Applications","Strong government data backbone available decision making, data-driven innovation, and private sector to build API's and applications to reach and serve a large population (225m+)",""],[1,"106","11","Anticipatory Personalized Public Service Delivery","Drive economic benefits and enhance government delivery of anticipatory, personalized services.",""],[1,"107","13","Digitalization of In-House Processes and Examination System Automation","Digitalization of In-House Processes & Automation of Examination System of Public",""],[1,"108","1","Smart Islamabad Initiative","Smart Islamabad Initiative",""],[1,"108","6","Strengthening and Expansion of the National Judicial Automation Unit","Strengthening and Expansion of National Judicial Automation Unit (NJAU)",""],[1,"108","7","Expansion of Federal Tax Ombudsman IT Systems","Expansion of IT Systems of the Office of Federal Tax Ombudsman including Computerization of 5 newly established FTO Regional Offices",""],[1,"108","9","Archiving and Digitalization of Legislation and Records","Archiving and Digitalization of Legislation and Record of Ministry of Law and Justice","Ministry of Law and Justice"],[1,"319","3","E-Governance and Digital Public Administration Initiatives","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""],[1,"319","3","AGPR Online Billing Solution","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""],[1,"319","3","Audit Management Information System","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""],[1,"321","9","Technology Integration for Better Governance","Optimize technology integration for better governance with robust cybersecurity measures",""],[1,"325","5","Public Sector Modernization and Digitization Initiative","A series of strategic policies and initiatives to modernize, digitize, and optimize functioning of public sector will be initiated.",""],[1,"326","6","National Database Integration and Digital Identity Management","NADRA being the torch bearer in introducing new technologies in the field of Registration and compiling of National Database shall continue to strive ahead connecting private and public databases across Pakistan.",""],[1,"327","1","Cross-Field Data Integration and System Development","NADRA shall be an active contributor in developing systems with a corroborative approach to channelize cross field consolidation through exploring capital markets, labour and skill development, planning and housing, societal inclusion, and health sector digitization.",""],[1,"327","2","Open and Smart Governance Reform","The Plan aims to introduce open and smart governance practices across all public departments including PSEs.",""],[1,"327","2","National ICT Infrastructure for Electronic Governance","For Electronic-Governance a reliable ICT infrastructure will be established by using ICT-based systems to promote efficiency, transparency and accountability.",""],[1,"327","2","Public Sector IT Infrastructure and Training Programme","Ministries/ Divisions/Departments will be encouraged to strengthen their IT infrastructure and facilitate IT training programs to ensure effective online delivery of public services.",""],[1,"327","2","Comprehensive E-Filing and Innovation Governance System","A comprehensive e-filing system and innovation governance for public sector will further streamline administrative processes and enhance accessibility of citizens to public services.",""],[1,"327","5","Government-Wide Central Database Computerization","computerization through central database management interlinked through NADRA will be introduced on a single standard in all the government departments, which will serve as a central databank for quick and accurate decision making at government level.",""],[1,"337","4","Comprehensive E-Filing System","A comprehensive e-filing system and innovation governance for public sector to further streamline administrative processes and enhance accessibility of citizens to public service delivery",""],[1,"337","4","Public Sector Innovation Governance Framework","A comprehensive e-filing system and innovation governance for public sector to further streamline administrative processes and enhance accessibility of citizens to public service delivery",""],[1,"337","13","Open and Smart Governance Practices Across Public Departments","Introduction of Open and smart governance practices across all public departments including Public Sector Enterprises (PSEs) to enhance transparency in decision making and service delivery",""],[1,"337","30","Data and Information Dissemination for Decision-Making","Enhanced dissemination of data and information at federal, provincial, ministerial, and institutional levels for decision making",""],[1,"337","33","National Data Center Establishment","Establishment of National Data Center to integrate, manage and publish both current and historical datasets to assess country future requirements",""],[1,"337","34","Seventh Agriculture Census","Conduct 7th Agriculture Census",""]],"5":[[1,"11","7","Start-up Promotion and Innovation Culture Initiative","fostering a culture of innovation to enable over 10,000 start-ups per year",""],[1,"23","5","Pakistan Startup Fund","Major projects include the Pakistan Startup Fund to boost venture capital, the E-Rozgaar program for youth employment, and initiatives to establish Pakistan as a global Al hub.",""],[1,"23","5","E-Rozgaar Youth Employment Program","Major projects include the Pakistan Startup Fund to boost venture capital, the E-Rozgaar program for youth employment, and initiatives to establish Pakistan as a global Al hub.",""],[1,"23","5","Global AI Hub Initiative","Major projects include the Pakistan Startup Fund to boost venture capital, the E-Rozgaar program for youth employment, and initiatives to establish Pakistan as a global Al hub.",""],[1,"23","5","National Semiconductor Human Resource Development Program","Additionally, projects like the National Semiconductor HR Development Program aim to build technical capacity and improve governance.",""],[1,"23","6","Science, Technology and Engineering for Development Program","Science, Technology and Engineering for Development (STED) program and Quantum Valley as well as Pakistan Startup Fund (PSF) will be major flagship projects.",""],[1,"23","6","Quantum Valley Initiative","Science, Technology and Engineering for Development (STED) program and Quantum Valley as well as Pakistan Startup Fund (PSF) will be major flagship projects.",""],[1,"23","6","Pakistan Startup Fund","Science, Technology and Engineering for Development (STED) program and Quantum Valley as well as Pakistan Startup Fund (PSF) will be major flagship projects.",""],[1,"23","6","Expansion of Higher Education Access in ICT","The access to higher education especially in ICT sector will be encouraged and venture capital funds will be established.",""],[1,"23","6","Venture Capital Fund Establishment","The access to higher education especially in ICT sector will be encouraged and venture capital funds will be established.",""],[1,"23","6","Startup Creation Target","At least 1000 new startups will be established and Pakistan will prepare to welcome 4th and 5th industrial revolution.",""],[1,"54","24","Implementation of IT and IT-Enabled Services Export Strategy 2023","Implementation of IT and IT enabled Services Export Strategy 2023",""],[1,"99","9","Government Startup Champion Entity","There is a dire need to create an entity responsible for championing startups from within the government.",""],[1,"100","1","CPEC-Enabled Startup and IT Hardware Growth Initiative","Capitalize on CPEC's potential as an engine of entrepreneurial and startups growth, particularly in the IT hardware and products sector.",""],[1,"100","6","ICT Startup Enablement Policy","Government will enable startups through conducive policies, emphasizing global market capture, local problem-solving, and transformative innovation in traditional industries using ICT as an enabling platform.",""],[1,"101","7","National Startup Initiative and Agency","A national Startup initiative and agency will be established to promote startup policies across sectors like IT, Sports, Textiles, Logistics, Medical Devices, and Agriculture.",""],[1,"101","9","Annual National Startup Competition and Expo","Launching an Annual National Startup Competition and Expo to enhance the visibility of the startup community.",""],[1,"101","10","Startup Support Grants Programme","Introducing a Startup Support Grants Programme for incubators, accelerators, and ORICs to nurture early-stage ideas.",""],[1,"101","11","Venture Capital Funding Mechanism","Developing a venture capital funding mechanism in collaboration with stakeholders.",""],[1,"101","12","Small Stocks Market Development","Partnering with entities like the Pakistan Stock Exchange to create a Small Stocks Market, supporting startup capitalization and exits.",""],[1,"101","13","Scaling and Globalization Platform for Startups","Establishing a Scaling and Globalization Platform, starting with networks in Silicon Valley and Shenzhen, to aid startups in global expansion.",""],[1,"101","14","Standalone Startup Development Oversight Entity","Forming a standalone entity with multi-ministerial representation to oversee startup development across sectors.",""],[1,"102","1","National Incubation Centre Startup Support","NICs in major cities (Islamabad, Lahore, Karachi, Peshawar, Quetta, Faisalabad, Hyderabad, NASTP Rawalpindi) support 1,000 startups annually through MOITT funding.","MOITT"],[1,"102","1","Expansion of Incubators to Second-Tier Cities","Establish NICs in second-tier cities (Multan, Bahawalpur) and create sector-specific incubators for health-tech and fintech.",""],[1,"102","2","Venture Capital and Startup Regulatory Reform","Reform venture capital and startup regulations to enable local risk capital generation and allocation.",""],[1,"102","2","High-Level Committee for SECP Rule Review","Establish high-level committee to review SECP rules for global competitiveness.",""],[1,"102","2","Disruptive Innovation Enablement Framework","Foster environment enabling disruptive innovation across government, transportation, logistics, agriculture, finance, hospitality, and e-commerce sectors.",""],[1,"102","3","CPEC Startup and IT Growth Strategy","Develop targeted strategy through Ministries of IT & Telecom and Commerce to leverage CPEC for IT, telecom, e-commerce, and fintech growth.","Ministries of IT & Telecom and Commerce"],[1,"104","1","IT SME Investment Certificates Scheme","A scheme may be introduced as IT SME Investment Certificates on IT export earnings.",""],[1,"104","1","Venture Capital Promotion in the IT Sector","Venture Capital may be promoted in IT Sector.",""],[1,"104","1","Tax Breaks for Angel Investment in Startups and SMEs","Angel investors be provided with tax breaks on the investments made in local startups/ SMEs as well as exportable services/ products.",""],[1,"105","1","Venture Capital Framework for Startup Ecosystem","The Plan will develop a framework for Venture Capital firms to facilitate the startup ecosystem in the country.",""],[1,"105","3","Startup Support through the National Incubation Centre","At least 1,000 startups supported through the National Incubation Centre's plus at least 3-5 times more created and supported within the broader startup eco-system that survive beyond 2 years of their creation.",""],[1,"105","5","Startup Ecosystem Support and Regulatory Reform Package","By enabling a conducive ecosystem for startups + through venture capital, incubation networks, and regulatory reforms, the Plan aims to drive inclusive job creation and technological advancement.",""],[1,"107","7","PM's Initiative Support for IT Startups, Specialized IT Trainings and Venture Capital","PM's Initiative Support for IT Startups, Specialized IT Trainings and Venture Capital",""],[1,"107","10","Digital Economy Enhancement Project","Digital Economy Enhancement Project (DEEP)",""],[1,"107","12","ICT and AI-Based Precision Agriculture System","Development of ICT and Al based Prevision Agriculture System utilizing Dual Use Aerospace Technologies - Green Al",""],[1,"107","19","Islamabad Planetarium Construction","Construction of Planetarium at Islamabad",""],[1,"107","20","Spaceport Establishment","· Establishment of Spaceport",""],[1,"107","22","Pakistan Lunar Exploration Rover Development","Development of Pakistan Lunar Exploration Rover (PLExR) for Change E-8 Mission",""],[1,"108","2","Gwadar Safe City Phase I","Gwadar Safe City (Phase - I)",""],[1,"108","3","Operational Improvement of the Federal Investigation Agency in AML/CFT","Operational Improvement of Federal Investigation Agency in AML/CFT,",""],[1,"108","11","Technology Park Islamabad Phase II and Technology Park Karachi","Establishment of Technology Park Islamabad (Phase -II) and Technology Park Karachi",""],[1,"116","7","Startup Support and Incubation Ecosystem Development","Support over 1000 startups through the National Incubation Center (NIC) and develop startup funding ecosystem and enable the NIC to enhance entrepreneurship capabilities",""],[1,"116","8","Venture Capital Funding Landscape Enhancement","Promote and enhance venture capital funding landscape",""],[1,"119","12","Startup Support and Funding Ecosystem Development","Support over 1000 startups through the National Incubation Center (NIC) and develop startup funding ecosystem",""]],"6":[[1,"38","7","Livestock Disease Control and Breeding Improvement Programme","Whereas, livestock, the most stable sub-sector, is expected to grow at an average rate of 4.6 percent, supported by disease control programs, improved breeding practices, value chain development, and rising domestic and exports demand for dairy, meat, and poultry products.",""],[1,"39","1","Livestock Breeding and Disease Control Programmes","For the livestock sector, actionable interventions will focus on improved breeding programs, disease surveillance and disease control programs such as National Peste des Petits Ruminants (PPR) Eradication Program.",""],[1,"49","8","Special Livestock Farms Along CPEC Routes","Establishment of special livestock farms for meat, milk, and dairy products along the CPEC routes in areas.",""],[1,"54","21","Special Livestock Farms Establishment","Establishment of Special Livestock farms",""],[1,"158","2","Private Sector Animal Breeding Centres","Promote animal breeding centres with healthy calves having recorded history in the private sector.",""],[1,"158","8","Transboundary Animal Disease Surveillance and Control Mechanism","Establish transboundary animal disease surveillance, monitoring, and control mechanism in each province, so that we can access the quality markets in meat.",""],[1,"158","9","Animal Vaccine Registration and Regulatory Framework for Private-Sector Mass Production","Develop mechanism and infrastructure to register animal vaccine in DRAP, and regulatory framework for vaccine mass production in the private sector.",""],[1,"160","7","Animal Vaccine Registration Enforcement","Enforcement of the law for registration of animal vaccine in DRAP before its commercial production and distribution",""],[1,"161","8","Animal Disease Surveillance, FMD Control and Traceability Mechanism","Establishment of mechanism for Animal Disease Surveillance, FMD Control and Animal Track and Traceability - in Compliance with National and International Standards in the country.",""]],"7":[[1,"138","2","Coastal Protection and Climate-Resilient Agriculture Programme","Strengthen coastal protection and promote climate-resilient agricultural practices, including modern irrigation systems, drought- and heat-tolerant crops, and sustainable land use.",""],[1,"138","3","Climate-Smart Agriculture Growth Strategy","Develop a long-term Climate-Smart Agriculture Growth Strategy, integrate watershed management, and promote efficient water use and quality improvement.",""],[1,"138","4","Mainstream Sustainable Land Management and Coastal Ecosystem Protection","Mainstream Sustainable Land Management (SLM) and protect coastal and marine ecosystems as natural buffers against climate impacts.",""],[1,"139","14","Climate-Resilient Agriculture and Food Systems Development","Build climate-resilient infrastructure, develop climate-resilient agriculture and food systems, and accelerate policy coherence for UN Sustainable Development Goals.",""],[1,"143","6","Climate-Smart Agriculture Expansion","Pakistan will advance Climate-Smart Agriculture (CSA) by introducing drought- and heat-tolerant crop varieties, micro-irrigation technologies, and efficient water-use systems.",""],[1,"143","6","CSA Growth Strategy Development","A long-term CSA Growth Strategy will be developed to integrate watershed management, soil health, and water quality improvements.",""],[1,"143","6","Sustainable Land Management Mainstreaming","Sustainable Land Management (SLM) will be mainstreamed across agro- ecological zones.",""],[1,"143","6","Coastal and Marine Ecosystem Protection","Protection of coastal and marine ecosystems will be prioritized as natural buffers against climate impacts such as sea-level rise and salinity intrusion.",""],[1,"146","3","Drought-Resilient Agriculture and Water Supply Support","The programme will support the cultivation of drought- and heat-tolerant crops, solar-powered water supply schemes, and the construction of community-level water storage systems",""],[1,"232","6","Climate-Resilient Agriculture Support","Promote climate- resilient agriculture, asset transfers and livestock distribution to rural poor.",""],[1,"232","6","Micro-Credit and Value-Chain Linkages for Smallholders","Implement micro-credit and value-chain linkages for smallholders.",""],[1,"234","5","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Practices Expansion","Introduce climate-resilient agricultural practices across at least 50 percent of agricultural land by 2029",""]],"8":[[1,"11","9","Water Security Enhancement","We will focus on ... water security",""],[1,"25","6","Water Sector Investment Alignment and Efficiency Enhancement","The Plan aligns water sector investments in the light of National Water Policy targets i.e Reduction of 33 percent in the 46 MAF river losses, 10 MAF increase in storage, 30 percent increase in the irrigation efficiency, gradual replacement and refurbishing of decades old irrigation infrastructure, and Real-time monitoring of river flows, and establishment of data mechanism.",""],[1,"25","6","Water Conservation and Regulatory Framework Strengthening","By and large, emphasizing new storage facilities and system efficiency enhancements through strategic principles include water conservation, increased storage capacity, leveraging new technologies, promoting renewable energy, capacity building and research, and comprehensive regulatory frameworks.",""],[1,"68","6","Water Sector Priority Investment","Within infrastructure sectors, top priority will be assigned to the Transport and Communication Sector with 22 percent share followed by Water, Physical Planning and Housing and Energy sectors with 7 percent, 5 percent and 5 percent shares, respectively.",""],[1,"68","7","National Water Policy Implementation and Water Sector Investment Allocation","The Federal Government in consultation with all stakeholders announced National Water Policy 2018 which has taken cognizance of the emerging water crisis and to provide an overall policy framework and guidelines for a comprehensive plan of action.",""],[1,"69","3","Water Resources Augmentation Investment","Within the infrastructure sector, about 12 percent will be invested for augmentation of water resources",""],[1,"70","1","Priority Completion of Ongoing Water Sector Projects","In the water sector, priority will be given to the ongoing projects for an early completion.",""],[1,"70","1","Federal Water Sector Investment Under National Water Policy","Water sector investment under federal PSDP shall be as per National Water Policy 2018.",""],[1,"70","1","Provincial Small and Medium Dam and Irrigation Improvement Programme","The provincial governments will assume the responsibility to undertake small and medium dams, lining of irrigation and improving distributary channels for economical use of water.",""],[1,"70","1","Federal Financing for Large Multi-purpose Dams and Mega Projects","the federal government will continue to finance large multi-purpose dams and ongoing mega projects.",""],[1,"133","4","Water Storage and Groundwater Recharge Infrastructure","Strategic interventions will include large- and small-scale water storage infrastructure, promotion of groundwater recharge zones, and scaling up watercourse lining to reduce conveyance losses.",""],[1,"133","4","Wastewater Treatment and Recycling Expansion","Expansion of wastewater treatment and recycling systems, particularly for urban and industrial use, will be promoted alongside the introduction of water-efficient technologies in agriculture such as High-Efficiency Irrigation (HEIS) systems.",""],[1,"133","4","Safe Drinking Water Supply Investments","Access to safe drinking water will be improved through investments in filtration systems, groundwater quality monitoring, and decentralized water supply solutions.",""],[1,"133","4","Integrated Water Resource Management Coordination and Enforcement","Institutional coordination and enforcement of Integrated Water Resource Management (IWRM) principles will be critical to secure Pakistan's water future.",""],[1,"142","4","Small- and Medium-Scale Reservoir Construction","Additionally, the Plan underscores the urgent need to improve water resource management, particularly through the construction of small- and medium-scale reservoirs to enhance groundwater recharge, reduce water stress, and build resilience against drought and climate variability.",""],[1,"145","5","National Programme on Water Efficiency and Conservation","It is planned that a comprehensive National Programme on Water Efficiency and Conservation will be implemented to address increasing water stress across agricultural, urban, and industrial sectors.",""],[1,"193","7","Mega Dam Project Construction","Works initiated on mega dam projects of Diamer Basha Dam and Mohmand Dam",""],[1,"193","16","Drainage System Rehabilitation and Outfall Facilities Provision","To provide outfall facilities to the existing and proposed drainage project, to improve environmental conditions in Manchar and Hamal Lake.",""],[1,"194","7","Water Sector Investment and Efficiency Improvement Programme","The Plan prioritizes investments for water sector in the light of NWP to build new storage facilities and increase system efficiency for water conservation with a broader objective to achieve water- energy-food security.",""],[1,"195","3","Water Storage, Irrigation Efficiency, and Groundwater Regulation Programme","Construction of large, medium and small storage reservoirs, remodeling and lining of irrigation channels to reduce conveyance losses, promote water conservation measures through high efficiency irrigation system, controlling the impacts of water logging and salinity through adequate drainage facilities, sustainable management of groundwater through ensuring quality and quantity standards and development of ground water regulatory framework.",""],[1,"195","10","Water Storage Expansion through Dam Construction","The existing water storage capacity of 13.44 MAF shall be increased by construction of the Diamer-Basha Dam Project having 6.4 MAF live storage and Mohmand Dam having 0.68 MAF respectively.",""],[1,"195","10","Medium Dam Construction Programme","In addition to that, medium dams having storage capacity of at least 2 MAF will be constructed.",""],[1,"195","12","Irrigation Infrastructure Replacement and Refurbishment","Gradual replacement and refurbishing of decades old irrigation infrastructure in accordance with an adequate asset management plan.",""],[1,"196","7","Gradual Increase in Federal Water Sector PSDP Allocation","Gradual increase of federal PSDP allocation of water sector upto 20 percent till 2030.",""],[1,"196","8","Provincial Financing for Irrigation Projects","the provincial governments should provide financing for irrigation projects through their ADPs.",""],[1,"196","16","Water Emergency Committee for Resource Mobilization","Water Emergency has been declared and constituted a committee with membership from federal and provincial governments to firm up recommendations for resource mobilization for water storages.",""],[1,"196","17","Water Management Investment Programme","The Plan projects a substantial investment of Rs. 1201.13 billion towards crucial water management projects, with a significant portion directed towards the ambitious Basha and Mohmand Dam initiatives.",""],[1,"196","17","Canal Construction and Maintenance Programme","The investment will also contribute to the construction and maintenance of canals, promoting efficient water transportation and distribution systems for agricultural and domestic use.",""],[1,"196","17","Water Supply Projects Expansion","a considerable portion of the funds will be dedicated to water supply projects aimed at meeting",""],[1,"198","3","Canal Remodeling and Groundwater Regulation","Remodeling of Pat Feeder, CRBC (L-G) Lining of K.B Feeder, Kachhi Canal etc. Regulating ground water extraction and its management through Groundwater Regulatory",""],[1,"198","5","Irrigation Infrastructure Replacement and Refurbishment","Gradual replacement & refurbishing of decades old irrigation infrastructure",""],[1,"198","6","Sindh Barrages Improvement Project","Framework Sindh Barrages Improvement Project.",""],[1,"198","9","Flood Damage Rehabilitation of RBOD-I, II and III","Rehabilitation VE of PMflood damages of RBOD-I, II and III",""],[1,"198","9","Implementation of Other Drainage Projects","Implementation of other drainage projects",""]],"9":[[1,"169","5","Provincial Water Act Enactment","Water Act to be issued by all provinces",""],[1,"169","6","Water Regulatory Authorities Establishment","Water regulatory authorities to be set up to ensure untreated wastewater does not flow in rivers and water bodies",""],[1,"194","5","National Water Conservation Strategy","National Water Conservation Strategy (2023-27): NWCS has been developed as a guiding document considering challenges of water shortage in agricultural, Industrial and domestic sectors and suggests some necessary conservation measures to create a balance between demand and supply in cost-efficient manner.",""],[1,"194","7","Water Policy and Institutional Reform Package","This plan recognizes the need to introduce appropriate policy measures, institutional reforms and knowledge-based interventions to make water infrastructure and management system more efficient and sustainable.",""],[1,"194","7","Implementation of National Water Policy and Related Frameworks","The Plan will ensure implementation of National Water Policy, URAAN Pakistan: NETP, 5Es Framework, SDGs and 4RFs based on PDNA.",""],[1,"195","5","Real-Time River Flow Monitoring and Water Accounting System","Improved water governance through Real-time monitoring of river flows to maintain transparent water accounting system to check the increasing trend of unaccounted-for water in the Indus River System.",""],[1,"195","5","Water Sector Institutional Reform and Capacity Building","Establishing effective organizational and management mechanisms through institutional reforms, private sector participation and building capacity of water sector institutions",""],[1,"195","6","River Rights Revival and Environmental Flow Protection","Ensure socio-environmental sustainability and ecosystem preservation following international best practices of recognizing river rights through revival of rivers and ensuring optimum environmental flows.",""],[1,"195","6","GEDSI Mainstreaming in Water and Agriculture Sectors","Ensure GEDSI (Gender Equality and Social Inclusion) in water and agriculture sectors.",""],[1,"195","13","Real-Time River Flow Monitoring System","Real-time monitoring of river flows by IRSA/WAPDA is to be ensured through inter alia telemetric monitoring to maintain transparent water accounting system and to check the increasing trend of unaccounted-for water in the Indus System of Rivers.",""],[1,"196","1","Standardized Water Resources Data Collection and Sharing Mechanism","Federal and provincial water sector organizations would develop a standardized and uniform mechanism for data collection and sharing of various parameters of water resources including but not limited to rivers/canals gauge and discharge, rainfall/snowfall, depth to groundwater table, surface subsurface water quality parameters, river / canal and reservoirs sedimentation",""],[1,"196","3","National Groundwater Regulatory Framework","Formulation of National Groundwater Regulatory Framework",""],[1,"198","5","Standardized Real-Time River Flow Data Collection Mechanism","Standard & uniform mechanism for data collection Real-time river flows",""],[1,"198","6","Telemetry System Installation for Real-Time Discharge Monitoring","Installation of Telemetry System for-real time discharge Monitoring at 27 Key Sites on Indus Basin Irrigation System (IBIS)",""],[1,"198","9","Conjunctive Use of Surface and Groundwater in Saline Areas","Conjuctive use of surface and groundwater saline zone of groundwater",""],[1,"198","16","Feasibility and Technical Studies for Water Management","Feasibility/ Technical Studies, Ground Water Regulatory Framework, Flood zoning, studies to adapt Water Sensitive cities approach etc.",""],[1,"198","16","Groundwater Regulatory Framework","Feasibility/ Technical Studies, Ground Water Regulatory Framework, Flood zoning, studies to adapt Water Sensitive cities approach etc.",""],[1,"212","2","Smart Water Management Systems in Urban Areas","Implement smart water management systems in 10 urban areas, ensuring efficient and sustainable water use.",""],[1,"212","3","Improved Sanitation and Hygiene Access Initiative","Provide access to improved sanitation facilities and promote hygiene and health.",""],[1,"213","7","Implementation of the National Water Policy and National Sanitation Policy","The strategy focuses on the effective implementation of the National Water Policy and the National Sanitation Policy.",""],[1,"213","7","New Water and Sanitation Schemes","Key initiatives include the introduction of new water and sanitation schemes, the enactment of legislation to regulate groundwater extraction, and measures to prevent water contamination.",""],[1,"213","7","Groundwater Extraction Regulation Legislation","Key initiatives include the introduction of new water and sanitation schemes, the enactment of legislation to regulate groundwater extraction, and measures to prevent water contamination.",""],[1,"213","7","Water Contamination Prevention Measures","Key initiatives include the introduction of new water and sanitation schemes, the enactment of legislation to regulate groundwater extraction, and measures to prevent water contamination.",""],[1,"213","7","Rainwater Harvesting Promotion","The adoption of rainwater harvesting systems will be actively promoted, drawing on successful international models and best practices in integrated water resource management.",""],[1,"216","6","National Water and Sanitation Policy Implementation","Implement National Water Policy and National Sanitation Policy.",""],[1,"216","6","New Water Schemes and Groundwater Extraction Legislation","Pioneer new schemes and optimal groundwater extraction legislation.",""],[1,"216","6","Water Contamination Safeguards and Rainwater Harvesting Promotion","Safeguard against contamination and champion rainwater harvesting systems.",""]],"10":[[1,"27","3","Family Planning and Reproductive Health Service Expansion","The plan aims to address these by building on past efforts while tackling persistent issues like high fertility, low contraceptive use, limited awareness, inadequate healthcare infrastructure, and socioeconomic disparities.",""],[1,"27","4","National Knowledge Hub for Evidence-Based Policymaking","These include establishing a National Knowledge Hub for evidence-based policymaking",""],[1,"27","4","Advocacy and Behavior Change Campaigns","implementing robust advocacy and behavior change campaigns",""],[1,"27","4","Sustainable Financing and Governance Strengthening","ensuring sustainable financing and improved governance",""],[1,"27","4","Public-Private Partnership Service Expansion","expanding services through Public-Private Partnerships and LHW program reconfiguration",""],[1,"27","4","Universal Health Coverage Linkage","linking to Universal Health Coverage",""],[1,"27","4","Targeted Counseling and Youth Engagement","providing targeted counseling and youth engagement with cultural sensitivity",""],[1,"27","4","Federal Advisory Support for National Coordination","the federal government will provide essential moral support and advisory assistance to foster national coordination and ensure comprehensive policy implementation across all levels",""],[1,"237","4","Universal Safe Reproductive Health and Family Planning Access","Achieve universal access to safe reproductive health, including family planning services, by 2029",""],[1,"238","7","National Action Plan to Reduce High Fertility","The Plan focuses on devising and implementing a comprehensive national action plan to tackle high fertility rate by involving all the public and private sector stakeholders.",""],[1,"238","7","Free Contraceptive Provision","The Plan envisages political will to manage rampant population, free provision of contraceptives to the couples, integration of health department service delivery outlets for provision of family planning services and an aggressive advocacy and awareness campaign for promoting family planning and small family norms.",""],[1,"238","7","Integration of Health Service Delivery Outlets for Family Planning","The Plan envisages political will to manage rampant population, free provision of contraceptives to the couples, integration of health department service delivery outlets for provision of family planning services and an aggressive advocacy and awareness campaign for promoting family planning and small family norms.",""],[1,"238","7","Family Planning Advocacy and Awareness Campaign","The Plan envisages political will to manage rampant population, free provision of contraceptives to the couples, integration of health department service delivery outlets for provision of family planning services and an aggressive advocacy and awareness campaign for promoting family planning and small family norms.",""],[1,"238","12","Advocacy and Behaviour Change Communication Strategy for Small Family Norms","The Plan also envisions a robust advocacy and behaviour change communication strategy, engaging religious leaders, media, academia, and civil society to promote small family norms and responsible reproductive choices.",""],[1,"239","3","Universal Family Planning and Reproductive Health Service Expansion","A major focus of the plan is the expansion of universal access to Family Planning (FP) and Reproductive Health (RH) services.",""],[1,"239","3","Public-Private Partnership Scale-Up for Reproductive Health Services","Public-private partnerships will be scaled up to enhance service quality, expand post-partum contraception, and ensure outreach to marginalized populations.",""],[1,"239","3","Lady Health Worker Program Reconfiguration","The reconfiguration of the LHW Program will prioritize improved service delivery, capacity building, and equitable coverage.",""],[1,"239","4","Post-Pregnancy Family Planning Implementation Guidance","The Plan aims to provide clear guidance for implementing Post-Pregnancy Family Planning (PPFP) interventions.",""],[1,"239","6","Maternal Counseling and Facility-Based Delivery Services","Ensure provision of comprehensive counseling and services to mothers delivering at healthcare facilities",""],[1,"239","7","Home-Based PPFP Counseling and Referral Linkage Services","Extend PPFP counseling and services to mothers at home, establishing effective referral and linkage mechanisms.",""],[1,"239","8","Lady Health Worker Program Reconfiguration","The reconfiguration of the Lady Health Worker (LHW) program can also significantly enhance population management efforts in Pakistan by focusing on key areas: such as intensifying impact in covered communities, expansion into underserved areas, improving services quality, boosting workforce capacity, and fostering innovative partnerships.",""],[1,"239","9","Family Planning and Reproductive Health Service Expansion","Pakistan plans to enhance its FP and RH related health interventions by expanding population coverage, broadening the range of services, and reducing patient costs.",""],[1,"239","9","Increased Public Financing for Family Planning","Key prerequisites include increasing healthcare budget allocation as a percentage of GDP spent on FP related activities",""],[1,"239","9","Family Planning Service Availability Enhancement","and enhancing FP service availability.",""],[1,"239","9","Reduction of External Donor Dependence for Family Planning","Additionally, reducing reliance on external donor funding and ensuring accountability among service providers, managers, administrators, and policymakers is essential for sustainable progress.",""],[1,"239","9","Accountability Mechanism for Family Planning Service Delivery","Additionally, reducing reliance on external donor funding and ensuring accountability among service providers, managers, administrators, and policymakers is essential for sustainable progress.",""],[1,"240","1","Community-Based Adolescent Counseling Centers","Programs like Aghaaz are planned to establish community-based counseling centers staffed with trained counselors, psychologists, and social workers to offer confidential sessions.",""],[1,"240","1","Nationwide Family Planning Service Expansion","Implementing accessible and comprehensive family planning services nationwide is also planned being crucial.",""],[1,"240","2","Social Media Influencer Engagement for Family Planning","Social media influencers individuals are proposed to be engaged to shape public opinion and support family planning initiatives.",""],[1,"240","3","Youth Reproductive Health Education Integration","Youth engagement initiatives are also planned to integrate reproductive health and family planning content into university curricula and extracurricular platforms to ensure long-term behavioral change and informed decision-making.",""],[1,"240","3","Family Health Clinic and Men Advisory Center Construction","The objective is to establish new purpose-built structures for Family Health Clinics and Men Advisory Centers to improve the quality of services provided, to ensure the privacy of clients coming for counseling on adolescent health problems, and to attract the community by providing a more professional look and environment.",""],[1,"240","4","Community Outreach and Education for Family Planning and Reproductive Health","Moreover, community outreach and education programs are proposed for raising awareness about family planning and reproductive health.",""],[1,"240","4","Men's Advisory Centers for Family Planning and Men's Health Services","Men advisory centers planned to organize workshops, seminars, and information sessions with community leaders, religious institutions, and local NGOS.",""],[1,"240","4","Integration of Family Planning into Men's Health Programs","In addition, Men's advisory centers plans to serve as hubs for providing comprehensive men's health services, including family planning counseling and services.",""],[1,"240","4","Faith Leader Engagement for Family Planning Promotion","Likewise, engaging religious leaders in promoting family planning i.e. involvement of faith leaders (Imams & Khateebs) is planned to effectively enhance the use of contraceptives and decrease infant and maternal mortality.",""],[1,"240","5","Culturally Sensitive Family Planning Outreach Mechanism","The Plan proposed to focus on advisory services through an institutional mechanism to adopt culturally sensitive approaches, such as engaging religious leaders and influencers to promote family planning messages within their communities.",""],[1,"240","5","Public-Private Partnership Support for Family Planning","Moreover, PPPs offer a promising opportunity to enhance family planning efforts in Pakistan.",""],[1,"241","24","Advocacy and Behaviour Change Communication Strategy","Robust advocacy & behaviour change communication strategy (engaging religious leaders, media, academia, civil society)",""],[1,"241","26","BCC Strategy Development and Pilot","Develop BCC strategy; pilot with leaders & media.",""],[1,"241","27","Nationwide Awareness Campaigns and Stakeholder Engagement","Launch campaigns nationwide; engage civil society & academia.",""],[1,"241","30","Behavior Change Communication Institutionalization","Sustain advocacy; institutionalize BCC models.",""],[1,"241","44","Domestic Family Planning Investment Increase","Increase domestic investment in FP programs; reduce reliance",""],[1,"242","10","Expansion of Universal Family Planning and Reproductive Health Services","Expand universal access to FP/RH services (district hospitals, FP centres, BHUS, underserved areas, 40 percent lacking LHW coverage)",""],[1,"242","11","Service Gap Assessment and Expansion Planning","Assess service gaps; plan expansion for underserved areas.",""],[1,"242","12","Phased Expansion of FP/RH Service Points and Outreach","Phased Expansion: Begin phased expansion of FP/RH service points & outreach.",""],[1,"242","13","Universal Coverage and Lady Health Worker Outreach Expansion","Achieve Coverage: Make significant progress towards universal coverage & LHW outreach.",""],[1,"242","16","Public-Private Partnership Scale-Up","Scale up Public- Private Partnerships (PPPs) for",""],[1,"242","18","PPP Identification and Scale-Up Framework Development","Identify PPPs; develop frameworks for scale-up.",""],[1,"242","19","Pilot Public-Private Partnerships and Quality Monitoring","Implement pilot PPPs; monitor quality/outrea",""],[1,"242","20","Public-Private Partnership Expansion and Diversification","Expand successful PPPs; diversify",""],[1,"242","22","PPP Model Institutionalization for Service Delivery","Institutionalize PPP models for sustained service.",""],[1,"242","24","Lady Health Worker Program Reconfiguration","Reconfiguration of LHW Program (improved service delivery, capacity",""],[1,"242","26","Lady Health Worker Program Review and Reconfiguration Plan","Review LHW program; develop reconfiguratio n plan.",""],[1,"242","27","Reconfigured Program Implementation and Training","Implement & Train: Begin reconfigured program;",""],[1,"242","32","Master-Trainer and Trainer Capacity Development","Strengthen & develop skilled cadre of master-trainers & trainers",""],[1,"242","34","Master Trainer Needs Assessment and Training Programme","Assess & Train Master- Trainers: Conduct needs assessment; train master- trainers.",""],[1,"242","35","Cascade Training Programme for Service Providers","Cascade Trainings: Conduct cascading trainings for service providers.",""],[1,"242","36","Cadre Training Expansion and Skills Enhancement","Cover All & Enhance: Expand training to all cadres; enhance skills.",""],[1,"242","39","Maternal Counselling and Services at Healthcare Facilities","Ensure comprehensive counselling & services to mothers at healthcare facilities",""],[1,"242","41","PPFP Counselling Protocol Development and Dissemination","Develop & disseminate PPFP counselling protocols.",""],[1,"242","42","Target Facility Service Implementation and Compliance Monitoring","Implement services in target facilities; monitor adherence.",""],[1,"242","44","Counselling Quality and Service Uptake Monitoring","Monitor counselling quality & service uptake.",""],[1,"242","45","Integration of PPFP Services into Routine Maternal Care","Sustain PPFP services as routine maternal care.",""],[1,"243","1","Home-Based PPFP Counselling and Referral Services","Extend PPFP counselling & services to mothers at home, effective referral & linkage mechanisms",""],[1,"243","3","Pilot Home-Based Counselling and Referral Models","Pilot home- based counselling/ref errals; design scalable models.",""],[1,"243","4","Home-Based Postpartum Family Planning Outreach Scale-Up","Begin scaling up home- based PPFP outreach via LHWs.",""],[1,"243","5","Referral Linkage Strengthening","Strengthen referral linkages to facilities.",""],[1,"243","7","Home-Based Outreach and Referral System","Institutionalize home-based outreach & referrals.",""],[1,"243","9","Health System Expansion and Cost Reduction","Enhance health system (expand population coverage, broaden service range, reduce patient costs)",""],[1,"243","11","Universal Health Coverage Strategic Planning","Assess gaps; develop strategic plan for UHC.",""],[1,"243","12","Service Expansion and Pilot Programs","Expand & Pilot: Begin initial service expansion & pilot programs.",""],[1,"243","18","Fiscal Analysis and Budget Advocacy","Analyse & Advocate: Conduct fiscal analysis; advocate for increased budget.",""],[1,"243","19","Initial Budget Increase Implementation","Secure & implement initial budget increase.",""],[1,"243","25","Human Resources Assessment and Recruitment and Training Planning","Conduct HR assessment; develop recruitment/tr aining plans.",""],[1,"243","26","Health Service Staffing and Availability Improvement","Recruit new staff; begin improving service availability.",""],[1,"243","30","Durable Safety Nets","Establish durable safety nets",""],[1,"243","32","Feasibility Study and Durable Health Protection Safety Nets","Conduct feasibility; formulate durable safety nets for health protection.",""],[1,"243","36","Institutionalization of Sustainable Safety Nets","Fully institutionalize sustainable safety nets.",""],[1,"243","39","Pre-Marital Counselling for Adolescents","Pre-marital counselling for adolescents (community- based centres)",""],[1,"243","41","Pilot Communities and Centre Curriculum Development","Pilot communities; develop curriculum for centres.",""],[1,"243","42","Centre Expansion and Counsellor Training","Scale up centres; train additional counsellors.",""],[1,"243","43","Outreach Expansion and Workshop Programme","Expand Outreach: Expand reach to more areas; conduct workshops.",""],[1,"243","46","Nationwide Accessible Family Planning Services and Clinics","Implement accessible & comprehensive FP services nationwide (establishing clinics/centres)",""],[1,"243","47","Health Facility Mapping and Clinic Upgrading Plan","Map facilities; plan for new/upgraded clinics.",""],[1,"243","48","Phased Establishment and Upgrading of Facilities","Establish & Staff: Begin phased establishment/ upgrading; staff adequately.",""],[1,"243","49","Family Planning Expansion and Mobile Unit Deployment","Continue expansion; deploy mobile FP units.",""],[1,"243","51","Nationwide Family Planning Services","Ensure & maintain nationwide FP services.",""],[1,"244","1","Social Media Influencer Campaigns","Engage social media influencers for campaigns (TV, radio, health fairs, seminars, workshops)",""],[1,"244","3","Influencer Identification and Content Strategy Development","Identify influencers; develop content strategy.",""],[1,"244","4","Launch and Engagement Campaigns","Launch initial campaigns; stimulate discussion.",""],[1,"244","5","Campaign Expansion and Misinformation Counteraction","Expand & Counter: Scale up campaigns; counteract misinformatio n.",""],[1,"244","15","Purpose-Built Family Health Clinics and Men Advisory Centres","Establish new purpose-built structures for Family Health Clinics & Men Advisory Centres",""],[1,"244","26","Outreach Expansion and Localization of Programs","Expand & Localize: Scale up outreach; develop localized programs.",""],[1,"244","28","Sustain and Adapt Community-Led Initiatives","Sustain & adapt community-led initiatives.",""],[1,"244","31","Service Package Design and Pilot Centre Identification","Design service packages; identify pilot centres.",""],[1,"244","32","Pilot Centre Operationalization and Integrated Services","Operationalize pilot centres; begin integrated services.",""],[1,"244","34","Men's Family Planning Engagement Monitoring","Monitor men's engagement in FP & service use.",""],[1,"244","35","Integrated Men's Health and Family Planning Services","Sustain comprehensive men's health/FP services.",""],[1,"244","36","Religious Leader Engagement for Family Planning Promotion","Engrain religious leaders in promoting family planning",""],[1,"244","38","Sensitization Materials and Engagement Strategy Development","Develop sensitization material; create engagement strategy.",""],[1,"244","39","Initial Workshops and Dialogue Process","Workshops & Dialogue: Conduct initial workshops & dialogues.",""],[1,"244","40","Family Planning Message Integration and Outreach Expansion","Integrate FP messages; expand outreach.",""],[1,"244","44","Culturally Sensitive Community Engagement Approach","Adopt culturally sensitive approaches (engaging religious leaders & influencers)",""],[1,"244","46","Tailored Family Planning Messaging","Research sensitivities; develop tailored FP messages.",""],[1,"245","1","Supportive Policy Advocacy and Stakeholder Collaboration","Advocate for supportive policies & collaborate with government agencies, NGOs, stakeholders",""],[1,"245","4","Collaboration and Joint Initiatives Launch","Collaborate & Launch: Establish collaborations; launch joint initiatives.",""],[1,"245","8","Private-Public Partnerships for Family Planning","Leverage Private-Public Partnerships (PPPs) to enhance FP efforts",""],[1,"245","10","PPP Area Identification and Regulatory Framework Development","Identify PPP areas; develop regulatory frameworks.",""],[1,"245","11","Finalize Agreements and Pilot Innovative Models","Finalize agreements; pilot innovative models.",""],[1,"245","12","PPP Scale-Up and Diversification","Scale up successful PPPs; diversify types.",""]],"11":[[1,"7","2","Targeted Social Protection, Education, and Health Investments","Importantly, we will promote equity and empowerment through targeted social protections and investments in education and health.",""],[1,"12","1","Human Capital Investment Initiative","We will invest heavily in human capital through education, healthcare, and skills development with special initiatives for youth, women, and marginalized regions.",""],[1,"28","2","Primary Healthcare Strengthening","The Plan outlines 14 strategic policy objectives, including strengthening primary healthcare, scaling up RMNCAH and nutrition services, ensuring essential health service packages (EPHS), and addressing NCDs and mental health through national programs.",""],[1,"28","2","RMNCAH and Nutrition Service Scale-Up","The Plan outlines 14 strategic policy objectives, including strengthening primary healthcare, scaling up RMNCAH and nutrition services, ensuring essential health service packages (EPHS), and addressing NCDs and mental health through national programs.",""],[1,"28","2","Essential Health Service Package Provision","The Plan outlines 14 strategic policy objectives, including strengthening primary healthcare, scaling up RMNCAH and nutrition services, ensuring essential health service packages (EPHS), and addressing NCDs and mental health through national programs.",""],[1,"28","2","National NCD and Mental Health Programmes","The Plan outlines 14 strategic policy objectives, including strengthening primary healthcare, scaling up RMNCAH and nutrition services, ensuring essential health service packages (EPHS), and addressing NCDs and mental health through national programs.",""],[1,"28","2","Uraan Free Treatment Package","Flagship commitments under Uraan , such as free treatment for Hepatitis, Diabetes, and Cardiac care, are embedded within the plan.",""],[1,"28","2","National Health Awareness and Behaviour Change Communication Campaign","A national health awareness and Behaviour Change Communication (BCC) campaign will also be launched, reinforcing Uraan's focus on public engagement.",""],[1,"233","1","Primary Healthcare Strengthening and Universal Health Coverage Scheme","Strengthen primary healthcare and implement universal health coverage schemes.",""],[1,"233","1","Food Fortification and Maternal-Child Nutrition Programme","Combat malnutrition via food fortification and maternal-child health programs.",""],[1,"233","1","WASH Services and Rural Health Infrastructure Expansion","Prioritize WASH services and rural health infrastructure.",""],[1,"233","12","Rural Health Infrastructure Upgrade","Upgrade rural health infrastructure and scale up Social Health Insurance",""],[1,"233","12","Social Health Insurance Expansion","Upgrade rural health infrastructure and scale up Social Health Insurance",""],[1,"247","1","Health Coverage Expansion and Service Delivery Strengthening","Over the years, Pakistan has made important strides in expanding health coverage, investing in health workforce development, introducing social protection schemes, and strengthening disease surveillance and response mechanisms.",""],[1,"247","1","Universal Health Coverage and Digital Health Innovation","With a strong emphasis on UHC, digital health innovation, and community-based interventions, the sector is evolving toward a more inclusive and integrated model of service delivery.",""],[1,"248","6","Primary and Primary Health Care Strengthening and Communicable Disease Control","Strengthen primary and PHC and improve control of communicable diseases.",""],[1,"248","7","Essential Package of Health Services Delivery","Deliver an Essential Package of Health Services (EPHS) to advance UHC.",""],[1,"248","10","Health Human Capital Development Initiative","Advance human capital development for health, with a focus on regulation, quality, and workforce availability.",""],[1,"248","11","Hospital Care and Health System Capacity Improvement","Improve hospital care, service accessibility, and system capacity across all levels.",""],[1,"248","16","Health Financing Expansion","Secure optimal and sustainable health financing with increased budget allocations.",""],[1,"249","3","Expansion of RMNCH, Emergency, Family Planning, and Nutrition Services through BHUS/RHCs","Expand RMNCH, emergency, family planning, and nutrition services via BHUS/RHCs",""],[1,"249","3","Integration of Vertical Health Programs with Primary and Secondary Health Care","Integrate vertical programs with PHC & SHC",""],[1,"249","3","Minimum Service Delivery Standards Operationalization","Operationalize minimum service delivery standards",""],[1,"249","8","Expansion of Essential Package of Health Services","Expand EPHS to include family medicine, gerontology, under- nutrition, and newborn survival",""],[1,"249","8","Primary Health Care Diagnostics and Human Resources Upgrade","Equip PHC with essential diagnostics and HR",""],[1,"249","8","UHC Tracer Indicator Monitoring System","Monitor with UHC tracer indicators",""],[1,"249","8","Quality Assurance and Citizen Feedback Institutionalization","Institutionalize quality assurance and citizen feedback",""],[1,"250","12","Health Infrastructure Upgrade and Service Expansion","Upgrade infrastructure with labs/pharmacy/Parame dics - Develop rural general physician cadre - Weak referral system - Reach 18 beds/10,000 pop - PPPs for underserved areas under health insurance",""],[1,"250","12","Rural General Physician Cadre Development","Develop rural general physician cadre",""],[1,"250","12","Health Insurance Public-Private Partnerships for Underserved Areas","PPPs for underserved areas under health insurance",""],[1,"251","17","Universal Health Coverage Regulatory Reforms","Implement strategies and UHC regulatory reforms",""],[1,"252","2","Health Financing Expansion and Fiscal Reform Package","Raise health spending from <1 percent to 3 percent of GDP - Expand health insurance and conditional cash transfers - Introduce health taxes (tobacco, sugar) - Improve budget utilization and public- private financing",""]],"12":[[1,"248","8","RMNCAH and Nutrition Outcomes Improvement","Improve Reproductive, Maternal, Newborn, Child, and Adolescent Health (RMNCAH) and nutrition outcomes.",""],[1,"248","19","Nutrition-Specific Interventions Mainstreaming","Mainstream nutrition-specific interventions across all tiers of health service delivery.",""],[1,"249","13","Universal Sexual and Reproductive Health Services","Universalize Sexual and Reproductive Health (SRH), ANC, SBA",""],[1,"249","13","Integration of Family Planning and Safe Abortion Services","Integrate FP and safe abortion services across tiers",""],[1,"249","13","Early Childhood and Adolescent Health Expansion","Expand early childhood & adolescent health",""],[1,"249","13","Community-Based Nutrition and Breastfeeding Support","Community-based nutrition, breastfeeding support",""],[1,"252","20","Integration of Malnutrition Treatment into EPHS","Integrate treatment of acute/chronic malnutrition into EPHS",""],[1,"252","20","Expansion of Stabilization Centers and Outreach Services","Expand stabilization centers and outreach",""],[1,"252","20","Therapeutic Food and Micronutrient Supply Security","Secure therapeutic food and micronutrient supplies",""],[1,"258","1","Nutrition-Specific Services Expansion and Mainstreaming","Expanding coverage of nutrition specific interventions, ensuring full integration/ mainstreaming of nutrition specific/ direct services to all health service delivery points both at facility and community levels",""],[1,"259","11","National Multi-Sectoral Nutrition Program","Implementation of National Multi-Sectoral Nutrition Program to Reduce Stunting and other Forms of Malnutrition under Pakistan Nutrition Initiative (PANI)",""],[1,"260","4","Food Fortification and Bio-Fortification Scale-Up Program","Scale up of Food Fortification/ Bio- Fortification Program",""],[1,"260","10","Nutrition Cadre Staffing for Health Facilities","Dedicated human resources for nutrition initiatives in health facilities, including advocacy for nutrition cadre structure within the relevant National Provincial Ministries Departments",""]],"13":[[1,"70","2","SDGs Achievement Programme Funding","To achieve SDGs targets by 2030, substantial funding for SDGs Achievement Programme and other districts with 6 percent has been envisaged.",""],[1,"70","2","University Campus Strengthening for Higher Education Excellence","For promoting higher education, the federal government will continue its funding for strengthening of already established university campuses to make them a centre of excellence during the plan period.",""],[1,"70","2","Federal and Provincial University Resource Support","HEC would focus on federally charted universities and chip in resources from provinces for provincial chartered universities.",""],[1,"114","3","Tenure Track System Continuation","This funding also included continuation of Tenure Track System (TTS) and hiring of foreign faculty on tenure basis.",""],[1,"114","3","Foreign Faculty Hiring on Tenure Basis","This funding also included continuation of Tenure Track System (TTS) and hiring of foreign faculty on tenure basis.",""],[1,"117","3","Triple Helix Education Quality Improvement Initiative","Improve quality of education services and promote triple helix system",""],[1,"117","7","Higher Education Scholarship Expansion for Developing Countries","Expand higher education scholarships for developing countries by 2020, substantially expand globally the number of scholarships available to developing countries, in particular least developed countries, Small Island developing States and African countries, for enrolment in higher education, including vocational training and information and communications technology, technical, engineering and scientific programs, in developed countries and other developing countries.",""],[1,"118","2","Higher Education Access Expansion and Quality Improvement","To expand the Higher Education System's access through creation of new universities and ensure that quality of the system in universities and affiliated colleges.",""],[1,"118","3","Higher Education Curriculum Rebalancing Toward Humanities and Social Sciences","HEC must put an increased Emphasis on Humanities, Social Sciences, Arts and Design to rebalance its previous tilt towards Sciences and Engineering.",""],[1,"118","5","Higher Education Quality Improvement Focus","The Higher Education Sector must commit itself to a relentless focus on quality of research, teachers, students and researchers.",""],[1,"118","6","Tier-1 Local University Empowerment and World-Class Upgrade Initiative","To Empower and Enable 10 to 15 Tier-1 Local Universities to become World Class Institutions through greater autonomy and additional financial support.",""],[1,"118","8","Accreditation Bodies Strengthening and Establishment","Strengthening and establishment of accreditation bodies",""],[1,"119","3","Higher Education Quality Framework Implementation","HEC to implement its new Quality Framework developed in collaboration with British Council for improving overall quality of higher education",""],[1,"119","9","PhD Faculty Expansion in Universities","Enhance PhD Faculty in universities to grow from existing 27 percent of total faculty to 32 percent",""],[1,"119","19","Higher Education Infrastructure Consolidation and University Establishment Review","During the plan period, HEC in collaboration with all stakeholders must revisit its criteria for","HEC"],[1,"120","1","New University and Campus Establishment","establishment of new universities and university campuses in consultation with provincial governments and keep a track and check of the same in the light of available resources for development and recurring budgets.",""],[1,"120","1","Affiliated College Capacity Upgrading Programme","HEC in collaboration with provinces must also work for upgrading the capacity, curriculum and pedagogy requirements of affiliated colleges to bring them at par with universities.",""],[1,"120","1","Lifelong Learning and Flexible Education Expansion","It is also proposed that lifelong learning opportunities, flexible programs and continued education programs to be introduced for increasing access to higher education for everyone.",""],[1,"120","1","Mandatory DEI and Gender Equity Plans for Universities","HEC to make Diversity, Equity & Inclusion (DEI) and Gender Equity Plans a mandatory part of university policies as per guidance of HEC.",""],[1,"120","1","Dedicated Funding Platforms for New Universities","There must be dedicated funding platforms for new universities so that development capacity of existing universities is not affected.",""],[1,"120","1","Enhanced Provincial Funding for University Infrastructure","Funding from provincial governments for provincially chartered universities needs to be enhanced especially for infrastructure development.",""],[1,"120","2","Quality Framework Implementation and Monitoring Plan","There is need to develop action plan for implementation of the said framework along with continuous and robust monitoring.",""],[1,"120","2","University Quality Enhancement Cells Expansion","HEC already has an ongoing drive for establishment of Quality Enhancement Cells (QECs) in universities, which must be continued as these cells are facilitators and enablers for addressing the quality objectives.",""],[1,"120","2","Graduate Employability Reporting Requirement","HEC must publish the employability rates for university graduates as one of the measures of quality of their output.",""],[1,"120","2","Annual Graduate Quality Improvement Requirement","Universities shall be expected to demonstrate year by year improvement in the quality of graduates through improvements in teaching quality.",""],[1,"120","2","University Institutional Review Boards and Ethical Committees","Institutional Review Boards / Ethical Committees must be established at universities by HEC as a policy for zero tolerance towards plagiarism, fake journals and publishing, and academic fraud.",""],[1,"120","4","National Curriculum Review Committee Strengthening","There is need to focus on expanding and strengthening National Curriculum Review Committees (NCRCs) to keep undergraduate and graduate curricula abreast of fast-changing needs and developments according to international standards.",""],[1,"120","4","Quality Enhancement and Assurance Cell Strengthening","It also require to strengthen quality enhancement and assurance cells (PCSQA) through output analysis in response to emerging economic needs.",""],[1,"120","4","New Accreditation Councils for Emerging Industrial Areas","Urgent need to work for establishment of new accreditation councils in emerging areas of industrial needs or provide input on the same to the government in consultation with the relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"124","9","Higher Education Sector Consolidation and University Expansion Planning","HEC to concentrate on consolidation of sector and establishment of new universities / university campuses to be done only after proper feasibility, need assessment, supply-demand analysis and stakeholder consultation.","HEC"],[1,"124","10","Dedicated Funding Stream for Universities","HEC to establish a dedicated funding stream universities (prioritized as stated above), development capacity of existing universities affected.",""],[1,"124","14","Women-Only Campuses Expansion","More Women Only campuses to be established, as and where needed.",""],[1,"124","15","IT and Computer Higher Education Expansion","Focussing on IT / Computer related higher education programs and course to produce quality manpower of 200k IT graduates as envisaged in Uraan Pakistan",""],[1,"124","18","Implementation of the New Quality Framework","HEC to implement its new Quality Framework during the plan period",""],[1,"125","7","University Employability Statistics and Programme Recognition Requirement","HEC to ensure universities to publish their employability statistics and ensure that the program offered by the universities are recognized.",""],[1,"125","13","University Institutional Review Boards and Ethical Committees Policy","HEC to ensure during plan period that all universities have established Institutional Review Boards / Ethical Committees as a policy for zero tolerance towards plagiarism, fake journals and publishing, and academic raud.","HEC"],[1,"125","15","Strengthening Quality Enhancement and Quality Assurance Cells","Ministry of Science & Technology in collaboration with PSQCA and PNAC to ensure strengthening of Quality Enhancement Cells (QECs) and Quality Assurance Cells (QACs) through output analysis in response to emerging economic needs.","Ministry of Science & Technology | PSQCA | PNAC"],[1,"125","15","Strengthening PNAC Accreditation and Technical Support","PNAC under the ministry to strengthen its accreditation work and provide technical support to government for identifying emerging areas of industrial needs for accreditation","PNAC"]],"14":[[1,"232","7","School Access Expansion and Vocational Training Programme","Expand school access and vocational training, especially in rural areas.",""],[1,"232","7","Curriculum Alignment and Digital Learning Integration Reform","Align curricula with labor market needs and integrate digital learning.",""],[1,"232","7","Girls' Education and Inclusive Education Policy","Enhance girls' education and implement inclusive education policies.",""],[1,"233","16","Conditional Cash Transfers for Education Access","Improve access to education via conditional cash transfers and school-based skill programs",""],[1,"233","16","School-Based Skills Programme","Improve access to education via conditional cash transfers and school-based skill programs",""],[1,"264","2","Education Access, Quality, Equity, and Technology Integration Initiative","The Plan is designed with a strong commitment to align with URAAN Pakistan priorities and SDG-4 targets for education, ensuring concerted efforts towards improving and expanding access to education, optimizing the performance and quality of education, ensuring equitable access to education and incorporating technology tools in education.",""],[1,"264","13","Inclusive and Equitable Quality Education Access Initiative","Ensure inclusive and equitable access to quality education at all levels with a focus on reducing disparities, improving learning outcomes, and strengthening the foundational systems necessary for sustainable human development.",""],[1,"265","5","Inclusive Education Infrastructure and Quality School Development","To remove gender and regional disparities, this Plan focuses on investing in infrastructure, teacher training, curriculum development and establishing quality educational institutions to ensure no child is left behind.",""],[1,"267","17","Building Code Revision for Special Needs Education and Gender Parity","Building codes may be changed for special need education and to enhance gender parity.",""]],"15":[[1,"22","2","Capital Market Revitalization Initiative","The Plan aims to revitalize Pakistan's capital markets by promoting new business listings, financing infrastructure and SMEs, and expanding investment options.",""],[1,"58","10","Futures and Capital Market Regulatory Reforms","During the period under review, the SECP introduced various reforms to strengthen futures and capital markets.",""],[1,"59","1","PRIDE Online IPO Application System","the SECP in coordination with PSX, launched the \"Public Offerings Revolutionized through an Integrated & Digitized Experience (PRIDE)\" online system for streamlined Initial Public Offering (IPO) application submission and tracking",""],[1,"59","5","Professional Clearing Member Regime for Investor Custody","A number of risk management reforms have been introduced along with adequate measures to secure custody of investors through the implementation of a Professional Clearing Member regime.",""],[1,"62","16","Capital Market-Real Economy Linkage Initiative","Encourage closer linkage and connectivity of the capital market with the real economy and make practicable contributions towards future initiatives of the government;",""],[1,"62","17","Investor Protection Compliance and Transparency Promotion","Promote efficiency, transparency, integrity and a strong culture of compliance to investor protection;",""],[1,"62","18","Capital Market Outreach Expansion for Diversified Investment and Long-Term Savings","Provide diversified investment alternatives and facilitate long-term savings and investment by extending outreach of capital market;",""],[1,"62","20","Non-Banking Financial Sector Participation in Capital Market Development","Encourage participation of the non-banking financial sector in the development of a vibrant and active capital market including promotion of REITS in Pakistan;",""],[1,"62","22","Corporate Governance and Sustainability Promotion for Listed Companies and Capital Market Infrastructure Institutions","Promote sustainability and enhance governance practices at listed companies and Capital Market Infrastructure Institutions;",""],[1,"62","24","Debt Capital Market Development for Infrastructure Financing","Develop debt capital market with the aim to reduce cost of borrowing by government for financing new infrastructure projects;",""],[1,"63","2","Capital Market Diversification and Non-Banking Financial Sector Reform","During the Plan period, wide-ranging reforms will be initiated for diversification of the capital market and expansion of the non-banking financial sector.",""],[1,"63","3","SECP Regulatory Reform for Market Development and Investor Protection","Introduction of reforms in various SECP regulations to facilitate market development, provide ease of doing business and protection of investors.",""],[1,"63","4","Capital Market Governance Reform and Development Fund","Bringing governance reforms in Capital Market Infrastructure Institutions and introduction of Capital Market Development Fund in line with international best practices.",""],[1,"63","5","Securities Market Regulatory Framework Reform","Introducing regulatory framework for securities managers to enable securities brokers, shortening the settlement cycle from T+2 to T+1, facilitating operationalization of Online Only Brokers and issuance of ESG guidelines for listed",""],[1,"63","7","ESG Index and Climate Disclosure Requirements for Listed Companies","Facilitating launch of Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) Index at PSX and introducing requirements of climate related disclosures for listed companies aligned with National Green Taxonomy.",""],[1,"63","8","Derivative Products and Shariah-Compliant Market Development at PSX","Facilitating launch of derivative products, enhancement of circuit breakers at PSX, facilitating Shariah compliant market at PSX through introduction of Islamic products.",""],[1,"63","9","Corporate Governance Regulations Reform","Bringing further reforms in Code of Corporate Governance Regulations in light of international best practices.",""],[1,"63","10","Strengthening Cybersecurity Measures at Capital Market Infrastructure Institutions","Strengthening Cybersecurity Measures at Capital Market Infrastructure Institutions.",""],[1,"63","11","Introduction of Agri-only Futures Brokers","New category of futures brokers i.e. 'Agri-only' brokers with lower entry barriers and compliance requirements shall be introduced by PMEX to encourage new participants in the commodities futures market.",""],[1,"63","12","Linking PMEX Futures Trading with Agricultural Commodities Market","Linking futures trading at PMEX with the domestic agricultural commodities market and regular trading of Electronic Warehouse Receipt based futures contracts at its platform.",""],[1,"63","13","PMEX Clearing and Settlement Function Transfer Plan","Facilitating segregation of clearing and settlement functions of PMEX in coordination with both PMEX and National Clearing Company of Pakistan Limited (NCCPL), and finalizing an action plan to transfer the in-house clearing and settlement function of PMEX to another entity.",""],[1,"63","14","REIT Regulations Amendment and Registration and Trading Market Board","Amendments in REIT Regulations, 2022 to streamline the Regulations and help drive growth in the broader real estate market through REIT and introduction of new board for public unlisted companies namely \"Registration and Trading Market\"",""],[1,"64","14","Capital Market Governance Reform and Development Fund","Governance reforms in Capital Market :selected: Infrastructure Institutions and introduction of Capital Market Development Fund",""],[1,"64","15","Launch of ESG Index at PSX","Launch of Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) Index at PSX",""],[1,"64","16","Enhancement of Circuit Breakers and Introduction of Islamic Products at PSX","Enhancement of circuit breakers and introduction of Islamic products at PSX",""],[1,"64","19","Link PMEX Futures Trading with Domestic Agricultural Commodities Market","Linking futures trading at PMEX with domestic agricultural commodities market and enabling regular trading of Electronic Warehouse Receipt based futures contracts.",""],[1,"64","20","Segregation of Clearing and Settlement Functions of PMEX","Facilitating segregation of clearing and settlement functions of PMEX",""],[1,"64","21","Registration and Trading Market for Public Unlisted Companies","Introduction of new board for public unlisted companies namely \"Registration and Trading Market\"",""],[1,"330","2","SECP Digitalization and Cybersecurity Initiative","internal systems are also being digitized under SECP's Leading Efficiency through Automation Prowess (LEAP) initiative, which also includes introduction of a cyber-security framework to address vulnerabilities in the wake of increasing digitalization in the corporate and financial sectors.",""],[1,"330","2","Sustainability Disclosure and Gender Equality Regulatory Framework","Further, to address the Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) concerns, regulatory framework is being developed for providing sustainability related disclosures and promoting gender equality across its regulated sectors.",""],[1,"340","7","SECP Capital Market Reform Programme","Introduce SECP's capital market reforms by revamping primary market framework",""],[1,"340","8","SECP One-Window Registration System","Establishment of SECP one-window registration system in collaboration with federal, provincial and other state bodies to facilitate corporatization",""],[1,"340","9","Companies Act Review and Modernization","Review of Companies Act, 2017 to align the framework with developments in the digital space, rationalize reporting requirements, and enhance transparency",""],[1,"340","10","Legislative and Fiscal Reform for Financial Sector Regulation","Amendment and Fiscal Measures SECP Act 1997, NBFC Rule 2003, CRC Rules 1993, Modaraba Ordinance, Insurance Ordinance, Revamping of Corporate Laws & Tax Rationalization for Private Fund and Mutual Funds",""],[1,"340","12","ESG Disclosure and Gender Equality Regulatory Framework","Regulatory framework to address ESG concerns by providing sustainability- related disclosures and promoting gender equality across its regulated sectors.",""],[1,"340","13","Five-Year Insurance Sector Strategic Plan","Launching of five-year Strategic Plan to improve regulatory framework, policyholder protection and increase insurance penetration in the country",""],[1,"340","14","Cyber Governance and Risk Management Framework for SECP","Development of Cyber Governance and Risk Management Framework for SECP",""]],"16":[[1,"21","2","Domestic Resource Mobilization and Tax Reform Package","During the Plan period, major thrust of the fiscal policy would be on domestic resource mobilization.",""],[1,"21","2","Public Financial Management Reform","Fiscal policy involves intensive Public Sector Enterprises (PSEs) / State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) reforms, public financial management reforms and debt management reforms besides tax policy reforms.",""],[1,"21","2","Debt Management Reform","Fiscal policy involves intensive Public Sector Enterprises (PSEs) / State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) reforms, public financial management reforms and debt management reforms besides tax policy reforms.",""],[1,"21","2","Tax Policy Reform","Fiscal policy involves intensive Public Sector Enterprises (PSEs) / State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) reforms, public financial management reforms and debt management reforms besides tax policy reforms.",""],[1,"22","1","Broad Fiscal Reform Package","The Plan envisages broader fiscal reforms on both revenue and expenditure sides to address long-standing issues and ensure sustainable growth.",""],[1,"33","2","Macroeconomic Stabilization and Fiscal Consolidation","The Plan is aligned with Uraan Pakistan and emphasizes stabilizing the macroeconomic environment through prudent fiscal consolidation, enhanced domestic resource mobilization, and improved external sector solvency.",""],[1,"36","7","Macroeconomic Stability and Fiscal Consolidation Plan","The primary focus of this Plan is to sustain macroeconomic stability through fiscal consolidation and external sector solvency.",""],[1,"57","1","Fiscal and Monetary Policy Alignment Framework","The Plan aims to align fiscal and monetary policies with the objectives of Uraan Pakistan to achieve sustainable growth.",""],[1,"57","1","Domestic Resource Mobilization and Tax Base Broadening","During the Plan period, the fiscal policy will concentrate on mobilizing domestic resources by broadening the tax base and directing public spending to support growth and development goals.",""],[1,"60","2","Fiscal Policy Strengthening and Competitiveness Reform Agenda","The plan is aligned with Uraan Pakistan and focuses on robust recovery from existing fiscal challenges with an ambitious reform agenda in terms of strengthening fiscal policy and enhancing competitiveness.",""],[1,"60","4","Sustainable Domestic Resource Mobilization","Reduce reliance on borrowing through sustainable domestic resource mobilization;",""],[1,"60","5","Tax Base Broadening and Compliance Management Reform","Increase tax-to-GDP ratio steadily and consistently in accordance with peer countries by broadening _the tax base, rationalizing tax exemptions/concessions/rates and simplifying procedures.",""],[1,"60","5","Tax Compliance Management and Anti-Smuggling Enforcement Strategy","Specifically, by developing a comprehensive compliance management approach that includes anti- smuggling / anti-misinvoicing / enforcement strategies and leveraging technology- based solutions to prevent significant revenue loss and protect local industry competitiveness;",""],[1,"60","6","Broad-Based Progressive Taxation Reform","Create a broad-based taxation system with progressive and rationalized rates structure to encourage investment and implementation of multilateral trade facilitation agreements;",""],[1,"60","7","Tax Structure Reform to Increase Direct Tax Share","Reduce dependency on indirect taxes and increase the contribution of direct taxes in total tax collection;",""],[1,"60","8","Current Expenditure Rationalization and Subsidy Reform","Rationalize current expenditures including subsidies to increase fiscal space for development expenditure;",""],[1,"60","9","Provincial Own-Revenue Mobilization","Increase the provincial own revenue generating efforts especially in agriculture, services and real estate sectors;",""],[1,"61","2","Tax Administration Strengthening and Tax Policy Separation Reform","Strengthening the FBR's tax administration and improving the tax system's efficacy by separating tax policy and tax administration;",""],[1,"61","3","Tax Rate and Tax Exemption Rationalization","Rationalizing tax rates and tax exemptions/concessions given under various tax laws;",""],[1,"61","4","Efficient Expenditure Management Reform","Efficient expenditure management by curtailing non-productive current expenditures;",""],[1,"61","5","Informal Economy Documentation and Tax Base Expansion","Documentation of informal economy, expanding the tax net of retail trade and harmonization of tax regime to broaden the tax base;",""],[1,"61","6","Fiscal Federalism Reform under the New NFC Award","Improving fiscal federalism to provide provinces more incentives to rely on their own revenue-raising activities rather than federal transfers.",""],[1,"61","7","Indirect Tax Dependence Reduction and Compliance Enforcement Measures","Measures will be undertaken to reduce dependence on indirect taxation including strict regulation for those who conceal/misreport facts, effective crackdown on under/over invoicing, incentives for taxpayers and formal sectors, effective implementation of strategies, robust monitoring and evaluation framework to regularly assess the progress of strategy implementation;",""],[1,"61","8","Risk-Based Tax Auditing and Data Cross-Checking Reform","Tightening risk-based auditing and strengthening data cross-checks through CNIC, third-party data and/or point of sales.",""],[1,"61","8","Simplified Tax Filing and Accelerated Refunds","At the same time, the businesses will be facilitated through simplified tax filing and accelerated system of refunds;",""],[1,"61","9","Tax Litigation Backlog Resolution Plan","the FBR with the help of federal and provincial departments needs to develop a comprehensive plan to handle the backlog of tax cases pending in courts and expedite their resolution","FBR | federal and provincial departments"],[1,"61","11","Public Financial Management Reform Acceleration","Improving the Public Financial Management by expediting reforms agreed with the multilateral institutions for increasing the efficiency and transparency of fiscal spending;",""],[1,"64","2","Tax Administration Reform Package","Tightening risk-based auditing, simplifying tax filing and implementing a system of accelerated refund payments",""],[1,"64","3","Tax Case Backlog Clearance Plan","Developing a comprehensive plan to clear backlog of tax cases pending in courts",""],[1,"335","13","Contributory Pension Reform","Introduction of contributory pension reforms to reduce burden",""],[1,"335","14","Accounting Function System Improvement","Enhancement of accounting functions through system improvements including Green Channel Facility, Micro Payment Gateway etc.",""],[1,"335","18","Transition to Accrual Basis Accounting","Introduction of Transition from cash basis accounting to accrual basis of accounting",""]],"17":[[1,"24","2","Renewable Energy and Green Hydrogen Investment","The Plan prioritizes investment in renewable energy, particularly green hydrogen, and seeks to reorient public investment by leveraging climate and carbon financing.",""],[1,"24","2","Climate and Carbon Finance Mobilization","The Plan prioritizes investment in renewable energy, particularly green hydrogen, and seeks to reorient public investment by leveraging climate and carbon financing.",""],[1,"24","2","Green Climate Fund Engagement and Carbon Credit Instruments","The Plan calls for stronger engagement with mechanisms like the Green Climate Fund (GCF) and innovative instruments such as carbon credits.",""],[1,"40","1","Provincial Renewable Energy Project Prioritization","At the provincial level, in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Balochistan, several initiatives are being prioritized, which include renewable energy projects, mineral extraction, and the development of fisheries value chains.",""],[1,"50","7","Investment in Sustainable and Renewable Energy Sources","Moreover, Government will invest in sustainable and renewable energy sources to",""],[1,"132","1","Clean Energy Transition Investment Programme","Accelerating the transition to a diversified and cleaner energy mix will require targeted public and private investments in grid modernization, net metering, off-grid solutions, and utility-scale renewable projects, aligned with the 2030 renewable energy target of 60 percent clean energy in the generation mix as outlined in the Alternative & Renewable Energy (ARE) Policy 2019.",""],[1,"132","2","National Hydrogen Strategy Development","The Plan will focus to harness the green hydrogen opportunity by formulating a comprehensive National Hydrogen Strategy, conducting feasibility studies, and initiating pilot projects in collaboration with regional and global partners.",""],[1,"132","2","Green Hydrogen Pilot Projects","The Plan will focus to harness the green hydrogen opportunity by formulating a comprehensive National Hydrogen Strategy, conducting feasibility studies, and initiating pilot projects in collaboration with regional and global partners.",""],[1,"132","2","Green Hydrogen Strategic Interventions and Regulatory Reform Package","The Plan aims to chalk- out strategic interventions, international technology partnerships, R&D investment, regulatory reforms, and alignment with industrial decarbonisation plans to position green hydrogen as a core pillar of Pakistan's clean energy transition.",""],[1,"136","3","National Green Hydrogen Strategy","Formulate a comprehensive National Green Hydrogen Strategy that outlines Pakistan's long-term vision, key policy objectives, technological roadmaps, investment models, and implementation milestones.",""],[1,"136","4","Green Hydrogen Regulatory Framework","Develop a dedicated regulatory framework for the green hydrogen sector, covering environmental and safety standards, investment facilitation, tax and tariff incentives, grid integration protocols, and certification mechanisms to ensure sustainability, transparency, and investor confidence.",""],[1,"136","5","Green Hydrogen PPP Enabling Guidelines and Fiscal Incentives","Establish enabling guidelines and fiscal incentives for PPPs to attract domestic and foreign investment in green hydrogen production, storage, and distribution.",""],[1,"136","6","International Hydrogen Technology Cooperation and Domestic R&D Support","Foster international cooperation for technology transfer, capacity-building, and standard harmonization through partnerships with countries leading in hydrogen innovation.",""],[1,"136","6","Domestic Hydrogen R&D Grants and Incentives","Promote domestic R&D by providing grants and incentives to universities, startups, and private sector actors for adaptation and local innovation.",""],[1,"136","7","Pilot-Scale Green Hydrogen Projects","Launch pilot-scale green hydrogen projects in high-potential regions, particularly in synergy with renewable energy zones (e.g., wind corridors in Sindh, solar clusters in Balochistan), focusing on applications in transportation, fertilizer production, steel, and power generation.",""],[1,"142","5","National Green Hydrogen Strategy","Pakistan will formulate a National Green Hydrogen Strategy (NGHS) to outline a long-term roadmap for sectoral development, covering investment models, grid integration, and industrial applications aligned with energy transition and emission reduction targets.",""],[1,"142","5","Green Hydrogen Regulatory Framework","A dedicated regulatory framework will be established to address environmental and safety standards, grid codes, certification protocols, tax and tariff incentives, and investor protections.",""],[1,"142","5","Green Hydrogen Public-Private Partnership Incentive Scheme","Public-Private Partnerships (PPPs) will be promoted through fiscal incentives to mobilize investment in green hydrogen production, storage, and distribution, while encouraging local technology adoption and employment generation.",""],[1,"142","5","Pilot-Scale Green Hydrogen Projects","Pilot-scale green hydrogen projects will be initiated in synergy with Renewable Energy Zones (REZs), such as the wind corridor in Sindh and solar clusters in Balochistan focusing on applications in",""],[1,"143","1","Hydrogen Technology Transfer and R&D Support","Technology transfer, capacity-building, and R&D support will be pursued through international cooperation with leading hydrogen economies, alongside domestic grants for universities, startups, and industries.",""],[1,"176","1","Energy Mix Diversification and Renewable Energy Expansion","During the plan period 2024-29, Pakistan will embark upon a transformative journey of sustainable development, for which energy security will remain basis.",""],[1,"184","7","Renewable Energy Diversification Investment","For long term energy security, it is essential to diversify energy mix by investing in renewable energy sources like wind, solar, and hydro power.",""],[1,"184","7","Sustainable Development of Indigenous Thar Energy Resources","Likewise, Thar's indigenous sources will be utilized in an efficient and environmentally responsible manner.",""],[1,"184","7","Energy Sector Supply Chain Localization and Local Manufacturing Promotion","Furthermore, indigenizing the supply chain requires localization of technological hemisphere, being a crucial component to ensure self-sufficiency, must be gradually enhanced across the entire value chain of the energy sector.",""],[1,"185","1","Renewable Energy Investment Incentives","Initiatives may include public-private partnerships, regulatory reforms, and incentivizing private investment in renewable energy projects to diversify the energy mix and address challenges like power shortages.",""],[1,"186","1","Promotion of Indigenous Energy Resources for Power Generation","the Government's decision to promote the use of indigenous resources such as coal and renewable resources for power generation.",""],[1,"186","4","Renewable Energy Expansion and Fossil Fuel Reduction","future power generation will be made more environment friendly by adding more hydro and non-hydro renewable sources and reducing the use of fossil fuels.",""],[1,"187","2","Renewable Energy Expansion Projects","Similarly, green energy projects are in line with URAAN Pakistan and Alternative and Renewable Energy (ARE) Policy, 2019 which has set targets of increasing the share of renewables to 30 percent in power generation mix 2030.",""],[1,"187","2","Universal Electricity Access Expansion","100 percent electricity access by 2030 will be pursued through grid and off-grid solutions.",""],[1,"190","12","Fast-Track Implementation of Solar PV 2022 Guidelines","Fast Track implementation of Solar PV 2022 guidelines",""],[1,"191","17","Finalize Financial Model for Diamer Bhasha Power Facilities","Finalize the financial model of Diamer Bhasha power facilities, and complete the Mohmand and Dasu Dam including upgrades of existing hydropower fleet",""]],"18":[[1,"181","10","Climate Commitment Balancing Framework","Climate commitments (e.g., COP28 and Energy Transition Mechanism) must balance environmental obligations with existing coal investments.",""],[1,"188","6","Upstream Petroleum Regulator Establishment","An upstream regulator to be established for bifurcation of policy and regulatory functions currently exercised by the Petroleum Division.",""],[1,"188","12","Gas Tariff Rationalization","Rationalization of gas tariff for all sectors of economy shall be undertaken to prevent the further build-up of circular debt.",""],[1,"189","1","Electric Vehicle Regulatory and Standardization Framework","For accelerated adoption of electric vehicles, necessary regulatory, legal frameworks and technological standardization will be actualized to attain the prospective benefits on import bill and emissions.",""],[1,"189","3","Gas Market Liberalization and Utility Unbundling Reform","To liberalize the gas markets and enhance competition, the existing structure of gas utilities would be revamped including unbundling the two-gas company's infrastructure into distinct entities responsible for transmission and distribution.",""],[1,"189","4","Gas Trading Company Establishment","Gas trading companies may be established for not only procurement of hydrocarbons but also to extend risk management services, swaps in energy markets, hedging short- and medium-term exposure, financial assessment of LNG markets and chartering of LNG vessels.",""],[1,"189","6","Alternative Fuel Policy and Regulatory Framework Development","Development of alternative fuel such as biofuels, hydrogen etc. will be materialized via corresponding policy and regulatory frameworks.",""],[1,"191","22","Bifurcation of Policy and Regulatory Functions in Upstream Oil and Gas Sector","Implementation plan for bifurcation of policy and regulatory functions in upstream oil and gas sector",""],[1,"192","6","Gas Sector Reform and Market Liberalization","Gas sector reforms including tariff rationalizations, market liberalization and private sector participation in gas supply and sales",""],[1,"192","7","Alternative Fuel Development Initiative","Development of alternative fuel such as Biofuels, hydrogen etc.",""],[1,"331","2","Oil and Gas Regulatory Competition and Investment Promotion","Oil and Gas Regulatory Authority (OGRA) will foster competition, increase private investment and ownership in petroleum industry while protecting public interest, transparency and impartiality in decision making processes.",""],[1,"331","2","Brownfield Refinery Modernization Policy","Brownfield Refinery Policy aiming to encourage existing refineries to upgrade/modernize /expand their facilities to minimize black product such as Furnace Oil and produce environment friendly fuels as per Euro-V specifications will be implemented while addressing climate related concerns.",""],[1,"331","2","Review and Amendment of OGRA Regulatory Rules","OGRA is in process of reviewing/amending its existing Rules so as to make it more elaborate, comprehensive and investment friendly while addressing various issues of stakeholders.",""],[1,"342","1","Brownfield Refinery Modernization Policy","Implementation of Brownfield Refinery Policy to encourage existing refineries to upgrade/modernize /expand their facilities to minimize black product and produce environment- friendly fuels as per Euro-V specifications",""],[1,"342","2","Regulatory Framework Streamlining for Ease of Doing Business","Streamlining of regulatory frameworks for ease of doing business regime to make it more elaborate, comprehensive and investment friendly while addressing various issues of stakeholders",""]],"19":[[1,"297","4","National Sports City Construction","Construction of National Sports City (NSC) at Narowal",""],[1,"297","5","Construction of Mini-Sports Complexes","PC-II for construction of 250 mini-sports complexes at District/Tehsil level",""],[1,"297","6","Rehabilitation and Strengthening of PSB Coaching Centre Quetta","Rehabilitation/strengthening of existing facilities at PSB coaching centre Quetta",""],[1,"297","7","Rehabilitation and Strengthening of PSB Coaching Centre Karachi","Rehabilitation/strengthening of existing facilities at PSB coaching centre Karachi",""],[1,"297","8","Synthetic Hockey Turf Replacement and Installation","Replacement / Laying of Synthetic Hockey Turfs at Islamabad, Wah Cantt, Peshawar, Quetta and Gilgit.",""],[1,"297","9","PSB Coaching Centre Construction at Skardu","PC-II for construction of PSB Coaching Centre at Skardu, Gilgit-Baltistan",""],[1,"297","11","Rehabilitation and Upgradation of Pakistan Sports Complex Facilities","Rehabilitation/Upgradation of existing facilities at Pakistan Sports Complex (PSC) Islamabad for preparation/holding of South Asian Games",""],[1,"297","12","Electronic Display and Scoring System Installation","Provision and installation of electronic display and scoring system at different facilities of PSC Islamabad and PSB Coaching Centres",""],[1,"298","23","Mini-Sports Complex Construction Programme","Construction of mini-sports complexes in 250 districts (50:50 sharing ratio)",""],[1,"298","27","Basic Sports Infrastructure Provision","Provision of basic sports infrastructure which is accessible to children, young people and physically challenged people/PWD",""],[1,"298","28","Sports Facilities Strengthening and Upgradation","Strengthening / Upgradation of existing sports facilities.",""],[1,"299","8","Mini-Sports District and Tehsil Sports Complex Construction","Construction of 250 mini-sports district/tehsil sports complexes at dist level",""],[1,"299","9","National Sports City Establishment","Establishment of National Sports City at Karachi OF North",""],[1,"299","11","Synthetic Hockey Turf Replacement and Laying Programme","Replacement/Laying of Synthetic Hockey Turf in seven cities viz Islamabad, Faisalabad, Wah Cantt, Peshawar, Quetta, Muzaffarabad and Swat",""],[1,"299","12","Sports Infrastructure Strengthening and Rehabilitation at PSB Coaching Centers","Strengthening/Rehabilitation of existing sports infrastructure of PSB Coaching Centers at Peshawar, Lahore, Karachi and Quetta",""],[1,"300","9","Grassroots Sports Participation Promotion","Promotion of sports participation at grass root level through development of basic sports infrastructure throughout the country including availability of sports equipment in schools.",""],[1,"300","10","Sports Infrastructure Strengthening and Rehabilitation","Strengthening and rehabilitation of existing sports infrastructure",""],[1,"300","11","School-Based Exercise and Sports Promotion for Disabled Children","Promotion of basic exercise and sports activities for disabled children in schools.",""],[1,"300","17","Women-Friendly Sports Infrastructure Development","Encouraging of women in all major sports through construction of women friendly sports infrastructure",""]],"20":[[1,"11","2","Uraan Pakistan National Economic Transformation Plan Execution Framework","It is fully aligned with and serves as the foundational execution framework for the ambitious Uraan Pakistan: National Economic Transformation Plan 2024-2035.",""],[1,"13","1","Integrated Five-Year Development Framework","The 13th Five-Year Plan (2024-2029) has been formulated with consideration for the current socioeconomic context, aiming for growth through consistent policies, enhanced governance, and sound economic planning and implementation.",""],[1,"13","1","National Development Agenda Alignment Framework","Anchored in the national development agenda URAAN Pakistan and guided by the vision of equitable progress, the Plan reflects our collective resolve to address structural imbalances, unlock sectoral potential, and deliver tangible improvements in citizens' lives.",""],[1,"13","1","Integrated Development Framework for Inclusive and Resilient Growth","It provides an integrated development framework prioritising export-led growth, technological advancement, climate resilience, and human development, while fostering balanced regional development and institutional reforms.",""],[1,"21","1","Inclusive Economic Growth and Resource Allocation Strategy","The 13th Five Year Plan aims to ensure long-term sustainability of the economic growth with sufficient job creating ability to make the growth experience more inclusive as envisaged in Uraan Pakistan: 5Es (Exports; E-Pakistan; Environment-Water & Food Security; Energy & Infrastructure Development; and Equity, Ethics & Empowerment) based on National Economic Transformational Plan (2024-29).",""],[1,"21","1","Human Capital, Technology, Industry, Agriculture, Trade, SME, Finance, and Social Protection Strengthening Agenda","It builds on the strength of fundamentals such as quality human capital, upscaling of technological capability, industrial competitiveness, sustainable agriculture, strategic trade policy framework, national SME policy, financial inclusion, social protection and, above all, an investment strategy for efficient resource allocation.",""],[1,"24","6","Sector-Specific Policy Interventions","It proposes sector-specific policy interventions in housing, health, education, culture and heritage, irrigation and food security,",""],[1,"333","21","National Development Framework Development and Implementation","Development and implementation of National Development Framework to align PSDP/ADP investment with Plans/ Policies targets",""],[1,"333","24","Project Appraisal Workshop","Introduction of Project appraisal workshop to engage key stakeholders at design, approval and implementation of projects",""],[1,"338","25","Implementation of ECNEC-Approved Project Process Simplification Recommendations","Implementation of ECNEC-approved recommendations on simplification development processes/ procedures to improve project management",""]],"21":[[1,"12","2","Federal-Provincial Coordination Reform Agenda","It moves away from top-down imposition to a model of close federal-provincial coordination, fully respecting the 18th Amendment.",""],[1,"12","3","Rigorous Governance Structure for Plan Implementation","Therefore, this Plan is backed by a rigorous governance structure:",""],[1,"30","5","Governance Reform Agenda Alignment with Constitutional Obligations","The governance agenda for 13th Five Year Plan has been aligned with the constitutional obligations as mentioned in Part-II (Article 8 to 40) (Chapter: 1-Fundamental Rights and Chapter: II-Principles of Policy) of the Constitution of Islamic Republic of Pakistan.",""],[1,"30","5","Cross-Sectoral Governance Reform for Plan Implementation","The proposed reform agenda will not only improve governance indicators but also facilitate implementation of other sectors initiatives proposed for the Plan period.",""],[1,"30","6","Governance Reform and Institutional Strengthening Agenda","The governance reform agenda of the government will lay special emphasis on institutional strengthening, market fostering, inclusive and sustainable development, participatory approach in policy/ decision making process, civil service reforms, effective delivery of public services, performance management, business process re-engineering including digitization and transparent governance, strengthening criminal justice systems and procedures, domestic resource mobilization, financial management, procurement, legal and intellectual property rights enforcement, and reforming public sector enterprises.",""],[1,"30","7","Governance Innovation and Public Sector Reform Initiatives","The Plan focuses on innovation, capacity building, performance management, service delivery, access to justice, police, research, reforms in public sector including regulatory framework.",""]],"22":[[1,"12","6","Private Sector Enablement and Growth Facilitation","The public sector will play a facilitating and enabling role, focusing on policy reforms, infrastructure, and human capital development to spur private investment.",""],[1,"29","7","Private Sector Enabling Environment Support","Government will facilitate the private sector through providing enabling environment.",""],[1,"41","5","Public Sector Facilitation for Private Sector Participation","The Plan emphasizes the critical role of the public sector as a facilitator and focuses on enhancing skills, technological capabilities, industrial infrastructure, and financial resources, while creating a favourable environment for private sector participation.",""],[1,"41","6","Asaan Karobar Business Simplification Initiative","To streamline business operations, the Asaan Karobar Initiative, using a regulatory guillotine approach to simplify procedures and reduce compliance burdens is being operationalized.",""],[1,"41","6","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Investment Sectors","Key incentives include duty and tax benefits, and the promotion of public-private partnerships (PPPs), particularly in infrastructure, tourism, and services.",""],[1,"41","6","Special Investment Facilitation Council Single-Window Investment Platform","The Special Investment Facilitation Council (SIFC) will act as a single-window platform to attract investment in sectors like minerals, agriculture, IT, and energy, while an Investment Ombudsman system will address investor grievances and disputes.",""],[1,"41","6","Investment Ombudsman Grievance Redress System","The Special Investment Facilitation Council (SIFC) will act as a single-window platform to attract investment in sectors like minerals, agriculture, IT, and energy, while an Investment Ombudsman system will address investor grievances and disputes.",""],[1,"41","6","Strategic Resource Data Bank Development","Developing and maintaining data banks on critical resources such as minerals, gems, and high-value agricultural products will further support targeted FDI.",""],[1,"49","9","One-Window Investor Facilitation Mechanism","One-window operation will be established in consultation with the provinces and other stakeholders and develop guidelines to assist investors in establishing special",""],[1,"52","6","Economic Revival Plan","The \"Economic Revival Plan\" includes the establishment of SIFC to serve as a single window for investment facilitation and policy development.",""],[1,"52","6","Industrial Process Streamlining and Export Promotion Coordination","Various government bodies, will collaborate with provincial governments to streamline industrial processes and boost exports.",""],[1,"53","1","Pakistan Regulatory Modernization Initiative","The \"Pakistan Regulatory Modernization Initiative (PRMI)\" aims to reduce business compliance burdens through regulatory reforms and the establishment of the online Pakistan Business Portal (PBP).",""],[1,"62","23","Ease of Doing Business Reform through Digitization and Process Reengineering","Facilitate \"Ease of Doing Business\" through technology, digitization and process reengineering and promote close collaboration among SBP, FBR and SECP, etc .;","SBP | FBR | SECP"],[1,"79","1","Industrial Policy Framework Strengthening","Focus of the Plan will be on strengthening policy framework to improve the incentive regime for industry, augmenting firm level productivity, standardization, adaptation of new technology and competitiveness to attract higher private investment.",""],[1,"81","9","Business Ready (B-Ready) Business Environment Reform Assessment","EoDB has recently been replaced with Business Ready (B-Ready), a flagship project of the World Bank to assess business environment and to advocate for policy reforms.","Board of Investment (Bol)"],[1,"83","5","Integrated Business Solutions and One-Window Operations","Implementing integrated business solutions, such as one-window operations, and improving coordination between public and private stakeholders can further facilitate progress.",""],[1,"83","5","Business Regulatory and Contract Enforcement Reform","The regulatory framework, judicial processes, contract enforcement, labour regulations, and adherence to Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) standards offer opportunities for strengthening.",""],[1,"84","2","Business Process Streamlining and Efficiency Reform","streamlining processes leading to efficiency and creating conducive business/investment environment",""],[1,"84","2","New Industrial Policy for Competitive Product Markets","Improved product markets by the introduction of new industrial policy to provide level playing field, encouraging competitiveness and developing world class infrastructure will remain some of the key action areas",""],[1,"85","1","National Industrial Policy and Allied Regulatory Reform","National Industrial Policy (NIP) and allied regulations will boost industrial growth and investor confidence by fostering investments, technology upgrades, and a business-friendly ecosystem.",""],[1,"85","3","Public Sector Reform for a Level Playing Field","Skills training will improve SMEs workforce employability, while public sector reforms ensure a level playing field.",""],[1,"85","4","Pakistan Regulatory Modernization Initiative","The Pakistan Regulatory Modernization Initiative (PRMI), Regulatory Guillotine, and SMART initiative will streamline regulations for a transparent, business-friendly environment via public-private dialogues.",""],[1,"89","4","Regulatory Guillotine Agenda","Determine the scope Regulatory Guillotine that will discourage market seeking FDI it and will remove bottlenecks/ barriers to encourage efficiency seeking investment.",""],[1,"91","2","Regulatory Guillotine Implementation","Initiate implementation of Regulatory Guillotine at national and provincial level",""],[1,"91","2","E-Inspection Portal Establishment","Establish E-Inspection Portal",""],[1,"91","5","Tax Simplification and Harmonization Reform","Simplification of Taxation . Harmonization and amalgamation of taxes & levies rates, numbers and collection systems at federal and provincial levels .",""],[1,"91","5","SME Window at the Tax Ombudsman","SME window at Tax Ombudsman",""],[1,"92","1","Provincial Adoption of the Limited Liability Partnership Act 2017","Advocate for the adoption of the limited liability Partnership Act 2017 by the provinces as a more flexible model of partnership registration",""],[1,"335","28","Board of Investment Regulatory Reform for Ease of Doing Business and Export Promotion","Introduction of Regulatory reforms in the Board of Investment to provide ease of doing business environment and promoting exports",""],[1,"339","17","One-Stop Shop Business Facilitation Solutions","Establishment of One-Stop Shop solutions to promote ease of doing business.",""],[1,"339","18","Strengthening of Regulatory Institutions through Administrative and Financial Autonomy","Strengthening of regulatory institutions through administrative and financial autonomy",""],[1,"339","20","Public Awareness Media Campaign on Legal and Regulatory Framework","Enhancing public awareness of legal and regulatory framework through a media campaign for better understanding of general public/ businessman on legal and regulatory framework.",""],[1,"339","21","Regulatory Body Law Review and Reform","Review of laws of Regulatory bodies and introduce reforms to enhance their performance",""]],"23":[[1,"11","9","Forest Cover Expansion Initiative","We will focus on ... expanding forest cover",""],[1,"133","5","Large-Scale Afforestation and Forest Landscape Restoration","the federal and provincial governments have committed to large-scale afforestation and restoration efforts under the Bonn Challenge",""],[1,"134","1","Upscaling Green Pakistan Programme","the government has launched the Upscaling Green Pakistan Programme (GPP) as a continuation and expansion of the Ten Billion Tree Tsunami Programme (TBTTP).",""],[1,"138","8","Forest Fire Prevention and Forest and Landscape Restoration System","Prevent, control, and manage forest fires and support Forest and Landscape Restoration (FLR) through monitoring and early action systems.",""],[1,"138","9","Ecosystem-Based Green Cover and Renewable Energy Interventions","Increase green cover and promote renewable energy through ecosystem-based interventions.",""],[1,"139","5","Climate-Smart Land Use and Reforestation Projects","Promote climate-smart land use and reforestation projects that serve as carbon sinks, while ensuring co-benefits in terms of water conservation, biodiversity restoration, and community resilience.",""],[1,"139","16","Environmental Awareness, Skills, and Institutional Capacity Building for Tree Plantation and Conservation","Enhance awareness, skills, and institutional capacity, and promote tree plantation, conservation and sustainability.",""],[1,"143","8","Forest and Landscape Restoration Initiatives","Pakistan will implement large-scale Forest and Landscape Restoration (FLR) initiatives supported by early warning systems (EWSs) and fire risk monitoring platforms.",""],[1,"148","33","Reforestation and Climate-Smart Land Use Promotion","Promote reforestation, climate-smart land use, PES schemes",""],[1,"148","35","PES and Reforestation Programmes","Design PES & reforestation programmes",""]],"24":[[1,"9","2","Agricultural Productivity Enhancement","the Thirteenth Five Year Plan aims to revitalize our economy by focusing on key areas such as boosting agricultural productivity",""],[1,"11","9","Climate-Resilient Agriculture Programme","We will focus on climate-resilient agriculture",""],[1,"24","4","Governance and Institutional Reform for Agricultural Investment and Market Linkages","The main strategies of the plan to achieve these objectives include governance and institutional reforms that can attract and enhance effectiveness of the public and private sector investment, improve resource use efficiency and sustainability of natural resource to enhance productivity, connect agricultural stakeholders with national and international markets to boost export, promote agribusinesses and mechanization for competitiveness, and develop mechanisms and infrastructure to enhance food quality and safety.",""],[1,"24","4","Farmers' Entrepreneur Groups for Agricultural Service Delivery","To create ownership and inclusiveness, farmers will be organized into Farmers' Entrepreneur Groups (FEGs), all agricultural services and incentives will be channelled through these, and their capacity will be built for value chain development.",""],[1,"24","4","Corporate Sector Partnership for Agricultural Technology and Processing","The corporate sector will be engaged to supply technology, input, and link small scale processing with corporate industry.",""],[1,"38","7","Improved Seed and Irrigation Investment Package","Crop growth is expected to gradually recover, averaging 3.0 percent over the remaining years, supported by investments in improved seed varieties, advanced irrigation techniques, mechanization, and better pest and disease management.",""],[1,"38","7","Crop Resilience and Productivity Enhancement Interventions","The important crops sub-sector is projected to grow with an average rate of 2.0 percent, driven by targeted interventions to enhance resilience and productivity.",""],[1,"38","8","Agricultural Modernization and Diversification Programme","The Plan places particular emphasis on modernizing and diversifying agriculture, focusing on both crops and livestock.",""],[1,"39","1","Productivity-Enhancing Agricultural Investment Support","Increased investments from both the public and private sectors are envisioned to boost results, with the federal government under the PSDP prioritizing funding for productivity enhancing initiatives and strengthening research capacity.",""],[1,"39","1","Agricultural Mechanization and Green Investment Coordination","Federal and provincial governments will coordinate efforts to promote mechanization, achieve climate resilience, and encourage green investments to support sustainable agricultural growth.",""],[1,"49","11","Modern Agriculture Farming Initiatives through Land Information and Management Systems","Through the Land Information and Management Systems, modern agriculture farming initiatives are being introduced in over 4.4 million acres of land, including 1.3 million acres each in Punjab and Sindh, 1.1 million acres in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, and 0.7 million acres in Balochistan.",""],[1,"49","14","Edible Oil Cultivation Promotion Initiative","Their cultivation will be encouraged in the country through various initiatives special arrangements in this regard will be coordinated with the provincial governments.",""],[1,"49","15","Agricultural Development Policy Crop Promotion Measures","Cotton and pulses will be encouraged through the Agricultural Development Policy to reduce imports and save hard- earned foreign exchange.",""],[1,"152","9","Technology-Driven Agricultural Productivity Enhancement","The technology-drive productivity enhancement approach of the plan is to make the sector competitive in national and international market so that agriculture trade deficit can be converted into trade surpluses.",""],[1,"152","9","Agricultural Value Chain Development for Food Quality and Safety","Second, it thrives to develop value chain of agricultural commodities to meet international demand for food quality and safety.",""],[1,"152","9","Rural Agribusiness Promotion Initiative","Third, it goes beyond the farm level and thrives at rural transformation by promoting agri-businesses in rural areas.",""],[1,"152","9","Farmers' Entrepreneur Groups and Rural Service Delivery","Fourth, it engages rural communities in development efforts by organizing Farmers' Entrepreneur Groups (FEG) and providing rural services through these groups.",""],[1,"152","9","Corporate Sector Support for Agricultural Inputs and Capacity Building","Fifth, corporate sector is engaged in supplying technology and inputs, capacity building of stakeholders, and linking small scale processing with corporate industries.",""],[1,"152","10","Governance, Regulatory and Institutional Reform Package","The main strategies of the plan include governance, regulatory and institutional reforms that can attract and enhance effectiveness of the public and private sector investment to improve resource use efficiency and sustainability of natural resource, connect agricultural stakeholders including farmers and traders with national and international markets, promote mechanization for competitiveness, and develop infrastructure and mechanisms for food quality and safety.",""],[1,"154","6","Agricultural Growth and Land Reclamation Plan","The main objectives of the Uraan Pakistan are to bring private-sector led growth of the agriculture sector to 3.92% per annum and expand area under cultivation by reducing culturable waste and fellow lands and area under water logging and salinity, increasing cropping intensity by using the available water efficiently, and increasing water availability at the farm-level.",""],[1,"154","9","Agricultural Value Addition and Processing Improvement","Enhance food quality, safety and security by improving value addition and processing of agricultural commodities in rural areas, which will bring export prices of agriculture commodity at least at par to world average, if not better.",""],[1,"154","11","Rural Area Transformation through Agricultural Enterprise Development","Instigate overall transformation in Rural Areas by establishing agriculture businesses, creating respectful job opportunity, and enhancing incomes.",""],[1,"155","11","Corporate and Cooperative Investment Incentives for Agriculture","Corporate and cooperative laws to encourage their investment in the agriculture sector",""],[1,"157","1","Market Linkage and Efficiency Improvement Measures","Improve Market Efficiency by connecting producers, wholesalers, and traders with markets through corporates, improving market infrastructure and policies, providing market information, enhancing capacity of stakeholders, and bringing markets closer to the producers.",""],[1,"157","11","Small-Scale Industrial Revolution Programme","The purpose will be to bring \"Small-Scale Industrial Revolution (SSIR)\" by establishing small-scale agriculture-based processing and value addition units and providing environment friendly machines in rural which are owned and operated by Farmers Entrepreneur Group (FEP).",""],[1,"157","12","Farmers' Entrepreneur Group Business Development Initiative","Organize Farmers' Entrepreneur Group (FEGs) for business development in rural areas",""],[1,"157","17","Specific Credit Line for Small-Scale Agriculture Businesses","State Bank of Pakistan to create specific credit line for small-scale agriculture businesses offered through FEGs in rural areas.",""],[1,"157","18","Rural Agricultural Business Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of rural communities including wholesalers, traders, and processors for setting up agriculture businesses.",""],[1,"158","1","Rural Olive Commercial Processing Promotion","Promote commercial processing of olive in rural areas.",""],[1,"160","3","GST Removal on Agricultural Value Addition","Remove GST on the value addition to encourage value chain development of agricultural commodities",""],[1,"161","15","Olive Cultivation Expansion and Commercial Olive Processing Promotion","Expansion of olive cultivation and promotion of commercial olive processing",""],[1,"161","19","Cotton Productivity Revival Programme","Revival of cotton productivity by encouraging locally produced as well as imported GMO varieties and hybrids with pest-resistant, weedicide and heat-tolerant genes.",""],[1,"162","1","FEG Loan Package for Rural Agricultural Entrepreneurship","Work with State Bank of Pakistan to start loan package for FEGs to promote agriculture businesses and entrepreneurship in rural areas especially for young graduates and women with 3-5 years tax relaxation and technical support to start these businesses.","State Bank of Pakistan"]],"25":[[1,"24","5","Disaster Preparedness and Response Capacity Strengthening","The plan aims to strengthen adaptation capacity by enhancing governance and capabilities of state institutions.",""],[1,"24","5","Community-Based Risk Management and Technological Solutions","The plan focuses on constructing climate-resilient infrastructure, restoring lives and livelihoods, ensuring social inclusion and equitable access to economic opportunities, and engaging local communities in adopting technological solutions to manage risks, enhance disaster preparedness and response in a resilient and sustainable manner.",""],[1,"133","4","Glacial Lake Monitoring and GLOF Risk Reduction","To address growing risks from climate-induced disasters, enhanced monitoring of glacial lake formations and the implementation of GLOF risk reduction measures in vulnerable northern regions will be prioritized.",""],[1,"139","7","Disaster Risk Governance Institutional Framework Strengthening","Strengthen institutional frameworks for disaster risk governance, ensuring inclusive and risk-informed development planning.",""],[1,"139","8","Hydro-Meteorological Modernization and Early Warning Systems","Invest in hydro-meteorological modernization, including early warning systems and real-time climate hazard monitoring.",""],[1,"139","9","Inclusive Disaster Preparedness, Response, and Recovery Support","Prioritize support for vulnerable and marginalized groups in disaster preparedness, response, and recovery plans.",""],[1,"144","2","Disaster Risk Reduction Capacity and Early Warning Systems Upgrade","Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) efforts will focus on strengthening institutional capacities, mainstreaming risk-informed development, and upgrading hydro-meteorological services for real-time hazard monitoring.",""],[1,"144","2","Multi-Hazard Early Warning Systems Investment","Investments will be made in multi-hazard early warning systems (MHEWSs), with special focus on the inclusion of vulnerable and marginalized groups in preparedness and response frameworks.",""],[1,"144","2","Sendai-Aligned Disaster Risk Reduction Coordination Mechanism","Coordination mechanisms will be aligned with Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction (SFDRR) targets.",""],[1,"146","3","National Drought Resilience Programme","it is planned that a National Drought Resilience Programme (NDRP) will be launched, focusing on early warning systems, drought-resilient agriculture, and climate-smart infrastructure in vulnerable districts such as Tharparkar, Cholistan, and parts of Balochistan",""],[1,"146","3","Drought Contingency Financing and Index Insurance Scheme","new drought contingency financing mechanisms and index-based insurance schemes will be developed to provide timely financial relief to smallholder farmers and mitigate economic losses from prolonged dry spells",""],[1,"146","5","National GLOF Risk Reduction Programme","It is planned that the national response to Glacial Lake Outburst Floods (GLOFs) will be significantly enhanced through the upscaling of early warning systems, climate risk mapping, and community- based preparedness in northern mountainous regions.",""],[1,"146","5","GLOF Protective Infrastructure and Monitoring Measures","Structural measures such as controlled drainage channels, protective bunds, emergency evacuation routes, and weather monitoring stations will be installed in coordination with local communities, while institutional capacity at the district and provincial levels will be strengthened to manage GLOF risks in an integrated manner.",""],[1,"147","2","Scaled-Up Flash Flood Risk Management","It is also planned that flash flood risk management will be scaled up in climate-vulnerable hilly and semi-arid regions, particularly in Balochistan, South Punjab, and parts of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and AJK.",""],[1,"147","2","Watershed Mapping and Prioritization for Flood Intervention","Flash flood-prone watersheds will be mapped and prioritized for intervention through afforestation of upper catchments, construction of check dams and water retention structures, and community-led design of early warning and evacuation systems.",""],[1,"147","2","Flood-Resilient Infrastructure Investment","These efforts will be supported by investments in flood-resilient infrastructure such as culverts, bridges, and rural access roads to minimize disaster-related damage and restore economic connectivity in post-flood scenarios.",""],[1,"163","3","Climate-Resilient Development and Adaptation Planning","This demands the inclusion of adaptation planning, climate-resilient development in consultation with provincial governments, international cooperation on disaster management best practices, and improving adaptation capacity through resilient infrastructure as a national priority area.",""],[1,"163","4","Integrated Floodplains Management","Key initiatives include: Integrated floodplains management;",""],[1,"163","4","Scaling Up Glacial Lake Outburst Flood Risk Reduction","Key initiatives include: Scaling up GLOF risk reduction in northern Pakistan;",""],[1,"163","4","Mangrove Ecosystem Conservation and Restoration","Key initiatives include: Conservation and restoration of the mangrove's ecosystem;",""],[1,"163","4","Research and Development Strengthening for Early Warning Systems","Improving research and development through institutional strengthening and development of an early warning system;",""],[1,"164","1","Provincial Coordination for Environmental Policy Implementation","Improving coordination with provinces on the adoption and implementation of environmental policies and programs in the wake of devolution.",""],[1,"164","2","Climate Adaptation Integration and Resilience Building","It aims to integrate adaptation at all levels to reduce exposure and vulnerabilities to extreme weather events, and achieving sustainable economic growth by adopting policy and technological innovation, and allocating funds based on evidence and learning.",""],[1,"164","2","Disaster Preparedness and Flood Risk Management","The management of natural capital, preparedness against disasters notably floods, and building resilient infrastructure are central to achieve resilience and sustainable development.",""],[1,"164","11","Climate-Resilient Flood Recovery and Reconstruction Measures","The magnitude of the 2022 flooding, necessitates extensive recovery and reconstruction of climate-resilient infrastructure in flood prone regions, and community adaptation from a people-cantered approach.",""],[1,"164","11","Flood Control and Disaster Management Capacity Strengthening","The plan has allocated resources for structural and non-structural measures through NFPP-IV, 4RF, and National Disaster Management Plan 2025 to improve institutional capacities, preparedness, and community adaptation.",""],[1,"165","1","Local Government and Community Adaptive Capacity Strengthening","Under the Plan, improved adaptative capacity of local governments and communities is being prioritized to reduce vulnerabilities, minimize damages and avoid losses through better response to future disasters.",""],[1,"165","1","Hydro-Meteorological Disaster Risk Reduction and Integrated Water Resources Management","The Federal Flood Commission planned establishment of Hydro- meteorological disaster risk reduction and integrated water resources management26.",""],[1,"165","1","Grassroots Disaster Risk Management Framework","NDMA planned to build and implement a comprehensive disaster risk management framework at grassroot level to enhance local capacities, risk prioritization, communications and coordination27.",""],[1,"165","2","Data Collection Mechanism Reform","the plan emphasis on reforming data collection mechanisms, ensuring the accuracy and availability of data.",""],[1,"165","2","NATCAT Risk Calculator for Public Investment Decisions","the plan is adopting technological solutions such as NATCAT Risk Calculator to generate evidence for public investment decisions to avoid future damages and losses.",""],[1,"165","2","Integrated Flood Resilience and Adaptation Project Early Warning Systems","early warning systems are being built under the 4RF through the Integrated Flood Resilience and Adaptation Project (IFRAP) project to provide a vast coverage.",""],[1,"165","5","4RF Strategic Recovery Area Funding Allocation","The plan has adopted the 4RF strategic recovery areas to strategies funds allocation for resilient recovery and improved adaptation.",""],[1,"165","5","4RF Project Implementation Portfolio","Currently, 4RF projects at implementation stage stands at USD 5.178 billion including USD 583.2 million co-financing from federal and provincial governments.",""],[1,"165","5","Recovery and Reconstruction Activities","Beside this, there are 105 recovery and reconstruction activities worth USD 38.096 million financed by NGOs/NPOs.",""],[1,"165","5","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Project","Additionally, the government has mobilised USD 636.36 million for an infrastructure project under public private partnership arrangements.",""],[1,"165","6","Disaster Risk Management and Community Adaptation Investment","There is need for investment in disaster risk management and community level adaptation",""],[1,"165","6","Governance and Institutional Capacity Building","and other areas notably, governance and institutional capacity building",""],[1,"165","6","Livelihoods and Economic Opportunities Support","and other areas notably, governance and institutional capacity building, livelihoods and economic opportunities, and social protection and inclusion",""],[1,"165","6","Social Protection and Inclusion Measures","and other areas notably, governance and institutional capacity building, livelihoods and economic opportunities, and social protection and inclusion",""],[1,"166","12","Innovative Climate Financing Modalities","The Plan aims to explore innovative financing modalities, such as pooled funding mechanisms, results-based financing, and blended finance, that can help optimize limited resources while strengthening accountability and measurable impacts.",""],[1,"166","12","Partnership Expansion for Climate Finance","Given the global transition in development cooperation, it is essential to broaden our engagement with non-traditional development partners, philanthropic foundations, private sector actors, and thematic financing sources such as Green Climate Financing.",""],[1,"166","12","Climate Finance Skills Development","The Plan aims to cultivate a pool of skilled human resources to navigate external finance notably Green Climate Financing - PSDP has allocated resources for the relevant ministry to improve technical capacities.",""],[1,"167","1","Integrated Disaster Management Framework","The Plan has adopted 4RF's Strategic Recovery Objectives (SROs) as a resilient development strategy and aims to develop an integrated and coordinated disaster management framework.",""],[1,"167","1","Grassroots Disaster Preparedness and Institutional Capacity Strengthening","The Plan prioritizes addressing climate vulnerabilities, emphasis on improving grassroot level preparedness, institutional capacities, and building resilient infrastructure guided by 5Es framework, National Adaptation Plan 2023, and the Sendai Framework 2015-30.",""],[1,"167","1","Disaster Management Partnership and Technology Transfer Cooperation","Moreover, the plan focusses on partnership building, securing global support for technology and knowledge transfer, and improved cooperation on disaster management and resilient development.",""],[1,"167","2","Climate Adaptation Mainstreaming Across Government Levels","Mainstream climate adaptation across federal, provincial, and local governments",""],[1,"167","3","Community Climate Resilience Strengthening","Strengthen resilience of vulnerable communities, reduce exposure to climate related extreme events",""],[1,"167","4","Governance and State Institution Capacity Enhancement for Logistics and Rescue Services","Enhance governance and the capacities of the state institutions - logistics and rescue services",""],[1,"167","6","Community Capacity Building for Nature-Based Risk Management","Engage local communities - build their capacities in adopting nature-based solutions to manage risks",""],[1,"167","7","Disaster Emergency Preparedness and Response through Early Warning Systems","Disaster emergency preparedness and response through early warning system and forecast; Establish integrated data governance for climate action",""],[1,"167","7","Integrated Climate Action Data Governance Framework","Establish integrated data governance for climate action",""],[1,"167","10","Climate Adaptation Integration into Development Planning","Integrate adaptation into Development Plans across federal, provincial, and local governments",""],[1,"167","11","Land Use Change Regulation Implementation","Implement land use change regulations to bolster resilient service provision",""],[1,"167","12","Flood Zoning Establishment and Promotion","Establishment and promotion of flood zoning",""],[1,"167","13","Community-Based Adaptation and Nature-Based Solutions Capacity Building","Community-based adaptation: Engage local communities, build capacities in adopting nature-based solutions to manage risks",""],[1,"167","14","Climate-Smart Municipal Services","Adopt climate-smart municipal services",""],[1,"167","17","Local Authority Capacity Strengthening for Loss and Damage Reduction","Strengthen the capacities of local authorities to reduce losses and damages",""],[1,"167","18","People-Centred Multi-Hazard Early Warning and Emergency Communication Systems","Build and strengthen people-centred multi-hazard multi-sectoral early warning systems and forecast, and emergency communication mechanisms",""],[1,"167","19","Public Investment Decision and Land-Use Planning Improvement","Improve public investment decisions and land-use planning",""],[1,"167","20","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Investment","Investment in Climate-Resilient Infrastructure including water, transportation, telecommunications, health and other facilities with build back better approach",""],[1,"167","21","Disaster Risk Finance Strategy Implementation","- Implement Disaster Risk Finance Strategy",""],[1,"167","23","Data Infrastructure and Knowledge Management Enhancement","Enhance data infrastructure and knowledge management",""]],"26":[[1,"7","2","Energy and Infrastructure Development","Environmental protection and climate action will safeguard our future, while energy and infrastructure development will ensure sustainable and affordable access for all.",""],[1,"11","8","Strategic Infrastructure Project Completion","This will be achieved by diversifying our energy mix towards renewables, reducing circular debt, and completing strategic infrastructure projects to unlock economic potential.",""],[1,"25","7","Transport and Logistics Sector Modernization Programme","The government is committed to modernizing this sector through comprehensive reforms and strategic investments, with 28-33 percent of the annual Public Sector Development Program (PSDP) allocated to it, though the",""],[1,"26","1","Multimodal Transport System Development","The new plan prioritizes developing a multimodal transport system with a projected investment of Rs. 1,644.8 billion, emphasizing green and sustainable transport.",""],[1,"26","1","Transport Sector Infrastructure Development and Strategic Planning","Major initiatives will focus on infrastructure development and strategic planning to support these goals.",""],[1,"40","6","Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Expansion","During the Plan period, the services sector is anticipated to experience accelerated expansion, mainly driven by investments in infrastructure, including new roads, expanded railway tracks, and the operationalization of Gwadar Port, are expected to generate positive spillover effects on the transport, storage, and communication sectors.",""],[1,"40","6","Supply Chain System Strengthening","Furthermore, the entire supply chain system, including raw material and inventory planning, strategic sourcing for efficient production, and logistical arrangements to deliver goods from origin to end markets, will play a crucial role in supporting and sustaining this growth momentum.",""],[1,"48","13","Road and Rail Freight Infrastructure Strengthening","Road and rail infrastructure will be further strengthened for quicker and hassle-free movement of goods from production centres to ports.",""],[1,"48","14","Cold Storage Facilities for Perishable Export Goods","the government will facilitate the establishment of cold storage facilities on a public-private partnership basis at airports and seaports.",""],[1,"54","9","Cold Storage Facilities Establishment","Establishment of cold storage facilities",""],[1,"199","1","Transport and Logistics Modernization Reforms and Investments","the government is undertaking comprehensive reforms and investments to modernize the transport and logistics landscape.",""],[1,"201","6","Inland Waterway Transport and Logistics Development","the forthcoming plan aims to explore and utilize other inland waterways for transportation and logistics.",""],[1,"201","9","Innovative Infrastructure Financing through PPP/BOT","Exploring innovative financing modes like PPP/BOT by NHA/Pak Railways is crucial to reduce the burden on constrained PSDP funds and prevent time and cost overruns in projects.",""],[1,"202","6","Domestic Economic Corridors Development","Development of Domestic Economic Corridors linking major business centers to maximize benefits from the national corridor.",""],[1,"202","15","Affordable Inclusive Transport Access Initiative","Promoting social inclusion and tackle poverty by seeking to ensure that affordable transport is accessible to all sections of the communities and provides good links to employment, education, Markets, tourist attractions, agricultural areas and healthcare facilities.",""]],"27":[[1,"27","2","Inclusive, Resilient and Regionally Balanced Development Strategy","The plan responds to emerging crises by emphasizing inclusive, resilient and regionally balanced development.",""],[1,"27","2","Expanded Access to Health, Education and Infrastructure","Strategic pillars include expanding access to quality health, education and infrastructure;",""],[1,"27","2","Rural and Agricultural Development Programme","promoting rural and agricultural development and revitalizing regional equalization programs.",""],[1,"27","2","Regional Equalization Program Revitalization","promoting rural and agricultural development and revitalizing regional equalization programs.",""],[1,"27","2","Strengthened Social Protection and Institutional Reform Agenda","strengthened social protection and institutional reforms are essential to achieve SDG targets and build long-term resilience.",""],[1,"30","3","Focused Development Efforts for Special Areas","To achieve this, focused development efforts are planned for special areas i.e. Azad Jammu & Kashmir, Gilgit Baltistan and merged districts of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, in collaboration with the governments of special areas and non- governmental developmental partners.",""],[1,"30","3","PSDP Block Allocations for Special Areas","Federal government is facilitating development efforts in special areas though providing funds in the form of PSDP block allocations.",""],[1,"30","4","Targeted Investment in Priority Development Sectors","The plan outlines priority development sectors that require targeted investments to generate revenues foster socio-economic development, particularly in special areas.",""],[1,"30","4","Cross-Regional Connectivity Enhancement Initiative","The plan also caters the initiatives aimed at enhancing cross- regional connectivity among special areas and encourages public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"233","5","Lagging Regions Infrastructure Investment","Invest in physical infrastructure (roads, electricity, water) in lagging regions.",""],[1,"233","5","Broadband Expansion for Digital Services","Expand broadband internet to facilitate e-governance, e-commerce, and digital education.",""],[1,"233","6","Targeted Regional Development Packages","Implement targeted regional development packages (Southern Balochistan, South Punjab, KP merged districts).",""],[1,"233","6","Decentralized Planning and Resource Allocation Reform","Decentralize planning and resource allocation with strengthened local governance.",""],[1,"234","7","Backward Districts Upliftment Projects","Implement projects for uplifting 20 backward districts",""],[1,"321","3","Inclusive and Sustainable Regional Disparities Reduction in Policy Design and Implementation","Promote inclusive and sustainable development in design and implementation of policies to address regional disparities through funding from PSDP/ADP.",""]],"28":[[1,"28","4","National Multisectoral Nutrition Program Scaling-Up","Central to the Plan is the implementation and scaling up of the National Multisectoral Nutrition Program, which focuses on addressing the underlying drivers of malnutrition through integrated, evidence-based interventions across health, food, education, and (WASH).",""],[1,"28","5","Nutrition Policy and Regulatory Strengthening","These include strengthening policy and legislative frameworks, harmonizing food standards and safety regulations, and expanding direct and indirect nutrition interventions, ranging from household food security initiatives to the integration of Early Childhood Development into relevant sectoral programs.",""],[1,"28","5","Household Food Security Initiatives","These include strengthening policy and legislative frameworks, harmonizing food standards and safety regulations, and expanding direct and indirect nutrition interventions, ranging from household food security initiatives to the integration of Early Childhood Development into relevant sectoral programs.",""],[1,"28","5","Early Childhood Development Integration into Sectoral Programs","These include strengthening policy and legislative frameworks, harmonizing food standards and safety regulations, and expanding direct and indirect nutrition interventions, ranging from household food security initiatives to the integration of Early Childhood Development into relevant sectoral programs.",""],[1,"253","4","BISP Nashonuma Nutrition Support Program","The initiation of the BISP Nashonuma Program enhanced the provision of health and nutrition services for Pregnant and Lactating Women (PLWs) and children (0-23 months).",""],[1,"258","4","Household Food Security and Nutrition Support Programs","Strengthening household food security and ensuring access to safe, nutritious and sustainable food/diet through income generations, livelihood and adaptive/shock responsive social protection programs",""]],"29":[[1,"28","6","Education Sector Reform and Modernization","It also focuses on reforms in teacher recruitment, training, and continuous professional development.",""],[1,"28","6","Education Accreditation and Public-Private Harmonization Framework","Institutional frameworks for accreditation, regulation, and public- private harmonization will be strengthened.",""],[1,"265","4","Education Institution Accreditation and Licensing System","Establishment of an accreditation system & licenses for both public and private educational institutions.",""],[1,"267","6","Regulation of Private Sector Educational Institutions","Regulation of private sector educational institutions as per government policy/rules.",""],[1,"267","8","Year-wise Education Target Planning by Provincial and Area Governments","Provincial/ Area Governments may prepare year-wise targets of education.",""],[1,"267","12","Inter-Provincial and Education Ministers' Conference Coordination Mechanism","Inter-Provincial & Education Ministers' Conference (IPEMC) should play an active nd effective role of coordination as per policy.",""]],"30":[[1,"9","2","Technology Adoption and Human Capital Development","the Thirteenth Five Year Plan aims to revitalize our economy by focusing on key areas such as ... leveraging state- of-the-art technologies, and enhancing human capital",""],[1,"11","7","Fourth Industrial Revolution Skills Certification Programme","certifying over 500,000 graduates in Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) technologies",""],[1,"29","3","Employment Generation and Labour Market Transformation Plan","The Plan sets targets to create 9.2 million jobs, 6.2 million domestically and 3 million through overseas employment by fostering economic growth, expanding demand-driven skill development, and promoting entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"29","3","Demand-Driven Skills Development and TVET Alignment","Key priorities include enhancing labour productivity, formalizing the informal economy, increasing female workforce participation, and aligning technical and vocational training with labour market needs.",""],[1,"29","3","Green Jobs and Digital Economy Employment Strategy","Special emphasis is placed on green jobs, digital economy opportunities, and targeted overseas migration strategies.",""],[1,"29","7","Training Academy Strengthening Initiative","Training academies will be strengthened.",""],[1,"50","1","IT and ITeS Training and Skills Development Initiatives","Comprehensive training and skills development initiatives are planned to support this growth.",""],[1,"52","4","Skilled Migrant Development for Export Markets","The Plan aims to broaden the range of export markets for migrants by creating highly skilled and professional migrants for advanced market economies.",""],[1,"55","7","Skilled Migrant Export Market Diversification","Broaden the range of export markets for migrants by creating highly skilled and professional migrants",""],[1,"269","3","Labour Force Participation and Job Creation Measures","the plan focuses on: (i) Increasing labour force participation rate, especially the female, (ii) Job creation",""],[1,"269","3","Skills Training Alignment with Labour Market Needs","Creating match between skill development/trainings and labour market requirements",""],[1,"269","3","Federal-Provincial Coordination for Demand-Driven Training","better coordination between federal and provinces for demand driven trainings",""],[1,"269","3","Decent Work Environment Improvement","Decent work environment",""],[1,"269","3","Green Job Creation Initiative","Green Job Creation",""],[1,"273","4","Coherent Cross-Sectoral Employment Strategy","Pakistan needs a coherent, cross-sectoral employment strategy that enhances labour productivity, formalizes employment, strengthens skills development, promotes gender equity, and expands access to higher-quality domestic and international job markets.",""],[1,"273","9","Female Labor Force Participation through Education and Skills Investment","Promoting female labor force participation through targeted education and skill development investments will help unlock underutilized human capital.",""],[1,"273","12","Transparent Labor Market Information System","Cross-cutting governance and structural reforms by introducing a transparent labor market information system, developing a national employment strategy, improving the enforcement of labor laws, and ensuring decent working conditions.",""],[1,"273","12","National Employment Strategy","Cross-cutting governance and structural reforms by introducing a transparent labor market information system, developing a national employment strategy, improving the enforcement of labor laws, and ensuring decent working conditions.",""],[1,"273","12","Labor Law Enforcement and Decent Working Conditions Reform","Cross-cutting governance and structural reforms by introducing a transparent labor market information system, developing a national employment strategy, improving the enforcement of labor laws, and ensuring decent working conditions.",""],[1,"274","14","R&D and Human Resource Development for Productivity Growth","Focus on R&D and human resource development to increase contribution of total factor productivity.",""]],"31":[[1,"29","4","Inclusive Social Protection Strategy","The Plan emphasises on uplifting vulnerable populations particularly women, children, elderly, transgender persons, and persons with disabilities through inclusive, social protection strategies.",""],[1,"29","4","Welfare Institution Capacity Strengthening","It calls for enhancing the capacity of welfare institutions, expanding services like education, healthcare, day care, senior citizen support, enabling women's mobility and economic participation.",""],[1,"29","4","Localized Social Planning and Digital Data Systems","Emphasis is placed on localized planning and digital data systems, to ensure effective implementation.",""],[1,"29","5","Social Welfare for Marginalized Groups","Overall, the Plan envisages social welfare initiatives that fosters dignity, resilience, and equitable development for all marginalized segments of society.",""],[1,"280","2","Provincial Social Protection Policies","provinces have initiated policies such as Punjab and Khyber Pakhtunkhwa introduced their Social Protection Policies in 2022",""],[1,"280","2","Sindh Social Protection Authority","Sindh established the Sindh Social Protection Authority (SSPA) in July 2022 to lead a comprehensive provincial strategy",""],[1,"280","2","Federal Social Protection Support in Balochistan","social protection efforts continue through federal initiatives such as the BISP and Pakistan Bait-ul-Mal",""],[1,"281","4","Social Protection System Strengthening and Safety Net Expansion","Strengthen social protection systems and expand social safety nets to ensure financial security and dignity for vulnerable populations.",""],[1,"281","16","Broad-Based Social Protection and Safety Nets System","The Plan aims to establish a broad-based, well-coordinated social protection & safety nets system to ensure economic security & resilience for the most vulnerable populations.",""],[1,"282","1","Expansion of Unconditional and Conditional Cash Transfers","it focuses on expanding unconditional & conditional cash transfers.",""],[1,"282","1","Individual Financial Assistance for Patients, Students, and Low-Income Individuals","PBM will provide Individual Financial Assistance to patients, students and low-income individuals, along with cochlear implants.",""],[1,"282","1","Social Protection Registry System Improvement","It also prioritizes improving the registry system for better targeting of children, women, youth and senior citizens.",""],[1,"282","1","National Rights-Based and Inclusive Social Protection Framework","Special emphasis would be placed on introducing a national social protection framework that is rights-based and inclusive to ensure that no one is left behind in times of economic stress or vulnerability.",""],[1,"282","6","Strengthening Social Welfare Institutional Frameworks","To ensure efficient, inclusive and accountable delivery of social welfare services, it is important to strengthen institutional frameworks.",""],[1,"283","8","National Social Protection Framework Development","Develop National Social Protection Framework 2",""]],"32":[[1,"29","5","Inclusive Education and Community Support Initiatives","The proposed initiatives aim to promote inclusive education, and support for communities.",""],[1,"29","5","Women's Empowerment and Protection Services","Women's empowerment remains a key focus, with aims increase literacy, boosting women's participation in the workforce, and strengthening protection services.",""],[1,"281","5","Gender Equality and Women's Empowerment Measures","Enhance gender equality and women's empowerment, particularly through economic inclusion, legal protection, and access to financial & social services.",""],[1,"281","10","Rural Women Empowerment Programme","Empowerment of rural women, through access to resources, training, and entrepreneurial opportunities.",""]],"33":[[1,"7","2","Export-Led Growth Strategy","The Plan prioritises export-led growth to reduce reliance on foreign loans and foster a knowledge-driven economy.",""],[1,"9","2","Export Diversification Promotion","the Thirteenth Five Year Plan aims to revitalize our economy by focusing on key areas such as ... promoting exports diversification",""],[1,"11","6","Export-Led Growth Strategy","We will revitalize the ecosystem for exports, diversify our trade basket, and aggressively integrate into global value chains.",""],[1,"33","2","Export-Led Growth Strategy","The Plan prioritizes export-led growth to ensure sustainable, inclusive, and resilient economic development.",""],[1,"36","7","Export-Led Growth Strategy","Aligned with the Uraan Pakistan and based on 5Es framework, the Plan envisages export led growth by targeting globally expanding sectors, and aligning product lines with international standards and compliance requirements to strengthen competitiveness and market access.",""],[1,"41","5","Export Promotion for High-Value Goods","By capitalizing on international market improvements, Pakistan aims to boost exports of high-value goods such as engineering products, technical textiles, and processed fruits, attracting substantial foreign investment through joint ventures, equity partnerships, and brand development.",""],[1,"41","5","Brand Development Support for Global Competitiveness","Recognizing the importance of marketing and R&D, the government plans to actively support brand development to strengthen global competitiveness.",""],[1,"46","5","Strategic Trade Policy Framework for Export Competitiveness","the Strategic Trade Policy Framework (STPF) 2020-25 has been prepared that aimed to enhance export competitiveness of Pakistan through a framework of interventions having an impact across the value chains.",""],[1,"47","3","Export Diversification and Product Sophistication Roadmap","The Plan outlines a roadmap to increase exports through product sophistication as well as product and market diversification, besides integrating the domestic production with global value chains specifically in 11 sectors as determined in STPF 2020-25.",""],[1,"47","3","Research, Technology Upgradation, Value Addition, and Branding Support","Product sophistication and diversification will be pursued through targeted efforts in research and development, technology upgradation, value addition, and branding.",""],[1,"48","1","Trade Sector Revitalization Strategy","The Plan envisages a comprehensive strategy to reinvigorate trade sector in order to generate higher foreign exchange earnings.",""],[1,"48","1","External Sector Structural Reform Agenda","Structural reforms in the external sector are vital to promoting economic resilience, ease of doing business and strengthening global competitiveness.",""],[1,"48","2","External Sector Reform and Export Competitiveness Enhancement","External sector reforms play a crucial role in the overall economic development of a nation.",""],[1,"48","4","National Priority Sectors Export Strategy","National Priority Sectors Export Strategy (NPSES) has been formulated with a focus on 10 out of 18 priority sectors which aims to enable and sustain a new cycle of export growth for Pakistan, exploiting its vast untapped potential for trade and investment development.",""],[1,"48","7","Export Cluster Development and SME Market Linkage Support","Developing export clusters, facilitating Small and Medium Enterprises (SME's) to establish their businesses, to enhance their production capacity and to develop linkages to global markets.",""],[1,"48","11","Export Promotion Measures","To address trade balance issues and foster export culture in the next five years the following steps will be taken by different stakeholders.",""],[1,"48","12","Tariff Rationalization for Export Promotion","In order to promote outward orientation and eliminate the anti-export bias, tariffs will be rationalized in accordance with the National Tariff Policy 2019-24.",""],[1,"49","1","Trade Related Investment Policy Framework Development","the Trade Related Investment Policy Framework is yet to be developed on the basis of broader principles outlined therewith to promote investment in export-oriented sector and competitive import substitution.",""],[1,"49","2","Regional Input Support for Export-Oriented Sectors","Efforts will be made to provide regionally competitive inputs to export oriented sectors.",""],[1,"49","15","Domestic Cotton Yield and Quality Improvement Initiative","Yield and quality of domestic cotton needs to be significantly improved to reduce/eliminate reliance on imported cotton and increase the share of domestic value added in textiles and apparel exports.",""],[1,"49","16","Man-Made Fiber and Synthetic Textiles Production Expansion","Efforts will be made to increase production of MMF & synthetic textiles for the domestic market - without a domestic market for MMF & synthetics, these products cannot become competitive enough for export.",""],[1,"50","1","Services Trade Development Council and Trade in Services Wing","To support this, Services Trade Development Council (STDC) has been set- up and a Trade in Services Wing aimed at promoting domestic liberalization and boosting service exports through sectoral reforms.",""],[1,"50","1","IT Export Promotion under Uraan Pakistan","The target of IT export is aligned with Uraan Pakistan, which is envisioned to reach $15 billion.",""],[1,"50","1","International Payment Gateway Engagement for Freelancers","Moreover, international payment gateways are being engaged to support freelancing communities.",""],[1,"50","2","Export Market Expansion and Trade Diversification","the plan aims to use more advanced technologies in the production of goods, resulting in more diversified products.",""],[1,"51","6","Global Value Chain Participation Reform","To increase Pakistan's participation in GVCs, necessary reforms including tariff and trade facilitation (as discussed above) will be implemented during the Plan period.",""],[1,"54","4","Export Cluster Development Initiative","Developing exports clusters to enhance share of SMEs and to establish global linkages",""],[1,"79","1","Export Preparedness and Product Development Support","Objectives of the plan mainly consist of improvement in the trade balance through productivity & competitiveness enhancement, product development, export preparedness and generating productive jobs leading towards the socio-economic development of the country.",""],[1,"82","2","Export Incentive and Product Upgrading Measures","There is significant potential to introduce incentives that encourage industries to transition from lower-value to higher-value products.",""],[1,"82","2","Import Restriction Simplification for Export Competitiveness","Additionally, simplifying import restrictions can enhance export competitiveness.",""],[1,"83","6","Infrastructure and Raw Materials Support for Export-Oriented Firms","Enhancing infrastructure and access to raw materials and essential inputs can strengthen business capabilities.",""],[1,"83","6","Trade Facilitation and Export Market Development Measures","Market and product development can be advanced through improved trade facilitation measures, better access to timely information, and increased participation in international exhibitions, alongside efforts to strengthen branding and standardization, particularly for SMEs and export-oriented sectors.",""],[1,"83","6","Certification Streamlining for Global Competitiveness","Streamlining certification processes can further enhance global competitiveness.",""],[1,"84","7","High-Technology Export Promotion and Diversification","Promote high-technology exports in areas like aerospace, electric vehicles, shipbuilding, chemicals, engineering, and pharmaceuticals, alongside product and market diversification, trade facilitation, export enhancement, and brand development.",""],[1,"85","4","Market Access Expansion and Trade Promotion","Government will expand market access, fostering partnerships and participation in exhibitions.",""],[1,"85","4","Regional Trade Diversification with ECO Countries and the Middle East","Regional trade with ECO countries and the Middle East, supported by the STPF and National Tariff Policy 2025-30, will diversify exports.",""],[1,"86","3","Export Promotion and Competitiveness Enhancement Measures","Promotion of exports through effective marketing, value addition, improvement in local/ international trade infrastructure, improving competitiveness/diversification of the products especially within textiles & apparel sector and markets, image building by promoting \"Made in Pakistan\" branding, improving commercial intelligence, tariff rationalization, trade policies' implementation, regional connectivity, compliance of anti-dumping duties, countervailing duties, setting up Geographical Indications (GI) Cell, commercial zones with warehousing facilities for export sector inputs and other ancillary services to facilitate exports and reduce turnaround times, etc.",""],[1,"86","4","Foreign Investment and Joint Venture Promotion","This needs a paradigm shift towards encouragement of foreign investment, joint ventures, skill development according to global needs, improving infrastructure, simplifying trade procedures, fostering innovation & technology adoption in tandem with R&D, improve policy & regulatory environment, political stability, promote regional integration and trade unions.",""],[1,"86","4","Trade Procedure Simplification and Regulatory Improvement","This needs a paradigm shift towards encouragement of foreign investment, joint ventures, skill development according to global needs, improving infrastructure, simplifying trade procedures, fostering innovation & technology adoption in tandem with R&D, improve policy & regulatory environment, political stability, promote regional integration and trade unions.",""],[1,"89","2","Investment Promotion Policies and Action Plans for Export-Oriented Sectors","Formulate investment promotion policies/ strategies/ action plans to channel both domestic and FDI in export-oriented sectors .",""],[1,"92","9","Negotiation Cell Establishment in the Ministry of Commerce","Establishment of Negotiation Cell in Ministry of Commerce","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"92","12","National Brand Building Initiative","Strengthening of national brand building initiative; Support to firms in development and acquiring of brands",""],[1,"92","13","National Trade Facilitation Portal","Establishment and operationalization of the National Trade Facilitation Portal,",""],[1,"93","1","Trade Facilitation Units Establishment","Establishment of Trade Facilitation Units (TFUs) in TDAP;",""],[1,"93","1","National Quality Infrastructure Improvement","Improvement of National Quality Infrastructure (NQI);",""],[1,"93","2","Tariff Structure Anomaly Identification and Tariff Reform Roadmap","Roadmap to identify anomalies in tariff structure with tariff reforms in key manufacturing industries",""],[1,"101","3","Brand Pakistan Public-Private Partnership Campaign","Brand Pakistan Initiative: Launch public-private partnership to brand Pakistan as attractive outsourcing destination, addressing customer fears and image problems.",""]],"34":[[1,"69","5","Railway Infrastructure Modernization Programme","During the Plan, the policy to modernize railway infrastructure would continue to reduce the transportation cost and to reduce congestion on the highways that ultimately reduce the maintenance cost of highways.",""],[1,"202","19","Railway Commercial Viability Enhancement","Commercial viability enhancement for railway operations.",""],[1,"202","20","Private Sector Participation in Railway Operations","Encouraging private sector participation in railway operations while maintaining railway infrastructure in the public sector.",""],[1,"203","2","Sustainable Asset Management and Rail Safety Improvement","Adoption of sustainable asset management practices and improved rail safety.",""],[1,"203","3","Railway Infrastructure Modernization and Expansion","Modernization and expansion of railway infrastructure, including the comprehensive Main Line 1 (ML-1) reconstruction project under CPEC or through other modes of financing to refurbish a significant portion of the rail network.",""],[1,"203","4","Rail Freight Transport and Logistics Connectivity Enhancement","Focusing on rail for long-haul freight transportation to reduce road freight and enhancing connectivity between ports, dry ports, and industrial zones.",""],[1,"203","5","ML-3 Rehabilitation for Reko Diq Connectivity","Rehabilitation of ML-3 in connection with Reko Diq.",""],[1,"205","12","Railway Infrastructure Modernization and Expansion","Continue modernization and expansion of railway infrastructure.",""],[1,"205","13","Railway Land and Asset Leasing Revenue Initiative","Generate revenue through leasing of railway land and assets.",""],[1,"205","14","Mining Area Rail Connectivity Project","Connect Thar, Reko Diq, and other mining areas to the rail network.",""],[1,"205","15","Long-Haul Freight and Intermodal Connectivity Development","Focus on long-haul freight and enhance intermodal connectivity between ports, dry ports, and industrial hubs, including development of passenger terminals in urban areas.",""],[1,"206","20","Railway Line Upgradation and Expansion Programme","Upgradation of ML-1, Const. of Thar Coal Rail Link Rehab. of ML-3 and Const. of ML-4 Loco and Rolling stock induction and modernization",""],[1,"221","10","Main Line I Railway Sector Modernization","Strategic cooperation will be extended to upgrade Main Line-I and modernize rail infrastructure, including rolling stock, signaling systems, and workforce capacity-building through technical training.",""]],"35":[[1,"70","3","Science and Information Technology Research and Development Investment","For research and development in the field of science and information technology, Rs. 255 billion have been proposed during the Plan period.",""],[1,"70","3","Federal Public Investment in Research and Development","The federal government will continue to invest in research, development and in those areas where the private sector is reluctant to invest.",""],[1,"121","1","Competitive and Merit-Based Research Grant Expansion","HEC and Ministry of Science & Technology are already implementing few projects for providing competitive and merit-based research grants.","HEC | Ministry of Science & Technology"],[1,"122","4","Competitive Research Grants and HRD Support for Private Universities","private universities - particularly those working under the non-profit (trust) model that demonstrate the willingness to invest and engage in funded or sponsored research may be supported through participation in competitive research grants and HRD programs.",""],[1,"123","2","Strengthening of National Centres through R&D Investment","There is need to further strengthen these National Centres with R&D investments from local industries and public in PPP model to attract investments in innovation.",""],[1,"123","3","National Initiative for Indigenous Scientific Instruments and Industrial Machinery Development","Launching a national initiative for the indigenous design and development of scientific instruments and industrial machinery in another such important focus area.",""],[1,"126","4","Competitive Research Strengthening Initiative","Competitive Research in key areas through: · Strengthening of existing and development of new National Centers in emerging technologies · Strengthening existing Research Program for S&T Organization and Universities etc · Promoting Academia-Industry Linkage · Encouraging and facilitating global partnerships in R&D and allied activities through individual and G to G exchange programs",""],[1,"128","18","R&D Support and National Research Facility Development","Support for R&D in climatology, forest, biodiversity, oceanographic resources, glacial studies and to set-up a centralized national research facility for developing Nanotechnology, Materials Science, Lasers & Photonics products, Centre for Lithium/Sodium Batteries production and Centre for Conversion of Classic Cars to Electric in accordance with the national needs",""]],"36":[[1,"9","2","Industrial Capacity Strengthening","the Thirteenth Five Year Plan aims to revitalize our economy by focusing on key areas such as ... strengthening industrial capacity",""],[1,"22","6","Industrial Policy Framework Strengthening","Key strategies include fortifying policy frameworks, expanding industry incentives, promoting standardization, and adopting innovative technologies to attract private investment.",""],[1,"22","6","Industry Incentives Expansion","Key strategies include fortifying policy frameworks, expanding industry incentives, promoting standardization, and adopting innovative technologies to attract private investment.",""],[1,"22","6","Industrial Standardization Promotion","Key strategies include fortifying policy frameworks, expanding industry incentives, promoting standardization, and adopting innovative technologies to attract private investment.",""],[1,"22","6","Technology Adoption for Industrial Investment","Key strategies include fortifying policy frameworks, expanding industry incentives, promoting standardization, and adopting innovative technologies to attract private investment.",""],[1,"22","6","ICT and Skills Development for Export Competitiveness","The objective is to elevate Pakistan's global economic standing by 2029 through advancements in ICT, technology adoption, vocational training, skill development, and fostering a supportive business environment.",""],[1,"22","6","Supportive Business Environment Development","The objective is to elevate Pakistan's global economic standing by 2029 through advancements in ICT, technology adoption, vocational training, skill development, and fostering a supportive business environment.",""],[1,"39","7","National Industrial Policy Development","The Plan includes key initiatives such as developing a National Industrial Policy for regulatory consistency, establishing SEZs to improve infrastructure, and promoting Industry 4.0 technologies like loT and automation for innovation.",""],[1,"39","7","Industry 4.0 Technology Promotion","The Plan includes key initiatives such as developing a National Industrial Policy for regulatory consistency, establishing SEZs to improve infrastructure, and promoting Industry 4.0 technologies like loT and automation for innovation.",""],[1,"39","7","Construction Sector Incentive Scheme","The construction sector will also be incentivized during the Plan period to stimulate economic activity.",""],[1,"41","4","Infrastructure, Industrial Modernization, and Technology Upgrade Investment","fixed investment is expected to rise to 15.3 percent of GDP, reflecting increased spending on infrastructure, industrial modernization, and technology upgrades.",""],[1,"48","5","National Productivity Master Plan","Doubling up the productivity by introducing major interventions under a comprehensive National Productivity Master Plan (NPMP).",""],[1,"48","6","Intellectual Property Rights Regulatory Reform","Reforming Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) regulations to attract FDI and promote indigenous innovation.",""],[1,"48","8","Academia-Private Sector R&D Linkage Initiative","Developing linkages of academia with private sector to promote research and development in the manufacturing sector.",""],[1,"82","4","Digital Innovation Support for SMEs and Startups","In this notion, businesses use tech-based and innovative interventions to give their processes and business models a boost.",""],[1,"83","2","Five-Year ICT and Tech-Based Firm Development Plan","a much-needed 5-year Development Plan is being focused on to boost ICT and tech-based firms.",""],[1,"84","4","Industrial Relocation and Upgradation Support","Foster industrial growth, augmenting productivity, and job creation by promoting industries relocation, technological upgradation, and a conducive investment and business environment to enhance global competitiveness and ease of doing business, while discouraging ad hoc policy changes to ensure stability for manufacturing investments.",""],[1,"84","6","Capacity Building and Technology Upgrade for Traditional Sectors","Enhance capacity building and technology upgrades in traditional sectors like sports goods, surgical instruments, medical devices, light engineering, food processing, and textiles/garments, while prioritizing innovation and R&D in export-oriented sectors such as textiles, apparels, leather, and food processing.",""],[1,"84","8","Competitive Industrial Energy Pricing Policy","Support SMEs development, nurture local entrepreneurship, and ensure regionally competitive energy prices to strengthen the international competitiveness of Pakistani industries.",""],[1,"84","9","ESG-Compliant Manufacturing Sector Development","Ensure ESG compliant sustainable development of manufacturing sector, incorporating the Clean Development Mechanism (CDM) and compliance with the EU Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism expected in 2026.",""],[1,"85","1","Industrial Infrastructure Development and Productivity Enhancement","The thrust will be on industrial infrastructure development, SMEs development, skills development, technology upgradation, facilitating innovation, enhancing the competitiveness of local products, encouraging FDI, promoting exports through new/better market access, competitive incentives and facilitating G2G, B2C, B2B, C2C interactions to boost productivity, earnings potential, and competitiveness.",""],[1,"85","1","Smart Factory and Industry 4.0 Modernization","Upgraded infrastructure will provide plug-and-play facilities, while smart factories, Industry 4.0, loT, and automation will enhance product quality and quantity, meeting international standards through certifications and testing.",""],[1,"85","3","Innovation and R&D Support","Innovation and R&D will drive efficient processes and product diversification.",""],[1,"85","5","Balanced Startup Regulation and Innovation Collaboration","Entrepreneurship will be promoted with balanced startup regulations, and academia-industry- government collaboration will spur innovation.",""],[1,"85","5","Auto Industry Electric and Hybrid Vehicle Development Policy","The Auto Industry Development and Export Policy 2021-26 will advance electric and hybrid vehicles to promote green technology, reduce import costs, and combat climate change.",""],[1,"90","7","Innovation Product and Service Development Initiative","Initiate process to Develop innovative products and services.",""],[1,"90","7","Standards Adoption and Competitiveness Support Initiative","Support in adopting standards to become Competitive and demand oriented across the world",""],[1,"90","7","Green Industrialization Projects","Initiate green industrialization projects by focusing on international grants and funding initiatives",""],[1,"91","1","Hi-Tech Products and Services Development Programme","Introduce programs and projects on hi-tech products and services and by reverse engineering support the domestic industry to produce these for local and international markets",""],[1,"101","2","ePAdS Procurement Reform and Local Supplier Support","ePAdS now fully implemented, government needs to ensure its mature adoption by promptly addressing stakeholder challenges and enhancing overall system effectiveness.",""],[1,"117","13","Domestic Technology Development and Industrial Diversification Support","Support domestic technology development, research and innovation in developing countries, including by ensuring a conducive policy environment for, inter alia, industrial diversification and value addition to commodities.",""]],"37":[[1,"40","1","Private Sector Lending Coverage Scheme","Coverage Scheme is planned to de-risk private sector lending, to double SME financing over five years.",""],[1,"41","7","Domestic Savings Mobilization through Digital Finance","To reduce dependence on foreign aid and build sustainable growth, the Plan emphasizes boosting domestic savings through expanded use of mobile wallets, branchless banking, and digital savings products.",""],[1,"41","7","Fintech and Digital Payment Integration for Financial Inclusion","By integrating fintech and digital payment systems, the government aims to formalize informal savings, enhance financial inclusion, and strengthen economic resilience.",""],[1,"61","13","Banking System Development and Financial Inclusion Expansion","The focus will also be on financial sector development through efficient and effective banking system.",""],[1,"63","1","Corporate Retirement Benefits Funding Initiative","Encourage corporations (both private and public) to go for funding retirement benefits.",""],[1,"84","2","ICT and Technology Adoption Initiative","During the Plan period, focus will remain on ICT and technology adoption",""],[1,"84","2","Vocational Training and Skills Development Programme","During the Plan period, focus will remain on ICT and technology adoption, vocational training and skill development",""],[1,"84","8","SME Development and Local Entrepreneurship Support","Support SMEs development, nurture local entrepreneurship, and ensure regionally competitive energy prices to strengthen the international competitiveness of Pakistani industries.",""],[1,"85","3","Subsidized Credit and Lower Loan Rate Support","Competitiveness will be enhanced by reducing input costs, offering subsidized credit, lowering loan rates, and providing the Long-Term Financing Facility (LTFF) for machinery imports.",""],[1,"85","3","Long-Term Financing Facility for Machinery Imports","Competitiveness will be enhanced by reducing input costs, offering subsidized credit, lowering loan rates, and providing the Long-Term Financing Facility (LTFF) for machinery imports.",""],[1,"85","3","SME Skills Training Programme","Skills training will improve SMEs workforce employability, while public sector reforms ensure a level playing field.",""],[1,"85","7","SME Sector Support Strategy","The Plan suggests a strategy for boosting up SMEs sector.",""],[1,"85","8","SME Productivity and Capacity-Building Initiative","strategy is to boost up its productivity and build up capacity to gain an edge in the international market",""],[1,"91","7","Collateral-Free SME Financing Targeting Scheme","Targeting Collateral Free Financing for SMES based on size, sector, geography & gender.",""],[1,"91","7","Credit Guarantee Mechanism Operationalization","Operationalization of Credit Guarantee mechanism and institutions.",""],[1,"91","9","Land Allocation for SMEs in Existing Industrial Estates","Land Allocation for SMES in existing Industrial Estates",""],[1,"92","1","Entrepreneurship and Incubation Programs","Implementation of entrepreneurship and incubation programs.",""],[1,"92","3","Women Entrepreneurship Policy Development and Implementation","Development and Implementation of Women Entrepreneurship Policy",""],[1,"92","5","SME Portal and SME Database Establishment and Operationalization","Establish and Operationalize SME Portal and SME database",""]],"38":[[1,"26","4","CPEC 2.0 Multi-Sector Operationalization Initiative","CPEC 2.0 aims to operationalize multiples of bilateral initiatives that span across critical sectors: modernizing logistics and energy infrastructure, accelerating industrialization and export growth, enhancing agricultural productivity, fostering a digital economy, promoting scientific research, and ensuring inclusive socio-economic development.",""],[1,"26","4","Special Economic Zones Development and Activation","The targeted outcomes include: fully functional Special Economic Zones creating numerous jobs; a diversified and resilient energy portfolio with clean energy; improved transport corridors reducing logistics costs; increased digital exports and nationwide broadband coverage; and empowered communities with greater access to education, health, and livelihood opportunities.",""],[1,"39","7","Special Economic Zone Development","The Plan includes key initiatives such as developing a National Industrial Policy for regulatory consistency, establishing SEZs to improve infrastructure, and promoting Industry 4.0 technologies like loT and automation for innovation.",""],[1,"39","7","Foreign Investment Attraction through CPEC","The plan also focuses on value addition in sectors like textiles, attracting foreign investment through CPEC, and supporting SMEs with digital transformation and export promotion, aligning with Uraan Pakistan's export-led and digital advancement goals.",""],[1,"47","3","Special Economic Zones Industrial Cooperation Initiative","A considerable surge in FDI and technology transfer is anticipated, driven by industrial cooperation under the planned Special Economic Zones (SEZ's) within CPEC and SIFC Initiative.",""],[1,"52","1","Special Economic Zones and Industrial Infrastructure Development","Special Economic Zones, Export Processing Zones, Industrial Parks, and other specialized infrastructure are also being created to encourage investment and improve returns.",""],[1,"53","2","National Special Economic Zones Development Programme","Special Economic Zones (SEZs) are being developed nationwide to attract industrialization and investment, with 35 SEZs currently operational.",""],[1,"53","2","One Stop Service for SEZ Investors","Efforts are underway to create a \"One Stop Service\" for SEZ investors to expedite approvals.",""],[1,"53","2","CPEC Industrial Cooperation Framework Agreement","The Framework Agreement on Industrial Cooperation under the CPEC seeks to strengthen Pakistan's export-oriented industrial base with Chinese support.",""],[1,"55","4","Early Operationalization of Special Economic Zones and Industrial Relocation","Early Operationalization of SEZ's and relocation of industries with particular focus on Chinese industry.",""],[1,"84","5","Industrial Zone and Special Economic Zone Hub Development","Leverage CPEC and non-CPEC industrial zones and SEs to create hubs of economic activity, emphasizing value addition for export-led growth.",""],[1,"86","2","Special Economic Zones Development Programme","SEZs on low-cost land with plug-and-play facilities will be developed across the country in consultation with respective Provincial Governments to create investment opportunities.",""],[1,"86","2","SEZ One Stop Service Mechanism","Another important step will be establishing One Stop Service for SEZs to provide time bound public services in SEZs in particular, and the country in general.",""],[1,"86","2","SEZ Infrastructure and Utilities Provision","The SEZs will provide the required infrastructure, including development and utilities across the country in line with the responsibilities under the SEZs law and rules & regulations.",""],[1,"86","2","CPEC Industrial Cooperation Framework Implementation","Framework Agreement on Industrial Cooperation under CPEC will be vigorously implemented as it encompasses relocation of Chinese industries into the SEZs which aims to facilitate export-oriented industrial relocation and creation of a conducive environment for Chinese and other foreign companies.",""],[1,"89","6","Industrial Relocation Attraction Mechanism","Develop mechanism for actively attracting efficiency seeking and reroute supply chains in the region leading to increased labour productivity, growth and capital deepening.",""],[1,"89","8","Regulatory Simplification and Single-Window Clearance for Special Economic Zones","Regulatory processes simplified and based on a single window for Special Economic Zones and country in general.",""],[1,"89","9","Special Economic Zone Need Assessment and Dynamic Planning Framework","Need assessment of SEZs and dynamic planning till 2029, in locations that have locational and economic advantages.",""],[1,"89","9","Phased SEZ Infrastructure and Utilities Planning","Infrastructure & utilities planning for SEZs in phased manner.",""],[1,"90","1","Multimodal Foreign Partner Development Initiative","Multimodal development to bring on-board foreign partners in private or public mode.",""],[1,"90","1","Federal SEZ Development through Public-Private Partnership","One (1) economically viable Federal SEZ to be developed through public private partnership model.",""],[1,"90","1","G2G and PPP Joint Venture Development Model","G2G, PPP/JVs development model will be followed",""],[1,"90","2","IT-Enabled One Stop Service for SEZs","Establishment of an IT enabled One Stop Service for SEZs for provision of end-to- end time bound approvals and services to investors.",""],[1,"99","6","IT-Focused Special Economic and Export Processing Zones","Therefore, set up SEZs and EPZs focused on IT and related Exports is required.",""],[1,"100","10","IT-Focused Special Economic Zones and Export Incentive Reform","Establish IT-focused SEZs to address physical space constraints for export firms.",""],[1,"218","2","Special Economic Zone Development under CPEC Phase I","AIIC continues to allocate industrial plots, and development at Dhabeji is progressing, with plot allotments expected by mid-2025.",""],[1,"218","7","Industrial Diversification for Export-Led Growth","The Plan aims to drive a diversified, inclusive, and sustainable economic transformation by enhancing regional connectivity, promoting climate-resilient agriculture, export-led growth through industrial diversification, advancing clean energy, and strengthening IT and technological innovation all through deepened strategic cooperation with China, aligned with the 5Es Framework and national development priorities.",""],[1,"219","1","Special Economic Zones Establishment and Operationalization","Drive export diversification and industrial competitiveness through the establishment and operationalization of Special Economic Zones (SEZs).",""],[1,"219","2","Operationalization of Prioritized Special Economic Zones","Fully operationalize the four prioritized SEZs: Rashakai, Allama Iqbal, Dhabeji, and Bostan in first phase followed by replication of successful practices in other SEZs",""],[1,"219","2","Industrial Relocation Incentive Package","Encourage industry relocation from China by offering competitive incentives, utility infrastructure, and ease of doing business",""],[1,"219","2","Cluster-Based Industrial Development Initiative","Promote cluster-based development in agro-processing, textile, automotive, pharmaceuticals, IT, and minerals",""],[1,"220","7","Export-Led Industrialization and SEZ Development Package","Export-led industrialization, SEZ development, value- added manufacturing, marketing/ road shows, logistics upgrades, market access to China.",""],[1,"222","5","Special Economic Zones Operationalization and Development Programme","One of the central pillars of the second phase of the CPEC will be the operationalization of SEZs i.e. Rashakai in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Allama Iqbal Industrial City in Punjab, Dhabeji in Sindh, and Bostan in Balochistan.",""],[1,"222","5","Model Special Economic Zones Development Initiative","further collaborative efforts will focus on the development of model SEZs in key metropolitan centers such as Karachi and Islamabad.",""]],"39":[[1,"23","2","Mining Sector Support and Green Mining Promotion","The Special Investment Facilitation Council (SIFC) is committed to supporting this sector through efficient utilization of geological resources, implementing international standards, fostering joint ventures, advancing institutional reforms, integrating data, developing mineral corridors, promoting mechanization, enhancing marketing, building capacity, and adopting green mining practices.",""],[1,"40","1","Provincial Mineral Extraction Initiatives","At the provincial level, in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Balochistan, several initiatives are being prioritized, which include renewable energy projects, mineral extraction, and the development of fisheries value chains.",""],[1,"87","2","Mineral Sector Modernization and Capacity Development","This can be achieved by modernizing the regulatory framework, enhancing infrastructure at mining sites, advancing technological capabilities, developing workforce skills, securing financial resources, and improving marketing strategies.",""],[1,"88","1","Mineral Sector Institutional and Regulatory Reform","Institutional reforms will enhance mineral-related entities, update national policies, Acts, and Mines & Mineral Rules, and address gaps in existing frameworks.",""],[1,"88","1","National Mineral Data Centre Integration","National Mineral Data Centre (NMDC) will integrate data to improve ease of doing business",""],[1,"88","1","Mineral Corridor and Logistics Hub Development","mineral corridors, one- window operations for mining leases, and logistic hubs near mineral clusters will reduce bureaucratic obstacles.",""],[1,"88","2","Mining Mechanization Support through Equipment and Machinery Pools","Mining mechanization will be supported through equipment and machinery pools for smaller miners.",""],[1,"88","2","Mineral Marketing and Capacity Building Coordination Mechanism","Marketing and capacity building will involve coordination among federal institutes and provinces to share non-sensitive mineral data and lab facilities, strengthen institutions, offer fiscal incentives like mineral blocks as SEZs, and provide assistance in project diligence and contract management.",""],[1,"88","3","Research-Industry-Academia Innovation Linkage Initiative","Linkages among research organizations, industry, and academia will foster innovation and sustainable policies.",""],[1,"93","11","Non-Sensitive Mineral Data and Laboratory Facilities Sharing Framework","Developing a framework/mechanism for sharing of Non-Sensitive Mineral Data & Lab Facilities among PAEC/GSP/SoP/SUPARCO/Provinces, etc.",""],[1,"93","13","National Mineral Data Centre Establishment","Establishment of National Mineral Data Centre",""],[1,"93","17","Mining Law Promulgation and Enforcement","Promulgation and implementation of Mining Laws across Pakistan and ensuring legal rights of investors at Quarries vis-à-vis non-productive / non-active leaseholders",""],[1,"94","3","Legal Consultancy for Model Mineral Agreement and Regulatory Framework Update","Legal Consultancy Services for drafting of Model Mineral Agreement and updating of Regulatory Framework",""],[1,"107","18","Accelerated Geological Mapping and Mineral Expansion Programme","Accelerated Geological Mapping and Mineral Expansion Using Advanced Satellite Image Based Technologies for Unmapped Areas",""]],"40":[[1,"100","7","Telecommunications Liberalization and 5G Broadband Promotion","Build upon two decades of deregulation of 3G/ 4G license awards to position Pakistan as a regional leader in 5G and broadband technologies.",""],[1,"102","4","Telecom Sector Deregulation and Innovation Policy Continuation","The Plan envisages continuation of de-regulation and innovation policy in the Telecom Sector which will enable Pakistan to leverage past investments and capitalize on future growth potential.",""],[1,"102","15","Supportive Regulation for Mobile Network Operator Transition","The transition of Mobile Network Operators (MNOs) from voice to data providers and growth in NGMS subscribers creates challenges and opportunities requiring proactive, supportive regulation.",""],[1,"102","15","5G Piloting and Launch Initiative","5G piloting and launch will fuel telecom investment and revenue growth while driving",""],[1,"103","1","Fiber Optic Network Enhancement for BTS","The Plan aims to enhance fiber optic network of base transceiver stations (BTS) for fast, robust data links through government-private sector collaboration.",""],[1,"103","1","5G Deployment Market Assessment and Promotion","Assess demand and identify prime markets for meaningful 5G deployment in loT, smart cities, factories, farms, and transportation.",""],[1,"107","1","5G Network Pilot and Service Launch","Pakistan will experiment with 5G networks and launch services by Plan period end.",""],[1,"107","1","High-Speed Mobile Broadband Investment","The 4th Industrial Revolution's trends - blockchain, big data, cloud computing, and loT- require continued high-speed mobile broadband investment.",""],[1,"107","3","5G Service Deployment","5G Launch: Deploy 5G services during Plan period with 100 million NGMS subscribers including 10 percent 5G users",""],[1,"107","5","Broadband Expansion and Network Modernization Framework","Key priorities encompass digital inclusion, security, infrastructure and spectrum sharing, and local telecom equipment production support.",""],[1,"107","5","5G Rollout and Advanced Connectivity Promotion","PTA leads 5G rollout with industry partners while promoting Wi-Fi 6E and Fiber-To-The-Tower technologies for advanced applications like AR/VR.",""],[1,"107","9","Expansion of FTTH Services in Existing Cities","Expansion of FTTH Services (GPON) in Existing Cities of AJ&K and GB (Phase-IV)",""],[1,"107","11","Optical Fiber Cable Deployment for Transmission Network Expansion","Deployment of Optical Fiber Cable for Expansion of Transmission Network in GB",""],[1,"111","3","Telecom Infrastructure Upgradation and 5G Rollout","Continued growth and upgradation of telecom infrastructure and sector will lead to at least 10 percent year on year growth in Telecom industry revenues and tax collections to match the planned growth targets for services sector.",""],[1,"111","3","5G Services Launch and Next-Generation Mobile Services Expansion","Launching of 5G services during the Plan period and transitions and transformations at the intersection of voice/data shall continue to fuel telecom growth with at least 100 million next generation mobile services (NGMS) subscribers including 10 percent SG users",""],[1,"111","3","Digital Network Readiness for the Fourth Industrial Revolution","Merger of connectivity, data, and devices shall enable the network to become ready for the 4th Industrial Revolution.",""],[1,"331","3","Next-Generation Telecom Networks Deployment","PTA with a vision to foster innovation and connectivity will embrace cutting-edge technologies and facilitate the deployment of next-generation networks.",""],[1,"331","3","Telecom Policy Development and Implementation Partnerships","Collaborations Swith industry stakeholders, government bodies, and international organizations will be made to develop and implement robust policies that address the challenges and opportunities presented by the ever-changing telecommunications environment.",""],[1,"331","3","National Telecom Infrastructure and Service Expansion","An enabling environment for the availability of high-quality telecom services and robust infrastructure will be provided across the country to bridge the digital divide.",""],[1,"331","3","Broadband Adoption Promotion Initiative","PTA will actively promote adoption of widespread broadband through concerted efforts.",""],[1,"331","3","Digital Gender Inclusion Initiative","PTA will also take initiatives to promote digital gender inclusion, aiming to enhance women's access to digital technology.",""],[1,"331","3","5G Technology Introduction","PTA will proactively pursue the introduction of 5G technology in Pakistan.",""],[1,"331","3","Satellite Broadband and Wi-Fi Advancement","PTA is poised to revolutionize connectivity in Pakistan by leveraging satellite broadband and taking strategic measures to ensure the advancement of Wi-Fi technology in Pakistan, in harmony with global trends.",""],[1,"331","3","National Cybersecurity Enforcement Measures","Robust cybersecurity measures will be enforced to safeguard the integrity and privacy of digital communications.",""],[1,"331","3","Digital Pakistan Vision Implementation Partnerships","To proactively implement the \"Digital Pakistan\" vision, national and international collaborations will be forged to achieve the 'Leading' 5G regulator status under the International Telecommunication Union (ITU) ranking system.",""],[1,"339","23","Data Protection and Privacy Collaboration Framework","Address concern related to data protection privacy which impact on competition through collaboration with data protection authorities",""],[1,"341","13","Multi-Stakeholder Policy Development and Implementation Collaboration","Collaborations with industry stakeholders including government bodies, and international organizations to develop and implement robust policies to address sectoral challenges and opportunities",""],[1,"341","14","5G Technology Rollout Collaboration","Proactively pursue the introduction of 5G technology in collaborations with industry and other stakeholders for 5G rollout on account of Digital Pakistan vision",""],[1,"341","15","Satellite Broadband and Wi-Fi Connectivity Enhancement","Strategic measures to enhance connectivity through Satellite broadband and through adaptation of advancement of Wi-Fi technology",""]],"41":[[1,"111","2","Awareness and Training Programs through Sectoral Cooperation","creating awareness and offering training programs through sectoral cooperation.",""],[1,"116","4","Indigenous Technology and Innovation Development Initiative","The Plan adopts an approach that places greater importance on the development of indigenous technologies and innovation, while also focusing on incorporating the latest technologies available globally.",""],[1,"118","10","Governance Systems Improvement in Higher Education and Science and Technology Organizations","Improving governance systems within HEIs and S&T organizations",""],[1,"118","11","Science and Technology Policy Mechanism Reform","Reform the policy mechanisms necessary to put science and technology at the center of a national strategy",""],[1,"118","12","University and Science and Technology Commercial Income Enhancement","· Enhance income generation capacity of universities and commercial income of S&T for financial sustainability",""],[1,"118","13","National Faculty, Researchers, and Scientists Capacity Building","Establish a strong faculty, researchers and scientists base within the country",""],[1,"118","16","Innovation-Friendly Policy Regime","Create effective and innovation-friendly policy regime to support innovation",""],[1,"118","17","Multi-Sector Knowledge Diffusion Engagement Models","Create and implement innovative models of engagement between academia, public, private, and defence sectors for knowledge diffusion",""],[1,"118","18","Indigenous Technology Research and Innovation Initiative","Create indigenous technologies through research and innovation, S&T initiatives to grow economy and address local needs in key areas of urgency",""],[1,"119","7","University Own-Source Revenue Mobilization","Universities to achieve income to cover 50percent of recurring expenditure and 25 percent of development expenditure from own resources by tuition/ other charges, philanthropy, alumni engagement,",""],[1,"119","8","Science, Technology and Innovation Commercialization Returns Framework","Transitioning STI from Public Sector S&T organizations for intended use to deliver at least 1-3 returns within 5 years and 3-5 returns within 10 years of GoP investment.",""],[1,"119","11","Expansion of ORIC and BIC Network in Higher Education Institutions","Expand the network of ORICS by establishment of ORICs and BICs in all universities / HEIs in the next 5 years",""],[1,"119","15","Science and Technology Commercialization Framework","This will ensure availability of science and technology based potential civilian applications to private sector investors.",""],[1,"119","17","Mega Initiatives for Science, Technology, and Innovation","Fund at least 5 Mega Initiatives to address both national needs as well as future aspirations in science and technology and innovation to ensure indigenization and local technological content, S&T capacity building, and civilian spillovers with a focused effort and mechanism in place to deliver short-to-medium term outcomes within a 3-5-year period and impact in 5-10 year timeframe.",""],[1,"121","2","Public Sector Science and Technology Capability Reform","There is need to build public sector S&T capability to support industrial competitiveness by reforming and reinvigorating the Pakistan Council for Scientific and Industrial Research (PCSIR).",""],[1,"121","2","R&D Organization Mandate Reform and Reorganization","Moreover, needs to reform, re-organize, and re-negotiate mandates / mission of R&D organizations in MoST and outside within first year of the plan period and subsequent publishing of substantive and outcome- oriented research KPIs on a six-monthly basis to demonstrate performance improvement.","MoST"],[1,"121","2","National Science and Technology Performance Reporting Mechanism","MOST must put up a consequential national agenda and performance reporting for STI at the very highest level of the government through regular meetings of the National Commission for Science and Technology (NCST) at the very least on an annual basis.","MOST"],[1,"121","7","Science and Technology Policy Mechanism Reform","Reform of the S&T policy mechanism is required particularly reviving and making the National Commission for Science and Technology (NCST) an effective, proactive, and administratively efficient body to periodically review, oversee, and approve policies, priorities, programs, and mega",""],[1,"122","1","Review of National Science, Technology and Innovation Policy","There is also need for immediate review of National Science Technology & Innovation (STI) Policy along with other relevant sectoral policies.",""],[1,"122","1","Mandate and Performance Audit of Science and Technology Organizations","The Ministry of Science and Technology shall carry out an exhaustive review of the mandates and missions of its various organizations, an audit of their performance till date, and revise the mandates (where needed) to deliver on meaningful and realistic targets and KPIs.","Ministry of Science and Technology"],[1,"122","1","Public Sector R&D Salary Alignment Reform","The salary structures within the public sector R&D organizations must be brought at par with those in academia.",""],[1,"122","1","Resource Efficiency and Private-Sector Fundraising Mechanism","In addition, it is imperative to improve mechanisms for resource efficiency and institutionalizing the practice of fundraising from private sector.",""],[1,"126","12","Regular NCST Research Direction Meetings","Regular meetings of NCST under the chairmanship of Prime Minister to set direction of research for MOST",""],[1,"127","3","R&D Organization Reform and Reorganization","Reform, re-organize, negotiate mandates / R&D organizations in substantive and oriented research improvement of productivity as per needs of the country",""],[1,"128","6","Science, Technology and Engineering for Development Program","Science, Technology and Engineering for Development (STED) program in collaboration of through various ministries or a Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV) created for this purpose.",""]],"42":[[1,"68","6","Energy Sector Priority Investment","Within infrastructure sectors, top priority will be assigned to the Transport and Communication Sector with 22 percent share followed by Water, Physical Planning and Housing and Energy sectors with 7 percent, 5 percent and 5 percent shares, respectively.",""],[1,"68","8","Private Sector Investment Promotion in the Power Sector","government is encouraging private sector to invest in Power sector",""],[1,"68","8","Public Sector Energy Generation and Distribution Investment","Rs. 1072 billion is anticipated to be spent on energy generation and distribution in the public sector during the plan period by WAPDA, PEPCO and NTDC as self-generated resources in the power sector",""],[1,"68","8","Completion of Ongoing Mega Power Projects","The main focus will be given to the completion of ongoing mega projects",""],[1,"68","8","New Public and Private Power Schemes","new schemes will also be initiated through public and private investment especially in such a way that these schemes will become operational during the Plan period",""],[1,"69","3","Power Sector Investment Allocation","Within the infrastructure sector, about 12 percent will be invested for power sector",""],[1,"69","6","Energy Sector Investment Expansion","A substantial increase of investment in the energy sector, both through budget and self-financed, will cater to the financial requirements of the strategic projects of the WAPDA, PEPCO and other energy projects that are being executed by the Pakistan Atomic Energy Commission.",""],[1,"69","6","Private Sector Energy Investment Facilitation Framework","To supplement efforts of the government, investment by the private sector in the energy projects will be encouraged by strengthening the existing legal, financial and regulatory framework.",""],[1,"69","6","PSDP Support for WAPDA and PEPCO","Furthermore, assistance will be provided to the WAPDA and PEPCO through PSDP budget.",""],[1,"177","3","Private-Sector-Driven Energy Market Reform","Given fiscal constraints, the five-year plan aims to pivot from a public-sector-led model to a more private-sector-driven energy market, focusing on financial viability and institutional reform.",""],[1,"178","7","National Electricity Plan Implementation Framework","To operationalize the policy, the National Electricity Plan (2023-27) provides implementation guidelines and tools31.",""],[1,"178","7","Competitive Trading Bilateral Contracts Market Introduction","The Competitive Trading Bilateral Contracts Market (CTBCM) is being introduced to enable competitive wholesale electricity trading, with gradual retail market liberalization.",""],[1,"178","7","Circular Debt Management Plan","To address financial sustainability, a Circular Debt Management Plan (CDMP), developed jointly by GoP and IMF, focuses on cost optimization, timely tariff setting, subsidy release, and reduction of losses.",""],[1,"179","1","Competitive Bidding for Future Power Generation Additions","future additions planned via competitive bidding under IGCEP",""],[1,"179","1","Private Transmission Expansion through PPP or BOO/BOOT Models","future expansion must adopt PPP or BOO/BOOT models supported by viability gap funding",""],[1,"179","1","CTBCM Rollout for Power Market Liberalization","the CTBCM rollout will open wholesale- and later retail-markets to private players",""],[1,"179","1","Privatization or Leasing of Distribution Companies","The government is also considering privatization or leasing of DISCOs to improve efficiency, reduce losses, and enhance affordability",""],[1,"184","8","Competitive Electricity Tariff Policy","To maintain regional competitiveness, it is essential to ensure that electricity tariffs are competitive for businesses, allowing them to effectively utilize energy for productive purposes.",""],[1,"184","8","Competitive Electricity Market Reform through CTBCM","Advent of CTBCM and its long-term affect is expected to bring competitiveness in electricity market especially for the industries and manufacturing sector.",""],[1,"184","9","Energy Sector Financial Sustainability and Market Reform","The financial sustainability of the energy sector, coupled with an effective circular debt management plan and the establishment of a liquid energy market, is crucial for achieving an optimum mix of productive and consumptive use of energy resources.",""],[1,"184","9","Electricity Market Liberalization and Market-Based Pricing","Furthermore, the establishment of a liquid electricity market, characterized by efficient power trading mechanisms and market-based pricing, promotes competition, transparency, and market efficiency.",""],[1,"185","1","Public-Private Partnerships for Energy Sector Development","Initiatives may include public-private partnerships, regulatory reforms, and incentivizing private investment in renewable energy projects to diversify the energy mix and address challenges like power shortages.",""],[1,"187","2","National Electricity Plan 2023-27","These key policies, reforms and programs, inter-alia, include National Electricity Plan (2023-27) which focuses on six key objectives diversification, resilience, self-sufficiency, affordability, financial viability, and sustainability supported by twenty priority areas with clear targets to ensure clean, reliable, and affordable energy.",""],[1,"187","2","Electricity Tariff Regime Reform","The tariff regime will be revised to eliminate uncapped dollar indexation and rebalance currency risk among stakeholders.",""],[1,"187","2","GENCO Phase-Out and Regulatory Performance Review","Inefficient state- owned GENCOs will be phased out, and regulator performance will be reviewed per the National Electricity Plan 2023-27.",""],[1,"187","4","Retail Electricity Market Reform and DISCO Restructuring","GoP will explore options such as privatization, provincialisation, long-term concessions, and outsourcing of DISCOs to reduce its footprint.",""],[1,"187","4","Targeted Distribution Loss Reduction Programme","Targeted loss reduction programs using technologies like AMI, ABCs, and APMS will be implemented to cut technical losses.",""],[1,"187","4","Electricity Debt Recovery Support Mechanism","Under the National Electricity Plan 2023-27, recovery of bad debts from disconnected consumers will be pursued with the help of local governments and law enforcement.",""],[1,"187","4","DISCO and Bulk Power Consumer Capacity Building","Capacity building of DISCOs and Bulk Power Consumers will also be undertaken to support CTBCM implementation and ensure efficient operations through an enabling business model.",""],[1,"188","2","Energy Sector Price Deregulation","The long-term financial sustainability of the energy sector depends upon price deregulation in the mid-stream and downstream.",""],[1,"188","2","Stakeholder-Consulted Energy Deregulation Rollout","This deregulation would be implemented in consultation with all local stakeholders in order to ensure a smooth rollout and avoid any dry out situations in the country.",""],[1,"191","6","DISCO Privatization and Outsourcing Reform","Privatization, provincialisation, recovery outsourcing or management outsourcing of DISCOS",""],[1,"191","11","Circular Debt Reduction Measures","Reducing any further buildup of circular debt as per CDMP",""],[1,"191","12","CTBCM Implementation and Retail Electricity Market Planning","Accelerate implementation of CTBCM and further plan for retail electricity markets.",""],[1,"191","20","Targeted Subsidy Mechanism for Vulnerable Groups","Targeted subsidy mechanism for vulnerable segments of society",""]],"43":[[1,"25","4","Enhanced Oil and Gas Exploration and Production","The focus in the fuel sector will be to bridge the wide demand-supply gap through enhanced E&P activities",""],[1,"25","4","Refinery Upgradation and New Refinery Development","upgradation of existing refineries as well installation of new refinery",""],[1,"25","4","Gas Contract and LNG Procurement Framework","development of a framework for ensuring an optimal balance between long-term gas contracts and spot LNG buying while considering the affordability of the end consumer",""],[1,"25","4","Alternative Fuels Policy and Regulatory Framework","The development of alternative fuels such as biofuels and hydrogen will be encouraged through corresponding policy and regulatory frameworks to ensure diversification of energy supply chain",""],[1,"40","1","Coal Mining Tax Credit Scheme","For the mining sector, a tax credit scheme focusing on coal mining in Sindh, aimed at supplying coal exclusively for power generation, is also being emphasized.",""],[1,"180","1","TAPI Pipeline Project","Progress continues on the TAPI pipeline, seen as strategically significant.",""],[1,"180","6","Foreign Supplier Petroleum Inventory Facility","Allows foreign suppliers to maintain petroleum inventory/in Pakistan without foreign exchange outflows.",""],[1,"180","8","Strategic Private Sector Partnerships for LNG and Refinery Development","The government plans strategic partnerships with the private sector for LNG import terminals, gas distribution reforms, and new refinery development under recently approved policies.",""],[1,"188","1","Fuel Sector Policy Reform for Domestic Energy Production and Consumption Rationalization","During the Plan, the fuel sector will implement policy reforms to enhance indigenous oil, gas, and coal production, refining capacity, and with special emphasis rationalize fuel consumption in major sectors like transport.",""],[1,"188","5","Exploration and Production Policy Review for Hydrocarbon Investment","E&P policies would be reviewed to incentivize investment in exploration and production particularly tight gas, shale gas, offshore production.",""],[1,"188","7","New Crude Oil Refinery Development","Setting up at least one new deep conversion, state of the art crude oil refinery to bridge the demand supply gap in the local and imported refined petroleum products and better-quality fuel products as per refinery policy 2023.",""],[1,"188","8","LNG Infrastructure Upgradation and Expansion","Upgradation and expansion of the existing LNG infrastructure in the country through the development of additional LNG terminal, an onshore storage facility and allied infrastructure to cater for the increased demand for imports of LNG.",""],[1,"188","9","Natural Gas Import Pipeline Projects","natural gas import projects like TAPI and IP would be pursued expeditiously in the context of regional cooperation and energy security.",""],[1,"188","9","Pipeline Connectivity Exploration with UAE and Oman","possibilities of connecting with energy-rich regions of UAE and Oman through pipelines would be explored during the plan period.",""],[1,"188","10","New Petroleum Terminal Development Outside Karachi","a new terminal location outside Karachi (at Gwadar, Hub etc.) will be pursued to provide strategic security to the country's fuel supply chain.",""],[1,"188","11","Cross-Country Oil Pipeline Dual-Fuel Upgrade and Storage Expansion","Cross-country oil pipeline will be geared to handle dual fuel with additional oil depots installations and storages to ensure robustness in energy supply chain.",""],[1,"189","2","Gas Storage Facility Development","gas storage facilities would be built at depleted gas fields.",""],[1,"189","5","Gas Procurement Balance Framework","A robust framework for optimal balance between long term gas contracts and spot buying would be developed.",""],[1,"189","8","Local Coal Production and Utilization Programme","Increasing local coal production and effective economic utilization of this indigenous resource remains the integral part of this 5-year plan.",""],[1,"189","9","Conversion of Imported Coal Power Plants to Local Coal","It is envisaged that imported coal power plants will be converted on local coal which would help save burden on foreign exchange and international price shocks.",""],[1,"189","10","Thar Coal Utilization for Fertilizer and Petrochemicals","efforts would be made to utilize Thar Coal reserves in fertilizer via coal gasification and petrochemicals industries through coal liquefaction.",""],[1,"189","11","Thar Coal Rail Link Completion","its supply chain routes including railways need to be strengthened and the Thar Coal Rail Link project will be completed during the plan period.",""],[1,"192","3","Fast-Track TAPI and Iran-Pakistan Gas Pipeline Implementation","Fast track implementation of TAPI and Iran Pakistan gas pipeline",""],[1,"192","5","Comprehensive LNG and Oil Infrastructure Review","Comprehensive review of the LNG and oil related infrastructure including storages need to be completed",""],[1,"192","9","LPG Adoption as Alternate Fuel Policy","To mitigate the depletion of indigenous gas, adoption of LPG as an alternate fuel; LPG policy to be concluded",""],[1,"192","11","Thar Coal Utilization for Fertilizer and Petrochemicals","Implementation plan to utilize Thar Coal reserves in fertilizer via coal gasification and petrochemicals industries through coal liquefaction",""]],"44":[[1,"11","8","Energy Mix Diversification and Circular Debt Reduction","This will be achieved by diversifying our energy mix towards renewables, reducing circular debt, and completing strategic infrastructure projects to unlock economic potential.",""],[1,"25","3","Transmission and Distribution System Bottleneck Removal","The bottlenecks and congestion in the transmission and distribution system will be removed for smooth operation of the least cost electricity generator as per the economic merit order of dispatch.",""],[1,"25","3","Power Sector Planning Alignment and Synchronization","Efforts shall be made for alignment and synchronization of Transmission System Expansion Plan (TSEP) with Integrated Generation Capacity Expansion Plan (IGCEP) and distribution infrastructure investment plans (DIIP).",""],[1,"25","3","DISCO Privatization and Outsourcing Reform","GOP will focus on various options of privatization, concessions, and partial outsourcing of DISCOs to reduce the GoP footprint.",""],[1,"25","3","DISCO Institutional Readiness Reassessment","Similarly, for the transition period GoP will reassess and reorganize the institutional readiness of DISCOs with respect to their business plans.",""],[1,"331","5","Strengthening of NEPRA Regulatory Autonomy","National Electric Power Regulatory Authority (NEPRA) will be further strengthened by providing autonomy in implementation of its regulatory decisions especially the Indicative Generation Capacity Expansion Plan (IGCEP), Transmission System Expansion Plan (TSEP) and Competitive Trading Bilateral Contract Market (CTBCM).",""],[1,"332","1","NEPRA Risk Management Framework Development","A robust risk management framework will be developed to identify and address the potential risks to the effective functioning of NEPRA and the implementation of its regulatory decisions.",""],[1,"341","3","Strengthening NEPRA Autonomy in Power Sector Planning and Market Reform","Strengthening NEPRA through autonomy in Transmission Implementation System Expansion Plan (TSEP) and Competitive Trading Bilateral Contract Market (CTBCM) and Indicative Generation Capacity Expansion Plan (IGCEP- 2022-31)",""]],"45":[[1,"70","4","Agricultural Innovation and Research Support","Though the agriculture sector has been devolved to the provinces, yet it needs federal attention for innovation and research to ensure food security in the country.",""],[1,"70","4","Production Sector Investment for Research and Development","To promote agriculture, industry & commerce and minerals on modern lines and to attract private investment, production sector has been planned investment of Rs. 84 billion during the Plan period.",""],[1,"70","4","Productivity and Value-Addition Enhancement Initiative","This amount will mainly be spent on research and development to boost productivity and promote value-addition in the domestically produced products so that these become competitive, and earn more foreign exchange through export of agro-based industrial products.",""],[1,"155","12","Agriculture Innovation System Reform","Introduce reforms in the Agriculture Innovation System (AIS) of Pakistan to make it responsive to the needs of stakeholders along the value chain in each cluster.",""],[1,"155","12","Cotton Productivity Revival Initiative","Special emphasis will be given on the revival of cotton productivity by enhancing R&D investment and import of pest-resistant and heat tolerant gene to be incorporated in local varieties.",""],[1,"155","14","Private Sector AIS Investment Support Mechanism","Encourage private sector to enhance investment on AIS by developing IPR protecting, material and information sharing mechanism.",""],[1,"155","15","Establishment of Autonomous Boards with Private Sector Participation","Establishing autonomous boards with private sector members in these boards, and the autonomy trickle down to scientists' level.",""],[1,"155","16","Competitive Research Grant Expansion for AIS","Higher Education Commissions, both at federal and provincial levels, will expand their competitive grant mechanism to cover all research activities of AIS.",""],[1,"155","17","Research System Projectisation and Competitive Grant Funding Reform","Projectise the whole research system; all projects should be won through grants, and they must be multi-disciplinary, inter-institutes, and problem solving with quantifiable KPIs.",""],[1,"155","18","Regular Research Planning Mechanism","Mechanism for regular research planning at national and regional level by engaging stakeholders",""],[1,"155","19","Periodic Review of Research Organizations","Periodic internal and external review of research organizations to evaluate their performance",""],[1,"155","20","Independent Project Activity Monitoring Mechanism","An independent monitoring mechanism of project activities.",""],[1,"156","1","Agricultural Technology Import Special Fund","Assign a special fund for the import of agriculture technologies, especially models of machines, pest-resistant and environment-tolerant genes, and management models.",""],[1,"156","2","Agricultural Technology Collaboration and Transfer Initiative","Develop collaboration with China, USA and other global / regional economies to bring researched technologies for bovine vaccines, sexed sorting and genomic technologies, varieties/hybrids of various crops including fruits, vegetables, fodder, etc., heat tolerant and pest-resistant genes, farm management models and machinery.",""],[1,"159","8","Agriculture Innovation System Reform Program","Reform program for the agriculture innovation system to make it responsive to stakeholders' issues along the whole value chain, autonomous, plural and collaborative with other national and international centers in the public and private sector having sustainable funding sources.",""],[1,"160","21","Speed Breeding Center Establishment and Hybrid Development Programme","Establish Speed Breeding Center in NARC and NIAB and develop hybrids in cotton, rice, oilseed, and grains.",""],[1,"160","22","Animal Genomics Center and Sex-Sorting Technology Promotion","Establishment of Animal Genomics Center at NARC and promotion of sex-sorting technology in the private sector for genetic Improvement of milk and meat animals",""],[1,"161","1","Tissue Culture Laboratory and SOP Establishment","Establishment of tissue culture labs and SOPs for tissue culture seedling for major fruits, vegetables and flowers, especially for dates, banana and potato",""],[1,"161","5","R&D Strategic Infrastructure Improvement","Improvements of R&D strategic infrastructure in NARC and in provincial research institutes, especially vaccine research institutes, value added livestock product institutes, post-harvst research institute",""]],"46":[[1,"286","11","Media Regulatory Framework Improvement and Implementation","To improve and implement the regulatory framework for print, electronic, social and digital media.",""],[1,"286","17","Dedicated PID Media Cell for CVE Pilot Project","Establishment of Dedicated PID Media Cell to CVE-Pilot Project (Islamabad), PID",""],[1,"287","4","National Media Policy Development","A National Media Policy will be developed in consultation with stakeholders to guide the Mass Media Sector.",""],[1,"287","4","Federal Ministry for Information Broadcasting, Technology and Telecommunication","A single Federal Ministry for \"Information Broadcasting, Technology and Telecommunication\" will be established, consolidating functions currently managed by separate ministries and integrating cinema oversight.",""],[1,"287","5","Update Media and Online Content Regulation","PEMRA's laws and regulations will be updated to address challenges posed by WebTV, OTT, and online content services, ensuring fairness, transparency, accountability, and independence.",""],[1,"287","8","Journalist Accreditation Agency","An independent agency will accredit journalists to promote professionalism.",""],[1,"287","8","Social Media Regulatory Oversight","A regulatory body will manage social media to ensure responsible use and prevent harmful content.",""],[1,"287","9","Public Service Broadcasting and Media Cybersecurity Framework","Public service obligations for TV and radio, quality standards for content, and a national cybersecurity framework for media organizations will be established.",""],[1,"289","11","Update of ICT Laws, Policies, and Regulations","Update the outdated laws, polices, regulations etc. as per the targets of ITU and to cope with the requirement of digital platforms",""],[1,"331","4","PEMRA Amendment Bill Implementation and Media Regulatory Reform","Pakistan Electronic Media Regulatory Authority (PEMRA) will implement Pakistan Electronic Media Regulatory Authority (Amendment) Bill, 2023 while expanding scope of public entertainment, education and information with improved administrative and disinformation control mechanisms.",""],[1,"331","4","Media Authenticity and Code of Conduct Review Mechanism","Regulatory framework will ensure authenticity of news especially matters pertaining to social tolerance, general development, energy and economic development.",""],[1,"331","4","Interactive Media House Code of Conduct Review Sessions","Interactive sessions for review and update code of conduct for media houses will be conducted.",""],[1,"341","12","News Authenticity Regulatory Framework Implementation","Effective implementation of regulatory framework for the authenticity of news especially matters pertaining to social tolerance, general development, energy and economic development",""]],"47":[[1,"297","10","Foreign Coach Hiring and Sports Equipment Procurement","Hiring of foreign coaches for training of national athletes for participation in mega events and purchase of sports equipment",""],[1,"297","13","National Training Camps for International Sports Mega Events","Organization of National Training Camps for preparation/participation in international sports mega events at PSC Islamabad",""],[1,"298","26","Establishment of Pakistan's First Sports Institute","Establishment of Pakistan's first sports institute",""],[1,"298","32","Sports Nurseries in Schools and Colleges","Revival of sports in educational institutions by declaring of schools and colleges as sports nurseries.",""],[1,"299","3","Specialized Training Programs for Elite Coaches and Physical Education Teachers","Launching of specialized training programs for elite coaches and physical education teachers",""],[1,"299","15","Bio-Mechanical Laboratory Establishment","Establishment of Bio-Mechanical Lab at Pakistan Sports Complex, Islamabad",""],[1,"299","17","Elite Sportspersons Development Plan","Launching of elite Sportspersons Development Plan (ESDP)",""],[1,"299","19","Elite Sports Training and Scholarship Programme","Launching of foreign and domestic training programs and scholarships for elite players, coaches and umpires etc.",""],[1,"299","20","PSB Coaching Centre Construction in Skardu","Construction of PSB Coaching Centre at Skardu (Gilgit- Baltistan)",""],[1,"299","21","Arshad Nadeem/Shahbaz Sharif High Performance Sports Academy Establishment","Establishment of Arshad Nadeem/Shahbaz Sharif High Performance Sports Academy at Pakistan Sports Complex (PSC), Islamabad",""],[1,"300","12","Standardized Physical Education Curriculum and Examination","Ministry of Federal Education and Professional Training in collaboration with Pakistan Sports Board and provincial sports department will develop standardized Physical Education (PE) curriculum and examination for evaluating physical fitness, basic sports knowledge and skills across all primary and secondary schools in the country","Ministry of Federal Education and Professional Training | Pakistan Sports Board | provincial sports department"],[1,"300","13","Talent Hunt and Development Program","Launching of Talent Hunt and Development program in collaboration with national sports federations and provincial sports departments/boards.",""],[1,"300","16","Elite Pool of Sportspersons and Specialized Training Programme","Establishment of 'Elite Pool of Sportspersons' comprising of professional athletes/players who have shown brilliant performance in national and international sporting events and organization of specialized trainings and coaching programs for them in the country and abroad as well.",""],[1,"301","1","Athlete Participation and Competition Opportunities","Creation of opportunities for athletes to participate /compete at sports events at all levels.",""],[1,"301","4","Institute of Sports Establishment","Establishment of institute of sports to promote sports education.",""],[1,"301","16","Sports Talent Hunt and Development Program","Launching of sports talent hunt and\na\ndevelopment program",""],[1,"301","17","Elite Pool of Sportspersons","Establishment of 'Elite Pool of Sportspersons' comprising of players who have shown brilliant performance in national and international sporting events",""],[1,"301","18","Arshad Nadeem/Shahbaz Sharif High Performance Sports Academy","Establishment of Arshad Nadeem/Shahbaz Sharif High Performance Sports Academy at PSC, Islamabad",""],[1,"301","21","Institute of Sports Establishment","Establishment of Institute of Sports",""]],"48":[[1,"321","2","Local Government System Strengthening for Municipal Service Delivery","Enhance delivery of public services, especially critical municipal services, by strengthening local government system to ensure effective delivery of essential services",""],[1,"321","12","Decentralized Governance Systems Development and Stabilization","Develop and stabilize efficient, sustainable, decentralized governance systems at all levels to foster markets, facilitate and create opportunities for individuals and private sector to invest and flourish businesses in accordance with Amendment",""],[1,"322","2","Local Government System Strengthening","During the Plan period, local government system will be strengthened by fostering inclusive governance, empowering communities, and ensuring efficient service delivery at grassroots level.",""],[1,"322","2","Local Government Law Revision and Fiscal Devolution","The existing local government laws will be revisited to ensure timely local government elections and devolve more financial and administrative authority to the local governments for addressing community-specific needs and priorities effectively.",""],[1,"322","2","Local Government Procurement Alignment with PPRA Rules","Public procurements within local government domain will be made in alignment with PPRA rules.",""],[1,"322","2","Timely Audit of Local Government Accounts","Auditor General of Pakistan will ensure timely audit of local government's accounts for effective accountability.",""],[1,"322","3","Local Government System Continuity and Reform Programme","To further strengthen local governments focus will be on continuity of local government system with assessment of its loopholes and improvements instead of repeated experimentations;",""],[1,"322","3","Provincial Finance Commission Institutionalization","institutionalizing Provincial Finance Commission (PFC) will be ensured in consultation with provinces to be aligned with National Finance Commission;",""],[1,"322","3","Incentive-Based Local Government Resource Allocation","diverting need-based resource allocation to incentive-based allocation e.g., matching grants for local governments under PFC;",""],[1,"322","3","Local Revenue Generation and Fee-Based Financing Measures","wealth maximizing/revenue generating activities by using local resources e.g., land, public spaces along with revenue raising through various fees and taxes;",""],[1,"322","3","Local Business Promotion Initiative","promotion of local business;",""],[1,"322","3","Local Government Jurisdiction Clarification Reform","clear jurisdiction of the local government will be determined to minimize influence from legislators and strengthening capacity of the local administration including local representatives through mandatory trainings for effective provision of local services.",""],[1,"332","3","Governance Reform Investment Programme","In order to accomplish the reform agenda, investment will be made in the activities relating to innovation, capacity building, performance management, service delivery, justice sector, police, research, reforms in public sector including regulatory framework and statistics sectors.",""],[1,"333","4","Local Government System Review and Reform Recommendations","Review of local government system, identify loopholes and recommend improvements in consultation with provinces",""],[1,"333","6","Provincial Finance Commission Institutionalization and Strengthening","Institutionalizing Provincial Finance Commission in line with National Finance Commission and making PFC more effective",""],[1,"333","8","Local Government Administrative and Financial Autonomy","Grant maximum administrative and financial antimony to the local government",""],[1,"333","10","Local Government Revenue-Generating Efficiency Enhancement","Wealth maximizing/revenue-generating activities of Local Government by using its own resources to enhance efficiency.",""],[1,"333","12","Public Service Standards and Performance Indicator System","Development and implementation of standards for public services and performance indicator system to provide time bound services and measure the efficiency and effectiveness of service delivery",""],[1,"333","14","Mandatory Training for Local Administration Capacity Building","Strengthening capacity of the local administration through mandatory training by effective utilization of local government training institutes",""],[1,"333","19","Stakeholder Participation Mechanism for Development Processes","Establishment and implementation of mechanism to ensure participation of all stakeholders in development processes",""],[1,"333","26","Advisory Committee Establishment Mechanism","Establishment of Advisory Committees in each Ministry/ Division/ Department and District/Local Level to advise in design and implementation of development agenda.",""]],"49":[[1,"319","3","Ministry Performance Agreements with the Prime Minister","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""],[1,"321","10","Strengthening Parliamentary Fora and Committee Capacity","Strengthen and enhance the role and capacity of Parliamentary fora, including the Senate, National Assembly and Provincial Assemblies and their committees, to ensure democratic governance",""],[1,"325","6","Parliamentary Leadership and Capacity Strengthening Programme","The Plan focuses on enhancing leadership skills of parliamentarians in general and women in particular.",""],[1,"325","6","Parliamentary Committee Research Support Initiative","Specialized research in specific areas of parliamentary committees, especially dealing with strategic policies pertaining to provincial, national and international issues, will be facilitated.",""],[1,"325","6","Parliamentary Services Institutional Strengthening","Institutions of parliamentary services will be strengthened by providing additional resources for enhancing capacity of parliamentarians.",""],[1,"326","1","Electoral Reform","Electoral reform will be introduced to strengthen electoral system.",""],[1,"326","1","Legislative Quorum Enhancement","A limit for quorum of legislative forum will be enhanced up to 50 percent of the total strength of respective house.",""],[1,"326","2","Parliamentary Institutional Support and Service Modernization","The focus will be on provision of parliamentary services emphasizing importance of institutional support for lawmakers with key recommendations including continuous training for parliamentary staff, enhanced research capabilities, and maintenance of a technologically advanced parliamentary library.",""],[1,"326","2","Digital Parliamentary Document Management System","The integration of modern technology, including digital document management systems, will be encouraged to streamline processes and improve transparency.",""],[1,"326","3","Open Government and Regulatory Integrity Framework","the plan will focus on a framework to safeguard public interests through various initiatives, including implementing open government initiatives, whistle-blower protection laws, and Regulatory Impact Assessments (RIA) to assess the potential impact of proposed regulations on public interests.",""],[1,"326","3","Public Consultation and Legislative Oversight Strengthening","Stakeholder engagement through public consultations, strengthened legislative oversight, and enforcement of anti-corruption measures will be conducted.",""],[1,"326","3","Parliamentary Legal and Regulatory Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening legal and regulatory framework through parliamentary services will be emphasized with collaborative approach requiring involvement of legislators, parliamentary staff, civil society organizations, legal experts, and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"328","3","Enhanced Parliamentary Oversight of Plan Implementation","Parliamentary oversight through Standing Committees will be enhanced in reviewing the Plan and implementation relating to overall policies, strategies, key result areas, while assessing developments both at macroeconomic and sectoral levels and making recommendations for action.",""],[1,"335","10","Strengthening Public Accounts and Parliamentary Standing Committee Oversight","Develop and implementation strengthen the Roles of Public Account and Parliamentary Standing enhance oversight on public ensuring transparency and accountability",""],[1,"337","16","Legislative Decision-Making and Oversight Strengthening Policy","Develop and implement policy for Enhancing role of legislators in the decision-making process and greater oversight at both provincial and national levels.",""],[1,"337","18","Parliamentarian Leadership Skills and Research Support Programme","Enhancing leadership skills of parliamentarians in general and women in particular by providing them research support",""],[1,"337","20","Parliamentary Services Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening of institutions of parliamentary services by providing additional resources for enhancing capacity of parliamentarians",""],[1,"337","25","Electoral and Parliamentary Legal Reform","Electoral/parliamentary reforms in the legal and regulatory framework through consultative approach",""],[1,"338","8","Parliamentary Oversight for Accountability","Establish Parliamentary oversight for accountability",""]],"50":[[1,"321","4","Legal and Judicial System Strengthening","Strengthen rule of law by enhancing effectiveness of legal and judicial system with timely dispensation of justice",""],[1,"323","2","Justice Sector Institutional Reform Programme","To ensure good governance and implement institutional reforms in Justice Sector, efforts will be made by Law and Justice Commission of Pakistan (LJCP) in coordination and supervision of National Judicial Policy Making Committee (NJPMC).","Law and Justice Commission of Pakistan (LJCP) | National Judicial Policy Making Committee (NJPMC)"],[1,"323","2","Court Process and Record Digitization","Digitization of court processes and record will be further strengthened on the recommendation of National Judicial Automation Committee (NJAC).","National Judicial Automation Committee (NJAC)"],[1,"323","2","National Judicial Automation Unit Implementation Mechanism","A National Judicial Automation Unit (NJAU) has already been established for implementation of NJAC recommendations.",""],[1,"323","2","Artificial Intelligence for Legal Processes","Artificial Intelligence (Al) into legal processes will be promoted to leverages technology for improving efficiency and delivery of the justice sector.",""],[1,"323","3","Legal Wing and Central Law Officer Capacity Enhancement","Capacity of Legal Wings and Central Law Officers of the Ministry of Law and Justice and Litigation/Legal Wings of Federal Ministries/Divisions will be enhanced.","Ministry of Law and Justice"],[1,"323","3","Wafaqi Mohtasib Secretariat Online Complaint Hearing Upgrade","Wafaqi Mohtasib Secretariat (WMS) will be strengthened by upgrading its online hearing system of complaints resolution.",""],[1,"323","3","Prisons Reform Recommendations Implementation","Recommendations of National Committee on Prisons Reforms constituted to review the status of prisons in Pakistan will be implemented for improving the overall conditions of prisons.",""],[1,"323","4","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanism","Alternate Dispute Resolution mechanisms, legally sanctioned, will be instituted by engaging community notables at local levels which will reduce burden on judicial system.",""],[1,"334","12","Artificial Intelligence Legal Process Efficiency Initiative","Implementation of Artificial Intelligence legal processes for improving efficiency delivery of the justice sector",""],[1,"334","21","Legally Sanctioned Alternate Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","Establishment of legally sanctioned Alternate Dispute Resolution mechanisms by engaging community notables at local levels to reduce burden on judicial system",""],[1,"334","25","National Plan to Leverage Technology and AI for Judicial Efficiency","Develop and implementation of national plan to leverages technology and Al for improving the efficiency of the judiciary in service delivery.",""],[1,"335","29","Case Management System Digitization","Digitization of case management system including complaint documents and other important records placed in Reference.",""]],"51":[[1,"323","5","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Law Enforcement","Anti-Money Laundering (AML) and Counter-Terrorism Financing (CTF) Laws will be implemented to curb white collar crimes.",""],[1,"327","4","Accountability Institution Capacity Strengthening","During the Plan period, efforts will be made for strengthening accountability institutions such as NAB, the Auditor General Office, FIA, and other federal and provincial entities, including Anti- Corruption Departments by enhancing their capacities through training, career progression, financial incentives and granting administrative autonomy.",""],[1,"327","4","Whistleblowing Policy and Procedure Framework","Accessible whistleblowing policies and customized procedures will be established to curb menace of corruption.",""],[1,"327","4","Comprehensive Accountability Legal Framework","Comprehensive legal framework and paraphernalia of accountability will be developed for each organ of state.",""],[1,"327","5","White-Collar Crime Investigation and Accountability Law Reform","The Plan emphasizes on investigation of white-collar crimes through appropriate amendments in the national accountability laws and multidimensional approach encompassing account scrutiny, IT handling, revenue records scrutiny, cyber forensics and ledger maintenance etc.",""],[1,"327","5","Specialized Training Framework for Investigating Officers and Judges","To promote specialization, a comprehensive training framework aimed at cultivating expertise among investigating officers/ judges in the examination of white-collar crimes and Accountability Courts and Anti-Corruption Courts will be established.",""],[1,"327","5","Autonomy Enhancement for Accountability Institutions","More financial and administrative autonomy will be provided for strengthening of accountability institutions.",""],[1,"327","6","National Anti-Corruption Strategy and Compliance Framework","The plan also underscores importance of a comprehensive national anti-corruption strategy and featuring measures like a compliance management framework and increased prosecution capacity.",""],[1,"327","6","FIA Internal Accountability and Performance Management Reform","During plan period, policy level interventions will include development of internal Accountability Mechanism, defining KPI's of each Functional Units of FIA, linking performance of FIA staff with the final outcome of the cases i.e. Conviction of offenders by competent court of law and training of staff for investigating Money Laundering cases.",""],[1,"328","1","Prosecution Capacity Enhancement for Complex Financial and Cyber Crimes","Capacity of prosecution will be further enhanced to handle complex nature white-collar crimes, banking and internet frauds, cyber offenses, money laundering, and terrorist financing.",""],[1,"328","1","Anti-Corruption and Governance Transparency Initiative","The multifaceted approach will be adopted to combat corruption, improve governance, and create an environment of transparency and accountability",""],[1,"338","6","Anti-Corruption Institutional and Legal Framework Development","Development of proper institutional and frameworks to eliminate corruption",""],[1,"338","10","Capacity Building for Corruption Investigators","Capacity Building of investigators to investigate corruption cases especially White-collar crimes",""],[1,"338","13","Whistleblowing Policy and Procedure Framework","Establish and implement whistleblowing policies and customized procedures to curb menace of corruption",""],[1,"338","15","Establishment of Accountability and Anti-Corruption Courts","Establishment of Accountability Courts and Anti- Corruption Courts with enhanced financial and administrative autonomy",""]],"52":[[1,"321","5","Citizen Participation and Governance Transparency Initiative","Encourage citizen participation by promoting transparency and accountability in governance processes",""],[1,"322","4","Participatory Policy Coordination Framework","The Plan focuses on participatory approach and effective coordination among federating units in designing and implementing of government policies.",""],[1,"322","4","Coordinated Development Project Framework","Encouraging coordinated and synergized projects within development programme across different institutions will promote collaboration and workability among departments.",""],[1,"322","4","Public Information and Communication Strategy","Effective public information communication strategy will be adopted to seek inputs and build ownership of the stakeholders on government policies and initiatives.",""],[1,"322","4","Stakeholder Advisory Committees","Advisory Committees comprising of all stakeholders will be established in each Ministry/ Division/ Department and District/Local Level to advise in design and implementation of development agenda.",""],[1,"325","6","Public Awareness on Parliament Roles Initiative","Effective public awareness on role and responsibilities of the Parliament and Parliamentarians will contribute to further strengthening of democratic",""],[1,"326","2","Parliamentary Public Outreach and Committee Support Programme","Outreach programs for public engagement, support for parliamentary committees, and promotion of transparency and accountability within parliamentary services will also be key components of the proposed plan.",""],[1,"328","1","Public Service Standards and Grievance Redress Mechanism","Departments will define service standards while ensuring timely provision of public services with built-in grievance redressal mechanisms.",""],[1,"328","1","Right to Information Act Review","The Right to Information Act will be reviewed for enhanced access of citizens.",""],[1,"329","2","Public Legal and Regulatory Awareness Campaign","Public awareness of legal and regulatory framework will be enhanced through a media campaign for a better understanding of general public/businessmen on legal and regulatory framework.",""],[1,"334","2","Public Information and Communication Strategy Development","Development and implementation of Effective public information communication strategies to build ownership of the stakeholders on government policies and initiatives.",""],[1,"343","1","13th Five-Year Plan Communication Strategy","The communication strategy for the 13th Five-Year Plan is designed to foster wide-reaching awareness, promote stakeholder engagement, and enable effective dissemination of the Plan's priorities, initiatives, and implementation roadmap.",""],[1,"343","2","Integrated Public Engagement and Communication Strategy","This strategy will engage key audiences including policymakers, experts, academia, civil society, media, youth, development partners, and the general public through an integrated media approach combining traditional, digital, and institutional communication channels.",""],[1,"343","4","Stakeholder Mobilization for Seamless Implementation","Mobilize support from federal and provincial stakeholders for seamless implementation.",""],[1,"343","5","Participatory Planning and Transparency Platforms","Build confidence in the planning process through transparency, dialogue, and participatory platforms.",""],[1,"343","7","National Conference on the Plan","the first step involves organizing a National Conference on the Plan to engage stakeholders effectively.",""],[1,"343","9","Plan Coverage in Print Media","Ensuring coverage of the Plan in Print Media, including all English and Urdu Newspapers.",""],[1,"343","11","Public Awareness and Outreach Publications","Advocating through the publication of monthly newsletters, brochures, booklets, special editions, and promotional material.",""],[1,"343","12","Public Information Dissemination and Interactive Media Outreach","Disseminating information and conducting interactive sessions through TV and Radio, especially FM channels.",""],[1,"343","15","Press Club Outreach and Media Briefing Mechanism","Engaging all Pakistan Press Clubs and Press Club Associations to disseminate the information.",""],[1,"343","16","Media Engagement for Plan Communication","Collaborate with influential journalists and media personalities to feature in-depth interviews and discussions on various aspects of the Plan.",""],[1,"343","17","Comprehensive Media Kit Development","Develop a comprehensive media kit containing key highlights, fact sheets, and visual materials to facilitate media coverage and reporting.",""],[1,"343","18","Government Communications Capacity-Building and Social Media Outreach","Disseminating information through capacity-building programs with social media activists/bloggers, effectively democratizing government communications and influencing public opinion.",""],[1,"344","1","Social Media Campaigns for Plan Objectives","Designing social media campaigns tailored to the major objectives of the Plan, with a particular focus on Health, Education, Poverty Alleviation, SDGs, Climate Change, Energy, PP&H, Water, Nutrition, Trade, and Industrialization, aimed at positively branding Pakistan and engaging both local and international audiences.",""],[1,"344","2","Plan Promotion Through Multimedia Outreach","Promoting the Plan through the use of video clips, video messages, live sessions/streaming, and other multimedia formats.",""],[1,"344","3","Plan Infographics and Social Media Outreach","Create a series of informative and visually appealing infographics highlighting key statistics, achievements, and goals of the Plan.",""],[1,"344","3","Regular Social Media Dissemination of Plan Infographics","Share these infographics regularly on social media platforms to educate and engage the audience.",""],[1,"344","5","Development Project Showcase Video Production","Creating and producing videos to showcase the government's development projects initiated under the Plan.",""],[1,"344","7","User-Generated Content Engagement Campaigns","Encouraging user-generated content by launching contests, challenges, or hashtag campaigns related to the Plan, encouraging public engagement and participation.",""],[1,"344","8","Social Media Monitoring and Rapid Public Response","Monitoring social media channels closely for feedback, questions, and concerns from the public, and respond promptly with accurate information and clarification.",""],[1,"344","9","Social Media Public Engagement Q&A Sessions","Hosting live Q&A sessions (Ask the Minister) on social media platforms where stakeholders can ask questions about the Plan, its objectives, and implementation strategies.",""],[1,"344","10","Virtual Workshops and Webinars on Plan Themes","Organizing virtual workshops and webinars on social media platforms to delve deeper into specific topics or themes covered by the Plan.",""],[1,"344","11","Plan Information Dissemination via Official Ministry Website","Disseminating information about all sections of the Plan through the official website of the Ministry.","Ministry"],[1,"344","12","Stakeholder Information and Engagement Live Streaming","Live streaming related events and highlighting top stories to keep stakeholders informed and engaged.",""],[1,"344","14","Bilingual Press Release Publication","Uploading all relevant press releases in both Urdu and English mediums to reach a wider audience and ensure accessibility.",""],[1,"344","15","Multimedia Resource Library for the Plan","Developing a multimedia resource library containing videos, podcasts, presentations, and other multimedia materials related to the Plan.",""],[1,"344","16","Interactive Events Calendar for Plan-Related Activities","Developing an interactive events calendar highlighting upcoming conferences, workshops, seminars, and other events related to the Plan.",""],[1,"344","17","Accessible Website Design for Persons with Disabilities","Ensuring the website is accessible to all users, including those with disabilities, by incorporating features such as alternative text for images, keyboard navigation, and adjustable font sizes.",""],[1,"344","18","Interactive Data Visualization Platform","Creating interactive data visualizations, such as charts, graphs, and maps, to illustrate key statistics, trends, and progress related to the Plan's objectives.",""]],"53":[[1,"67","16","Capping and Closure of Sick, Slow-Moving, and Provincial Projects","Capping and closing of sick, slow moving and provincial projects",""],[1,"67","17","Project Reprioritization of Core and Foreign-Funded Projects","Reprioritize core and foreign funded projects",""],[1,"67","24","Public Sector Investment Support for Development Programmes and New Initiatives","The enhanced level of the public sector investment will provide required resources to development programmes / projects and new initiatives for achieving objectives of the Plan, which provides country's long-term development agenda to make Pakistan a globally competitive and prosperous country by achieving the status of upper middle-income country.",""],[1,"69","1","Alignment of the Federal Investment Portfolio with the National Plan","the guidelines and priorities would be set to align the existing portfolio with national Plan",""],[1,"69","1","Completion of Core Strategic Ongoing Projects","focusing on core strategic ongoing projects of national significance for timely completion, particularly mega projects of energy, water resources, transport and communication and other important social and governance sector projects",""],[1,"69","3","Federal Development Program for Ongoing and Mega Infrastructure Projects","The main thrust of the programme is on completion of ongoing projects and initiation of mega projects in the infrastructure sector with proposed share of 63 percent of the program, being the primary responsibility of the federal government.",""],[1,"70","5","Federal Policy on Financing Provincial-Nature Schemes","Thus, it was decided by the National Economic Council (NEC) that the Sponsoring/ Executing Agencies should follow NEC approved policy 2021 regarding compelling provincial nature schemes and should bear at least 50 percent capital cost of such projects except in case of strategic nature important projects.",""],[1,"70","5","Closure and Transfer Modalities for Provincial Projects in Federal PSDP","The NEC also approved modalities for closure/ transfer of provincial nature projects in federal PSDP 2023-24 and barring inclusion of provincial development projects in Federal PSDP",""],[1,"71","2","Prioritization of Development Funds for Core Ongoing Projects","Priority should be accorded to allocation of development funds to strategic and core on-going projects, with particular focus on water resources, transport, railways, communications, and energy sectors.",""],[1,"71","3","Priority Completion of High-Expenditure Projects","Priority should be accorded to projects with 80 percent plus expenditure in all sectors with the aim of completing them during FY25.",""],[1,"71","6","Allocation of Development Budget to New Priority Projects","Only 10 percent of development budget FY25 should be considered for allocation to new projects, with particular focus on supporting exports, enhancing productivity, fostering competitiveness, deepening and spreading digital infrastructure, innovation driven enterprises, industrial development, agroindustry and seed development, blue economy, science & technology, R&D and innovation reforms.",""],[1,"71","7","Priority Allocation Rule for DDWP-Approved PSDP Projects","While making allocations for PSDP projects, DDWP approved projects will only be allocated resources after full needed allocations have been made as per serial no (iii) above.",""],[1,"71","8","Moratorium on Approval and Budgeting of O&M and Recurring Expenditure Projects","There will be a moratorium on approval / budgeting of projects involving O&M and recurring nature expenditures.",""],[1,"71","9","Foreign Aid Estimate and Projection Preparation","Economic Affairs Division (EAD) will provide firmed up foreign aid estimates to be disbursed during FY25, with further two years' projection in consultation with all stakeholders.","Economic Affairs Division (EAD)"],[1,"71","10","Priority Funding for Foreign-Funded Projects","Ministries / Divisions should prioritize and allocate adequate rupee cover to the foreign funded projects within the IBC for smooth execution of foreign funded projects and uninterrupted inflow of foreign exchange and to honor international obligations.","Ministries / Divisions"],[1,"71","11","Selective Financing of Provincial Nature Projects","Provincial nature projects shall not be considered for approval / financing except those in 20 least developed districts, as determined by Planning Commission, and the Newly Merged Districts (NMDs).",""],[1,"71","12","Project Director Placement and Project Monitoring System","Principal Accounting Officers should ensure placement of full-time Project Directors as per applicable guidelines and put in place qualitative / quantitative monitoring indicators to avoid time and cost overruns.",""],[1,"71","14","Adoption of PIMA and C-PIMA Recommendations for PSDP","Recently, Public Investment Management Assessment (PIMA) and Climate Change (C-PIMA) reports by International Monetary Fund (IMF) has been adopted by the Government.",""],[1,"71","16","Capital Expenditure In-Year Adjustment Review","Review the scope to reduce the within year adjustment of capital expenditure",""],[1,"71","17","Project Selection Criteria for PSDP Funding","Develop & publish criteria for selecting projects to receive the funding in PSDP",""],[1,"71","18","PSDP Transparency and Documentation Initiative","Improving transparency by presenting documentation on key aspects of the PSDP.",""],[1,"322","3","Public Expenditure Monitoring, Evaluation and Risk Management System","Monitoring, evaluation and risk management systems will be established for effective utilization of public expenditure.",""],[1,"328","2","National Development Framework and Project Appraisal Workshop","To streamline development processes, National Development framework and project appraisal workshop will be introduced to improve project design, implementation framework, monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"328","2","Alignment-Based PSDP and ADP Financing Rule","Only those Projects will be financed from PSDP and ADP that are aligned with National Development Framework/Plan/ policy targets.",""],[1,"328","2","Development Process Simplification and Project Management Reform","ECNEC approved recommendations on simplification development processes/procedures to improve project management will be implemented to further streamline the development process.",""],[1,"328","3","PPP Financing for Infrastructure and Social Sector Projects","Collaboration through PPP mode of funding in infrastructure and social sector projects will be promoted.",""],[1,"328","3","Strengthening of Public Private Partnership Authorities","Public Private Partnership Authorities will be strengthened and rules on PPP will be revisited at the federal level for enhancing ease of doing business.",""],[1,"328","3","Development Projects Manual Update","Manual for Development Projects has been developed which will be further updated as per emerging requirement of development sector.",""],[1,"328","3","Annual NEC Performance Reporting","The NEC annual performance report will be published.",""],[1,"328","4","Project Design Quality Improvement","Quality of development projects at design stage will be focused through need assessment, feasibility studies, incorporating lesson learnt and best practices followed.",""],[1,"328","4","Project Monitoring, Evaluation, and Risk Management Strengthening","Mechanism for project monitoring, evaluation and risk management will be further strengthened for effective utilization of public investment.",""],[1,"328","4","Mandatory Monitoring and Evaluation Framework for Programme and Project Documents","Monitoring and Evaluation framework will be included as an essential part of programme/project document, like technical and economic part with highlights of impact, output, project activities, inputs, assumptions and risk identification/management with indicators (baseline targets) for comprehensiveness and enhancing objectivity and development effectiveness.",""],[1,"328","4","Legal Backing for Policy Making and Implementation","Efforts will be made to strengthen the policy making and its implementation process with legal backing.",""],[1,"328","5","Technology-Led Project Automation and Monitoring Systems","The Plan prioritizes technology-led transparent development through Intelligent Project Automation System (IPAS), Project Monitoring and Evaluation System (PMES)and PSDP Portal to provide cost effective access to information facilitating informed decision making.",""],[1,"328","5","Project Preparation and Design Facilitation Services","Facilitation will be provided at preparation and design stage of development projects by Planning Commission at the federal level, and Planning and Development Departments at the provincial level including on-line services.",""],[1,"328","5","Merit-Based Performance Contracting for Project Staff","Incentive based appointment of project director and project staff on merit through competitive process and a performance-based contract will be followed.",""],[1,"328","5","Strategic Alignment of PSDP Investments","The PSDP investment will be aligned with Plan targets and strategically aligned projects will be approved and included in PSDP.",""]],"54":[[1,"319","3","Pakistan Raises Revenue Initiative","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""],[1,"324","3","Tax Base Broadening and Tax Administration Reform","Measures for creation of central database of potential taxpayers by obtaining data from NADRA, Telco's, Banking Cos, educational institution and development authorities will be initiated.",""],[1,"324","3","Tax Exemption Removal and Rules Simplification","Tax base will be broadened through removal of discretionary exemptions and concessions and simplification of rules and procedures.",""],[1,"324","3","Tax Administration Transparency and Automation Reform","Transparency in tax administration will be ensured by strengthening Integrity Management Unit, end to end automation, provision of high-quality tax facilitation services while strengthening FBR, provincial tax departments and revenue authorities.",""],[1,"324","4","Tax Administration Digitalization and Compliance Reform","To enhance tax collection efficiency and reduce compliance costs, focus will be on leveraging technology including SWAPS (Synchronized Withholding Tax Administration & Payment System), third-party data integration, and artificial intelligence.",""],[1,"324","4","Track and Trace System Implementation","Initiatives include implementation of systems like Track and Trace in certain sectors; strengthening of Point-of-Sale Integration in the retail sector and introduction of Digital Invoicing to digitize less-documented sectors of the supply chain.",""],[1,"324","4","Point-of-Sale Integration and Digital Invoicing Expansion","Initiatives include implementation of systems like Track and Trace in certain sectors; strengthening of Point-of-Sale Integration in the retail sector and introduction of Digital Invoicing to digitize less-documented sectors of the supply chain.",""],[1,"324","4","Regional Tax Office Restructuring and Digitization","Restructuring of field formations with a focus on broadening of the tax base and digitization at Regional Tax Offices (RTOs) will also be made.",""],[1,"324","4","Provincial Tax Coordination and Data Sharing Reform","Effective collaboration with provincial tax departments/authorities will be focused for harmonizing tax reforms, tax laws and procedures, integrating taxpayer processes, and sharing data to improve revenue while reducing compliance costs.",""],[1,"324","5","Federal Tax Ombudsman Institutional Strengthening and Digital Case Management","Federal Tax Ombudsman (FTO) will be strengthened by providing physical infrastructure, IT systems, and human resources for effective functioning.",""],[1,"335","20","Federal Board of Revenue Revamping and Tax Base Broadening","Revamping of Federal Board of Revenue (FBR) to achieve sustainable increase in revenues, broadening of tax base facilitating trade",""],[1,"335","22","Central Taxpayer Database Establishment","Establishment of central database of potential taxpayers by obtaining data from NADRA, Telcos, Banking Cos, educational institution and Development Authorities",""],[1,"335","24","Tax Collection Automation and Digitization Reform","To enhance tax collection efficiency and reduce compliance costs of all tax collection institutions, through automation/ digitization including SWAP, third party integration and Artificial Intelligence will be introduced",""],[1,"335","26","Tax Base Broadening and Tax Administration Reform","Broadening Tax base through removal of discretionary exemptions and concessions, simplification of rules and procedures by strengthening Integrity Management Unit, end to end automation, provision of high-quality tax facilitation services",""]],"55":[[1,"12","5","Performance-Based Dashboards for Government Performance Management","Performance-Based Dashboards: Shifting from traditional reporting to real-time, data-driven performance management across all tiers of government .",""]],"56":[[1,"12","7","Diaspora Investment and Engagement Incentive Scheme","We will create incentives for our overseas Pakistanis to invest, bring know-how, and serve as our ambassadors to the world.",""],[1,"52","1","Diaspora Investment Mobilization","Furthermore, missions will also mobilize the Pakistani Diaspora to undertake productive investment in Pakistan.",""]],"57":[[1,"22","2","Monetary Policy and Financial Sector Reform Roadmap","The Plan aims to support price and financial system stability, and economic growth through reforms roadmap envisaged by State Bank of Pakistan (SBP).",""],[1,"53","3","Monetary and Exchange Rate Management Policy Development","The SBP will develop monetary and exchange rate management policies prioritizing external sector stability, the accumulation of foreign exchange reserves, and maintaining export competitiveness by considering the REER.",""],[1,"53","3","Exchange Rate Regime Alignment with Macroeconomic Fundamentals","Thus, the exchange rate regime will be aligned with macroeconomic fundamentals.",""],[1,"53","3","Measures to Curb Speculative and Illegal Tendencies","Nevertheless, the necessary measures to curb the speculative/illegal tendencies will be further strengthened.",""],[1,"57","1","Monetary Policy Coordination for Price Stability and Credit Access","The monetary policy will remain synchronized with the fiscal policy to maintain price stability, strengthen the financial system, and ensure sufficient credit access for productive sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"61","12","Public Debt Management Initiatives","The public debt management will include various initiatives including expanding the investor base, ensuring a well-functioning domestic debt capital market, extending the maturity profile of domestic and external debt portfolio, mobilizing maximum available concessional external financing, and ensuring presence in the International Capital Markets (ICM) through issuance of various bonds.",""],[1,"61","13","Monetary Policy Effectiveness and Price Stability Strategy","The SBP's Strategic Plan FY2024-28 aims at making monetary policy more effective to achieve price stability in the presence of evolving risks and challenges to the economy and financial stability, including volatile global economic environment / geopolitical tensions, rising risks associated with climate change and rapid digital innovations.",""],[1,"61","13","Insurance Sector Development and Opportunity Exploration","The potential in the insurance sector will be explored by channelizing the opportunities available in the sector.",""],[1,"61","13","Financial Transparency and FATF Compliance Measures","Measures will be taken to ensure transparency of transactions and the compliance of the requirements of Financial Action Task Force (FATF) to improve the investment climate.",""],[1,"62","2","Inflation Expectation Management and Price Stability Policy","Manage inflationary expectations and ensure price stability;",""],[1,"62","3","Prudent Monetary Policy for Price and Financial Stability","Pursue an effective and prudent monetary policy aimed at achieving price stability, financial stability and economic growth;",""],[1,"62","4","Financial Sector Efficiency, Stability, and Inclusion Reform","Improve efficiency and stability of financial sector and achieve maximum financial inclusion;",""],[1,"62","5","Savings and Investment Promotion for Financial Inclusion","Promote a culture of savings and investment in the general public for broader financial inclusion in the society;",""],[1,"62","6","Financial Sector Transparency and Anti-Speculation Measures","Ensure transparency, curb speculation and rent seeking in financial sector;",""],[1,"62","7","Payment System Improvement","Improve the payment system.",""],[1,"62","9","Monetary Policy Rate and Regulatory Adjustment","Timely intervention through policy rate and regulatory adjustments to strike a balance between price and financial stability;",""],[1,"62","10","National Financial Stability Council Establishment","Enhancing the role of financial regulators for developing financial sector on the lines of best international practices especially through the establishment of National Financial Stability Council (NFSC);",""],[1,"62","11","Financial Sector Competition and Efficiency Enhancement","Strengthening competition and efficiency of financial sector through product innovations and entry of new banks;",""],[1,"62","12","Banking System Promotion for Financial Services Access","Promoting banking system to meet the needs of the public for financial services with the aim to stimulate economic growth and financial stability;",""],[1,"62","13","Risk-Based Supervisory Framework for SBP","Strengthening and streamlining SBP's supervisory framework through implementation of risk-based approach;",""],[1,"62","14","DSIB Resolution and Recovery Planning Mechanism","Developing and implementing mechanism for effective resolution and recovery planning for Domestic Systemically Important Banks (DSIBs).",""],[1,"64","9","National Financial Stability Council Establishment","Establishment of National Financial Stability Council (NFSC)",""],[1,"64","11","Risk-Based Supervisory Framework Streamlining","Strengthening :selected: streamlining SBP's supervisory framework through implementation of risk-based approach",""],[1,"64","12","DSIB Resolution and Recovery Planning Mechanism","Developing implementing mechanism for oping and effective resolution and recovery planning for fective resoluti Domestic Systemically Important Banks (DSIBs)",""]],"58":[[1,"22","4","Federal Public Sector Development Programme Funding for Core National Projects","The focus of the federal PSDP (i.e. Rs. 6040 billion) would be funding of core national projects including foreign funded development investments particularly in infrastructure sector as per assigned functions under 18th Amendment with estimated share of 63 percent of total PSDP.",""],[1,"22","4","Priority Infrastructure Investment in Transport, Energy, Water, and Housing","Within infrastructure priority will be given to Transport & Communications (T&C), followed by energy sector, water resources and Physical Planning & Housing (PP&H) Sectors.",""],[1,"22","4","Provincial Social Sector, Poverty Reduction, and Governance Investment Programmes","On the other hand, Provincial Programmes have been set with major investment in the core social sectors, poverty elevation and governance related projects.",""],[1,"41","4","Public Investment for Strategic Infrastructure and Social Sector Projects","Public investment is projected at 3.7 percent of GDP in the terminal year, underlining the government's continued role in driving strategic infrastructure and social sector projects.",""],[1,"66","4","Resilient Recovery, Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Framework","The 4RF is the Government of Pakistan's strategic policy and prioritization document which will guide the recovery, rehabilitation and reconstruction of the country.",""],[1,"66","5","Public-Private Partnership Financing for Development Projects","In order to ease out burden on PSDP, efforts would be made to promote innovative mode of financing of development projects such as public private partnership to make development process more inclusive and effective.",""],[1,"66","6","Alternative Economic Governance and Liberalization Approach","An alternative approach such as shift towards devolution of authority and responsibility, greater community participation, privatization, decontrol, deregulation and liberalization may be adopted instead of conventional approach i.e. largely depend on public sector investment.",""],[1,"66","7","Public Sector Investment to Enable Private Sector Crowding-In","the government through public sector investment will provide an enabling environment for crowding in the private sector and fostering public-private partnerships and joint ventures.",""],[1,"66","7","Institutional Strengthening for Public-Private Partnerships and Joint Ventures","Such partnership or cooperation requires strengthening of institutions within or outside",""]],"59":[[1,"23","5","PRSS-02 Remote Sensing Satellite Launch","The PRSS-02 remote sensing satellite will be launched to enhance agricultural monitoring and disaster response.",""]],"60":[[1,"7","2","Environmental Protection and Climate Action Measures","Environmental protection and climate action will safeguard our future, while energy and infrastructure development will ensure sustainable and affordable access for all.",""],[1,"11","9","Climate-Resilient Development Mainstreaming","the Plan integrates climate action into all development policies.",""],[1,"11","9","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Development","We will focus on ... building infrastructure that can withstand environmental shocks.",""],[1,"24","5","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Construction","The plan focuses on constructing climate-resilient infrastructure, restoring lives and livelihoods, ensuring social inclusion and equitable access to economic opportunities, and engaging local communities in adopting technological solutions to manage risks, enhance disaster preparedness and response in a resilient and sustainable manner.",""],[1,"27","2","Pro-Poor and Climate-Resilient Investment Programme","increasing pro-poor and climate-resilient investments;",""]],"61":[[1,"26","2","Ecologically Based Participatory Urban and Regional Planning System","The Plan aims to establish an ecologically-based participatory urban and regional planning system to create sustainable urban environments and equitable development opportunities.",""],[1,"26","2","New Urban Planning Laws","It proposes several strategic interventions, such as enacting new urban planning laws, establishing model districts for sustainable development, and addressing housing shortages through innovative solutions.",""],[1,"26","2","Model Districts for Sustainable Development","It proposes several strategic interventions, such as enacting new urban planning laws, establishing model districts for sustainable development, and addressing housing shortages through innovative solutions.",""],[1,"26","2","Innovative Housing Shortage Solutions","It proposes several strategic interventions, such as enacting new urban planning laws, establishing model districts for sustainable development, and addressing housing shortages through innovative solutions.",""],[1,"26","2","Participatory Urban Governance Structures","It also focuses on improving urban governance through participatory structures, enhancing water and sanitation management, and promoting sustainable urban forms.",""],[1,"26","2","Urban Water and Sanitation Management Improvement","It also focuses on improving urban governance through participatory structures, enhancing water and sanitation management, and promoting sustainable urban forms.",""],[1,"26","2","Promotion of Sustainable Urban Forms","It also focuses on improving urban governance through participatory structures, enhancing water and sanitation management, and promoting sustainable urban forms.",""]],"62":[[1,"29","6","Digitalization of PTVC and PBC Terrestrial Transmission Networks","The Plan aims at digitalization of the terrestrial network of Pakistan Television Corporation (PTVC) and analogue transmission/broadcasting network of Pakistan Broadcasting Corporation (PBC).",""],[1,"29","7","National Image Promotion Campaign","Soft image of the country will be propagated.",""],[1,"29","7","Media Laws and Regulations Review","The media related acts, rules and regulations will be reviewed.",""],[1,"29","7","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Promotion Programme","Appropriate policies will be adopted and projects/programs will be carried out to preserve, conserve and promote the rich and diverse cultural heritage of Pakistan.",""],[1,"52","1","Pakistan Global Image Promotion Initiative","Moreover, endeavours to improve Pakistan's image globally will be further strengthened.",""]],"63":[[1,"30","1","Basic Sports Infrastructure Development","The Plan focuses on sports based-policy interventions/ initiatives that will help to revive the sports culture in the country through nationwide development of basic sports infrastructure, launching of talent identification and development program, establishment of Sports Endowment Fund, construction of institute of sports and promotion of good governance in national sports bodies/organizations.",""],[1,"30","1","Talent Identification and Development Programme","The Plan focuses on sports based-policy interventions/ initiatives that will help to revive the sports culture in the country through nationwide development of basic sports infrastructure, launching of talent identification and development program, establishment of Sports Endowment Fund, construction of institute of sports and promotion of good governance in national sports bodies/organizations.",""],[1,"30","1","Sports Endowment Fund","The Plan focuses on sports based-policy interventions/ initiatives that will help to revive the sports culture in the country through nationwide development of basic sports infrastructure, launching of talent identification and development program, establishment of Sports Endowment Fund, construction of institute of sports and promotion of good governance in national sports bodies/organizations.",""],[1,"30","1","Institute of Sports Construction","The Plan focuses on sports based-policy interventions/ initiatives that will help to revive the sports culture in the country through nationwide development of basic sports infrastructure, launching of talent identification and development program, establishment of Sports Endowment Fund, construction of institute of sports and promotion of good governance in national sports bodies/organizations.",""],[1,"30","1","Good Governance in National Sports Bodies","The Plan focuses on sports based-policy interventions/ initiatives that will help to revive the sports culture in the country through nationwide development of basic sports infrastructure, launching of talent identification and development program, establishment of Sports Endowment Fund, construction of institute of sports and promotion of good governance in national sports bodies/organizations.",""]],"64":[[1,"30","2","Private-Sector-Led Tourism Sector Development","The Plan focuses on growth in the tourism sector led by private sector, with the public sector playing an enabling and facilitating role.",""],[1,"40","5","Liberal Visa Regime for Tourism Promotion","A liberal visa regime is being introduced to significantly increase the number of foreign tourists, attracting visitors for recreational, adventure, business, government, and religious purposes.",""]],"65":[[1,"49","3","FASTER Refund System Expansion","To provide a favorable and liquid business environment, all refunds will be brought under the FASTER system.",""],[1,"49","5","Standards Compliance and Dispute Resolution Roadmap","Compliance of standards which include convergence of local and international certifications, protection of intellectual property rights, and efficient and effective dispute resolution mechanism, will be ensured.","Ministry of Commerce & Textile | Federal Board of Revenue | Ministry of Industries and Production"],[1,"49","9","Food Standards Implementation","Food standards will be implemented to meet international market requirements.",""],[1,"50","8","Pakistan Single Window Trade Facilitation Platform","The most significant is the establishment of Pakistan Single Window (PSW), which is an Integrated Digital Platform that allows parties involved in trade to lodge standardized information and documents.",""],[1,"51","2","Exporter Compliance Support for SPS and TBT Standards","the necessary policy measures would be strengthened so that the Pakistani exporters could meet the requirements of SPS (Sanitary and Phytosanitary) standards and (TBT) Technical Barriers to Trade.",""],[1,"54","25","Electronic Data Interchange System and Trade Facilitation under PSW Initiative","Establishment of electronic data interchange systems and strengthening trade facilitation under PSW initiative.",""]],"66":[[1,"49","6","Trade Agreement Concessions Review and Renegotiation","Concessions granted under Trade Agreements will be appraised in terms of their impact on bilateral trade and, thereafter, reviewed/renegotiated accordingly.",""],[1,"49","7","Negotiation of New Trade Arrangements for Value-Added Exports","New trading arrangements would be negotiated/made with utmost care to protect local industry and focus on market access for value added goods and not merely commodities.",""],[1,"51","4","Regional Integration for Trade Promotion","The Plan has greater focus on regional integration to promote trade and contribute to socio-economic development of the country.",""],[1,"51","4","GCC Free Trade Agreement Negotiation Completion","After signing of the investment-related part of the FTA with the Gulf Cooperation Council, it is expected that the negotiations on the remaining areas of FTA will be concluded in the near future.",""],[1,"51","4","Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Accession Consideration","Pakistan will also be looking at other options such as joining the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP), which is the world's largest free trade bloc, comprising 10 ASEAN countries along with China, Japan, Australia, New Zealand, and South Korea.",""],[1,"52","1","Coordinated Trade and Investment Framework","A coordinated framework is being developed to address trade and investment matters while considering supply-side issues and market analysis.",""],[1,"52","1","Trade and Investment Officer Targeting under SIFC","Also, the government under SIFC is assigning specific targets to the trade and investment officers (TIOs) to promote FDI projects, expansion and diversification of exports and enhance their role for better trade diplomacy.",""],[1,"54","17","Regional Trade Committee","Setting up of \"Regional Trade Committee\" to promote trade with regional countries.",""]],"67":[[1,"39","7","SBP Export Facilitation Scheme Expansion","Under export facilitation schemes, the expansion of the SBP",""],[1,"51","3","EXIM Bank Export Financing Facility","EXIM bank has recently been operationalized to facilitate exporters and boost exports.",""],[1,"54","15","Export Financing Enhancement through EXIM Bank","Enhancing the export financing through EXIM Bank",""]],"68":[[1,"50","6","Clean Energy Transition for Export Competitiveness","To keep exports competitive, compliance with CBAM and for similar schemes, requires an immediate towards clean energy.",""],[1,"50","7","CBAM Compliance Support for Export Industries","Government will make efforts to facilitate export industry to comply CBAM regulations to mitigate the adverse effects of climate change and environmental degradation.",""],[1,"55","5","Export Industry CBAM Compliance Support","Facilitation of export industry to comply with CBAM requirements/ regulations",""]],"69":[[1,"37","1","Domestic Stabilization Program","supported by a domestically designed stabilization program that adopts a human centred approach.",""],[1,"37","1","Interest Rate Adjustment to Encourage Investment","interest rates are gradually adjusting to encourage investment",""],[1,"37","1","Business Cost Reduction Initiatives","initiatives to lower the cost of doing business are gaining momentum.",""],[1,"37","2","Structural Reform and Inclusive Growth Support Measures","By focusing on macroeconomic stability, policy consistency, and fostering a more competitive business environment, the Plan aims to create the conditions necessary for broad-based, resilient, and inclusive economic growth, ultimately laying the groundwork for higher job creation and poverty reduction.",""]],"70":[[1,"40","5","Domestic Commerce Policy","The first-ever draft Domestic Commerce Policy addresses a wide range of key areas, including enterprise productivity and modernization, SME and firm development, retail and wholesale sector growth, local brand promotion, transportation, storage and warehousing, and skill development.",""],[1,"61","1","Services Sector Development and Property Tax Compliance Reform","services sectors and improve property tax regimes in terms of policy and compliance;",""]],"71":[[1,"52","5","Formal Remittance Promotion Measures","In order to promote remittances through formal channels from the overseas Pakistanis, the government has announced various measures like \"Sohni Dharti\".",""],[1,"52","5","Cross-Border Payment System Cooperation Agreement","Moreover, recently, the Arab Monetary Fund (AMF) and State Bank of Pakistan has signed an MoU to establish cooperation between Buna, a cross-border payment system owned by AMF and Raast, Pakistan's Instant Payment System.","State Bank of Pakistan"],[1,"55","9","Formal Remittance Inflow Incentive Mechanism","Incentivizing formal inflow of remittances by reducing cost and implementation of MOU signed between Arab Monetary Fund (AMF) and State Bank of Pakistan.","State Bank of Pakistan"]],"72":[[1,"68","6","Priority Physical Infrastructure Investment Programme","Physical infrastructure will be accorded the highest priority with planned investment of Rs. 8,511 billion claiming a share of 39 percent in the planned outlay over next five years period.",""],[1,"68","6","Transport and Communication Sector Priority Investment","Within infrastructure sectors, top priority will be assigned to the Transport and Communication Sector with 22 percent share",""],[1,"69","3","Transport and Communications Investment Allocation","Within the infrastructure sector, about 33 percent will be invested in the transport and communications sector",""],[1,"69","3","Transport and Communications Connectivity Enhancement","T&C sector would get higher share in terms of resources during plan period mainly to ensure better connectivity and economic integration on modern lines.",""]],"73":[[1,"72","5","Provincial Social Sector Investment Allocation","The provincial governments will invest 56 percent of their allocations in the social sector related programmes and projects, which include education, health, population welfare, rural development, culture, sports, tourism, youth, clean drinking water, drainage and farm to market roads etc.",""],[1,"72","5","Provincial Health and Education Budget Shares","Within the social sector, health sector and education including higher education will receive 9 percent share each.",""],[1,"72","5","Local and District Poverty Alleviation and Social Protection Funding","Local and district governments, poverty alleviation and social protection programmes will receive 31 percent of the total resources which may focus on provision of civic amenities by the Provincial and District Governments.",""]],"74":[[1,"72","7","Federal Development Financing for Special Areas","an amount of Rs. 716 billion has been proposed for these areas during Plan period.",""],[1,"72","7","Regional Annual Development Programme Formulation","the Area Governments will formulate their annual development programmes by incorporating regional and sectoral priorities.",""],[1,"72","7","Alignment of AJ&K and GB Development Programmes with National Plans","The AJ&K and GB governments should align the development programmes as per national plans envisaged as URAAN Pakistan.",""],[1,"72","8","Development Programmes for Merged Districts of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa","federal government is funding the development programmes even after merger of ex-FATA with KP after 25th Constitutional Amendment.",""],[1,"73","1","Annual Development Programme Funding for Merged Districts of KP","The federal Government also continued funding for the annual ADP for the merged districts of KP besides several other individual projects by various Ministries through PSDP.",""],[1,"73","1","PSDP Financing for Ex-FATA Accelerated Implementation Programme","substantial funds under PSDP released for 10 years AIP plan.",""]],"75":[[1,"83","3","Public-Private Collaboration for SDG Implementation","The public and private sectors must work in close collaboration to accomplish the SDGs, rather than depending solely on public sector efforts.",""],[1,"83","3","Business Environment Support for SDG Delivery","Potential areas where the public sector can guarantee favourable business eco-systems and the private sector can take the lead are innovation capability, people resources, technical information, and inputs.",""],[1,"90","7","Inter-Ministerial Committee for Private Sector Engagement","Inter-Ministerial Committee Led by MoPD&SI for · Private Sector Engagement to lead projects through PPP","MoPD&SI"]],"76":[[1,"87","5","Mineral Sector Investment Attraction Initiative","SIFC, focuses on attracting investment in the mineral sector.",""],[1,"87","5","Reko Diq Project Reconstitution","The reconstitution of the Reko Diq Project has bolstered investor confidence.",""],[1,"87","5","Mineral Sector Investment Negotiations","Ongoing negotiations with friendly countries are expected to result in new investments",""],[1,"87","6","Mineral Sector Fiscal Incentives and Public-Private Joint Ventures","Priorities include providing fiscal incentives, fostering public-private joint ventures, developing geo-parks, and enhancing collaboration with other countries for technology and capital inflow.",""],[1,"87","6","Geo-Park Development Initiative","Priorities include providing fiscal incentives, fostering public-private joint ventures, developing geo-parks, and enhancing collaboration with other countries for technology and capital inflow.",""],[1,"87","6","Mineral Sector Professional Training and International Collaboration","The Plan emphasizes efficient use of geological resources, aligning mineral policies with institutional mechanisms, and training professionals.",""],[1,"87","7","Mineral Resource Transparency and Investment Promotion","Pakistan's mineral resources will be using international standards like JORC and NI 43-101 to enhance transparency and attract global investment.",""],[1,"87","7","Mineral Contract Management and Auditing System","The Mineral Contract Management (MCM) and Mineral Auditing System (MAS) will safeguard national interests and encourage investment.",""],[1,"87","7","Mineral Sector Joint Ventures for Technology Transfer","Joint ventures with global partners will prioritize technology transfer and local capacity building to strengthen mineral sector.",""],[1,"88","2","Mineral Marketing Promotion and Value-Addition Initiative","Mineral marketing will be advanced through standardized statistics, promotion via seminars, conferences, exhibitions, and newsletters, identifying large-scale mining commodities, forming joint ventures with regional partners for value addition, and engaging third-party marketing expertise when needed.",""],[1,"88","3","Green Mining Strategy","A green mining strategy will improve resource efficiency, protect the environment, and enhance enterprise-community relationships.",""],[1,"94","1","Minerals Marketing and Standardized Mineral Statistics Reporting","Minerals Marketing . Standardized Reporting of Mineral Statistics .",""],[1,"94","1","Mineral Value-Addition and Import Substitution R&D","R&D for Value-addition & Substitution of Imported Minerals .",""],[1,"94","1","Promotion of Mineral Sector Potential","Promotion of Mineral Sector Potential",""]],"77":[[1,"100","2","International Payment Gateway Development","Need for International Payment Gateway to support digital, fintech, and eCommerce innovation.",""],[1,"103","1","End-to-End Automation of National Savings and Post Office Networks","End-to-end automation of National Savings and Post Office networks will further facilitate financial inclusion.",""],[1,"103","4","Digital Government Payments and Financial Inclusion Expansion","Meaningful financial inclusion for at least 50 million people by next 5 years including, but not limited to, the transfer of all government-linked transactions and cash-transfers through digital means",""],[1,"103","8","Fintech Financial Inclusion and Digital Payments Expansion","Several domestic initiatives are underway to boost electronic transactions, supported by policy reforms, legal enhancements to build trust, and upgrades to the digital infrastructure necessary for widespread adoption.",""],[1,"104","1","E-Commerce Enabling Environment and Global Payment Systems","To increase the potential of e-commerce within the country, globally accepted payment systems like PayPal will be provided.",""],[1,"104","8","Freelancers Framework for Digital and Physical Bank Account Opening","Freelancers Framework: The freelancers will now be able to open the bank accounts both digitally and physically at their choice with minimum documentation requirements.",""],[1,"104","8","Concurrent Opening of Exporters' Foreign Currency Accounts","Further, their ESFCAs shall be opened concurrently with the opening of their primary PKR account.",""],[1,"104","8","Freelancers' Export Proceeds Retention and Payment Flexibility","The freelancers can retain 50 percent of their export proceeds or USD 5,000/- per month, whichever is higher, in their ESFCAs and can make all payments from these accounts without any approval from SBP or banks.",""]],"78":[[1,"86","4","Global Skills Development and Infrastructure Upgrade","This needs a paradigm shift towards encouragement of foreign investment, joint ventures, skill development according to global needs, improving infrastructure, simplifying trade procedures, fostering innovation & technology adoption in tandem with R&D, improve policy & regulatory environment, political stability, promote regional integration and trade unions.",""],[1,"100","5","ICT Skills Development and Reskilling for Software Exports","Expand and improve human resources through skill-development and re-skilling of young professionals for software exports and the 4th Industrial Revolution, focusing on industry certifications like CMMI and ISO.",""],[1,"101","4","IT Human Resource Expansion Initiative","IT Human Resource Expansion: Expand quality IT HR availability leveraging Pakistan's 300,000+ English-speaking IT professionals, 13 software technology parks, and 75,000+ annual IT graduates.",""],[1,"101","4","IT Skills Expansion in Secondary Cities","Focus on 2nd and 3rd tier cities including Hyderabad, Faisalabad, Multan, Bahawalpur, Peshawar, and Quetta through expanded high-quality programs and innovative new initiatives.",""],[1,"101","5","21st Century Global Skills Initiative","21st Century Global Skills Initiative: Train 100,000 youth over 5 years in 4IR areas including Artificial Intelligence, Blockchain, Big Data, Cyber Security, e-commerce, Cloud Computing, and Enterprise Automation.",""],[1,"101","6","Freelancing and Digital Work Expansion Program","Freelancing and Digital Work Programs: Expand specialist training for freelancing targeting government's 10 million job creation goal through ICT.",""],[1,"102","2","Mobile Technology and Fintech Job Creation Initiative","Mobile technologies and fintech could generate 250,000 jobs annually during Plan period.",""],[1,"104","9","Youth Freelancing Employment Initiative","positioning freelancing as a powerful tool for youth employment",""],[1,"105","8","IT Industry Employment Training Programme","Training of selected nationals of Pakistan (IT and Non-IT) on specific platforms for employment in the IT industry.",""],[1,"105","9","Industry Tutors Specialized Training Programme","Industry Tutors Specialized Training (Train the Trainers): Master trainers will be produced in the field of Artificial Intelligence, Blockchain, ERP & CRM, Cloud computing, Cybersecurity, Digital twin, E-learning, E-agriculture, and AR, VR & MR.",""],[1,"114","3","Human Resource Development Initiatives","An allocation of Rs. 42 billion was provided HRD initiatives.",""],[1,"116","6","Computer Science and IT Graduate Expansion","Producing quality manpower in cutting edge technologies especially grow the number of Computer Science and IT graduates to 200k per year",""]],"79":[[1,"104","9","IT and Digital Services Export Promotion Strategy","the outlined targets aim to promote IT and digital service exports",""],[1,"107","16","GDPR-Driven ISO Compliance and IT Export Enhancement","GDPR Driven ISO Compliance and IT Export Enhancement",""],[1,"108","12","Technology Export Marketing Program","Technology Export Marketing Program",""],[1,"109","11","IT Export Expansion and Skilled Workforce Development","Increase IT exports to USD 10 - 15 billion.",""]],"80":[[1,"100","7","Data Protection, Privacy, and Cybersecurity Policy Regime","Advance telecommunications liberalization while ensuring data protection, privacy, and cybersecurity through an enlightened policy regime that attracts investment and creates level playing fields for both large operators and startups.",""],[1,"100","9","National Data Protection Policy Development","The Plan aims to develop national data protection policy governing national data centre and cloud services at competitive prices.",""],[1,"100","9","Cybersecurity Agency Establishment","Establish cybersecurity agency is collaborating with Ministry of Interior and strategic organizations.","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"106","2","Enhanced Encrypted Cybersecurity Systems","Secure systems and networks while preventing data leakages through enhanced encrypted security features.",""],[1,"106","2","Cybersecurity Investment Expansion","Increased cybersecurity investments will build trust for corporate, retail, industrial, and other national systems.",""],[1,"106","2","National Computer Emergency Response Team Support","In line with the cybersecurity policy and establishment of National Computer Emergency Response Team NCERT is providing support in;",""],[1,"106","3","Cybersecurity Awareness, R&D, and Digital Protection Policies","Promoting cybersecurity awareness, drive research and development initiatives, and implementing robust policies to safeguard Pakistan's digital landscape.",""],[1,"106","4","National and Provincial Cybersecurity Framework","Design cybersecurity framework at national and provincial levels.",""],[1,"106","4","Malware Blocking Through DNS Filtering","Work with ISPs and telecom operators to block malware attacks through DNS blocking/filtering of known malware domains.",""],[1,"106","4","Active Cyber Defense Strategy","Develop active defense strategies with stakeholder engagement.",""],[1,"106","5","Email Phishing and Spoofing Prevention on Public Networks","Prevent email phishing and spoofing activity on public networks.",""],[1,"106","6","Internet Governance Security Practices Promotion","Promote best security practices through Internet governance organizations including ICANN, APNIC, IETF, RIPE, and UN Internet Governance Forum.",""],[1,"106","7","International Cybercrime Law Enforcement Cooperation","Collaborate with international law enforcement channels to protect Pakistani citizens from cyber-attacks originating from unprotected overseas infrastructure.",""],[1,"106","8","Secure Digital Ecosystem Framework","To build a secure digital ecosystem, this section aligns with Uraan's objective of enabling resilient and trusted infrastructures.",""],[1,"107","8","Cyber Security for Digital Pakistan Phase-I","Cyber Security for Digital Pakistan (Phase-I)",""],[1,"110","2","National and Provincial Cybersecurity Framework","Designing of a Cyber security framework at national and provincial tiers",""],[1,"110","2","ISP and Telecom Malware Blocking Measures","Working with Internet Service Providers (ISPs) and Telecom operators to block malware attacks, by restricting access to specific domains or websites that are known sources of malware (known as Domain Name System (DNS) blocking / filtering, etc.).",""],[1,"110","2","Active Cyber Defense Strategy Development","Active defense strategies will be formulated with the engagement of respective stakeholders.",""],[1,"110","2","Public Network Phishing and Spoofing Prevention","Preventing email phishing and spoofing activity on public networks.",""],[1,"110","4","International Cybersecurity Cooperation and Internet Governance Engagement","Promoting security best practice through Internet governance organizations; such as Internet Corporation for Assigned Names and Numbers (ICANN), Asia Pacific Network Information Center (APNIC), the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF), European Regional Internet Registry (RIPE), and UN Internet Governance Forum (IGF), etc.",""],[1,"110","4","International Law Enforcement Cooperation Against Cyber-Attacks","Work with international law enforcement channels to protect Pakistan citizens from cyber-attacks from unprotected infrastructure overseas",""],[1,"117","1","Cyber Security Capacity Enhancement and International Collaboration","Enhance cyber security capabilities with greater international collaboration",""]],"81":[[1,"103","7","AI Integration in Manufacturing, Health, and Public Services","Emphasis will be placed on integrating Al into smarter manufacturing, augmenting healthcare, and enabling data-driven governance to extend affordable public services.",""],[1,"103","7","Expansion of the HEC AI Centre of Excellence","The HEC's Al Centre of Excellence will be expanded, with plans to develop industry partnerships for Al applications.",""],[1,"106","9","National Artificial Intelligence Policy","National Al Policy, transforming Pakistan into a knowledge-based economy by creating an enabling environment for responsible Al use, stimulates growth, identifies development areas, and address evolving job markets through the National Artificial Intelligence Fund (NAIF).",""],[1,"106","10","AI Solutions Development, Testing, and Scaling","Develop, test, and scale Al solutions while refining governance and impact management.",""],[1,"106","12","AI Public and Workforce Awareness and Competency Development","Raise public and workforce Al understanding, ensuring professionals possess competencies for the Al economy.",""],[1,"106","13","AI Adoption Awareness and Targeted Training for Industry","Guide industries toward effective Al adoption through awareness campaigns and targeted training via national IT boards.",""],[1,"106","14","Innovation and Workforce Preparation Framework","This framework supports Uraan Pakistan's cutting-edge innovation goals and workforce preparation for emerging technologies.",""],[1,"107","15","National Artificial Intelligence Advancement Initiative","National Artificial Intelligence Advancement Initiative",""],[1,"110","6","AI Research and Innovation Centers","Establishment of research & innovation centers in Al for developing, test-bedding, deploying, and scaling Al solutions.",""],[1,"110","6","Responsible AI Governance and Trusted Use Framework","Responsible use of Al to generate economic gains and improve lives.",""],[1,"110","6","AI Awareness and Workforce Readiness Initiative","Pakistan shall increase awareness and understanding of Al technologies and their benefits; our workforce will be equipped with the necessary competencies to participate in the Al economy.",""],[1,"110","6","Sectoral AI Transformation Support","Transformation & Transformation of sectors and industries towards effective use of Al, facilitated by national IT boards through",""],[1,"116","11","Artificial Intelligence Framework and Local AI Capacity Development","Develop Artificial Intelligence (AI) Framework and local capacity for developing Al solutions",""]],"82":[[1,"120","3","Academic, Research and Innovation Strategies","Academic, Research and Innovation Strategies must be formulated by universities to improve quality of research, its outcomes, and formulation of policies to incentivize internationalization, quality teaching, research and innovation.",""],[1,"120","3","Graduate Education Programmes in Basic Sciences","There is also need for prioritizing the creation of high- quality graduate education programs in basic sciences, supported by foreign PhDs, through large- scale teacher training programs.",""],[1,"120","3","Curriculum and Pedagogy Reform for Teaching Quality","Improvement of teaching quality also requires improving educational standards by revamping of curriculum, books, mode of teaching, pedagogy, assessment styles and use of technology.",""],[1,"120","3","Faculty Recruitment, Retention, and Pedagogical Training","In addition, teaching quality needs to be ensured by hiring and retention of high-quality faculty, providing pedagogical trainings.",""],[1,"120","3","Annual Award for Pedagogical Innovation","There is a need for instituting an annual award for pedagogical innovation in higher education to create a culture of improved pedagogies.",""],[1,"121","1","National Computer Literacy and Programming Initiative","Launching a national initiative to build computer literacy and culture, making computer programming a critical part of the school curriculum.",""],[1,"122","4","Short Courses and Programs in Emerging Technologies","there is a need to introduce short university courses and programs in the critical areas of emerging technologies like Al, Cyber Security, Big Data, Data Sciences, Block Chain, Analytics, Machine Learning, Gaming, Graphics, Digital Marketing, Freelancing, Fin-Tech, Agri- Tech, Food Technologies, Health sciences etc.","Ministry of Science & Technology"],[1,"125","11","Affiliated Colleges Capacity and Curriculum Upgrade Programme","HEC to undertake a comprehensive upgrade of capacity, curriculum, faculty, and pedagogy in 4000+ affiliated colleges through the use of modern technology to bring them at par with universities","HEC"],[1,"125","14","Technology-Enabled Teaching and Research Mechanism","Develop mechanism to ensure use of technology for teaching / research, digital resources for quality of education and recognizing performers in faculty by annual awards",""],[1,"126","5","Student Laptop Distribution Programme","Around 300,000 laptops to be distributed students during plan period to enhance educational material and online education employment opportunities.",""],[1,"126","7","Higher Education Network Connectivity and Eduroam Expansion","Almost all HEIs will be connected to PERN offered campus-wide Eduroam.",""]],"83":[[1,"121","5","New Model University Ordinance","A new Model University Ordinance needs to be created through a wide consultation of key stakeholders to enable HEC to effectively play its enforcement role while ensuring academic and institutional autonomy of the University.",""],[1,"121","5","Higher Education Management Information System and Identity Management","Governance at HEIs needs to be strengthened by introducing a Higher Education Management Information System (HEMIS) and identity management for better management and transparency.",""],[1,"121","5","Merit-Based Vice Chancellor Selection Reform","Similarly, there is urgent need for implementing an unbiased selection process for Vice Chancellors based on merit and providing them with adequate authority to implement their vision.",""],[1,"121","6","Evidence-Based Higher Education Policy Pilots","This means creating a limited pilot to be rigorously evaluated before further scaling up of the same.",""],[1,"121","6","Higher Education Regulatory and Policy Coordination by HEC","The Federal Higher Education Commission shall carry out its constitutionally mandated responsibility of a regulator, promote national policy, and address gaps, where necessary, but will also work with provincial HEDs to build capacity and coordinate policy, where possible.","The Federal Higher Education Commission | provincial HEDs"],[1,"121","6","Private Provision Expansion in Higher Education","HEC needs to encourage Private Provision as an Important Part of the Higher Education System.","HEC"],[1,"121","6","Needs-Driven Public Policy Regime for Higher Education","HEC must embrace a needs-driven and evidence-based public policy regime as it builds upon past successes to further expand provision of higher education.","HEC"],[1,"121","6","Higher Education Governance and Leadership Reform","To continue the reforms in Governance and Leadership within Higher Education Sector to attract Visionary leaders to create research and innovation driven universities.",""],[1,"126","17","Higher Education Governance and Funding Dialogue","High level dialogue among HEC, Provincial HECs, HEDs and other stakeholders on issues like: Development / recurring funding of HEIs and governance mandates of the federation and provinces",""],[1,"126","19","Model University Ordinance Development","HEC to develop a new Model University Ordinance through a wide consultation of key stakeholders to enable HEC to effectively play its enforcement role while ensuring academic and institutional autonomy of the University",""],[1,"126","21","Higher Education Information System (HEMIS) for Universities","ensure Higher Education Information System (HEMIS) universities and ensuring unbiased process for VC and other important HEIS",""]],"84":[[1,"120","3","University Grant Linkage to Quality Standards","Another important way forward would be linking institutional investments to quality standards issued by HEC (e.g. linking portion of university grants to the quality of graduates).",""],[1,"121","1","University Ranking Reform Linked to Research Output","HEC may devise and improve current rankings systems of universities on the basis of research output targets and link grants to this ranking.","HEC"],[1,"121","1","University Reporting Awareness for Global Rankings","Steps must also be taken to arrange awareness to universities about reporting to global ranking agencies so that more and more universities can acquire global rankings.",""],[1,"124","12","University Tier System Reform","Implementing Tier System for Universities: · Strengthen and fund 10 to 15 Tier-1 Research Universities based on their performance, global ranking and research productivity / employability.",""],[1,"124","12","Technical University Track for Skills Development","The Tier-2 universities may be technical universities for Skill Development.",""],[1,"125","9","University Data Submission for Global Rankings","HEC to encourage universities to submit the data and statistics to global ranking institutions like QS and Times.",""],[1,"125","10","National University Ranking System Revamp and Restart","HEC to revamp and restart national ranking of universities by FY 2026-27 as per global standards",""]],"85":[[1,"122","3","Higher Education Scholarship Program Consolidation","Based on this evaluation, HEC should focus on consolidation of all Scholarships programs into two programs i.e. one each for indigenous and foreign scholarships.","HEC"],[1,"122","3","Tenure Track and Returning PhD Talent Retention Strategy","Enhancing the hiring and retention of high-quality PhDs, through the expansion and better management of the Tenure Track System (TTS) and effective utilization of returning PhDs from abroad must be the parallel strategy to be adopted by HEC and MOST for acquisition of requisite trained manpower in key disciplines.","HEC | MOST"],[1,"122","3","Industrial PhD Collaboration Programme","HEC must start industrial PhD programs in collaboration with local industries to resolve local issues of industries through research.","HEC"],[1,"122","3","Internationalization Scholarships for Developing Country and LMIC Students","HEC also needs to introduce internationalization programs, particularly scholarships for students from developing economies and LMIC, for improvement in the students mix and diversity.","HEC"],[1,"127","8","Scholarship Scheme Consolidation for PhD Human Resource Development","Re-evaluate foreign / indigenous scholarships schemes for consolidation of HRD initiatives into one program each for local and foreign PhDs along with its transfer to recurring or endowment funding",""]],"86":[[1,"122","2","Research Commercialization and Industrial Income Strategy","S&T organizations (and other similar entities) must be encouraged to generate at least 30percent of their recurring expenses through research commercialization and industrial income.",""],[1,"122","2","Revenue-Sharing Incentive Scheme for S&T and Higher Education Staff","The sector needs to ensure incentives that these revenues may be shared as discretionary spending, bonuses and reward with senior leadership and staff to further encourage commercial income.",""],[1,"122","2","Research and Innovation Commercialization Frameworks","They also need to come up with research and innovation commercialization frameworks to generate income through technology transfer, licensing, and commercialization of indigenous technologies",""],[1,"123","1","Evaluation and Expansion of University ORICs","However, the output of these units needs immediate evaluation, subsequent reorientation of mandate and further expanding of ORICs to deliver the goods.",""],[1,"123","1","University-Based Science and Technology Research Parks","There is need for creation of university-based Science & Technological Research (STR) Parks in HEIs and industrial zones.",""],[1,"123","1","Innovation Support Mechanisms for Commercialization","Effective use of innovation mechanisms such as incubators, accelerators, challenges, grand prizes, and specially designed organizational frameworks and a host of other mechanisms must be adopted to advance innovation across the public-academic-private divide.",""],[1,"123","1","Startup Incentives and R&D Tax Credits","Policies and incentive mechanisms (like R&D tax credits etc.), to incentivize and facilitate start-ups, particularly science and technology-based start-ups are required to transition and spin-off intellectual property out of the public S&T and HEC lab systems for the collective benefit of the public and effective utilization of public money.",""],[1,"123","2","Standards, Accreditation, and IPR Framework for Technology Commercialization","Ministry of Science & Technology also needs to continue playing its role for setting of standards, accreditation, policies and legal framework for patenting, IPRs and technology transfer and commercialization of technologies.","Ministry of Science & Technology"],[1,"123","2","HEI-Based Spin-Off Establishment","There is also need for establishment of HEI-based spinoffs etc. to be implemented in universities through HEC and S&T.",""],[1,"123","2","Pakistan Start-up Fund","It is necessary to start Pak Start-up Fund (PSF) with a Board of Governors having industrial representation and develop a National Innovation Framework to support policy/ frameworks for improving innovation ecosystem outcomes.",""],[1,"123","2","National Innovation Framework","It is necessary to start Pak Start-up Fund (PSF) with a Board of Governors having industrial representation and develop a National Innovation Framework to support policy/ frameworks for improving innovation ecosystem outcomes.",""],[1,"123","2","Venture Capital Funds for Innovation Investment","In addition, there must be Venture Capital Funds (VCEs) for investments in innovation.",""],[1,"123","2","Technology Transfer Office Network in HEIs and S&T","HEC and MOST must collaborate and establish network of Technology Transfer Offices in HEIs and S&T for technology transfer to industries.",""],[1,"123","2","Defence-Civil R&D Partnership for Spin-On and Spin-Off","In addition, it is required to establish a partnership of defence sector with civil (public / private) sector R&D organizations / industry for spin-on and spin-offs of science and technology.",""],[1,"127","14","Expansion of ORIC Offices in Higher Education Institutions","Strengthening of existing 88 ORICs and 38 establishing these offices in rest of all HEIs five years.",""]],"87":[[1,"131","5","Climate-Resilient Development Mainstreaming","This will entail embedding climate resilience and environmental sustainability into macroeconomic planning, infrastructure design, and public investment frameworks, while strengthening institutional capacities and fostering climate finance mobilization.",""],[1,"134","5","Climate Mitigation Mainstreaming in Public Planning and Budgeting","Key priorities will include the development of a national carbon market framework, operationalization of Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) systems, and integration of climate mitigation indicators across public sector planning and budgeting.",""],[1,"136","8","Climate-Aligned Infrastructure and Resilience Project Pipeline Development","Collaborate with the P3A and relevant stakeholders to identify, design, and maintain a pipeline of climate-aligned infrastructure and resilience projects, with clear guidance on integrating climate finance instruments and carbon credit monetization pathways at the project preparation stage.",""],[1,"139","6","Climate-Tagged Public Investment Framework Integration","Integrate GHG mitigation targets and climate tagging into national and provincial public investment frameworks, enabling alignment of development spending with Pakistan's Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs).",""],[1,"139","14","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Development","Build climate-resilient infrastructure, develop climate-resilient agriculture and food systems, and accelerate policy coherence for UN Sustainable Development Goals.",""],[1,"139","14","SDG Policy Coherence Acceleration","Build climate-resilient infrastructure, develop climate-resilient agriculture and food systems, and accelerate policy coherence for UN Sustainable Development Goals.",""],[1,"140","10","Mandatory Climate Risk Screening for Development Projects","Operationalize climate risk screening for all PSDP projects in accordance with the Planning Commission's approved Handbook, making it a mandatory step from PC-I to PC-V stages for both federal and provincial development portfolios.",""],[1,"140","11","Climate Risk Screening Automation in iPAS","Automate the climate risk screening process by embedding the Handbook's tools and templates into the Integrated Project Appraisal System (iPAS) to enable digital submission, real-time assessment, climate tagging, and transparent reporting of climate-responsive investments.",""],[1,"140","12","Climate-Related Expenditure Tracking in iPAS","Estimate and track climate-related expenditures (mitigation, adaptation, and co- benefits) through standardized modules within iPAS, aligned with the UNFCCC's Enhanced Transparency Framework (ETF) and Pakistan's NDCs.",""],[1,"140","13","Climate and Gender Proofing of PC-I Project Appraisal","Mainstream climate and gender proofing into PC-I formats via iPAS, ensuring systematic inclusion of risk classification, resilience options, and social inclusion safeguards in project design and appraisal.",""],[1,"140","14","Climate Risk Tool Capacity-Building for Planning and Execution Agencies","Strengthen institutional capacities of line ministries, planning departments, and executing agencies to apply climate risk tools within iPAS through dedicated training, guidelines, and Help Desk support.",""],[1,"142","2","Climate-Responsive Public Investment Management Reform Roadmap","The C-PIMA process, supported by international partners including the IMF, will guide the formulation of a robust reform roadmap and capacity development framework.",""],[1,"142","2","Climate Risk Screening Integration in Infrastructure Planning and Budgeting","It identifies institutional gaps in climate-responsive Public Investment Management (PIM) and recommends actionable reforms to integrate climate risk screening into infrastructure planning and budgeting.",""],[1,"142","3","Sustainable Finance Project Preparation Facility","The plan emphasises upon collaboration with relevant stakeholders for advancing the establishment of a Sustainable Finance Project Preparation Facility (SF-PPF) as a strategic initiative.",""],[1,"143","2","Climate-Aligned Infrastructure Project Pipeline","In collaboration with the P3A and development partners, a pipeline of climate-aligned infrastructure projects will be maintained, integrating carbon credit monetization and climate finance instruments at the project design stage.",""],[1,"144","5","Mandatory Climate Risk Screening for PSDP Projects","Climate risk screening will be mandatory for all Public Sector Development Programme (PSDP) projects and embedded from PC-I to PC-V stages through the iPAS.",""],[1,"144","5","Digitization of Climate Risk Screening Tools","Tools from the Handbook on Climate Risk Screening of PSDP Projects will be digitized to facilitate climate tagging, risk classification, and real-time reporting.",""],[1,"144","5","Climate Expenditure Tracking and Transparency Reporting","Climate-related expenditures will be tracked in line with the Enhanced Transparency Framework (ETF) of the UNFCCC and Pakistan's NDCs.",""],[1,"144","5","Integration of Environmental and Social Management System into iPAS","The Environmental and Social Management System (ESMS) will also be integrated into iPAS to meet environmental safeguards required by international financiers.",""],[1,"144","5","Climate Screening Capacity Building and Helpdesk Support","Capacity-building programmes and a dedicated helpdesk will assist ministries and provincial departments in effective implementation.","ministries and provincial departments"]],"88":[[1,"132","3","Climate and Carbon Finance for Development Projects","The Plan aims to optimize the financing of development projects by switching towards climate and carbon finance.",""],[1,"137","2","National Climate Finance Strategy","Formulate and implement a National Climate Finance Strategy and a complementary Disaster Risk Financing Strategy, aligning public investment frameworks with international financing opportunities (e.g., GCF, GEF, Adaptation Fund).",""],[1,"137","2","Disaster Risk Financing Strategy","Formulate and implement a National Climate Finance Strategy and a complementary Disaster Risk Financing Strategy, aligning public investment frameworks with international financing opportunities (e.g., GCF, GEF, Adaptation Fund).",""],[1,"137","3","National Climate Finance Facilitation Platform","Establish a National Climate Finance Facilitation Platform to assist federal ministries, provincial departments, and the private sector in the preparation of green projects, accessing concessional and results-based financing, and mobilizing voluntary and compliance carbon markets.",""],[1,"137","4","International Climate Negotiation and Climate Finance Engagement","Strengthen Pakistan's engagement in international climate negotiations and global financial platforms, ensuring access to technical assistance, concessional finance, and market mechanisms, while contributing to global knowledge exchange.",""],[1,"137","5","Climate Finance Coordination and Project Bankability Initiative","Enhance coordination with multilateral development banks, climate funds, and global knowledge-sharing networks to tap into non-traditional and innovative climate financing sources and improve project bankability.",""],[1,"137","7","Climate Finance MRV and Compliance System","Establish a robust Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) and compliance system to track climate finance flows and ensure timely reporting on Pakistan's international commitments, including NDCs, Biennial Transparency Reports (BTRs), and global stock take contributions under the UNFCCC.",""],[1,"141","18","Green Sukuk Financing for Sustainable Infrastructure","the Government will promote the issuance of Green Sukuk-Shariah-compliant financial instruments dedicated to funding climate-resilient and low- carbon infrastructure.",""],[1,"141","19","Panda Bond Financing for Climate-Smart Infrastructure","Pakistan will explore the issuance of Panda Bonds-Renminbi-denominated instruments in Chinese capital markets-to finance climate-smart infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"143","2","Green Finance Scale-Up Mechanism","Mechanisms such as green bonds, climate insurance, and blended finance will be scaled to attract concessional and commercial capital.",""],[1,"143","2","National Climate and Disaster Risk Financing Strategies","The NCFS and a complementary Disaster Risk Financing Strategy (DRFS) will be implemented to align public investment frameworks with international opportunities like the GCF, GEF, and Adaptation Fund (AF).",""],[1,"143","2","Climate Finance Facilitation Platform","A dedicated Climate Finance Facilitation Platform (CFFP) will provide technical support to ministries, provinces, and private stakeholders.",""],[1,"143","2","Climate Finance MRV System","A robust Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) system will be established for tracking finance flows and ensuring compliance with Pakistan's international commitments, including NDCs, Biennial Transparency Reports (BTRs), and Global Stocktake (GST) under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC).",""],[1,"147","4","Pakistan Green Fund","The Plan aims to create Pakistan Green Fund, sovereign green bonds, and climate risk insurance schemes.",""],[1,"147","4","Sovereign Green Bonds","The Plan aims to create Pakistan Green Fund, sovereign green bonds, and climate risk insurance schemes.",""],[1,"147","4","Climate Risk Insurance Schemes","The Plan aims to create Pakistan Green Fund, sovereign green bonds, and climate risk insurance schemes.",""],[1,"147","4","National Green Investment Taxonomy","The strategy will also promote the development of a national taxonomy for green investments in line with international climate finance standards to facilitate alignment with global investors and multilateral funds.",""],[1,"147","4","Green Growth Capacity Building and Mainstreaming Programme","Capacity building for both public and private sector actors, along with integration of nature-based solutions, circular economy principles, and job-rich green industrial practices, will be prioritized.",""],[1,"148","7","Pakistan Green Fund","Establish Pakistan Green Fund, Sovereign Green Bonds, Panda Bonds",""],[1,"148","7","Sovereign Green Bonds","Establish Pakistan Green Fund, Sovereign Green Bonds, Panda Bonds",""],[1,"148","7","Panda Bonds","Establish Pakistan Green Fund, Sovereign Green Bonds, Panda Bonds",""],[1,"148","10","Green and Panda Bond Issuance","Issue first green/panda bonds",""],[1,"148","11","Private Finance Mobilization and Instrument Expansion","Expand instruments, mobilize private finance",""],[1,"148","15","Climate Risk Insurance Schemes","Develop Climate Risk Insurance Schemes; Establish Carbon Trading System",""],[1,"148","16","Insurance and Carbon Market Framework Development","Design insurance and carbon market framework",""]],"89":[[1,"133","1","National Climate and Disaster Data Repository","this Plan will prioritize the establishment of a National Climate and Disaster Data Repository (NCDDR) as a unified platform for standardized data collection, storage, and dissemination.",""],[1,"133","2","Capacity-Building for Data Governance and Climate Analytics","Capacity-building programs for federal and provincial stakeholders will be scaled up, focusing on data lifecycle management, geospatial analytics, and climate modelling tools.",""],[1,"133","2","Digital Infrastructure for Real-Time Data Systems","Technical assistance and digital infrastructure investments will be mobilized to support real-time data acquisition, integration, and visualization.",""],[1,"133","2","Enhanced Data Governance for Climate Reporting","Enhanced data governance will not only improve risk-informed planning and policy coherence but also strengthen Pakistan's ability to access climate finance and fulfil international reporting obligations under the UNFCCC and SDGs.",""],[1,"137","8","Centralized Climate and Disaster Data Repository","Establish a comprehensive, centralized data repository for climate change and disaster-related information in Pakistan, ensuring seamless access and integration for all stakeholders.",""],[1,"137","9","Interagency Data Sharing Protocols and Mechanisms","Develop protocols and mechanisms for efficient data sharing between government agencies, research institutions, and relevant stakeholders, facilitating collaborative analysis and action.",""],[1,"137","10","Standardized Climate and Disaster Data Quality Control System","Implement standardized methodologies, formats, and rigorous quality control measures to ensure consistency, accuracy, and comparability of climate and disaster-related data.",""],[1,"137","11","Data Governance Framework Strengthening for Climate Resilience","Strengthen existing data governance frameworks and create policies promoting effective data management, secure sharing, and collaborative use for climate resilience planning and action.",""],[1,"137","12","Stakeholder Data Management and Evidence-Based Decision-Making Capacity Building","Provide stakeholders with comprehensive training and technical assistance on data management, analysis, visualization tools, and evidence-based decision-making.",""],[1,"137","13","Sector- and Region-Specific Climate Vulnerability and Risk Assessments","Conduct sector- and region-specific climate vulnerability and risk assessments, including hazard exposure, sensitivity, and adaptive capacity analyses, to inform climate-resilient development planning, infrastructure design, and investment prioritization.",""],[1,"143","3","Centralized Climate and Disaster Data Repository","A centralized Climate and Disaster Data Repository (CDDR) will be established to enable real-time access to climate-related information by government agencies, research institutions, and development partners.",""],[1,"143","3","Climate Data Interoperability and Quality Assurance System","Data sharing protocols, common methodologies, and rigorous quality assurance (QA) systems will be developed for interoperability and reliability.",""],[1,"143","3","Technical Training for Climate Data Analysis","Technical training in data visualization, geospatial tools, and evidence-based analysis will be provided to stakeholders to enhance planning and monitoring capacities.",""],[1,"143","5","Comprehensive Climate Vulnerability and Risk Assessments","Comprehensive Climate Vulnerability and Risk Assessments (CVRAs) will be conducted at regional and sectoral levels to inform the design of climate-resilient infrastructure, investment prioritization, and urban planning.",""],[1,"145","4","Provincial Climate Performance Index","Provincial Climate Performance Index (PCPI) will be introduced to foster competitive federalism by ranking provinces on indicators such as green investments, forest cover growth, EIA compliance, GHG emissions reduction, and climate resilience outcomes.",""]],"90":[[1,"134","3","Ecosystem-Based Wildlife Conservation Programme","The Plan prioritizes ecosystem-based wildlife conservation through habitat restoration, expansion of protected areas, and development of species recovery plans for threatened and endangered species.",""],[1,"134","3","Wildlife Enforcement and Anti-Poaching Mechanism","Strengthening enforcement mechanisms to combat poaching and illegal trade will be central, alongside the digitization of wildlife databases and enhanced coordination through the National Council for Conservation of Wildlife (NCCW).",""],[1,"134","3","Community-Based Wildlife Conservation and Benefit-Sharing Scheme","Community-based conservation models will be promoted to reduce human-wildlife conflict and incentivize protection through ecotourism and benefit-sharing schemes.",""],[1,"134","3","Provincial Wildlife Authority Capacity-Building Initiative","Capacity-building initiatives for provincial wildlife authorities, and collaboration with organizations like WWF, IUCN, and UNDP, will play a key role in advancing evidence-based conservation and strengthening Pakistan's wildlife governance framework.",""],[1,"138","10","Biodiversity Safeguarding Initiatives in Priority Ecological Zones and Critical Habitats","Implement biodiversity safeguarding initiatives in priority ecological zones and critical habitats.",""],[1,"138","14","Critical Habitat and Wildlife Corridor Conservation Programme","Conserve and restore critical habitats, protected areas, and wildlife corridors to ensure the long-term survival of threatened and endemic species, particularly in ecologically sensitive zones such as northern mountain ecosystems, wetlands, deserts, and coastal areas.",""],[1,"138","15","Wildlife Protection Legal and Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen the legal, institutional, and enforcement mechanisms for wildlife protection, including updates to the Wildlife Acts, capacity building of provincial wildlife departments, and improved monitoring of poaching and illegal trade.",""],[1,"138","16","Expansion and Management of Protected Areas","Expand and effectively manage terrestrial and marine protected areas (PAs) to meet national targets under Agenda 2030 and the Post-2020 Global Biodiversity Framework, through the establishment of National and Provincial Protected Area Services.",""],[1,"140","2","National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan Implementation","Implementation of National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan (NBSAP) developed by Ministry of Climate Change and Environmental Coordination and IUCN.","Ministry of Climate Change and Environmental Coordination"],[1,"140","4","National and Provincial Protected Areas Service","For effective planning, coordination, management and financing of Protected Areas, establish National and Provincial Protected Areas Service.",""],[1,"140","5","Terrestrial and Marine Protected Areas Strengthening","Designate and strengthen Terrestrial and Marine Protected Areas to achieve the targets of Agenda 2030.",""],[1,"142","4","Protected and Conserved Areas Management Strengthening","The Plan also prioritizes the strengthening of management practices in protected and conserved areas, with a focus on certifying additional sites under the IUCN Green List of Protected and Conserved Areas, to ensure global standards of conservation effectiveness and governance.",""],[1,"144","1","Biodiversity Safeguarding Programmes in Ecologically Sensitive Zones","the development of biodiversity safeguarding programmes in ecologically sensitive zones (ESZs)",""],[1,"144","1","National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan Implementation","The National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan (NBSAP) will be implemented in coordination with the Ministry of Climate Change and Environmental Coordination (MoCC&EC) and International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN)","Ministry of Climate Change and Environmental Coordination (MoCC&EC) | International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN)"],[1,"147","6","Critical Habitat Protection and Restoration Programme","national efforts for wildlife and biodiversity conservation will be significantly strengthened through the protection and restoration of critical habitats, including mountain ecosystems, wetlands, deserts, and coastal zones, to safeguard endangered and endemic species.",""],[1,"147","6","Protected Areas Expansion and Management System","A network of terrestrial and marine protected areas (PAS) will be expanded and managed in accordance with international benchmarks under Agenda 2030 and the Post-2020 Global Biodiversity Framework, supported by the establishment of National and Provincial Protected Area Services.",""],[1,"147","6","Wildlife Legal and Institutional Strengthening Reform","Legal and institutional frameworks will be enhanced through the revision and enforcement of Wildlife Acts, capacity building of provincial wildlife departments, and deployment of surveillance",""],[1,"148","1","Illegal Wildlife Trade Combat Systems","systems to combat illegal wildlife trade.",""],[1,"148","40","Protected Areas Expansion and Management","Expand & manage Protected Areas (PA); Community- based Conservation",""],[1,"148","42","National and Provincial PAS Establishment","Establish National/ Provincial PAS",""],[1,"148","43","Protected Area Management Strengthening and Ecotourism Pilots","Strengthen PA management, ecotourism pilots",""]],"91":[[1,"134","5","National Carbon Market Framework Development","Key priorities will include the development of a national carbon market framework, operationalization of Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) systems, and integration of climate mitigation indicators across public sector planning and budgeting.",""],[1,"134","5","MRV System Operationalization","Key priorities will include the development of a national carbon market framework, operationalization of Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) systems, and integration of climate mitigation indicators across public sector planning and budgeting.",""],[1,"136","10","National Carbon Emission Trading Policy Development and Operationalization","Support the development and operationalization of a national Carbon Emission Trading Policy, including market-based mechanisms for carbon pricing, offset",""],[1,"137","6","Carbon Credit Generation and Climate Revenue Mobilization","Facilitate carbon credit generation through climate-resilient infrastructure, land- use, renewable energy, and reforestation projects, while exploring additional revenue streams (e.g., biodiversity credits, ecosystem services markets) to support national climate targets.",""],[1,"139","3","National GHG Emissions Inventory and MRV System","Operationalize a national GHG emissions inventory and Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) system to ensure transparency, accuracy, and compliance with international reporting obligations under the UNFCCC.",""],[1,"139","4","Carbon Market and Offset Mechanisms","Implement market-based mechanisms such as a Carbon Emission Trading System, carbon credit certification, and offset programmes aligned with Article 6 of the Paris Agreement, to unlock domestic and international carbon finance.",""],[1,"148","2","Carbon Emission Trading System and Carbon Credit Mechanisms","Pakistan will advance the design of a Carbon Emission Trading System, along with mechanisms for carbon credit certification, offsets, and access to voluntary and compliance markets.",""],[1,"148","15","Carbon Trading System","Develop Climate Risk Insurance Schemes; Establish Carbon Trading System",""],[1,"148","18","Carbon Compliance Market TES","Launch carbon compliance market TES",""],[1,"148","21","National GHG Inventory and MRV System Operationalization","Operationalize National GHG Inventory and MRV System",""],[1,"148","22","MRV System Design Finalization","Finalize MRV system design",""]],"92":[[1,"135","2","National Clean Air Framework","The Plan intends to implement a comprehensive National Clean Air Framework focusing on multi- sectoral interventions to reduce emissions from transport, industry, energy, and agriculture.",""],[1,"135","2","National Air Quality Monitoring Network","Urban air quality will be monitored through the establishment of a national air quality monitoring network integrated with real-time public information platforms.",""],[1,"135","2","Urban Greening and Brick Kiln Regulation Measures","Greening of urban spaces through plantation drives, regulation of brick kilns through zigzag technology, and restrictions on crop burning will be enforced through strengthened provincial EPAs.",""],[1,"135","2","Transboundary Air Pollution Coordination and Awareness Campaigns","Cross-border coordination with regional partners and public awareness campaigns will also be launched to address transboundary air pollution and promote behavioural change.",""],[1,"145","6","National Clean Air Programme","It is also planned that a National Clean Air Programme (NCAP) will be rolled out to improve air quality in urban and industrial centres through regulatory enforcement and technological upgrades.",""],[1,"146","1","National Ambient Air Quality Monitoring Network","a national network of ambient air quality monitoring stations will be established to provide real-time data on key pollutants.",""],[1,"146","1","Digital Air Quality Index Dashboard","These systems will be integrated into a digital air quality index dashboard to guide policy responses and public health advisories.",""],[1,"146","2","Regional Smog Prevention Strategy","it is planned that a Regional Smog Prevention Strategy will be implemented in coordination with provincial governments and neighbouring countries",""],[1,"146","2","Zero-Tillage and Mechanized Residue Management Promotion","This strategy will include the promotion of zero-tillage practices and mechanized residue management to prevent stubble burning",""],[1,"146","2","Cleaner Zigzag Brick Kiln Conversion","along with the conversion of conventional brick kilns to cleaner zigzag technology",""],[1,"146","2","Satellite and Drone Emissions Monitoring System","The use of satellite imagery and drone surveillance will be institutionalized for real-time monitoring of emissions and enforcement of pollution controls",""],[1,"146","2","Smog-Buffer Urban Plantation Programme","Smog-buffer urban plantations will also be established around major cities to serve as natural filtration zones and improve overall urban air quality",""],[1,"147","3","National Ambient Air Quality Monitoring Network","It is further planned that a National Ambient Air Quality Monitoring Network will be established to address deteriorating air quality in urban and industrial areas.","Pakistan Environmental Protection Agency (Pak-EPA) | provincial EPAs"],[1,"149","8","Urban Monitoring Station Installation","Install monitoring stations in cities",""],[1,"149","9","Air Quality Standards Enforcement","Enforce air quality standards",""]],"93":[[1,"135","4","Integrated Solid Waste Management Programme","The Plan aims to adopt an integrated approach to solid waste management (SWM), focusing on the waste hierarchy of reduce, reuse, recycle (3Rs) and the promotion of circular economy principles.",""],[1,"135","4","Waste Segregation and Municipal Collection Expansion","Key interventions will include waste segregation at source, expansion of municipal collection capacity, establishment of engineered landfill sites, Material Recovery Facilities (MRFs), and introduction of waste-to-energy and waste-to-compost technologies.",""],[1,"135","4","Waste Recycling Investment Incentive Framework","Trash-to-cash models and PPPs will be incentivized to unlock private sector investment in recycling and waste processing.",""],[1,"135","4","Community-Based Solid Waste Management Models","Community-based solid waste management models will be promoted in peri-urban and underserved areas to ensure inclusivity.",""],[1,"135","4","Solid Waste Regulatory and Local Capacity Strengthening","Regulatory frameworks and local government capacities will be strengthened for effective enforcement, while awareness campaigns will be launched to promote behavioural change in waste generation and disposal practices.",""],[1,"141","2","Integrated Solid Waste Management Projects","Develop and implement integrated solid waste management projects, including the establishment of scientifically engineered landfill sites, material recovery facilities, and waste-to-energy and composting plants.",""],[1,"141","3","Public-Private Partnerships for Waste Management","Foster public-private partnerships to mobilize private sector investment, innovation, and operational efficiency in waste collection, recycling, treatment, and disposal systems.",""],[1,"141","4","Circular Economy Promotion and Extended Producer Responsibility Mainstreaming","Promote circular economy practices through waste segregation at source, adoption of \"reduce-reuse-recycle\" models, and mainstreaming of Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR) in key urban and industrial sectors.",""],[1,"141","5","Waste Management Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Enhance institutional and municipal capacities for planning, monitoring, and enforcement of waste management regulations at local and provincial levels.",""],[1,"145","1","Integrated Solid Waste Management Projects","Integrated Solid Waste Management (SWM) projects will be implemented in collaboration with municipalities and private sector actors.",""],[1,"145","1","Extended Producer Responsibility Mandate","Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR) will be mandated for key sectors to promote sustainable packaging and recycling practices.",""],[1,"145","1","3Rs Mainstreaming Through Education and Municipal Regulations","The \"reduce-reuse-recycle (3Rs)\" approach will be mainstreamed through education and municipal regulations.",""],[1,"145","1","Capacity Building for Local Government Departments and Urban Utilities","Capacity-building for Local Government Departments (LGDs) and Urban Utilities will be prioritized to strengthen planning, enforcement, and citizen participation in the transition to a circular economy.",""]],"94":[[1,"136","2","Gender Mainstreaming in Climate and Environmental Policy","The Plan focuses on institutionalizing gender mainstreaming across climate change and environmental policies, plans, and projects.",""],[1,"139","11","National Climate Change Gender Action Plan Implementation","Implement the National Climate Change Gender Action Plan (ccGAP) for gender- responsive climate adaptation and DRR, ensuring the inclusion of women, youth, and vulnerable populations in climate actions.",""],[1,"139","13","Climate-Integrated Pro-Poor and Gender-Sensitive Adaptation Policy","Pursue economic growth addressing climate challenges, integrate climate policy with national policies, and focus on pro-poor, gender-sensitive adaptation.",""],[1,"140","3","National Climate Change Gender Action Plan Implementation","Implementation of National Climate Change Gender Action Plan (ccGAP).",""],[1,"144","3","Climate Change Gender Action Plan Operationalization","The government will operationalize the Climate Change Gender Action Plan (ccGAP) to ensure gender-responsive climate action, social equity, and inclusion of women, youth, indigenous peoples, and persons with disabilities (PWDs) in climate policy and practice.",""],[1,"147","5","Gender Mainstreaming in Climate Policy and Project Implementation","The ccGAP provides a structured framework for mainstreaming gender across climate policy, planning, and project implementation at both federal and provincial levels.",""],[1,"147","5","Gender-Responsive Access to International Climate Finance","Its implementation will support Pakistan in fulfilling its international commitments under the UNFCCC, achieving national climate, and strengthening gender-responsive access to international climate finance, particularly through the GCF and other multilateral sources.",""]],"95":[[1,"138","5","Climate-Resilient Urban Development through Nature-Based Solutions","Bolster climate-resilient urban development through Nature-Based Solutions (NbS), green infrastructure, and climate-smart municipal services.",""],[1,"138","7","Green Financing Instruments for Urban Growth and Infrastructure","Develop and promote green financing instruments to support low-emission, resilient urban growth and infrastructure.",""],[1,"143","7","Nature-Based Urban Resilience and Green Infrastructure Planning","Nature-Based Solutions (NbS) and Ecosystem-based Approaches (EbA) will be adopted to improve the climate resilience of urban settlements, support sustainable municipal infrastructure, and mitigate urban heat islands and flood risks.",""],[1,"143","7","Urban Master Plan Revision for Green Infrastructure","Urban master plans will be revised to incorporate green infrastructure (e.g., urban forests, wetlands, bioswales).",""],[1,"143","7","Green Municipal Bond Financing for Climate-Resilient Urban Development","Innovative instruments, including green municipal bonds, will be promoted to mobilize financing for climate-resilient urban development.",""],[1,"146","6","Urban Flood Resilience Programme","It is planned that urban flooding will be addressed through a dedicated programme to strengthen the climate resilience of cities and towns increasingly affected by intense and erratic monsoon rainfall.",""],[1,"147","1","Urban Flood Risk Reduction in City Master Plans","flood risk reduction into city master plans, with special focus on Karachi, Lahore, Rawalpindi, Peshawar, and other vulnerable urban centres.",""]],"96":[[1,"138","6","Nature-Based Solutions and Ecosystem-Based Adaptation for Mitigation and Adaptation","Leverage NbS and Ecosystem-based Approaches (EbA) for mitigation and adaptation in urban, peri-urban, and rural settings.",""],[1,"138","11","Payment for Ecosystem Services Schemes for Mountain Ecosystem Conservation","Develop Payment for Ecosystem Services (PES) schemes and strategies to conserve mountain ecosystems ensuring sustainable downstream flows.",""],[1,"138","12","Nature-Based Sustainable Tourism Promotion","Promote nature-based sustainable tourism to support local livelihoods while conserving ecological integrity.",""],[1,"138","13","Biodiversity Credits Framework","Initiate frameworks for biodiversity credits, in parallel with carbon markets, to monetize ecosystem conservation benefits.",""],[1,"138","17","Community-Based Conservation and Nature-Based Sustainable Tourism","Promote community-based conservation and nature-based sustainable tourism, enabling local stewardship of biodiversity and generation of green livelihoods, especially for youth and marginalized groups.",""],[1,"139","1","Innovative Biodiversity Financing Mechanisms","Develop innovative financing mechanisms for biodiversity, including Payment for Ecosystem Services (PES) schemes and biodiversity credit frameworks, to monetize conservation benefits and attract private investment.",""],[1,"144","1","Payment for Ecosystem Services Scheme Development and Pilot","The country will develop and pilot Payment for Ecosystem Services (PES) schemes",""],[1,"144","1","Biodiversity Credit Market Exploration","explore biodiversity credit markets, complementing carbon market mechanisms",""],[1,"144","1","Nature-Based Tourism Promotion","Nature-based tourism will be promoted to generate green jobs and improve local livelihoods",""],[1,"146","4","Mainstream Eco-Tourism and Nature-Based Tourism","it is also planned that eco-tourism and nature-based tourism initiatives will be mainstreamed into national and provincial development frameworks",""],[1,"148","1","Innovative Conservation Financing Mechanisms","Pakistan will develop and pilot innovative mechanisms such as Payment for Ecosystem Services (PES) and biodiversity credit frameworks, enabling the monetization of ecosystem services and stimulating private sector participation in biodiversity restoration.",""],[1,"148","33","Payment for Ecosystem Services Schemes","Promote reforestation, climate-smart land use, PES schemes",""],[1,"148","37","Biodiversity Credits Framework","Introduce biodiversity credits",""],[1,"148","38","PES Framework Institutionalization","Institutionalize PES frameworks",""],[1,"148","45","Biodiversity Credit Framework Development","Develop biodiversity credit frameworks",""],[1,"149","3","Biodiversity Credit Registry","Establish biodiversity credit registry",""]],"97":[[1,"139","10","Nationwide Climate and Environmental Literacy Programme","Implement a nationwide climate and environmental literacy programme through schools, civil society, academia, and the private sector; promote youth engagement through Nature Clubs.",""],[1,"144","3","National Environmental Literacy Programme","A National Environmental Literacy Programme (NELP) will be launched, integrated into school curricula, community outreach, and digital learning/platforms.",""],[1,"144","3","Nature Clubs and Youth Climate Champions Initiative","Nature Clubs and youth climate champions will be established across schools and universities.",""]],"98":[[1,"134","3","Strategic Environmental and Social Assessment Institutionalization","Strategic Environmental and Social Assessments (SESA) will be institutionalized for infrastructure projects in ecologically sensitive areas to ensure wildlife-friendly planning and development.",""],[1,"139","12","Environmental Protection Legal and Coordination Framework","Strengthen legal frameworks for environmental protection, define roles for government agencies, promote transparency, develop mechanisms for monitoring environmental initiatives and coordinate international efforts.",""],[1,"140","1","Strategic Environmental and Social Assessment of Mega Infrastructure Projects","Undertake Strategic Environmental and Social Assessment (SESAs) of mega infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"140","6","Strengthening National and Provincial Coordinating Bodies","Strengthen National and Provincial Coordinating bodies to enhance inter-provincial coordination.",""],[1,"140","7","Nature-based Solutions Standards Implementation","Make efforts to implement global standards of Nature-based Solutions (NbS) at national provincial levels.",""],[1,"140","15","ESMS Integration into iPAS","Ensure full integration of Environmental and Social Management System (ESMS) into iPAS to improve environmental safeguards, reduce project-level risks, and meet international financing standards.",""],[1,"140","16","Environmental Impact Assessment Regime Strengthening","Strengthen the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) regime by enhancing legal, procedural, and institutional frameworks to ensure timely, transparent, and scientifically robust assessments of development projects, in line with national environmental quality standards and international best practices.",""],[1,"140","17","Integrated E-EIA Portal Development","Digitize and streamline the EIA process through the development of an integrated e- EIA portal for submission, review, and public disclosure to improve efficiency, reduce processing time, and promote accountability.",""],[1,"140","18","EPA Technical Capacity Strengthening for EIA Review and Enforcement","Build technical capacity of federal and provincial Environmental Protection Agencies (EPAs) for effective EIA review, monitoring, and enforcement, including the use of",""],[1,"144","4","Environmental Governance Legal and Institutional Reform","Environmental governance will be strengthened by updating laws, rules, and institutional mandates across all tiers of government.",""],[1,"144","4","Strategic Environmental and Social Assessment Institutionalization","Strategic Environmental and Social Assessments (SESAs) will be institutionalized for all mega-infrastructure projects to ensure sustainability and social safeguards.",""],[1,"144","4","Multilateral Environment Agreements Compliance Cell","The MoCC&EC will establish a Multilateral Environment Agreements (MEA) Cell to monitor compliance with international treaties and support climate diplomacy.","MoCC&EC"],[1,"144","6","Environmental Impact Assessment Regime Modernization","The EIA regime will be modernized through legal reform, digitization, and institutional capacity enhancement.",""],[1,"144","6","Integrated e-EIA Portal Development","An integrated e-EIA portal will be developed for streamlined submission, review, and public disclosure of project documents.",""],[1,"144","6","EPA GIS and Climate Risk Tool Upgrading","Federal and provincial Environmental Protection Agencies (EPAs) will be equipped with Geographic Information Systems (GIS), climate risk tools, and Strategic Environmental Assessments (SEAs).",""],[1,"144","6","Public Participation Strengthening for EIA Processes","Public participation mechanisms will be strengthened to ensure transparency and inclusivity, particularly for projects in critical ecological zones.",""]],"99":[[1,"128","19","Quality Control, Testing and Certification System Strengthening","Strengthening system of quality control, testing and certification: for making exports competitive.",""],[1,"134","5","Renewable Energy and Low-Emission Transition Incentives","Accelerated deployment of renewable energy technologies, electric mobility, and low-emission industrial practices will be promoted through targeted policy incentives and PPPs.",""],[1,"139","2","National Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Programme","Reduce national GHG emissions across key sectors, energy, transport, agriculture, industry, and waste by accelerating the shift toward low-carbon technologies, renewable energy, and energy efficiency solutions.",""],[1,"145","2","Climate Change Mitigation in Energy, Agriculture, and Transport","The plan aims to mitigate climate change by focusing on key sectors like energy and agriculture, developing technological packages for livestock, poultry, and crop sectors.",""],[1,"145","2","Vehicle Emissions Standards and Fleet Modernization Measures","It also addresses vehicular emissions by advocating for standardized standards, phasing out old vehicles, and promoting cleaner engines and hybrid vehicles.",""],[1,"145","2","National E-Vehicle Policy","The National E-Vehicle Policy is set to replace 30 percent of vehicles by 2030, signalling a commitment to sustainable transportation.",""],[1,"145","3","Climate Innovation and Technology Accelerator","a Climate Innovation and Technology Accelerator (CITA) will be established under public-private partnership.",""],[1,"148","2","National Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Strategy","Pakistan will pursue a comprehensive national strategy for GHG emissions reduction, targeting key emitting sectors such as energy, transport, agriculture, industry, and waste.",""],[1,"148","2","Low-Carbon Technology and Energy Efficiency Deployment","The government will accelerate the deployment of low-carbon technologies, renewable energy systems, and energy efficiency measures, while promoting a shift to climate-smart practices in agriculture and urban development.",""],[1,"148","13","Public Finance System Institutionalization","Institutionalize within public finance system",""]],"100":[[1,"149","13","Brick Kiln Technology Adoption Strategy","Develop strategy, tech adoption (zig- zag kilns, Happy Seeders)",""],[1,"149","16","Satellite Monitoring Integration","Integrate satellite monitoring",""],[1,"149","19","Early Warning and Preparedness System","Design early warning & preparedness",""],[1,"149","33","Green Infrastructure Implementation","Implement green infrastructure 7",""],[1,"149","38","Recycling Infrastructure Development","Develop recycling infrastructure",""],[1,"149","54","IPAS Screening Integration","Integrate screening into İPAS",""],[1,"149","55","Capacity Building in Ministries","Build capacity in ministries",""],[1,"149","59","Provincial Climate Performance Index Development","Develop Provincial Climate Performance Index (PCPI)",""],[1,"149","62","Climate Innovation and Technology Accelerator","Establish Climate Innovation & Technology Accelerator (CITA)",""]],"101":[[1,"154","13","Agricultural Governance and Regulatory Reform","Reform required to improve governance structure to make it consistent with the changing demands for the agriculture, like food quality, safety and processed agriculture products, and provide regulatory framework friendly to the private sector investment.",""],[1,"155","1","Agricultural Ministry and Department Reform","Reform structure of the Ministry and Department to meet the changing agriculture sector demands",""],[1,"155","2","Federal-Provincial Development Coordination","Federal government development activities will be aligned with provincial government, and efforts will be made to start collaborative projects with the provinces.",""],[1,"157","5","Agricultural Price Control Liberalization","Work with federal and provincial governments to reduce and finally eliminate the government control on agricultural input and output prices and their regional movements.",""],[1,"158","17","Agricultural Governance and Value Chain Reform Package","comprehensive strategies covering governance and institutional reforms, market efficiency, improved value chain, development of agri-business, mechanization of farm operations, and provision of infrastructure will be implemented",""],[1,"159","10","Agriculture Sector Institutional Reform and Alignment","Reforms MNFSR and provincial departments to align these with the emerging demand on the agriculture sector, like food quality and safety, value addition, processing, etc.","MNFSR | provincial departments"],[1,"159","12","Market Liberalization for Staple and Food Commodity Trade","Gradually relax the government control on wheat, sugar, milk, meat, and fruits and vegetable markets, including their local control on auctions, prices, inter-regional movement, and trade.",""],[1,"160","10","Livestock Sector Industrial Status Reform","Grant livestock the status of industry to avail the benefits similar to other agriculture sectors.",""],[1,"160","11","Maize and Soybean Tariff Rationalization","Rationalize the production and import tariffs for maize and soybean as major feedstuff of animal and poultry feed.",""]],"102":[[1,"156","3","Specialized Agricultural Extension Implementation","Gradually replace \"Generalized Extension (GE)\" which focusses on all issues of different crops and animals, with \"Specialized Extension (SE)\", which tries to resolve most important issue at one time.",""],[1,"156","4","Demand-Driven Fee-Based Extension Services","Promote demand-driven and fee-based extension preferably through digital models.",""],[1,"156","5","Stakeholder Training for Horticulture and Livestock Value Chain Development","Work with provincial extension departments to develop trainings courses for all stakeholders (i.e., producers, wholesalers, traders, etc.) for the development of value chain of major horticulture & livestock products and develop agricultural businesses,",""],[1,"156","6","Regulatory Framework for Public-Private Partnership in Extension","Provide regulatory framework for synergistic public-private partnership in extension.",""],[1,"158","10","Digital Producer Awareness Applications for Disease Management","Digital applications to enhance awareness of producers about animal and crop disease management during pre-and post-harvest.",""],[1,"158","11","Digital Food Safety Awareness Applications","Develop digital applications for mass awareness about food quality and safety standards.",""],[1,"161","11","Value Chain Stakeholder Capacity Building","Capacity building for value chain development of all stakeholders along the value chain including farmers, wholesalers, traders, processors, etc.",""],[1,"161","21","Animal Breeding Centers with Genomic- Tested Bulls","Establishment of animal breeding centers with genomic tested bulls bulls through FEGs.",""]],"103":[[1,"154","10","Resource Use Efficiency and Sustainable Natural Resource Management","Improve sustainability of resources by increase input-use efficiency, especially of water, machines, labour, fertilizer, improve productivity and sustainability of rangeland, forestry, and fishery resources.",""],[1,"156","8","Agricultural Input-Use Efficiency and Natural Resource Productivity Reforms","Here the purpose is to introduce reforms and implement policies that can enhance the agriculture input-use efficiency, improve the productivity of natural resources, like forestry, fisheries, rangeland, and fruit gardens.",""],[1,"156","9","National Drainage Plan","Chalk out national drainage PLAN, especially in the low-lying areas of Punjab and Sindh",""],[1,"156","10","Targeted Waterlogged and Saline Land Reclamation Program","Introduce targeted program to reclaim water logged and saline areas, especially in Sindh",""],[1,"156","11","Farm-Level Soil Health and Tubewell Water Quality Monitoring","Document and regularly update the soil health condition at farm-level and water quality at tubewell level.",""],[1,"156","12","Environment-Based Crop Model Development and Farmer Literacy Improvement","Work with provinces to develop environment-based crop models, and improve farmers' literacy to use these models to stop soil and land degradation.",""],[1,"156","13","High-Efficiency Irrigation and Resource Conservation Technology Promotion","Working with provinces, encourage high-efficiency irrigation and resource conservation technologies",""],[1,"156","14","Watercourse Lining Program in Sindh","Strengthen lining of water course program in Sindh",""],[1,"156","15","Canal Water Pricing Reform","Bring canal water prices closer to its economic value",""],[1,"156","16","Best Resource Management Practices for Forestry, Fisheries, and Range Management","Introduce best resource management practices in forestry, fisheries, and range management as recommended by international centers, to enhance their productivity and sustainability.",""],[1,"160","8","Community Management of Natural Resources","Transfer the state control on natural resources, like forestry, fisheries, rangeland, and water to the local communities and capacity building of communities to manage these resources.",""],[1,"161","17","Distribution of Low-Carbon and Climate-Resilient Agricultural Technologies","Distribution of low-carbon and climate resilient machines, tools, computer-based crop/animal management models through FEG.",""]],"104":[[1,"156","7","Online Commodity Exchange Portals","Develop portals for the on-line commodity exchanges",""],[1,"157","2","Rural Trading Platforms Establishment Review","Review legal framework, operational model and incentive structure for the establishment of Trading Platforms (TPFs) in rural areas furnished with modern market facilities and owned by farmers group.",""],[1,"157","3","Agri-Malls Establishment Framework","Provide legal framework, operational model and incentive structure for the establishment of Agri-Malls, the centers for agricultural machinery rental services and input-delivery centers in rural areas.",""],[1,"157","4","Review of Legal and Financial Hurdles for Private-Sector Agricultural Wholesale Markets","Review the legal and financial hurdles in the establishment and functioning of modern agriculture wholesale markets in the private sector.",""],[1,"157","7","Quality-Standard-Based Food and Agricultural Input Price Monitoring System","Introduce quality-standard-based food and agricultural input price monitoring system.",""],[1,"157","8","Agricultural Export Information Portals","Establish information portals for major exportable agricultural commodities for fast track changes in international markets related to market size, price, quality standards, and government regulations.",""],[1,"157","9","Online Commodity Trading Portals","Develop portals for on-line current and future commodity trading.",""],[1,"158","14","Private Sector Farm Storage and EWRF Linkage","Encourage farm-storages in the private sector and link these with Electronic Warehouses Receipt Financing (EWRF) of commercial banks",""],[1,"160","15","Farm-Level Storage with Receipt Warehouse Financing System","Promotion of farm-level storage having Receipt Warehouse Financing (RWF) system in the private sector preferably through farmers' groups",""],[1,"160","17","Rural Trading Platforms Establishment","Establishment of \"Trading Platforms\" in rural areas equipped with value addition equipment, storage facilities, computerized recording system, etc. and operated by Farmers' Entrepreneur Groups (FEG).",""],[1,"160","19","Agri-Malls in Rural Areas","Establishment of \"Agri-Malls\" in rural areas supplying machinery rental and maintenance services and inputs.",""]],"105":[[1,"157","6","Food Quality Standards Development","Develop food quality standards for major horticulture and livestock products, and inputs like machinery and pesticides.",""],[1,"158","7","Food Quality and Safety Improvement Mechanism","Here the emphasis is to develop infrastructure, and provide mechanism to improve food quality and safety.",""],[1,"158","12","Agricultural Commodity Traceability, Certification, and Branding Initiative","Invite international reputed companies for traceability, certification and branding of agricultural commodities",""],[1,"158","13","Private Sector Accredited Food Quality Testing Labs","Encourage accredited food quality-testing labs in the private sector",""],[1,"158","16","Friendly Regulatory Infrastructure for Corporate Investment in Rural Food Quality Infrastructure","Invite and provide friendly regulatory infrastructure for corporate sector to invest on food quality infrastructure in rural areas.",""],[1,"160","1","Grade-Based Retail Marketing and Monitoring","Promote grade-based retail marketing and monitoring.",""],[1,"160","5","Truth-in-Label Enforcement for Seed and Pesticide Marketing","Implement truth-in-label in seed and pesticide marketing.",""],[1,"161","6","Food Testing Laboratory Establishment","Encourage the establishment of food testing labs in the public and private sector",""]],"106":[[1,"157","13","Legal Framework for Rural Agro-Processing and Value Addition Units","Provide legal framework to own and operate small scale agriculture commodity processing and value addition units in rural areas, and provide a mechanism to protect investment in these units.",""],[1,"157","14","Private Sector Agro-Commodity Processing and Value Addition Units","Encourage private sector to establish small-scale agriculture-commodity processing and value addition units through FEG in the focal points of major horticulture livestock clusters in each province, including abattoirs, cheese and juice processing, drying of fruits and vegetables, etc.",""],[1,"157","15","Eco-Friendly Agricultural Machinery Manufacturing Incentives","Incentivize the local manufacturing and supplying of eco-friendly machines for targeted agricultural operations.",""],[1,"158","6","Rural Small-Scale Processing Unit Investment and Training Support","Encourage the corporate sector to invest on small-scale processing units in rural areas, provide training to processors, and link these units with corporate industry in urban areas.",""],[1,"161","13","Support for Small-Scale Agro-Processing Units in Rural Clusters","Encourage the small-scale processing units in major fruits, vegetable, and livestock clusters operated by FEGs in rural areas (like abattoir, juice extraction, driers, chips and cheese making, etc.).",""],[1,"161","13","Corporate Branding and Marketing of Semi-Finished Agro-Products","The corporate sector will be encouraged to take these semi-finished products for the branding and marketing in large scale industries E in urban areas.",""]],"107":[[1,"157","10","Halal Meat Export Promotion","· Enhance halal meat export.",""],[1,"158","3","Fisheries, Poultry and Aquaculture Value Chain Promotion","Promote fisheries, poultry and aquaculture value chains for national and international markets.",""],[1,"158","4","Agro-Tourism and Culinary Tourism Promotion","Promotion of agro-tourism along with culinary tourism.",""],[1,"158","5","CPEC Business Opportunity Exploration","Explore business opportunities under China-Pakistan Economic Corridor (CPEC)",""],[1,"160","12","Level Playing Field for Export-Oriented Meat Processors","Permit export-oriented meat processors to compete in the domestic market on a level playing field.",""],[1,"161","23","Tilapia and Shrimp Farming and Export Incentives","Incentives to promote tilapia fish and shrimp farming and their exports",""]],"108":[[1,"168","3","Hazard-Resistant Housing Reconstruction Grants","Conditional housing reconstruction grants: Disbursement based on flood- resistant engineering designs and construction standards",""],[1,"168","3","Flood Plain Housing Relocation and Compliance Regulation","Houses located in the 5-year flood plain will be relocated - unless they obtain permission and comply flood plain construction regulations",""],[1,"168","4","Flood Plain Housing Restriction and Seismic-Resistant Reconstruction Standards","Housing settlement will not be allowed in the flood plain unless permission obtained in accordance to the Flood Plain Act.",""],[1,"168","5","Floodplain-Compliant Reconstruction and Relocation of Facilities","Reconstruction / relocation of facilities considering flood plain requirements",""],[1,"168","6","Flood Plain Construction Permit Restriction","No facility constructions will be allowed in the flood plain unless permission is obtained complying Flood Plain Act",""],[1,"168","7","Flood-Plain-Compliant Reconstruction and Relocation of Facilities","Reconstruction and relocation of facilities considering flood plain requirements",""],[1,"168","8","Flood Plain Construction Permit Restriction","No facility constructions will be allowed in the flood plain unless permission is obtained complying Flood Plain Act GIVES",""],[1,"168","11","Provincial Flood Plain and Water Acts","Flood Plain Acts to be issued in all provinces Water Acts to be issued by all provinces",""],[1,"168","11","Flood and Drainage Infrastructure Engineering Audit","Engineering audit of flood and drainage structures to be undertaken to assess whether they can withstand highest / prolonged water flows",""],[1,"168","11","Flood Plain Construction Survey and Retention Review","Surveys of flood plain construction to be undertaken along with their necessity and special building requirements if required to be retained.",""],[1,"168","12","Flood Protection Structure Upgrading Programme","Existing Flood protection structures to be made capable of withstanding highest / prolonged flood flows",""],[1,"168","12","Hill Torrent Drainage Resilience Upgrade","Existing Drainage structures in hill torrents IST Food flow and plains to be made capable of taking highest / prolonged flood flows to rivers/sea",""],[1,"168","12","NFPP-IV Flood Protection Construction Programme","New Flood protection structures identified by NFPP-IV, capable of withstanding / managing highest and prolonged flood flows to be constructed (Naulong dam etc.)",""],[1,"168","12","Flood Drainage Infrastructure Construction in Undrained High-Flood Areas","New drainage structures, capable of taking highest/prolonged flood flows to rivers/sea to be constructed in undrained high flood areas.",""],[1,"169","3","Engineering Audit and Impact Assessment of Transport and Communication Lines","Engineering audit and impact assessment, of existing transport and communication lines, will be conducted to assess resilience costs",""],[1,"169","4","Climate-Resilient Drainage Design Review","Proposed drainage design of project will include 20 percent additional capacity for climate change and will be reviewed through simulation modelling to ensure they are not affected in 100-year return period.",""],[1,"169","10","Stepwise Evacuation, Rescue, and Relief Planning Procedure","A stepwise procedure for evacuation rescue and relief plan with clearly defined role of participating institutes / forces.",""],[1,"169","11","Flood Early Warning System Expansion","Early warning system for areas at high risk of floods; subsequently covering most part of the country",""],[1,"169","11","Floodwater Storage and Groundwater Recharge Infrastructure","Building water storage/reservoirs/small- dams to accommodating the flood water through designed flood routes to infiltration system for recharge of ground water aquifers & areas that receives minimum rainfall.",""],[1,"170","6","Flood Response Emergency Housing Project (Phase-II)","Flood Response Emergency Housing Project (Phase-II) ADB/GOS Financing",""],[1,"170","14","Sindh Schools Rehabilitation Project","Sindh Schools Rehabilitation Project undue Flood Restoration Program (ADB- Emergency Assisted)",""],[1,"171","4","DRR Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Project","DRR Project for Rehabilitation / Reconstruction - NDRMF (Flood damaged Water Conversation Structures Balochistan + Building Resilience Damaged Flood Mitigation Sindh).",""],[1,"171","8","National Urban Strategy and Climate-Resilient Spatial Planning Guidelines","Formulation of National Urban Strategy & guidelines to reduce impacts of Urban Flooding, Droughts, climate disasters, and national guidelines for spatial planning considering climate change/disaster risks in Pakistan",""],[1,"171","9","School Construction and Reconstruction Programme in Flood-Affected Sindh","Prime Minister's Programme for Construction / Reconstruction of Existing Schools in Sindh affected under Rain / Flood 2022 in Sindh (1800 Units) (50:50)",""],[1,"171","11","Prime Minister's Programme for Rebuilding Houses in Flood-Affected Areas of Sindh under 4RF","Prime Minister's Programme for Re- building of Houses in Flood Affected Areas of Sindh under 4RF",""],[1,"171","20","Indus Basin Flood Management Enhancement Project","The Project for Flood Management Enhancement in the Indus Basin-JICA Grant",""]],"109":[[1,"187","3","Transmission System Expansion Planning","NTDC will expedite the preparation of Transmission System Expansion Plan (TSEP), which shall be an integrated investment plan.",""],[1,"187","3","Transmission Grid Augmentation and Upgradation Projects","NTDC will expedite the execution of ongoing augmentation, upgradation and extension projects of grid stations and transmission lines.",""],[1,"187","3","NTDC SCADA Capacity Enhancement","Furthermore, the capacity of NTDC will be enhanced to immediately implement Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) systems.",""],[1,"187","3","Transmission Bottleneck Removal","Bottlenecks and congestion in the transmission system (Jamshoro for south and Lahore circle in North) will be removed for smooth operation of least cost electricity generator as per the economic merit order of dispatch.",""],[1,"187","3","Transmission Investment Incentives and Provincial Grid Development","To attract private investment, incentives will be offered under the 2015 Transmission Policy, and provinces will be encouraged to develop their own grids.",""],[1,"187","3","Transmission Land and Right-of-Way Reform","Legal reforms will be introduced to streamline land and Right of Way (RoW) acquisition for transmission expansion.",""],[1,"191","2","Transmission System Bottleneck and Congestion Removal","Removal of bottlenecks and congestion in the transmission system through TSEP",""],[1,"191","4","National Grid Modernization and Provincial Grid Company Operationalization","Modernization and strengthening of national grid & operationalization of provincial grid companies",""]],"110":[[1,"182","4","National Energy Efficiency and Conservation Policy 2023","National Energy Efficiency and Conservation Policy 2023 delineates that energy conservation remains a strategic priority as a first fuel from planning and decision making to the execution of the action plans of all sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"182","5","National Energy Efficiency and Conservation Plan","The National Energy Efficiency & Conservation Plan (2023-30) is also approved by the Federal Cabinet in August this year with an investment potential of about USD 18 billion by 20230.",""],[1,"182","6","NEEC Policy and Action Plan Implementation Framework","Overall, the NEEC Policy and Action Plan segregate actions into short-, medium- and long-term sectoral measures.",""],[1,"182","6","Priority Action Package for Policy Implementation","Activities like identification of opportunities; baseline studies; formulation of sectoral strategies; development of information systems; demonstration and implementation of low and medium-cost, fast pay-back interventions are considered high priority areas of action during the initial period of policy implementation.",""],[1,"182","6","Short- and Medium-Term Sectoral Intervention Plans","Short- and medium-term sectoral intervention plans covering a period up to 2030 will be devised to ensure systematic implementation of planned activities on a case-to-case basis in collaboration with federal, provincial, and local governments, national & international partner organizations, and private sector stakeholders.",""],[1,"182","7","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Regulatory Strengthening","there is need of effective regulatory mechanism and trained human resource for the implementation of EE&C measures.",""],[1,"189","14","Energy Planning Framework and Resource Centre","Planning Commission, by taking has already started working on establishing a framework for an energy planning for sustainable development of the country.",""],[1,"189","15","Institutionalization of Existing Efforts through EPRC Establishment","Existing efforts will be institutionalized on recurring basis by establishing EPRC on regular basis after completion of first phase by June, 2027 of the IEP project under PC-I regime.",""],[1,"190","1","National Action Plan for Energy Efficiency and Conservation","National Action Plan (NAP) for Energy Efficiency & Conservation (EE&C), 2023-30 identifies 29 major action areas with an investment potential of 1 billion USD per year to reap EE&C benefit through public private partnerships and international climate financing platforms.",""],[1,"190","2","National Action Plan Regulatory, Capacity-Building and Advocacy Measures","The actions are divided into three components i.e. regulatory, capacity and advocacy.",""],[1,"190","2","Integration of NEEC Policy Provisions Across Cross-Sectoral Plans","Further, the NAP 2023-30 ensured integration of the provisions/measures of the NEEC Policy 2023 with all the cross-sectoral policies and plans, wherever it was required.",""],[1,"190","3","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Regulatory and Awareness Package","Pakistan Energy Label Regulations, Banning the Inefficient Product, Pakistan Energy Conservation Building Codes-2023, Public Registry Systems, and robust awareness campaigns will be pursued rigorously.",""],[1,"190","3","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Implementation Support Mechanism","Government of Pakistan to facilitate the implementation of the EE&C targets, financing through international development partners with local assistant from federal and provincial government as well as Private / PPP.",""],[1,"192","13","Accelerated Implementation of the National Action Plan on Energy Efficiency and Conservation","Accelerated implementation of National Action Plan on EE&C",""]],"111":[[1,"193","3","Flood Emergency Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Projects","several flood emergency rehabilitation and reconstruction projects were launched in flood affected areas based on 4RFs with cooperation of international financial institutions",""],[1,"193","3","Water Sector Development Projects","all efforts were made to achieve substantial progress on on-going water sector's development projects",""],[1,"194","3","Balochistan Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Projects","a number of projects are under execution including USD 400 million projects in Balochistan for rehabilitation and reconstruction",""],[1,"194","4","National Flood Protection Plan IV Update","National Flood Protection Plan- NFPP-IV was updated in the wake of 2022 floods and to incorporate Hill torrents, is a 10 years plan based on Integrated Flood Risk Management approach consisted of total 375 projects amounting to Rs. 824 billion.",""],[1,"194","4","Structural Flood Protection Component","The interventions include Structural Component, non-Structural component, Integrated Watershed Management, National Master Plan for Flood Telemetry Network, National Watershed Management Plan and National Flood Drainage Master Plan.",""],[1,"194","4","Non-Structural Flood Protection Component","The interventions include Structural Component, non-Structural component, Integrated Watershed Management, National Master Plan for Flood Telemetry Network, National Watershed Management Plan and National Flood Drainage Master Plan.",""],[1,"194","4","Integrated Watershed Management","The interventions include Structural Component, non-Structural component, Integrated Watershed Management, National Master Plan for Flood Telemetry Network, National Watershed Management Plan and National Flood Drainage Master Plan.",""],[1,"194","4","National Flood Telemetry Network Master Plan","The interventions include Structural Component, non-Structural component, Integrated Watershed Management, National Master Plan for Flood Telemetry Network, National Watershed Management Plan and National Flood Drainage Master Plan.",""],[1,"194","4","National Watershed Management Plan","The interventions include Structural Component, non-Structural component, Integrated Watershed Management, National Master Plan for Flood Telemetry Network, National Watershed Management Plan and National Flood Drainage Master Plan.",""],[1,"194","4","National Flood Drainage Master Plan","The interventions include Structural Component, non-Structural component, Integrated Watershed Management, National Master Plan for Flood Telemetry Network, National Watershed Management Plan and National Flood Drainage Master Plan.",""],[1,"195","4","Flood Risk Management Enhancement Programme","Enhancement of Flood Risk Management through structural, non-structural measures including Nature based Solutions (NBS), Hill Torrents Management and to upgrade Flood Forecasting and Early Warning Systems.",""],[1,"197","1","Flood Protection Investment Programme","Flood protection measures will be bolstered with a significant investment, providing communities with improved resilience against natural disasters and safeguarding valuable agricultural lands.",""],[1,"197","1","Water Management Studies and Research Initiative","a portion of the investment will be allocated to studies and research initiatives, developing a deeper understanding of water management challenges and solutions.",""]],"112":[[1,"195","3","Water Sensitive Cities and Circular Urban Water Management Initiative","In addition to optimize demand and supply of domestic and industrial use by adopting emerging concepts of 'Water Sensitive Cities' and urban water management through Circular Cities Approach by initiating activities including rainwater harvesting, recycle and reuse of waste water, installation of water treatment and desalination plants.",""],[1,"196","2","Pakistan Building Code Update for Rainwater Harvesting","Updating of Pakistan Building Code to incorporate Rainwater Harvesting for new and existing Buildings",""],[1,"196","4","Flood Zoning and Construction Code Update","Flood Zoning and establishment guidelines and updation of design codes of construction of roads, highways and building in flood prone areas.",""],[1,"196","6","Water Sensitive Cities and Circular Cities Pilot Projects","Pilot projects for adaptation of models of water sensitive cities and concept of circular cities in big cities.",""],[1,"196","9","Private Sector High-Efficiency Irrigation Projects","The private sector may take technology based commercial projects such as high efficiency irrigation.",""],[1,"196","10","Community-Led Watercourse Rehabilitation","Farmers should take over rehabilitation of water courses.",""],[1,"198","16","Flood Zoning and Water-Sensitive Cities Studies","Feasibility/ Technical Studies, Ground Water Regulatory Framework, Flood zoning, studies to adapt Water Sensitive cities approach etc.",""]],"113":[[1,"201","7","Oil Transport Shift to Pipelines and Railways","The plan aims to shift oil transportation primarily to pipelines and railways to mitigate these issues.",""],[1,"202","8","Freight Modal Shift to Rail and Pipeline","Shifting freight movement from road to rail and pipeline by integrating agriculture rail stations, dry ports, and pipelines.",""]],"114":[[1,"202","10","Road Safety Promotion through Safe System Approach","Active promotion of road safety through the adoption of the UN Safe System Approach, and international safety standards.",""],[1,"202","11","Road User Charges and Axle Load Regime","Implementing road user charges reflecting policy priorities and addressing vehicle overloading issues i.e. implementing axle load regime.",""],[1,"202","16","Sustainable Drainage Integration for Transport Networks","Incorporating sustainable drainage system any transportation and communication networks to make transport networks flood resilient and reduce the risk of flooding in downstream floodplains, improve quality of the storm water runoff to help reduce saltation of dams, reservoirs and ports and to avoid affecting aquatic life.",""]],"115":[[1,"203","6","Air Transport Liberalization under Open Skies Policy","Liberalizing air transport in line with the open skies policy to stimulate growth without compromising national interests.",""],[1,"203","8","Airport Land-Side Outsourcing for Revenue Generation","Outsourcing of Airports (land side) for enhanced revenue generation",""],[1,"205","16","Air Connectivity and Gwadar Aerotropolis Development","Promote international and domestic air connectivity, Gwadar as an 'Aerotropolis'.",""],[1,"205","17","Airport Infrastructure and Services Upgrade","Upgrade airport infrastructure and services in line with functional roles and ensure",""],[1,"205","19","PIA Restructuring and Aviation Tax Rationalization","Restructure/privatize PIA and rationalize aviation taxes with market-based pricing.",""],[1,"205","20","Airport Revenue Generation and Cost Reduction Outsourcing","Generate revenue and reduce airport operating costs through outsourcing",""],[1,"207","5","Airport Infrastructure Upgradation Programme","Flight procedures updation for Northern area airports Expansion of Terminal building of Lahore Airport Reconstruction of Main Runway at Karachi Airport Installation of E-gates at major Airports Upgradation of Skardu Airport (5years) Feasibility for new airport at DI khan",""],[1,"221","6","Technical and Operational Support for New Gwadar International Airport","Technical and operational support will be prioritized for the efficient operationalization of this strategic airport, which will serve as a regional aviation hub for cargo and passengers.",""]],"116":[[1,"203","9","National Ports Master Plan Development","Development of a national ports master plan including Gwadar Port Operationalization plan considering future capacities, goods evacuation, and urban integration.",""],[1,"203","10","Gwadar Port Capacity Expansion and Free Zone Development","Utilization of Karachi and Port Qasim as primary international ports, however, increasing the capacity of the Gwadar Port through business provision and development of Free Zone.",""],[1,"205","6","Port Efficiency Enhancement","Enhance port efficiency to support exports and strengthen security.",""],[1,"205","21","Maritime Trade and Passenger Flow Infrastructure Upgrade","Enhance infrastructure and operational capacity to support maritime trade and passenger flows.",""],[1,"205","22","Private Concessions for Coastal Port Facilities and Shipping Services","Promote coastal port facilities and shipping services through private concessions.",""],[1,"205","23","Maritime Regulatory Oversight and Navigation Infrastructure Strengthening","Strengthen regulatory oversight, navigation infrastructure, and support strategic trade via public sector shipping lines.",""],[1,"205","24","Ship Recycling and Shipbuilding Industry Development","Develop ship recycling/building industries and improve coordination for data-driven transport planning and PSDP resource allocation",""],[1,"207","2","Gaddani Ship Breaking East Bay Expressway Modernization","Modernization and Upgradation of Gaddani Ship Breaking East Bay Expressway",""],[1,"207","2","Gwadar Industrial Zone Land Acquisition","Phase II Land Acquisition for Industrial Zone in Gwadar",""],[1,"207","2","New Shipyard Feasibility Study Near Gwadar","F/S for new shipyard near Gwadar",""]],"117":[[1,"203","14","Pipeline Transport for Oil, Gas, and Bulk Liquids","Focusing on transporting oil, gas, and bulk liquids primarily through pipelines.",""],[1,"203","15","Strategic Pipeline Connectivity Development","Establishing pipeline connections to crucial areas like ports, refineries, storage depots, and urban zones.",""],[1,"203","16","Logistics Enabling Environment Prioritization","Prioritizing the regulatory, institutional, financial, commercial, and social environments for efficient logistics operation.",""],[1,"203","17","Private Sector Freight Logistics Engagement and Regulation","Encouraging private sector engagement in freight logistics while regulating through public trade and transportation facilitation agencies.",""],[1,"203","20","Trucking Policy Reform Implementation","Implementation of reforms based on the Trucking Policy to reduce external costs to the economy and businesses.",""],[1,"204","1","Integrated Cold Chain System Development","Development of a well-integrated cold chain system (CCS) via private sector participation to boost perishable goods exports.",""]],"118":[[1,"205","7","Alternative Financing for National Road Project Completion","Support PSDP through alternate financing modes for completion of national road projects.",""],[1,"205","8","Completion of Ongoing National Highways, Motorways, and Strategic Links","Prioritize and complete ongoing approved National Highways, Motorways, and strategic links.",""],[1,"205","9","Road Maintenance Funding Mechanism and Data Improvement","Establish a formal funding mechanism for road maintenance and improve road- related data for informed decision-making.",""],[1,"205","10","National Road Safety Plan","Expand road safety efforts, including accident data systems, and develop a National Road Safety Plan under the Ministry of Communications.","Ministry of Communications"],[1,"205","11","Axle Load Regime Implementation","Implement the axle load regime and promote climate-resilient infrastructure",""],[1,"205","11","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Promotion","Implement the axle load regime and promote climate-resilient infrastructure",""],[1,"206","4","Construction Quality Improvement and Advanced Construction Techniques","Improve construction quality and adopt advanced techniques to reduce infrastructure maintenance costs.",""],[1,"206","5","Road Maintenance Cross-Subsidy Mechanism","Cross-subsidize road maintenance by adjusting toll rates, enforcing axle load regime, and commercializing lands along major routes.",""],[1,"206","17","National Transport Corridor Realignment and Completion Programme","Realignment of KKH (Havellain Thakot) Sukkur Hyderabad Motorway (M-6) Conts. of M-9 (Karachi Hyderabad) Completion of M-8 missing links (Hoshab to Awaran and Awaran to Naal) KPEC Peshawar to Trokham Kohat Kharlachi Rail link Dulaization of N-25 Karachi - Quetta - Chamman",""],[1,"206","22","Sukkur-Hyderabad Motorway Completion","Sukkur Hyderabad Motorway (M-6)",""],[1,"206","22","Continuation of M-9 Karachi-Hyderabad Motorway","Conts. of M-9 (Karachi Hyderabad)",""],[1,"206","22","Completion of M-8 Missing Links","Completion of M-8 missing links (Hoshab to Awaran and Awaran to Naal)",""],[1,"206","22","Dualization of N-25 Karachi-Quetta-Chamman","Dualization of N-25 Karachi - Quetta - Chamman",""],[1,"221","7","East Bay Expressway Phase II Expansion","East Bay Expressway (Phase II): Further expansion of this road is vital for facilitating logistics from Gwadar Port to inland transportation networks.",""],[1,"221","8","Babusar Tunnel Road Connectivity Initiative","Babusar Tunnel on N-15: A critical infrastructure initiative aimed at improving road connectivity between the northern regions and central Pakistan, reducing travel time and enhancing year-round access.",""],[1,"221","9","Karachi-Hyderabad M-9 Motorway Construction","Karachi-Hyderabad M-9 Motorway: Construction of this crucial artery will relieve congestion and improve the flow of goods across southern Pakistan.",""]],"119":[[1,"205","2","Data Systems Modernization for Informed Planning","Improve data systems using modern tools for informed planning.",""],[1,"205","3","Unified Ministry of Transport","Establish a unified Ministry of Transport and avoid PSDP funding for provincial projects.",""],[1,"205","4","NHA and Railways Business Plan Approval and Governance and Financial Reform","Approve business plans of NHA and Railways, along with governance and financial reforms.",""],[1,"205","5","Transport Operations Outsourcing","Outsource operations of rail transport, airports, and PIA.",""],[1,"205","24","Data-Driven Transport Planning and PSDP Resource Allocation Coordination","Develop ship recycling/building industries and improve coordination for data-driven transport planning and PSDP resource allocation",""],[1,"206","11","Community and Stakeholder Consultation for Project Implementation","Engage local communities and stakeholders through consultative processes for effective project implementation.",""]],"120":[[1,"202","18","Low-Carbon Transport Network and Electric Vehicle Promotion","Reducing the transportation and communications sector's carbon footprint by providing efficient transport networks utilizing traffic modeling and promoting electric vehicles.",""],[1,"206","1","Public Transport Fleet Electrification and Hybrid Transition","Transition 25 percent of the public transport fleet to hybrid and electric vehicles to reduce carbon emissions by 30 percent.",""],[1,"206","2","Provincial Public Transport Strategy Development","Develop provincial public transport strategies and invest in EV charging infrastructure over the next five years.",""],[1,"206","2","EV Charging Infrastructure Investment","Develop provincial public transport strategies and invest in EV charging infrastructure over the next five years.",""],[1,"206","3","Route Optimization for Transport Efficiency","Optimize routes based on demand to reduce travel time and fuel consumption by 15 percent by 2025",""],[1,"206","6","Pedestrian-Friendly Urban Infrastructure Investment","Invest in pedestrian-friendly infrastructure in urban centers based on GIS data.",""],[1,"206","7","Dedicated Bus Lane Implementation","Implement dedicated bus lanes on key routes to reduce congestion by 25 percent during peak hours.",""],[1,"206","8","Energy-Efficient Technologies in Transport Hubs","Integrate energy-efficient technologies in transport hubs to cut energy use by 20 percent, saving PKR 500 million annually.",""],[1,"206","9","Rural Accessibility and Public Transport Expansion","Enhance rural accessibility by expanding road networks and public transport to essential services.",""],[1,"206","10","Rural Market Access and Sustainable Livelihoods Support","Promote rural development by improving market access and supporting sustainable livelihoods.",""]],"121":[[1,"209","1","Integrated Sustainable Urban Development Strategy","To address these challenges, the federal government prioritizes integrated sustainable urban development strategies, emphasizing affordable housing, climate resilience, and alignment with the 18th amendment's devolution of powers.",""],[1,"210","2","Integrated Urban Planning System Reform","The Plan aims to establish an ecologically sound, participatory, and integrated urban planning system, aligned with URAAN Pakistan and SDGs 6 and 11.",""],[1,"210","2","Local Government Financial Autonomy Reform","Key focuses include financial autonomy for local governments, smart infrastructure, affordable housing, and the integration of informal settlements.",""],[1,"210","2","Urban and Rural Environment Capacity Building","It prioritizes reforms, decentralized governance, and capacity building to foster sustainable urban and rural environments.",""],[1,"210","2","Decentralized Urban Governance Reform","It prioritizes reforms, decentralized governance, and capacity building to foster sustainable urban and rural environments.",""],[1,"210","2","Urban Planning Monitoring Framework","A comprehensive monitoring framework will track progress toward 2028-29 targets, ensuring accountability and measurable outcomes.",""],[1,"211","1","Spatial Planning Legislation and Policy Reform","The Plan focuses on enacting new spatial planning legislation and policies at both national and provincial levels.",""],[1,"211","1","Local and City Planning Capacity Strengthening","the revised legislative frameworks and enhanced capacities of local and city planning departments will support a participatory process in developing city and district-level plans that align with national and provincial development priorities.",""],[1,"211","1","Planning Evaluation and Monitoring Framework","Implementation will be supported by a comprehensive evaluation and monitoring framework with relevant indicators.",""],[1,"211","8","Integrated Development Plans and Effective Governance","Implement Integrated Development Plans and Effective Governance",""],[1,"211","13","Community Engagement and Citizen Participation Initiative","Promote sustainable practices, social inclusivity, and citizen participation in decision-making through increased community engagement, targeted programs, awareness campaigns, and digital platforms.",""],[1,"212","1","Technology-Enabled Governance and Service Delivery Improvement","Enhance governance effectiveness through the utilization of technology, achieving improvement in service delivery.",""],[1,"212","4","Climate-Resilient Urban Planning Strategy","Implement climate-resilient urban planning strategies, ensuring the protection of vulnerable areas from natural disasters.",""],[1,"212","7","Research Collaboration for Integrated Planning Reform","the strategy involves conducting an in-depth research collaboration with Provincial P&D Boards / Departments.",""],[1,"212","7","Urban Planning Law and Spatial Framework Reform","new urban planning laws, spatial frameworks, and participatory governance structures will be enacted at national and provincial levels.",""],[1,"212","7","Local Development Project Prioritization in Public Investment Programs","Local development projects will be prioritized in federal and provincial public sector development programs, increasing financial health of local governments.",""],[1,"212","7","Planning Empowerment Fund","Establish a dedicated fund for planning empowerment, and integrate green infrastructure and green financing.",""],[1,"212","8","Model Districts for Sustainable Development","Establish Model Districts for Sustainable Development: The strategy centers on the creation of \"Model Districts\" by implementing visionary city/district development plans.",""],[1,"212","9","Provincial and District Spatial Development Planning","the strategy involves formulating provincial and district/division spatial development plans.",""],[1,"213","2","Strengthen Planning Structures and Urban Information Management","Strengthen Planning Structures and Urban Information Management: This strategy emphasizes amplifying capacity within the Ministry of Planning, Development and Special Initiatives, engaging stakeholders in legislative and policy framework formulation, and establishing a robust data bank for an urban information management system.","Ministry of Planning, Development and Special Initiatives"],[1,"213","6","Integrated City and District Development Plans","This strategy involves the implementation of Integrated City/District Development Plans through participatory governance structures.",""],[1,"214","5","Pioneering Research Collaboration for Planning Reform","Undertake a pioneering research collaboration Identify transformative reforms for a vibrant planning system.",""],[1,"214","5","Urban Planning Law and Spatial Framework Reform","Enact visionary urban planning laws, spatial frameworks, and participatory governance structures.",""],[1,"214","5","Local Project Prioritization in Federal and Provincial PSDPs","Elevate local projects in federal and provincial PSDPs.",""],[1,"214","5","Planning System Empowerment Fund","Establish a dedicated fund for planning system empowerment.",""],[1,"214","5","Town Planner Recruitment and Capacity-Building Programme","Fortify the ranks_ of town planners.",""],[1,"214","5","Planning Capacity-Building Programme","Ignite capacity-building programs for a dynamic future.",""],[1,"214","8","Model Districts Development Initiative","Craft \"Model Districts\" a as beacons of sustainable success.",""],[1,"214","8","Visionary City and District Development Plans","Implement visionary city/district development plans showcasing SDG triumphs.",""],[1,"215","6","Planning Commission Capacity Enhancement","Amplify capacity within Planning Commission.",""],[1,"215","6","Collaborative Legislative and Policy Framework Formulation","Cultivate collaborative engagements for legislative and policy framework formulation.",""],[1,"215","6","Urban Information Management Data Bank","Establish a robust data bank for an urban information management system and real- time databases.",""],[1,"216","4","Integrated City and District Development Plans","Implement Integrated City/District Development Plans through participatory governance structures.",""]],"122":[[1,"209","2","Sustainable Urban Development and Inclusive Housing Initiatives","Its core objectives included managing rapid urbanization, developing national infrastructure to support urban and rural growth, fostering knowledge-sharing to tackle development issues, and promoting green, energy-efficient, and affordable housing through various initiatives.",""],[1,"210","2","Smart Infrastructure and Affordable Housing Initiative","Key focuses include financial autonomy for local governments, smart infrastructure, affordable housing, and the integration of informal settlements.",""],[1,"210","2","Informal Settlement Integration Programme","Key focuses include financial autonomy for local governments, smart infrastructure, affordable housing, and the integration of informal settlements.",""],[1,"211","1","Affordable Energy-Efficient Housing and Slum Regularization","The plan also emphasizes affordable, energy-efficient housing, and the regularization and integration of slum areas and Katchi Abadis.",""],[1,"211","11","Smart and Sustainable Financing for Adequate Housing and Services","Establish Smart and Sustainable Financing for Adequate Housing and Services",""],[1,"211","15","Informal Settlement Regularization and Inclusionary Housing Initiative","Initiate regularization, improvement, and integration of informal settlements (Katchi Abadies) through self-help approaches and a land readjustment model, while concurrently launching inclusionary housing initiatives.",""],[1,"211","16","Government Servants Housing Facility and Monetization Scheme","Provision of Housing Facility for Government servants including monetization of housing facility to encourage home ownership",""],[1,"211","17","Affordable Housing Provision for Low- and Middle-Income Groups","Provision of affordable housing for low-middle income groups through Workers Welfare Fund/EOBI/Cooperative Housing Societies;",""],[1,"211","18","Government Land Regeneration and Mega Housing Projects","Regeneration/revitalization of prime government land and construction of Mega Housing Projects on PPP mode;",""],[1,"211","19","Subsidized Housing for Low-Income Families","Provision of subsidized housing for the poorest of the poor/low income families through Bait-ul-mal/Zakat Fund;",""],[1,"211","20","Innovative Housing Finance Housing Programmes","Building together Housing Programmes based on innovative housing finance models.",""],[1,"211","21","Revision of the National Housing Policy","Revision of National Housing Policy by Ministry of Housing and Works in construction with all stakeholders","Ministry of Housing and Works"],[1,"212","10","National Housing Policy Revision and Housing Reform Package","The strategy seeks to revise the National Housing Policy by integrating global best practices in co-housing and affordable housing, prioritizing inclusivity, sustainability, and community-driven development.",""],[1,"212","10","Urban Land Management Policy Framework","Urban land management policies will be introduced, encouraging provincial governments to conduct comprehensive land and housing appraisals.",""],[1,"212","10","Property Records, Transfer, and Building Regulation Streamlining","Streamlined property records, transfer procedures, and building regulations will be implemented, along with various housing initiatives, drawing from global experiences in addressing housing shortages, especially innovative finance models and regulatory frameworks.",""],[1,"212","11","Katchi Abadies Regularization and Improvement Initiative","The strategy aims to improve livability standards by spearheading the regularization/improvement of Katchi Abadies",""],[1,"212","11","Inclusionary Housing Initiative","championing inclusionary housing initiatives",""],[1,"212","11","Subsidized Housing Program","subsidized housing programs",""],[1,"213","1","Mega Housing Projects","mega housing projects will be undertaken, implementing reforms under the National Housing Policy to ensure housing for all.",""],[1,"215","1","National Housing Policy Redefinition","Redefine the National Housing Policy with co-housing and affordable housing innovations.",""],[1,"215","1","Urban Land Management Policy Reform","Forge urban land management policies for visionary progress.",""],[1,"215","1","Provincial Land and Housing Appraisal Initiative","Galvanize provincial governments for comprehensive land and housing appraisals.",""],[1,"215","1","Property Transfer and Building Regulation Streamlining","Unveil streamlined property ceding div procedures, transfer records, and building regulations.",""],[1,"215","1","Diverse Housing Initiatives","Unleash diverse housing initiatives for a dynamic future.",""],[1,"215","3","Katchi Abadies Regularization and Improvement","Spearhead regularization/ improvement of Katchi Abadies.",""],[1,"215","3","Inclusionary Housing Initiative","Champion Inclusionary Housing Initiative and subsidized housing programs.",""],[1,"215","3","Subsidized Housing Programs","Champion Inclusionary Housing Initiative and subsidized housing programs.",""],[1,"215","3","Government Servant Housing","Pioneer economic recovery initiatives, government servant housing, and mega housing Revised National Housing Policy and enforce reforms from the National Housing Policy.",""],[1,"215","3","Mega Housing Development","Pioneer economic recovery initiatives, government servant housing, and mega housing Revised National Housing Policy and enforce reforms from the National Housing Policy.",""],[1,"215","3","Revised National Housing Policy Reform","Revised National Housing Policy and enforce reforms from the National Housing Policy.",""],[1,"215","3","National Housing Policy Reform Enforcement","Revised National Housing Policy and enforce reforms from the National Housing Policy.",""]],"123":[[1,"213","3","Urban Environmental Mainstreaming and Regulatory Reform","The strategy involves integrating environmental considerations into all development plans, refining legislations and regulatory bodies related to urban environmental quality.",""],[1,"213","3","Provincial and Local Urban Quality Investment Support","Extensive investments by provincial governments and local administrations will be encouraged to improve urban quality.",""],[1,"213","3","Green Infrastructure and Green Financing Promotion","Integrate environmental considerations into development plans, refine legislation, encourage investments in urban quality, and reference international standards while emphasizing green infrastructure and green financing.",""],[1,"213","8","Urban Revitalization and Inclusive Economic Development Programme","Initiate Urban Revitalization and Inclusive Economic Development: The strategy aims to initiate programs fostering microfinancing, nurturing informal economic activities, enhancing education, and rejuvenating brownfield areas within cities.",""],[1,"213","9","Sustainable Urban Densification and Transit-Oriented Development","This strategy encourages densification in low- density urban areas and high-rise development along transit routes.",""],[1,"215","8","Mainstream Environmental Considerations in Development Planning","Weave environmental considerations into every development canvas.",""],[1,"215","8","Urban Environmental Regulatory Reform","Refine legislations and regulatory bodies for urban environmental brilliance.",""],[1,"215","8","Provincial and Local Urban Quality Investment Initiative","Inspire significant investments from provincial governments and local administrations in elevating urban quality.",""],[1,"216","12","Urban Densification and Transit-Oriented Development","Encourage densification in low- density urban areas and high- routes. along transit",""],[1,"216","12","Climate-Resilient Urban Materials and Recycling Initiative","Harness modern technologies, recycling, and sustainable material management for climate-resilient urban forms.",""]],"124":[[1,"212","5","Sustainable Urban Development Fund","Establish a sustainable urban development fund and to provide financing for at least 10 projects from integrated participatory city/district-level development plan",""],[1,"213","4","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Housing and Infrastructure Development","To enhance resource flow and efficiency, the strategy focuses on elevating the landscape for private sector engagement in housing and infrastructure development.",""],[1,"214","2","Sustainable Urban Development Fund","The strategy involves establishing a Sustainable Urban Development Fund to provide partial finance for projects from Integrated Participatory City/District level Development Plans.",""],[1,"214","2","Private Sector Participation in Urban Housing and Services","Creating an enabling environment for private sector involvement in increasing access to adequate housing and urban services is a key focus, examining international models of sustainable urban financing and private sector involvement.",""],[1,"215","11","Private Sector Engagement in Housing and Infrastructure Development","Elevate the landscape for private sector engagement in housing and infrastructure development.",""],[1,"215","11","Resource Flow Efficiency Improvement","Ensure a seamless flow of resources for maximum efficiency.",""],[1,"216","15","Sustainable Urban Development Fund","Establish a Sustainable Urban Development Fund.",""]],"125":[[1,"211","23","Safe Cities Designation Programme","Approve 05 cities as safe cities, ensuring enhanced safety and security for residents.",""],[1,"213","5","Urban Security and Safety Strategy","Ensure Urban Security and Safety: The strategy adopts approaches similar to the safe city project, aiming to reduce violence and crime.",""],[1,"216","1","Safe City Project","Enact strategies akin to the safe city project, quelling violence and crime.",""],[1,"223","3","Safe City Projects","Safe City Projects: These projects will deploy integrated surveillance systems, Al- based analytics, and emergency response mechanisms in major urban centers.",""]],"126":[[1,"217","1","CPEC Expansion Through Five New Corridors","During the next five years, bilateral cooperation between China and Pakistan will be deepen by incorporation of five new corridors in the CPEC which will be aligned with Pakistan's national economic plan.",""],[1,"217","2","CPEC 2.0 Strategic Corridor Framework","The second phase of CPEC aims to broaden bilateral cooperation in industrialization, agriculture, socio-economic uplift, science and technology collaboration, and digital transformation.",""],[1,"218","6","CPEC Strategic Alignment Dialogue","CPEC's future direction is being shaped by strategic dialogue.",""],[1,"218","7","Regional Connectivity Enhancement","The Plan aims to drive a diversified, inclusive, and sustainable economic transformation by enhancing regional connectivity",""],[1,"218","7","Strategic Cooperation with China","The Plan aims to drive a diversified, inclusive, and sustainable economic transformation ... all through deepened strategic cooperation with China",""],[1,"220","5","CPEC 2.0 Dual-Framework Implementation","The effective execution of CPEC 2.0 has strategic coherence between national development objectives and bilateral cooperation structures.",""]],"127":[[1,"218","7","IT and Technological Innovation Strengthening","The Plan aims to drive a diversified, inclusive, and sustainable economic transformation by enhancing regional connectivity, promoting climate-resilient agriculture, export-led growth through industrial diversification, advancing clean energy, and strengthening IT and technological innovation all through deepened strategic cooperation with China, aligned with the 5Es Framework and national development priorities.",""],[1,"219","3","Digital Infrastructure, AI, and E-Government Development","Transform Pakistan into a regional technology hub through digital infrastructure, Al, and e-government.",""],[1,"219","4","Innovation Corridor Fiber Optics and 5G Connectivity Development","Develop high-capacity fiber optics and 5G connectivity under the Innovation Corridor.",""],[1,"219","4","Pakistan-China AI and Blockchain Research Hubs","Launch Pakistan-China Al & Blockchain Research Hubs and Smart Digital Infrastructure Programs.",""],[1,"219","4","Digital Literacy, Fintech Integration, and E-Commerce Capacity Building","Expand digital literacy, fintech integration, and e-commerce capacity building.",""],[1,"223","1","IT Capacity-Building in AI, Big Data, and Cybersecurity","Targeted training programs will develop a new generation of Pakistani tech professionals in collaboration with Chinese institutions.",""],[1,"223","17","Digital Infrastructure Projects","Digital Infrastructure Projects: Establishment of high-quality data centers, optical fiber backbones, and smart energy grids.",""],[1,"223","18","Software, Cloud, and Big Data Joint Ventures","Software, Cloud, and Big Data Joint Ventures: Promotion of cross-border collaboration in emerging digital industries to enhance productivity and innovation.",""],[1,"224","1","Cybersecurity and Spectrum Management Cooperation","Cybersecurity and Spectrum Management Cooperation: Strengthening national capabilities in cybersecurity, spectrum allocation, and regulatory oversight.",""],[1,"224","2","Digital Sector Talent Development Programme","Talent Development in the Digital Sector: Collaborative educational programs to train youth in programming, electronics, and advanced computing.",""],[1,"224","3","Industrial Cooperation for Semiconductor and Electronics Manufacturing","Industrial Cooperation in Semiconductors and Electronics: Connecting industrial associations to promote local manufacturing of consumer electronics and semiconductor components.",""],[1,"224","8","Cybersecurity Strengthening and Digital Talent Development","Cybersecurity will be strengthened via joint agreements, local data storage, and digital talent development.",""]],"128":[[1,"218","7","Climate-Resilient Agriculture Promotion","The Plan aims to drive a diversified, inclusive, and sustainable economic transformation by enhancing regional connectivity, promoting climate-resilient agriculture, export-led growth through industrial diversification, advancing clean energy, and strengthening IT and technological innovation all through deepened strategic cooperation with China, aligned with the 5Es Framework and national development priorities.",""],[1,"218","7","Clean Energy Advancement","The Plan aims to drive a diversified, inclusive, and sustainable economic transformation by enhancing regional connectivity, promoting climate-resilient agriculture, export-led growth through industrial diversification, advancing clean energy, and strengthening IT and technological innovation all through deepened strategic cooperation with China, aligned with the 5Es Framework and national development priorities.",""],[1,"219","9","EV Infrastructure Development","Establishment of EV infrastructure in collaboration with Chinese companies.",""],[1,"219","9","Industrial and Building Energy Efficiency Programme","Foster energy efficiency in industry and buildings, with carbon credit integration mechanisms.",""],[1,"220","3","Green Corridor Climate Mainstreaming for CPEC Projects","Embed climate change mitigation and adaptation into all CPEC projects through the Green Corridor.",""],[1,"220","4","Green Building Codes and Climate-Resilient Agriculture Promotion","Promote green building codes, smart irrigation, and climate resilient agriculture.",""],[1,"220","4","Biodiversity Conservation and Sustainable Agriculture Support","Support biodiversity conservation, and sustainable agriculture.",""],[1,"220","4","Carbon Credit Development and Trading Institutional Strengthening","Strengthen institutions to develop and trade carbon credits under global schemes.",""],[1,"224","7","CPEC 2.0 Risk Management Framework","A comprehensive risk management framework is vital for the successful implementation of CPEC 2.0, which spans strategic sectors such as infrastructure, energy, industrialization, agriculture, digital economy, and socio-economic development.",""],[1,"224","8","Green Standards and Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Enforcement","Environmental risks will be countered by enforcing green standards, climate-resilient infrastructure, and carbon trading frameworks.",""]],"129":[[1,"219","10","Interlink Road Construction for Logistics and Mobility","Construct interlink roads to strengthen intra-country and cross-border logistics and mobility to support trade and economic integration.",""],[1,"219","11","Completion of Key National Infrastructure Projects","Complete key infrastructure including Sukkur- Hyderabad Motorway (M-6), Main Line-1 (ML-1) Railway Upgrade, Fully Operationalization of Gwadar Port and extension of the Gwadar Port.",""],[1,"219","11","Gwadar Port Operationalization and Transit Trade Hub Development","Operationalize Gwadar port to make it transit trade hub",""],[1,"219","11","New Corridor Feasibility and Construction Programme","Launch feasibilities followed by construction of new corridors: Mirpur-Muzaffarabad-Mansehra, D.I. Khan-Zhob, Babusar Tunnel etc.",""],[1,"219","11","Digital Customs and Logistics Modernization","Enhance digital customs systems and logistics services at key ports.",""],[1,"221","3","Large-Scale Transport, Logistics, and Communication Infrastructure Development","Over the five-year period, priority will be given to large-scale transport, logistics, and communication infrastructure.",""],[1,"221","11","Hongqilav-Sust Border Facilities Upgrade","Hongqilav-Sust Border Facilities Upgrade: This project will support year-round trade via the Khunjerab Pass by modernizing customs and logistical facilities at the border.",""],[1,"221","12","Gwadar Port Operationalization and Transshipment Infrastructure Development","Efforts will be made to operationalize Gwadar port and development of shipbuilding yards and transshipment infrastructure will unlock Pakistan's maritime economic potential, creating jobs and boosting export revenues.",""]],"130":[[1,"218","5","CPEC Phase I Human Capital Development","Human capital development has been a key outcome: 25,000 Pakistani students are studying in China, and around 200,000 direct jobs were created under CPEC Phase I across sectors including engineering, transport, construction, and energy.",""],[1,"220","2","Vocational Training Expansion under the Livelihood Corridor","Expand vocational training, particularly for youth and women, under the Livelihood Corridor.",""],[1,"220","2","Cross-Sector Collaboration for Education, Rural Health, and Industrial Skills","Foster collaboration in education, Rural Health :unselected:\n:unselected:\nOutreach, and Industrial Skills Enhancement Programs.",""],[1,"220","2","Localized Water, Sanitation, and Rural Infrastructure Development","Ensure equitable access to water, sanitation, and rural development through localized infrastructure.",""],[1,"224","8","Social Inclusion Through Skills, Health, Education, and Regional Investment","Social inclusion will be promoted through vocational training, healthcare, education initiatives, and equitable regional investment.",""]],"131":[[1,"221","14","Siahdik Copper Downstream Processing Project","Siahdik Copper Project: Project aim to develop downstream processing unit for value addition.",""],[1,"222","1","Saindak Copper-Gold Project Expansion","Saindak Copper-Gold Project Expansion: Enhancing the output capacity and mineral processing capability of the Saindak project to increase Pakistan's copper and gold exports.",""],[1,"222","2","Duddar Zinc-Lead Mine Development","Duddar Zinc-Lead Mine Development: Strengthening the domestic supply of zinc and lead while generating employment in Balochistan.",""],[1,"222","3","Long-Term Mining Cooperation Framework","Long-Term Mining Cooperation Framework: The two countries will undertake joint geological surveys, invest in modern mining technologies, and initiate large-scale training programs to develop human capital in the extractive industries.",""]],"132":[[1,"222","7","Center for Sustainable Control of Plant Pests and Diseases","The creation of this center will enable better pest surveillance and management systems, reducing agricultural losses and improving productivity.",""],[1,"222","8","Scholarships for Agricultural Training in China","1,000 Scholarships for Agricultural Training in China: Human resource development in precision agriculture, seed technology, and agribusiness will be fostered through these scholarships.",""],[1,"222","9","China-Pakistan Technical Working Group on Agriculture","China-Pakistan Technical Working Group on Agriculture: This institutional mechanism will promote collaborative research in hybrid seed development, agri- mechanization, biotechnology, and corporate farming models.",""],[1,"222","11","China-Pakistan Earth Science Research Center","China-Pakistan Earth Science Research Center: This multidisciplinary research hub will focus on climate change, seismic activity, resource mapping, and disaster resilience.",""],[1,"222","12","Joint Participation in the Belt and Road Laboratory for Disaster Prevention","Five Pakistani universities will partner in cross-border knowledge exchange on intelligent disaster monitoring systems.",""],[1,"222","13","Joint Biotechnology Labs for Wheat and Cotton Breeding","Joint Biotechnology Labs for Wheat and Cotton Breeding: These labs will develop climate-resilient and high-yielding crop varieties to enhance national food security.",""],[1,"222","14","Remote Sensing Ground Station","Remote Sensing Ground Station in Karachi: This facility will enable real-time satellite data monitoring for environmental, agricultural, and disaster-related applications.",""],[1,"223","13","Participation in Belt and Road Science Alliances","Pakistani universities and think tanks will be encouraged to join science alliances to enhance research partnerships.",""],[1,"223","14","China-Pakistan Technology Transfer Matchmaking Conference","China-Pakistan Technology Transfer Matchmaking Conference: A major platform for linking Pakistani startups and R&D institutions with Chinese investors and firms.",""]],"133":[[1,"223","4","Security Infrastructure Upgrades for Intelligence Agencies","Security Infrastructure for Intelligence Agencies: Office and technological upgrades will enhance coordination and situational awareness across law enforcement agencies.",""],[1,"223","5","China-Pakistan Joint Security Venture","China-Pakistan Joint Security Venture: A public-private partnership will deliver surveillance, protection, and risk assessment services for key installations.",""],[1,"223","6","Mobile Scanning and Protective Vehicles","Mobile Scanning and Protective Vehicles: These assets will safeguard border checkpoints, energy corridors, and critical urban infrastructure.",""],[1,"224","7","Safe City Projects and Dedicated Protection Units","To mitigate these, joint security mechanisms, including Safe City Projects and dedicated protection units, will safeguard infrastructure and personnel.",""]],"134":[[1,"218","8","Strengthen Institutional, Financial, and Technological Cooperation with Chinese Institutions","Strengthen institutional, financial, and technological ties with Chinese institutions to accelerate joint development projects.",""],[1,"218","9","Expand Joint Cooperation Committee Sessions","Expand scope of Joint Cooperation Committee (JCC) sessions to cover emerging sectors.",""],[1,"218","9","Improve Investment Treaty and Regulatory Frameworks","Enhance bilateral investment treaties and streamline regulatory frameworks to encourage Chinese private sector investment in Pakistan.",""],[1,"224","4","CPEC Institutional and Governance Framework Upgrade","The cornerstone of CPEC's institutional architecture is the Joint Cooperation Committee (JCC), which will be upgraded to a more integrated framework with inclusion of new working groups.",""],[1,"224","6","Weekly Progress Review and Performance Reporting System","Weekly progress reviews and performance reports continued to ensure responsiveness, course correction, and knowledge sharing.",""],[1,"224","6","CPEC Secretariat Coordination and Digital Monitoring Reform","The CPEC Secretariat will continue to serve as the central coordinating body within the Government of Pakistan.",""],[1,"224","7","Restructured Joint Cooperation Committee","Institutional reforms like a restructured Joint Cooperation Committee and real-time digital monitoring will streamline governance and project delivery.",""],[1,"224","7","Real-Time Digital Monitoring System","Institutional reforms like a restructured Joint Cooperation Committee and real-time digital monitoring will streamline governance and project delivery.",""],[1,"224","8","Transparency, Audit, and Community Engagement Mechanism","Transparent communications, third-party audits, and community engagement will build trust and prevent reputational damage.",""],[1,"224","9","CPEC Phase II Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","A well-structured and transparent Monitoring & Evaluation (M&E) Framework is critical to ensuring the effective implementation of CPEC Phase II.",""],[1,"225","1","CPEC Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","the M&E Framework is designed to track progress, measure results, and ensure alignment with Pakistan's national development priorities, particularly the 5Es and CPEC's guiding principles of the 5Cs.",""],[1,"225","2","Evidence-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","The framework will focus on promoting evidence-based decision-making, enhancing cooperation and enabling timely corrective actions.",""],[1,"225","3","CPEC Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","the M&E Framework will play a pivotal role in sustaining momentum, ensuring transparency, and reinforcing CPEC's role as a catalyst for economic growth, regional connectivity, and inclusive development.",""]],"135":[[1,"223","9","Women's Health Workstations","Women's Health Workstations: Establishment of maternal and reproductive health units in underserved rural areas.",""],[1,"223","10","School Reconstruction in Flood-Affected Sindh","School Reconstruction in Flood-Affected Sindh: Education infrastructure will be restored with modern facilities to ensure continuity of learning in disaster-prone areas.",""],[1,"223","11","Housing Rehabilitation for Disaster Victims","Housing Rehabilitation for Disaster Victims: Reconstruction support will be provided for communities affected by climate-induced disasters.",""]],"136":[[1,"230","5","Unified Social Protection and Poverty Alleviation Framework","All major social protection initiatives in Pakistan-BISP, TVO, PBM and PPAF-are unified under the Ministry of Poverty Alleviation and Social Safety (PASS), which oversees poverty reduction food and shelter access, livelihood promotion and human capital investment nationwide.","Ministry of Poverty Alleviation and Social Safety (PASS)"],[1,"230","5","Benazir Kafaalat Cash Transfer Programme","Key programs include Benazir Kafaalat, providing Rs. 8,750 quarterly to 9 million poor women along with bank and mobile access;",""],[1,"230","5","Benazir Nashonuma Nutrition Support Programme","Benazir Nashonuma, tackling malnutrition via 488 centres across 156 districts for 769,000 beneficiaries;",""],[1,"230","5","Benazir Taleemi Wazaif Education Stipend Programme","Benazir Taleemi Wazaif, supporting 11.45 million students from grades 1-12;",""],[1,"230","5","Benazir Undergraduate Scholarships","Benazir Undergraduate Scholarships, offering tuition coverage and Rs. 4,000 monthly to 102,000 students.",""],[1,"230","5","National Poverty Graduation Programme","The National Poverty Graduation Programme has distributed 117,060 productive assets, trained 120,730 individuals and disbursed 2.4 million interest-free loans;",""],[1,"230","5","Sehat Tahaffuz Critical Health Financing Initiative","Additionally, the Sehat Tahaffuz initiative has funded 17,785 critical health cases in 14 hospitals across all provinces.",""],[1,"231","7","Expansion of BISP Social Protection Coverage","the government has continued efforts to address these challenges through various initiatives, including the expansion of BISP social protection coverage.",""],[1,"232","8","BISP Coverage Expansion and Targeting Improvement","Expand BISP coverage with improved targeting mechanisms using digital platforms.",""],[1,"232","8","Graduation Strategy Through Conditional Cash Transfers","Implement graduation strategies through conditional cash transfers and integrate existing programs to avoid duplication under M/o PASS.","M/o PASS"],[1,"233","8","Integrated Social Protection System","Integrated Social Protection System including BISP and integrate conditional cash transfers (e.g., Nashonuma, Taleemi Wazaif)",""],[1,"233","18","Digitized Poverty Registry and NSER Data Integration","Digitize poverty registry and integrate NSER data for targeted intervention",""]],"137":[[1,"230","8","Boosted PSDP Allocations","Boosted PSDP allocations to create jobs, improve infrastructure and promote equitable resource distribution.",""],[1,"231","1","Expanded Access to Education Support Measures","Expanded access to education via endowment funds, nutrition programs and health insurance schemes.",""],[1,"231","2","Youth Skills Development and Self-Employment Support","Strengthened poverty alleviation through youth skill development, self-employment schemes, microcredit programs via PPAF, RSPN, and SME support through improved energy supply.",""],[1,"232","2","Multi-sectoral Poverty Reduction Strategy","To reduce poverty and inequality through a multi-sectoral, regionally balanced and climate- resilient strategy, there will be emphasis on rural uplift, productive employment generation, digital inclusion and strengthened social protection.",""],[1,"232","2","Integrated Poverty Exit Pathways Package","Special focus will be placed on integrating macro-economic stability, export promotion, remittance facilitation, educational reform and healthcare investment to create sustainable pathways out of poverty.",""],[1,"232","2","Coordinated Inclusive Development Mechanism","Recognizing poverty as a cross-cutting challenge, the strategy aims to ensure coordinated and inclusive development by synchronizing efforts across agriculture, industry, trade, infrastructure, education, health and environment, ensuring no one is left behind.",""],[1,"232","3","Integrated Poverty Reduction Strategy","Pakistan aims to reduce CBN-based poverty from 21.9 percent to 15 percent by 2029 through coordinated efforts led by the MoPD&SI and provincial governments during the 2024-2029 period.","MoPD&SI | provincial governments"],[1,"232","3","Multidimensional Poverty Reduction Target","Simultaneously, the target is to lower the multidimensional poverty headcount from 30.5 percent to 25 percent by 2029.",""],[1,"232","3","Social Safety Nets and Social Protection Schemes","Key initiatives such as social safety nets, skill development programs, macroeconomic stability, infrastructure improvement, digital connectivity, and regional equalization play a crucial role in addressing its root causes.",""],[1,"232","3","Skill Development Programmes","Key initiatives such as social safety nets, skill development programs, macroeconomic stability, infrastructure improvement, digital connectivity, and regional equalization play a crucial role in addressing its root causes.",""],[1,"232","3","Infrastructure Improvement Investments","Investments in infrastructure and digital access open new economic opportunities, particularly in underserved regions.",""],[1,"232","3","Digital Connectivity Expansion","Investments in infrastructure and digital access open new economic opportunities, particularly in underserved regions.",""],[1,"232","3","Regional Equalization Measures","Key initiatives such as social safety nets, skill development programs, macroeconomic stability, infrastructure improvement, digital connectivity, and regional equalization play a crucial role in addressing its root causes.",""],[1,"232","5","Pro-Poor Public Sector Investment Expansion","Boost pro-poor public sector investment i.e. PSDP, especially in underdeveloped areas and expand targeted fiscal policies while reducing regressive taxation.",""],[1,"232","5","Targeted Fiscal Policy Expansion","Boost pro-poor public sector investment i.e. PSDP, especially in underdeveloped areas and expand targeted fiscal policies while reducing regressive taxation.",""],[1,"234","1","Poverty Alleviation Coordination Council Operationalization","Operationalize Poverty Alleviation Coordination Council (PACC) for federal-provincial alignment",""],[1,"234","2","Inclusive Public-Private Partnerships for PSDP Projects","Promote inclusive public-private partnerships in PSDP projects to support lagging regions",""],[1,"234","15","CSR-Based Poverty Reduction Initiative","Channelize CSR initiatives for poverty reduction in consultation with the private sector",""]],"138":[[1,"233","2","Female Labor Force Participation Support Measures","Promote female labor force participation through training and access to credit.",""],[1,"233","2","Workplace Safety and Accessibility Measures","Ensure safety and accessibility in workplaces.",""],[1,"233","3","Microfinance and Digital Banking Expansion","Expand microfinance and digital banking services targeting rural poor.",""],[1,"233","3","Youth Entrepreneurship Incubators","Establish incubators for youth entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"233","10","Self-Employment Support through Finance, Incubators, and Interest-Free Loans","Promote self-employment through access to finance, incubators, and interest-free loans",""],[1,"233","14","Youth and Women Skills Development and Vocational Training","Strengthen skill development and vocational training for youth and women",""]],"139":[[1,"233","4","Disaster Management Authority Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen DMAs' capacity to manage disasters with special focus on vulnerable populations.",""],[1,"233","4","Nature-Based Climate Resilience Solutions","Promote nature-based solutions and livelihood protection in climate-affected areas.",""]],"140":[[1,"234","4","Poverty Data Systems and MPI/CBN Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","Improve poverty data systems and strengthen MPI/CBN-based monitoring and evaluation",""],[1,"236","1","Plan Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","Monitoring and evaluation mechanisms should be strengthened to track progress, identify gaps, and adapt strategies as needed to ensure the plan's success in the long run.",""]],"141":[[1,"236","10","ICPD Beyond 2030 Progress Monitoring Committee","The Five-Year Plan outlines robust monitoring mechanisms, including the ICPD beyond 2030 Progress Monitoring Committee.",""],[1,"237","3","Population Growth Governance Mechanisms","Develop political ownership and robust governance mechanisms to manage population growth rate.",""],[1,"237","5","Multi-Level Program Implementation Strengthening","Ensure effective program implementation at the District, Tehsil, UC, and village levels.",""],[1,"237","6","Development Partner and Private Sector Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen partnership and involvement of development partners and the private sector.",""],[1,"237","7","Multi-Sectoral FPRH Systems Strengthening","Enable systems through legislation, awareness, implementation accountability, and sustained impact through a multi-sectoral approach for FPRH.",""],[1,"238","7","Federation-Province Coordination on Population and Family Planning","The consensus and coordination between the federation and provinces to resolve the population and family planning issues will be improved to activate their roles within the limits of devolution.",""],[1,"238","8","Cross-Sectoral Population Management Integration","The Plan aims to recognize population as a cross sectoral subject by integrating the population management across the 13 thematic areas",""],[1,"238","10","Integrated Multi-Sectoral Population Framework","Central to this strategy is the operationalization of an Integrated Multi-Sectoral Population Framework, developed through broad-based consultations with provinces, special areas, and key stakeholders.",""],[1,"241","3","Integrated Multi-Sectoral Population Framework","Develop and Operationalise Integrated Multi-Sectoral Population Framework",""],[1,"241","6","National Strategy Finalization and Embedding Process","Finalize, launch, and begin embedding into national strategies.",""]],"142":[[1,"238","11","Multi-Sectoral National Knowledge Hub and Data Portal","the plan emphasizes the establishment of a Multi-Sectoral National Knowledge Hub and Data Portal.",""],[1,"238","11","Use of NTA and NTTA Findings for Gender-Responsive and Youth-Inclusive Economic Policy","The dissemination and use of NTA and NTTA findings will promote gender-responsive and youth- inclusive economic policies by highlighting lifecycle deficits, unpaid care work, and consumption patterns.",""],[1,"238","12","Progress Monitoring Committee for ICPD","the plan will institutionalize a Progress Monitoring Committee for ICPD beyond 2030.",""],[1,"241","10","Multi-Sectoral National Knowledge Hub and Data Portal","Establishment of Multi-Sectoral National Knowledge Hub & Data Portal",""],[1,"241","11","Design Hub/Portal Feasibility and Finalization","Design Hub/Portal: Complete feasibility & finalize design.",""],[1,"241","18","Findings Dissemination Workshops","Disseminate Findings: Conduct workshops; disseminate NTA/NTTA findings.",""],[1,"241","19","Planning Integration and Analysis Capacity Building","Integrate insights into planning; build analysis capacity.",""],[1,"241","20","Economic Policy Adjustment Based on Findings","Apply findings to adjust economic policies.",""],[1,"241","22","Institutionalize NTA/NTTA Use for Ongoing Analysis","Institutionalize NTA/NTTA use for ongoing analysis.",""],[1,"241","31","Progress Monitoring Committee for ICPD","Institutionalize Progress Monitoring Committee for ICPD beyond 2030",""],[1,"241","33","Annual Review and Initial Reporting Mechanism","Conduct first annual review; prepare initial report.",""]],"143":[[1,"239","1","International Knowledge Exchange Forums and Conferences","International knowledge exchange will be promoted through high-level forums and conferences that bring together experts and practitioners to share innovative solutions and best practices.",""],[1,"239","2","Increase Domestic Financing for Population and Family Planning Programs","Domestic investment in population and family planning programs will be increased, while reliance on donor funding will be reduced to ensure program resilience and long-term impact.",""],[1,"239","2","Strengthen National and Provincial Implementation Capacity","Institutional capacities at national and provincial levels will be strengthened to drive effective implementation of these strategies, ensuring that Pakistan stays on course to achieve its population and development goals by 2030.",""],[1,"239","5","Master-Trainer and Trainer Capacity Development","Strengthening and developing a skilled cadre of master-trainers and trainers",""],[1,"241","38","Planning Forums and International Engagement","Plan forums; establish international engagement.",""],[1,"241","40","Expert Network Expansion and Collaboration Initiative","Expand expert networks; foster collaborations",""],[1,"241","42","Global Learning Mechanisms Institutionalization","Institutionalize global learning mechanisms.",""],[1,"241","46","Fiscal Analysis and Advocacy","Analyse & Advocate: Conduct fiscal analysis; advocate for",""],[1,"242","5","Initial Training and Support Programme","Initial Training: Implement initial training & support.",""]],"144":[[1,"244","8","Integration of RH/FP Content into University Curricula and Extracurricular Platforms","Integrate RH/FP content into university curricula & extracurricular platforms",""],[1,"244","10","Reproductive Health and Family Planning Module Development and University Pilot","Develop RH/FP modules; pilot in universities.",""],[1,"244","12","University Integration Expansion and Resource Support","Expand integration to more universities; provide resources.",""],[1,"244","14","RH/FP Education Institutionalization","Institutionalize RH/FP education.",""]],"145":[[1,"248","9","NCD and Mental Health Prevention, Diagnosis, and Management","Enhance prevention, diagnosis, and management of NCDs and mental health.",""],[1,"250","2","National Non-Communicable Disease Response Programs","Implement national response programs for hepatitis, diabetes, cardiovascular diseases, cancers, and chronic respiratory illnesses across all care levels",""],[1,"250","2","Free Treatment Pathways for Hepatitis, Diabetes, and Cardiac Stents","Ensure free treatment pathways for hepatitis, diabetes, and cardiac stents, especially in high-burden districts",""],[1,"250","2","Integrated Mental Health and Detox Services in Primary Care","Integrate mental health services into PHC, with detox centres and counselling in conflict-affected zones",""],[1,"250","2","Tobacco, Diet, and Pollution Control Enforcement","Enforce tobacco, diet, and pollution control regulations",""],[1,"250","2","National Public Awareness and Stigma Reduction Campaigns","Launch public awareness and stigma reduction campaigns nationwide",""]],"146":[[1,"248","12","Health Information and Research Systems Strengthening","Ensure availability of accurate health information and strengthen research systems.",""],[1,"251","2","DHIS2 Expansion to Private and Tertiary Levels","Expand DHIS2 to private/tertiary levels",""],[1,"251","5","Health Staff Data Validation and Use Training","Train health staff on data validation/use",""],[1,"251","5","CRVS and Health Survey Strengthening","Strengthen CRVS and health surveys",""],[1,"251","5","Local Research and One Health Studies Promotion","Promote local research and One Health studies",""]],"147":[[1,"248","13","Essential Medicines, Diagnostics, Supplies, and Health Technologies Access Guarantee","Guarantee access to quality medicines, diagnostics, supplies, and health technologies.",""],[1,"251","8","Health Commodities Supply Chain Improvement","Improve supply chains for medicines, vaccines, contraceptives, and reagents",""],[1,"251","13","Anti-Counterfeit Drug Regulation Enforcement","Enforce anti-counterfeit drug regulations",""],[1,"251","13","Antimicrobial Resistance Monitoring and Rational Drug Use Promotion","Monitor AMR and promote rational drug use",""],[1,"251","15","Local Vaccine and Medical Supplies Manufacturing Support","Support local manufacturing of vaccines and medical supplies",""]],"148":[[1,"248","14","Health Governance, Leadership, and Accountability Strengthening","Strengthen health governance, leadership, and accountability at all levels.",""],[1,"248","15","Inter-sectoral Health Coordination and Social Determinants Action","Promote inter-sectoral coordination and address the social determinants of health.",""],[1,"251","22","Human Resources, Finance, and Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Expansion","Expand HR, finance, M&E capacity",""],[1,"251","22","Public Health Law Enforcement","Enforce public health laws (tobacco, food safety, organ donation)",""],[1,"251","27","One Health and Health in All Policies Institutionalization","Institutionalize One Health and Health in All Policies EN - Align with education, WASH, food security, climate - Engage communities and local govts in planning - Integrate gender and equity monitoring tools",""]],"149":[[1,"248","17","Global Health Obligations and IHR Compliance Capacity Building","Build core capacities for global health obligations and compliance with International Health Regulations (IHR).",""],[1,"248","18","National Health Emergency Preparedness and Response Systems","Enhance health emergency preparedness and response systems nationwide.",""],[1,"249","3","Disease Prevention, Hygiene Promotion, and Infection Control Reinforcement","Reinforce disease prevention, hygiene promotion, and infection control",""],[1,"249","3","National Health Awareness and Behavioural Change Media Campaign","Launch a national health awareness and behavioural change media campaign promoting hygiene, prevention, and early care-seeking in rural and urban communities",""],[1,"252","7","International Health Regulations Compliance and Health Security Integration","Ensure International Health Regulations (IHR) compliance.",""],[1,"252","7","Rapid Response and Disaster Risk Reduction Team Training","Train rapid response and Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) teams",""],[1,"252","7","Health Security Integration into National Planning","Integrate health security into national planning",""],[1,"252","12","National Disease Surveillance Scale-Up","Scale up national disease surveillance Upgrade, labs and Points of Entry (PoE)",""],[1,"252","16","Quarantine and Contingency Plan Operationalization","facilities Operationalize quarantine and contingency plans",""]],"150":[[1,"250","7","Women Medical Officer and Rural Workforce Incentives","Expand Women Medical Officer (WMO) & rural workforce incentives",""],[1,"250","7","LHV and Nursing Production Expansion","Double LHV/nursing production",""],[1,"250","7","Health Human Resources Registry and Forecasting System","Establish HR registry and forecasting system",""],[1,"250","7","Licensure and Accreditation Enforcement for Public and Private NMEN","Enforce licensure & accreditation in public/private NMEN",""]],"151":[[1,"253","5","Nutrition Advocacy and Awareness Initiatives","Advocacy and awareness initiatives played a significant role in fostering public understanding and support for nutrition endeavours.",""],[1,"257","5","Multi-sectoral Nutrition Governance and PPP Scale-up","Strengthen multi-sectoral nutrition governance and enhance PPP to scale-up nutrition programs",""],[1,"257","17","Pakistan Multi-Sectoral Nutrition Strategy","under the umbrella and guidance of the Pakistan Multi-Sectoral Nutrition Strategy (2018-25) which has been developed following bottom-up approach defining clear roles and responsibilities.",""],[1,"257","17","Provincial Nutrition Strategy Harmonization and Action Plan","This takes care of gaps in provincial strategies and also delivers the responsibilities which fall under the national purview including incentivization of provinces and removal of inter-provincial disparities through the development of a plan of action.",""],[1,"258","9","Functional Coordination and Collaboration Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening functional coordination and collaboration mechanism",""],[1,"259","7","Cross-Network Collaboration for Nutrition Innovation","Promote cross network collaboration such as academia, industry, research institutions and civil society for innovating sustainable and cost-effective nutrition solutions",""]],"152":[[1,"257","3","Evidence-Based Nutrition Programming","Reduce the prevalence of undernutrition and micronutrient deficiencies in all population groups through evidence-based programming",""],[1,"257","7","Nutrition Program Monitoring and Evaluation Improvement","Improve monitoring and evaluation of nutrition programs for effective implementations",""],[1,"258","7","Nutrition Plan Integration into Government Performance Evaluation","Inclusion of nutrition plan into government performance evaluation",""],[1,"258","11","National Multisectoral Nutrition Research Agenda","Developing national multisectoral nutrition research agenda with focus on local cause and its local solution for sustainability and cost effectiveness including:",""],[1,"258","21","Local and Regional Cross-Learning for Program Improvement","Promote local and regional cross learning for better program design, implementation and scale up",""],[1,"260","18","Financing Tracking Tool Review and Update","Review and update the financing tracking tool, as well as conduct public expenditure review",""]],"153":[[1,"257","4","Overweight and Obesity Prevention Campaign","Halt the rise of overweight and obesity in all population groups through aggressive awareness campaigns and promoting healthy, sustainable, and diversified food",""],[1,"257","8","Food Advertising Regulation in Schools","Create conducive policy environment including the enactment of existing policies and strategies and formulation of new laws and regulations regarding emerging issues including legislation against advertisement of ultra-processed foods high in sugar, salt and fat including and junk foods within school premises",""],[1,"257","18","Nutrition Legislation and Food Regulation Package","Promote legislation and policy on nutrition, including the legislation of the BMS Act across all provinces/ areas and at federal level, mandatory food fortification bill and legislation against advertisement of ultra-processed foods high in sugar, salt and fat including ban on selling these junk foods within school premises",""],[1,"257","19","Technical Guidance on Nutrition Policies and Standards","Provide technical guidance on nutrition policies and standards",""],[1,"257","20","Food Safety Law and Standards Harmonization","Harmonize and standardize food safety laws, regulations and standards",""],[1,"259","4","Nutrition Labelling Promotion","Promote nutrition labelling of food products for informed decision-making risk reduction and resilience building for nutrition",""]],"154":[[1,"257","6","Nutrition Stakeholder Capacity and Innovation Linkage Initiative","Strengthening capacity of nutrition stakeholders and establishing linkages of Academia, Businesses, and other research institutions for nutrition innovative solutions and nutrition research, with focus on local causes and local solutions",""],[1,"257","21","Separate Nutrition Cadre Advocacy","Advocate for a separate nutrition cadre in health, education and industry etc.",""],[1,"258","6","Nutrition Programme Development and Implementation Capacity Strengthening","Capacity strengthening of both public and private sector organizations/ platforms for nutrition program development and implementation",""],[1,"258","16","Review and Scale Up Successful Nutrition Models","Review and scale up of successful local and regional nutrition models",""],[1,"258","18","Nutrition Programming Guidance Materials and Tools","Develop, adapt, and disseminate guidance materials and tools for nutrition-specific and nutrition-sensitive programming",""]],"155":[[1,"258","2","Nutrition-Responsive Multisectoral Intervention Design and Implementation","Designing and implementing nutrition responsive multisectoral nutrition interventions in WASH, Agriculture, education, social protection, population welfare and women's development sectors",""],[1,"258","3","Early Childhood Development Integration Across Social Sectors","Integrating Early Childhood Development into health, nutrition, education, WASH and social welfare/ protection programs",""],[1,"258","5","School Health, Nutrition and Meal Programmes","Designing and implementing context specific school health, nutrition and meal programs to improve health, nutrition and educational outcomes of pre-school and school age population especially girls",""],[1,"258","15","Food Value Addition and School Nutrition Programme","Food value addition to scale up program such as school nutrition/ meal and minimize seasonal impact of food insecurity",""],[1,"259","15","Early Childhood Development Policy Framework and Holistic ECD Programs","Early Childhood Development (ECD) Policy Framework and holistic ECD programs including the rollout of key family care practices across different services delivery platforms",""]],"156":[[1,"257","2","Nutrition Access and Awareness Initiative","Prevent hunger and promote appropriate nutritional practices through improved access to affordable and sustainable nutritious food and awareness",""],[1,"258","19","Nutrition Awareness Social and Behavior Change Strategy","Enhance awareness of nutrition by designing social and behavior change (SBC) strategies that target different audiences",""],[1,"258","20","Nutrition Promotion Through Influencer Engagement","Engaging influencers such as mainstream media, social media, celebrities, academia, parliamentarians, civil society alliance, religious institutions & other public and private platforms to promote nutrition",""],[1,"260","16","Mass Nutrition Advocacy and Awareness Campaign","Mass nutrition advocacy and awareness through media, engaging influencers and using other platforms such as universities etc.",""]],"157":[[1,"255","1","Olive Cultivation Promotion","Promotion of Olive cultivation",""],[1,"255","1","Sheep and Goat Development Programme","Sheep/ Goat Development Program",""],[1,"255","1","Mobile Food Testing Laboratories","The Government of GB established GB Nutrition Program, MNCH Program, Nashonuma program, Food supplementation program, CMAM Program, IYCF counselling program, Establishment of 240 ECD facilities in Government schools, Water Quality testing throughout GB, School Meal Program, a wasting management program and launched Key Family Care Practices parenting program at the community level.",""],[1,"259","1","Technical Support for Nutritious Agricultural Product Quality Improvement","Provide technical support to industries for the promotion of high-quality, nutritious agricultural products",""],[1,"259","3","Public-Private Partnership for Nutritious Food Production","Foster Public Private Partnership for local production and availability of cost effective nutritious safe and diversified food products",""]],"158":[[1,"259","6","Nutrition Preparedness and Emergency Response Strengthening","Strengthen preparedness and response for nutrition in disaster-prone districts and emergency situations",""]],"159":[[1,"264","14","Curriculum, Teacher Training, and Examination Reform","Optimize the performance of the education system through improving curriculum from rote learning to conceptual learning approaches along with reforming teacher's trainings, establishing high quality education in all schools and reforming examination system to align it with new conceptual curriculum.",""],[1,"265","3","Education System Performance Optimization Reform","The primary focus of the Plan is to optimize the performance of the education system through restructuring curriculum to make it more conceptual, revamping teachers training, providing quality teachers, promoting early childhood education and reforming examination system.",""],[1,"265","7","Continuous Professional Development for Teachers","The Plan will focus on continuous professional development programs to enhance teachers' subject knowledge, classroom management skills, use of innovative technology, values & life-skills based, making students responsible citizen, conceptual learning, critical thinking and positive reinforcement in teacher-student interactions.",""],[1,"267","15","Pre-Service Teacher Training Requirement for Induction","Pre-service training should be one of the prerequisites for induction of teachers.",""],[1,"267","19","Promotion Linked Training for Education Personnel","Promotion Linked Training (PLT) may be introduced for teachers/heads of institutions/education managers at all levels.",""]],"160":[[1,"264","15","Technology and AI Integration in Education Delivery","Incorporate technology tools and Al in education delivery and teaching methods to make education more accessible and modern.",""],[1,"265","6","Digital Education Transformation","Incorporation of technology in education delivery, such as e-learning platforms, digital records, personalized learning tools and institutionalization of digital education in the education system, supported by the necessary resources and infrastructure to facilitate a smooth digital transformation and human development.",""]],"161":[[1,"264","16","Madrasa Curriculum Mainstreaming","Ensure mainstreaming of Madrasa education by integrating body of knowledge into their syllabus.",""],[1,"265","1","Expansion and Institutionalization of Non-Formal Education","the Plan will prioritize the expansion and institutionalization of Non-Formal Education (NFE) as a parallel and complementary pathway to the formal education system.",""]],"162":[[1,"265","2","Applied Research and Academia-Industry Linkage Framework","Concerned Federal Education Ministry and Provincial / Area Governments Education Departments would develop a national framework to promote applied research and link academia with industry through incentivized grants and innovation hubs at college level education.","Federal Education Ministry | Provincial / Area Governments Education Departments"]],"163":[[1,"265","8","Education Sector Financing Increase","The Plan will prioritize substantial increases in education financing especially by the provinces, aiming to address the sector's diverse needs comprehensively.",""],[1,"267","2","Education Expenditure Increase","Government will enhance expenditure up to 5 percent of GDP on education progressively.",""],[1,"267","4","Increase Development Budgets for Basic and College Education","Federal/Provincial/Area Governments will increase their development budgets for basic & college education keeping in view the 18th Constitutional amendment.",""]],"164":[[1,"264","17","Skill-Based Education Promotion","Promote the skill-based education to enhance the relevance of basic and college education.",""],[1,"267","13","Matric Tech Scheme Introduction","Matric Tech Scheme will be introduced as per market demand in consultation with chamber of commerce and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"267","13","Curriculum Revision for Technical Education","Curriculum will be modified to introduce this scheme up to secondary level.",""],[1,"267","13","Expansion of Technical and Vocational Education Pathways","Students may be encouraged to join higher level technical and vocational education.",""],[1,"267","13","Expansion of Vocational Training and Technical Institutions","Vocational training facilities, polytechnic institutes and colleges of technology may be established on need basis.",""]],"165":[[1,"271","3","National Skills University Establishment","The establishment of the National Skills University in 2018",""],[1,"271","3","Federal and Provincial Skills Development Councils","the launch of multiple federal and provincial Skill Development Councils",""],[1,"271","3","Skills for All Strategy","the \"Skills for All\" strategy introduced in 2021 targets unskilled populations nationwide",""],[1,"273","14","Multi-Skills and Workforce Upgrading Programme","Promoting multi-skills for all to enhance their versatility, and upgrading the skills of the existing labor force from semi-skilled to skilled and skilled to highly skilled categories.",""],[1,"274","2","Sustainable Skills Development Financing Mechanism","Sustainable financing mechanisms must be established to support long-term skills development, while monitoring and evaluation systems should track performance and identify gaps.",""],[1,"274","2","Skills Development Monitoring and Evaluation System","Sustainable financing mechanisms must be established to support long-term skills development, while monitoring and evaluation systems should track performance and identify gaps.",""],[1,"274","3","Skills Development for Inclusive Economic Growth","The plan aims to promote not only employment but also inclusive and equitable economic growth through skills development.",""],[1,"274","3","Governance and Sustainable Financing for Skills System Implementation","The plan also emphasises the importance of strong governance and sustainable financing to support the effective implementation of the skills development system.",""],[1,"274","5","Modern Technical and Vocational Education Curriculum Reform","Introducing modern technical and vocational education such as Al based system, data analytics etc. in curriculum to promote entrepreneurship, especially women entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"274","9","IT-Based Skills Development for Emerging AI Economy","Provision of IT based skills keeping in view new world of Al.",""]],"166":[[1,"272","3","Gender-Responsive Migration Policy","Therefore, there is a need to devise a migration policy focusing on promoting gender-responsive recruitment to minimize challenges for women pursuing employment abroad.",""],[1,"272","3","Skills Training for International Labour Market Demand","Identifying skills in high demand in destination countries and providing training in these areas to match the needs of the international labour market.",""],[1,"273","10","Overseas Employment Policy Formulation","A comprehensive overseas employment policy should be formulated",""],[1,"273","11","Youth Overseas Employment Skills and Global Partnership Initiative","Preparing youth for overseas employment by enhancing exportable skills and building global partnerships.",""]],"167":[[1,"272","7","Informal Sector Formalization and Digital Registration Reform","To reduce informal sector activities, we may need to (i) streamline and digitize registration processes, especially for small enterprises, (ii) promote digital wallets, (iii) mobile banking and (iv)",""],[1,"273","1","POS Systems for Small Vendors and Home-Based Work Certification","POS systems for small vendors to formalize transactions and (v) recognize and certify home-based work.",""],[1,"273","8","Regulatory Framework for Employment Agencies and Labor Intermediaries","Establishing a robust regulatory framework for employment agencies and labor intermediaries is critical for efficient job matching and placement.",""],[1,"283","14","Policy for Home-Based Workers","Formulate Policy for Home-Based Workers",""]],"168":[[1,"274","1","Toolkit Provision and Entrepreneurship Training for Self-Employment","Special attention must be given to the provision of toolkits and entrepreneurship training for unskilled individuals to support self-employment and micro-enterprise growth.",""],[1,"274","7","Youth Entrepreneurship Skills Development Programme","Entrepreneurship skills development of the youth for startup a business.",""],[1,"275","4","E-Commerce Promotion through IT Training Partnerships","Promotion of E-Commerce activities by IT training collaborations in PPP & Public partnership mode",""]],"169":[[1,"279","2","Targeted Social Welfare Interventions","Targeted interventions were introduced to improve service delivery in special education, senior citizen welfare, child protection, and transgender rights.","Ministry of Human Rights | Ministry of Poverty Alleviation and Social Safety"],[1,"281","15","Inclusive Skills Training and Livelihood Support for Vulnerable Groups","The targeted interventions include skills training, inclusive education and enhancing livelihood opportunities.",""],[1,"281","15","Women Empowerment Centre Vocational Training","women will receive vocational training in Women Empowerment Centres",""],[1,"281","15","Productive Asset Support for Orphan Girls, Widows, and Poor Women","orphan girls, widows, and poor women will be provided with productive assets to support home-based income generation.",""],[1,"281","15","Financial Support and Inclusive Rehabilitation Services for Persons with Disabilities","PWDs will receive financial support, complemented by inclusive rehabilitation services.",""],[1,"282","3","Women Empowerment Vocational Training Programme","To increase women's participation in workforce, vocational training will be provided in various trades through Women Empowerment Centres under PBM.",""],[1,"282","3","Transgender Inclusion Support Services","The support services will be provided for mainstreaming transgender persons to ensure their equitable participation economic and social life.",""],[1,"282","5","Child Protection Institutional Strengthening","It aims to strengthen institutional arrangements for child protection and expand child-centered health and nutrition programs.",""],[1,"282","5","School for the Rehabilitation of Child Labor Program","Under the Pakistan Bait ul Mal initiative, street children will be provided with primary education in the School for the Rehabilitation of Child Labor program, while cochlear implant surgeries will be administered to children to address hearing impairments.",""],[1,"282","5","Inclusive Services for Persons with Disabilities","PWDs, the initiative includes inclusive education, vocational training, and provision of assistive devices.",""],[1,"282","5","Special Friends Disability Support Initiative","Under the \"Special Friends\" initiative, PWDs will receive financial and rehabilitation efforts.",""],[1,"282","5","Older Persons Social Protection Framework","The Plan proposes the formulation of a comprehensive social protection framework for older persons, ensuring their access to medical care, income support, and community-based services.",""],[1,"283","18","Special Friends Initiative for Persons with Disabilities","Provide financial support and assistive devices to PWDs under \"Special Friends\" initiative",""],[1,"283","19","Cochlear Implant Provision for Children with Hearing Impairment","Provide cochlear implants for children with hearing impairment",""]],"170":[[1,"281","3","Social Inclusion Mainstreaming in Development Process","Promote social inclusion through development process by integrating marginalized groups, including women, children, persons with disabilities, transgender individuals, and the elderly.",""],[1,"281","6","Child Rights Protection and Welfare Initiatives","Safeguard child rights and promote child welfare through protection, education and healthcare initiatives.",""],[1,"281","8","Human Rights Violation Reduction Measures","Reduction of human rights violations through awareness, enforcement, legal reform, and institutional capacity building.",""],[1,"282","2","Review and Modernize National Policy Frameworks","there is a need to review and modernize existing national frameworks.",""],[1,"282","2","Strengthen Legal Protections for Marginalized Groups","The strategy also focuses on strengthening legal protections for children, women, and transgender individuals through enforcement and civic awareness.",""],[1,"283","10","Revision of the National Policy for Persons with Disabilities","Revise National Policy for Persons with Disabilities (2002)",""],[1,"283","12","Elderly Welfare Policy Development","Develop Elderly Welfare Policy",""],[1,"283","16","Disability-Friendly PC-I Checklist","Prepare Disability-Friendly PC-I Checklist",""]],"171":[[1,"283","1","Social Protection Coordination and Integration Reform","The Plan also emphasizes the establishment of robust coordination mechanisms among federal, provincial, and local entities to harmonize efforts.",""],[1,"283","1","Integration of Federal and Provincial Social Protection Programmes","Efforts are underway to integrate federal and provincial social protection programmes to reduce duplication and improve coherence & coverage.",""],[1,"283","1","Marginalized Population Data Update Initiative","One of the priorities is to update data on marginalized populations.",""],[1,"283","1","Policy and Framework Review and Update","Institutional reforms will also focus on reviewing and updating key policies and frameworks to ensure their alignment with development needs and URAAN Pakistan priorities.",""]],"172":[[1,"281","12","Corporate Social Responsibility Coverage Enhancement","Enhancement of Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) coverage by integrating them into national development policies and encouraging private sector participation.",""],[1,"283","2","Public-Private and Civil Society Partnership Mobilization for Social Protection","The plan will focus on mobilizing national and international NGOS, community-based organizations, and the private sector to co-create programs for social protection and inclusion.",""],[1,"283","2","Corporate Social Responsibility Investment Promotion","The Plan will encourage the Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) within the national development process, facilitating the private sector's investment in vocational training, inclusive education, rehabilitation of PWDs, women's economic empowerment, and support for street children.",""],[1,"283","2","Institutionalized Partnership Coordination Mechanisms","These partnerships will be institutionalized through coordination mechanisms to ensure that shared efforts translate into tangible impacts for the underserved.",""],[1,"283","22","Public-Private Partnership and CSR Integration in Social Welfare Projects","Promote PPPs and integrate CSR in social welfare projects",""]],"173":[[1,"281","9","Government Employee Welfare Services Promotion","Promotion of welfare services for government employees, especially in education, healthcare, and housing.",""],[1,"281","13","Research and Development on Emerging Social Issues","Promotion of research and development on emerging social issues to inform evidence-based policy and planning.",""]],"174":[[1,"286","6","Digitalization of Media and Information Department Systems","Digitalization of existing outdated equipment and manual systems of Associated Press of Pakistan (APP), Press Information Department (PID), Information Services Academy (ISA), Central Board for Film Censors (CBFS) etc. to cope with demand of latest national/international requirements.",""],[1,"286","15","HPT Rawat Transmitting Station Upgradation","Up-gradation of HPT Rawat, Transmitting Station by Installing 1000 KW DRM-Enabled Medium Wave Transmitter",""],[1,"287","4","Digital Modernization of PTVC and PBC Networks","The digitalization of PTVC and PBC networks will transition from analogue to modern digital systems, enhancing coverage, reducing costs, and improving audio and HD visual quality.",""],[1,"287","4","Upgrade of Information and Broadcasting Ministry Equipment and Systems","Outdated equipment and manual systems in the Ministry of Information & Broadcasting will be upgraded to modern technology.","Ministry of Information & Broadcasting"],[1,"288","18","IPTV First Phase Launch","1st Phase will be launched in 1st half of 2024 (till June 2024)",""],[1,"288","21","STV Licensing Programme","Currently 140 STV licenses have been awarded.",""],[1,"289","2","Broadcasting Infrastructure Licensing Scheme","1-2 new licenses may be launched in the next 3-4 years depending on market potential.",""],[1,"289","7","Digital Modernization of State Media Equipment","Replacement of all the outdated and obsolete equipment of PTV, PBC, PID, APP, ISA etc. with digital technology.",""]],"175":[[1,"286","7","Media City Establishment","Establishment of Media City for provision of technical and teleport facilities to local entrepreneurs (PPP).",""],[1,"286","8","National Media University in PPP Mode","Establishment of a National Media University in PPP mode.",""],[1,"286","21","Film Institute Establishment at PTV Academy","Establishment of Film Institute at PTV Academy",""],[1,"289","3","Media City Development Project","Establishment of Media City for provision of technical and teleport facilities to local entrepreneurs (PPP).",""],[1,"289","4","National Media University in PPP Mode","Establishment of a National Media University in PPP mode.",""],[1,"289","10","National Media City and National Media University Establishment","Establishment of a National Media City and National Media University",""]],"176":[[1,"286","9","Rural and Far-Flung Cable TV Network Expansion","Digitalization and expansion of Cable TV Network to rural and far-flung areas (Private Sector)",""],[1,"286","10","Journalist Training Facilities Provision","Provision of training facilities to working journalists of print and electronic media (PP Sectors)",""],[1,"287","6","Facilitation of Specialized International TV Channels","International TV channels focused on sports, science, and education will be facilitated.",""],[1,"287","7","Media Personnel Training and Journalist Support Package","Training and capacity building for media personnel, comprehensive insurance for journalists, financial support for press clubs, and incentives for the film industry will be provided.",""],[1,"287","7","Film Studies Curriculum Integration","Colleges and universities will include film studies in their curricula, and a Film Financing Fund will be established.",""],[1,"287","7","Animation and Cartoon Academy Establishment","Animation and Cartoon Academy/Institution will be created to develop local talent in animation.",""],[1,"290","1","Media and Journalist Capacity Building for Modern Technology Platforms","Capacity building of media related persons and Journalists for handling the modern edge technology/platforms",""]],"177":[[1,"287","6","Intellectual Property Law Enforcement","Intellectual Property Organization (IPO) and copyright laws will be enforced to protect content creators and encourage innovation.",""],[1,"287","6","Promotion of Indigenous Digital Platforms","Indigenous digital platforms will be promoted to enhance national identity and cultural diversity.",""],[1,"287","8","Radio Sector Revitalization Initiative","The radio sector will be revitalized through digital content and community engagement.",""],[1,"287","9","Media Literacy Curriculum Integration","Media literacy programs will be integrated into school curricula to promote critical thinking and responsible media consumption.",""]],"178":[[1,"291","15","Archaeological and Historical Heritage Preservation and Restoration","Preservation, conservation, rehabilitation and restoration of archaeological/historical sites, monuments, museums, forts and stupas.",""],[1,"293","4","Pharwala Fort Conservation and Restoration Project","PC-II for Conservation, Preservation, Restoration and Development of Pharwala fort DOAM, Islamabad",""],[1,"293","15","Cultural Heritage Preservation Support","Efforts will be made at all levels to preserve these cultural phenomena.",""],[1,"294","6","Heritage Site Encroachment and Antiquities Protection Enforcement","Encroachments around historical sites and monuments as required by the Antiquities Act, 1975, will be controlled.",""],[1,"294","6","Anti-Illegal Excavation and Antiquities Trade Control","Illegal digging, destruction of archaeological sites/ monuments, and dealing in antiquities and works of art will also be restrained.",""]],"179":[[1,"291","16","Cultural Infrastructure Development and Strengthening","Development and strengthening of cultural infrastructure like museums, theatres, cinemas, art galleries, cultural centers, studios, concert halls, public parks, and auditoriums.",""],[1,"291","20","Development of National Cultural Institutions as Centers of Excellence","Development of Pakistan National Council of Arts (PNCA), Lok.Virsa, National Language Promotion Department (NLPD), Pakistan Academy of Letters (PAL) as centers of excellence for cultural and creative innovations and establishment of their offices/centers throughout the country.",""],[1,"291","21","Cultural Infrastructure Development Programme","To develop cultural infrastructure like museums, theatres, cinemas, art galleries, cultural centers, studios, concert halls, public parks, auditoriums, etc.",""],[1,"293","5","Construction of Faiz Ahmad Faiz Complex","Construction of Faiz Ahmad Faiz Complex",""],[1,"293","6","Iqbal National Monument and Library Complex Construction","Designing and construction of Iqbal National Monument and Library Complex, Islamabad",""],[1,"293","7","Establishment of PNCA Centres","Establishment of PNCA Centres at Peshawar, Quetta, Gilgit, Muzaffarabad",""],[1,"293","8","Allama Iqbal Culture and Research Centre Establishment","Establishment of Allama Iqbal Culture & Research Centre Sialkot",""],[1,"293","10","National Center for Performing Arts, Folk Music, and Qawali","Establishment of national center for performing art, folk, music, Qawali",""]],"180":[[1,"291","19","Endowment Fund for Arts and Artisans","Establishment of Endowment Fund for Arts and Artisans to support the local talent in fields of arts, crafts, music, dance, literature, museums, theaters and visual arts etc. and form their linkages with industry.",""],[1,"292","4","Promotion, Projection and Marketing of Cultural Products","Promotion, projection and marketing of cultural products",""],[1,"293","14","Cohesive Creative Industries Policy Framework","The government will focus on growth of creative industries through formulation of a cohesive policy framework, establishment of a national body on culture & creative industries to harness the full potential of these industries.",""],[1,"293","14","National Body for Culture and Creative Industries","The government will focus on growth of creative industries through formulation of a cohesive policy framework, establishment of a national body on culture & creative industries to harness the full potential of these industries.",""],[1,"293","14","Provincial Governance Support for Cultural Industries","Provinces will also take on the responsibility of nurturing, pruning, and developing governance systems to support, promote cultural industries and performing arts.",""],[1,"294","13","Endowment Fund for Arts","Establishment of Endowment Fund for Arts",""]],"181":[[1,"291","25","Gilgit Baltistan Rock Art Museums and Parks","Establishment of Gilgit Baltistan Rock Art Museums and Parks for Cultural Development and Tourism",""],[1,"291","26","Rock Art Identification and Documentation Initiative","Identify and document rock art in Diamer and other districts of GB",""],[1,"291","27","Rock Art Museums and Parks Development","Establish physical and virtual rock art museums and parks to display petroglyphs and inscriptions",""],[1,"291","28","Rock Art Museums and Parks Tourism Promotion","Promote rock art museums and parks in GB as a tourism destination for local and international visitors",""],[1,"292","1","Museum and Park Management and Maintenance Structures","Establish proper management and maintenance structures for the museums and parks",""],[1,"294","9","Gilgit Baltistan Rock Art Museums and Parks Establishment","Gilgit Baltistan Rock Art Museums and Parks will be established for cultural development of the area and to identify rock art in Diamer and other districts of GB, promote rock art museums and parks in GB as a tourism destination for local and international visitors and to establish proper management and maintenance structures for the museums and parks.",""],[1,"295","1","Gilgit Baltistan Rock Art Museums and Parks","Establishment of Gilgit Baltistan Rock Art Museums and Parks",""]],"182":[[1,"292","2","Funding and Incentives for Cultural Books and Educational Materials","Funding and incentives for producing books and educational material on culture",""],[1,"292","7","Archaeological Training and Restoration Institutes and Laboratories","Establishment of archaeological training and restoration institutes and laboratories with the help of International Cultural Organizations",""],[1,"292","12","National Language Enrichment and Translation Framework","To further enrich our national language by recognizing our rich linguistic diversity through research and study and by providing a framework of adaptation and assimilation through the encouragement of language translation from Pakistani languages and world literature into the national language and vice versa",""],[1,"292","18","Centre of Excellence at Lok Virsa","To establish of Centre of Excellence at Lok Virsa",""],[1,"292","20","National Language Processing Laboratory Establishment","Establishment of National Language Processing Laboratory (NLPD)",""],[1,"293","1","R&D Centre for Cultural Heritage Promotion","Establishment of Research & Development (R&D) Centre at Department of Archaeology and Museums to Promote soft image of Pakistan through Cultural Heritage",""],[1,"293","16","Youth Cultural Heritage and Creative Activities Programme","Schools, Colleges and Universities shall be the hubs of creative activities and cultural expressions.",""],[1,"293","16","Cultural Principles Education for Youth","The Cultural principles and priorities would be inculcated into the younger generation.",""],[1,"293","17","Museum and Library Modernization and Digitization Programme","To transform museums and libraries into centres of learning, research/ development, their collections will be increased.",""],[1,"293","18","Research Funding Support Scheme","Research funds will be established to sponsor research activities of Universities/Research Institutions/individuals as well as to support and fund the visual and performing artists.",""],[1,"294","4","Optional Arts and Cultural Studies Curriculum Inclusion","The subjects of art, cultural studies and aesthetic learning processes would be included in the academic curriculum of schools/colleges/universities as optional subjects.",""],[1,"294","4","University Department of Cultural Studies Establishment","The Department of Cultural Studies will be established in different universities.",""],[1,"295","3","Centre of Excellence at Lok Virsa","To establish of Centre of Excellence at Lok Virsa",""]],"183":[[1,"292","3","Legal Framework for Public-Private and NGO Cultural Ventures","A legal framework/enactment by the parliament be introduced for facilitating public-private/NGOs cultural ventures",""],[1,"292","5","Mainstream Culture in Development Process","Involvement of communities', individuals, private sector, NGOs and INGOs in putting culture in the mainstream development process and promoting cultural goods and services with strong industrial linkages",""],[1,"292","8","Affirmative Cultural Action for Social Harmony","To highlight the culture of tolerance, harmony and social integration inherent in the cultural fabric and to eradicate the culture of violence, intolerance and fanaticism by affirmative cultural action through education and legislation",""],[1,"292","9","National Media Cultural Promotion Initiative","To encourage a positive cultural response to negative aspects of foreign and local culture through national media by articulating cultural activities",""],[1,"292","11","Cultural Heritage Awareness and Dissemination Initiative","To meet the challenges of globalization by enhancing awareness and dissemination through traditional and modern technological means of our own cultural heritage and quality cultural expressions in performing and visual arts",""],[1,"292","13","Public-Private Partnership and Civil Society Cultural Support Measures","To encourage the growth of public-private partnerships and to support civil society cultural initiatives by providing material incentives, support and exposure",""],[1,"292","15","Cultural Exchange and International Interaction Program","To ensure a healthy interaction with other cultures through cultural exchange programs, exhibitions, and international interaction at governmental and non- governmental levels",""],[1,"294","3","Cultural Events and Festivals Promotion Programme","Cultural events and festivals will be organized more frequently so that artists from all parts of the country get more chances to perform and exhibit their work.",""],[1,"294","3","Public Media Cultural Promotion Coverage","Therefore, media particularly the public media (i.e. PTV and Radio Pakistan) would report extensively on local and national level cultural events and exhibitions.",""],[1,"294","5","Citizen Cultural Participation Promotion","Active participation of all citizens in the nation's cultural life will be encouraged through dialogue, diversity and dissemination of information about cultural activity and appreciation of cultural manifestations.",""],[1,"294","8","Civil Society Arts Support Scheme","Non-governmental civil society stakeholders in the field of theatre, dance and music will be supported by grants, subsidies, tax exemptions and access to state-owned educational and cultural infrastructure.",""]],"184":[[1,"294","2","Licensing Regime for Replicas of Antiquities and Artefacts","for promotion of tourism and cultural heritage, preparation and dissemination of replicas is very essential; therefore, making of replicas will be regulated through a proper licensing regime.",""],[1,"294","7","Cultural Atlas of Pakistan Preparation","A Cultural Atlas of Pakistan will be prepared by the National Heritage & Culture Division in collaboration with the Survey of Pakistan, showing the contiguity of the areas constituting Pakistan with detailed sketches of the centres of learning, historical monuments, urban planning and centres of culture.","National Heritage & Culture Division | Survey of Pakistan"]],"185":[[1,"298","22","National Sports Policy Formulation","Formulation of a national sports policy in consultation with relevant stakeholder",""],[1,"298","25","Sports Endowment Fund Establishment","Establishment of Sports Endowment fund",""],[1,"299","16","Sports Endowment Fund Establishment","Establishment of Sports Endowment fund (SEF)",""],[1,"300","6","Sports Development Fund under Corporate Social Responsibility","Establishment of Sports Development Fund (SDF) under Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR)* of multi-national corporations (MNCs) of county for promotion of sports and sports infrastructure.",""],[1,"300","8","Establishment of the Sports Authority of Pakistan","Establishment of Sports Authority of Pakistan comprising of representatives from all the provinces, regions, sports federations and private sector.",""],[1,"300","8","National Sports Policy Framework Development","Pakistan Sports Board (PSB) and M/o Federal Education and Professional to develop a comprehensive national sports policy framework aiming at promoting and growth of sports at all levels in the country.","Pakistan Sports Board (PSB) | M/o Federal Education and Professional"],[1,"300","14","Sports Endowment Fund","Establishment of Sports Endowment Fund (SEF) to provide financial support to needy and talented sportspersons who meet the criterion to be set by Board of Director of SEF under Pakistan Sports Board.","Pakistan Sports Board"],[1,"300","15","Revival of Departmental Sports Funding","Revival of departmental sports i.e. public departments, corporations and autonomous organization would again allocate funds for establishment of departmental teams especially in the disciplines of hockey, squash, athletics, badminton, wrestling and table tennis.",""],[1,"301","5","Sports Governance Promotion Initiative","Promotion of good governance for sports management at all levels.",""],[1,"301","6","Sports Law and Regulation Amendment","Amendment/updation in sports-related acts, laws and regulations for more effective sports development.",""]],"186":[[1,"298","29","Revival of Ethno-Traditional Sports","Revival of Ethno/traditional sports in the country.",""],[1,"298","30","Player Exchange Programs with Other Countries","Launching of player's exchange programs with other countries including China, Korea and Australia",""],[1,"298","31","Women's Sports Participation Promotion","Encouraging the women's participation in sports",""],[1,"299","1","Private Sector Investment Promotion and Sports Development through Public-Private Partnerships","Fostering of private sector investment promotion and development of sports in the country through Public-Private Partnerships (PPP).",""],[1,"299","2","National and International Sports Events Promotion","Organization of maximum number of national and international sports events in the country to have positive impact on country's image and also leverage sports tourism in the country.",""],[1,"299","4","Anti-Doping Awareness Conferences and Seminars","Organizing of sports conferences / seminars to raise awareness among athletes and sports officials regarding international convention against doping in sports",""],[1,"299","18","Financial Assistance to National Sports Bodies and Sportspersons","Provision of financial assistance to National Sports Federations/ Associations/ Clubs/ Sportspersons",""],[1,"300","18","Leasing of Underutilized Sports Facilities to the Private Sector","Efficient use of existing sports facilities by leasing out underutilized sports facilities to private sector.",""],[1,"301","3","Public-Private Partnership for Sports and Training Facilities","Promotion of Public-Private Partnership for investment in sports and training facilities.",""]],"187":[[1,"299","22","E-sports Academy Establishment","Establishment of E-sports academy at Islamabad",""],[1,"301","2","National E-Sports Academy","Establishment of National e-Sports Academy to provide training and support to aspirant online players.",""],[1,"301","19","National E-Sport Academy Establishment","Establishment of National e-Sport Academy at Islamabad",""]],"188":[[1,"305","3","Fiscal Incentives for Private Tourism Investment","Provision of fiscal incentives (i.e. tax reliefs, subsidized loan financing etc.) to attract private sector investment in Tourism Sector.",""],[1,"305","9","Tourism Sector Priority and Public-Private Coordination Initiative","Establishment of tourism industry as a priority sector at national and provincial levels for the future development of the country and to achieve cooperation within the public & private sector as well as all other stakeholders to facilitate sustainable growth of tourism in Pakistan.",""],[1,"305","12","Tourism Product Upgrading and Market Development Initiative","Creation of enabling business environment for private sector by upgrading existing tourism products and identify and promote new opportunities for the future development of the tourism products of Pakistan through market research and analysis of the country's competitive advantages.",""],[1,"305","13","Tourism Infrastructure Development Financing Mobilization","Seeking local/foreign investment and donor funding/technical assistance to contribute towards the country's tourism infrastructure development strategy.",""],[1,"307","2","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Tourism","Public-private partnerships will be encouraged, and a national tourism policy will be formulated with input from provincial and regional stakeholders.",""],[1,"307","3","Tourism Industry Reclassification and Investor Facilitation Reform","Tourism will be reclassified from Category \"C\" to Category \"A\" industry status, granting it benefits similar to other industries.",""],[1,"307","3","Tourism Visa Simplification and One-Window Investor Facility","Visa processes will be simplified, and a one-window facility for tourism investors will be established.",""],[1,"307","9","Aiwan-e-Sayahat Construction in PPP Mode","Construction of Aiwan-e-Sayahat in F-5/1, Islamabad in PPP mode",""]],"189":[[1,"305","6","Tourism Marketing and Entry Facilitation Measures","Increase in international tourist arrival through effective marketing and removal of avoidable restrictions at the points of entry as well as movement of tourists' to resort areas.",""],[1,"305","7","Domestic Tourism Promotion through Local Events and Exhibitions","Promotion of domestic tourism through holding local fairs/festivals and trade shows/exhibitions in different parts of the country.",""],[1,"305","10","International Tourism Marketing Strategy","Development of an effective marketing strategy linked with regional initiatives through an inter-provincial collaborative process to promote positive image of Pakistan in the international tourism markets as a unique and desirable tourist destination to visit.",""],[1,"306","3","International Tourism Promotion and Linkage-Building Participation","Participation in international tourism exhibitions World Travel Market (WTM), London, China Outbound Travel & Tourism Market(COTTM), Beijing, Travel & Adventure Show(T&A), New York, Internationale Tourismus-Börse (ITB), Berlin and Arabian Travel Market (ATM), Dubai etc.) and international and regional meetings of international organizations (ECO, SCO, UNWTO, OIC, D8 etc.) to promote government to government, government to business and business to business linkages.",""],[1,"307","4","Tourism Marketing Strategy","A marketing strategy will be developed to improve the country's image and attract tourists.",""]],"190":[[1,"305","5","Development of Archaeological and Heritage Tourism Products","Development of archaeological sites, historical monuments and national parks as tourism products.",""],[1,"305","8","Sikh and Buddhist Religious Heritage Tourism Development","Promotion of Sikh and Buddhist religious and heritage tourism by providing better facilities to pilgrims and developing infrastructure close to religious destinations.",""],[1,"305","18","Islamabad Capital Territory Tourism Development Initiative","Developing Islamabad Capital Territory as a gateway tourist destination by improving the existing tourism facilities, accessibility and accommodation facilities.",""],[1,"307","5","Pilgrim Tourism Regulatory Reform","For pilgrim tourism, regulations will be reviewed to make them more friendly, and the private sector will be encouraged to participate.",""],[1,"307","6","Public Tourist Facilities Network","A network of public facilities will be established at tourist locations.",""],[1,"307","11","Tourist Information Centers Establishment","Establishment of Tourists Information Centers (TICs)",""]],"191":[[1,"305","14","Tourism Service Quality Standards and Training Programme","Deliver quality services at all levels in the tourism industry through the establishment of national minimum standards and regulations, and by supporting training and human resource development.",""],[1,"305","16","Tourism and Hospitality Training Facilities Development","Develop sufficient training facilities and programs to achieve the tourism strategy goals, maximize employment opportunities, and ensure the desired standards of quality in tourism and hospitality services.",""],[1,"306","4","Tourism Education in Higher Secondary Curriculum","Introduction of tourism as a subject from higher secondary level to promote tourism education among the young people.",""],[1,"307","4","Tourism and Hotel Management Training Expansion","Training institutions for tourism and hotel management will be expanded in collaboration with the private sector.",""]],"192":[[1,"305","15","Sustainable Community-Based Tourism Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of PTDC, provincial tourism departments and private organizations dealing tourism industry to promote sustainable community-based tourism and to spread the benefits more widely amongst the local population.",""],[1,"306","1","Center of Excellence for Mountain Tourism","Setting up of Center of Excellence for Mountain Tourism at Skardu to promote safe and eco-friendly adventure tourism in the mountainous areas of Pakistan.",""],[1,"307","4","Ecotourism Promotion Initiative","Ecotourism will be promoted carefully to avoid damage to natural and cultural heritage.",""],[1,"307","5","Adventure Tourism Promotion and Safety Guidelines","A year will be designated for adventure tourism, with safety guidelines developed in consultation with stakeholders.",""],[1,"307","6","Women in Tourism Participation Initiative","Women's participation in tourism will be encouraged, including the concept of Women Tourist Police for family-oriented tourism.",""]],"193":[[1,"305","17","Strengthening of the National Tourism Coordination Body","Strengthening of NTCB as a national level tourism authority comprising of representatives of all the provinces, regions and private sector to develop a comprehensive tourism policy and strategy framework at national level.",""],[1,"306","5","Tourism and Hospitality Legal and Regulatory Update","Updating of all the tourism and hospitality related laws, rules and regulations for creating a conducive business environment for private sector to invest in the sector",""],[1,"307","1","Federal Tourism and Culture Ministry Establishment","To revitalize this sector, a new Tourism and Culture Ministry will be established at the Federal level to oversee development, administration, and policy.",""],[1,"307","1","National Tourism Coordination Body","A NTCB will be set up as an apex body to coordinate among stakeholders, conduct research, and recommend policy measures.",""],[1,"307","2","Tourism Infrastructure, Security, and Regulatory Support","The private sector will play a leading role in tourism development, with the public sector facilitating by providing necessary infrastructure, security, and regulations.",""],[1,"307","2","National Tourism Policy Formulation","a national tourism policy will be formulated with input from provincial and regional stakeholders.",""],[1,"307","4","Tourism Legislation Revision","Outdated legislative acts related to tourism will be revised to meet international standards.",""]],"194":[[1,"306","2","Coastal Infrastructure Development for Blue Tourism","Tapping of potential in emerging fields of blue tourism/coastal through development of infrastructure in coastal areas in collaboration with provincial governments of Sindh and Balochistan.",""],[1,"306","10","Quality Hotel Room Expansion","Add 20,000 more quality hotel rooms all over Pakistan",""],[1,"306","12","New Tourist Destinations Development","Open 20 new tourist destinations",""],[1,"306","13","Tourism and Hospitality Job Creation Initiative","Create 1 million more jobs in tourism and hospitality in next 5 years",""],[1,"307","3","Tourism Information Website and Mobile App Development","A user-friendly website and mobile app will be developed to provide comprehensive information on tourist attractions.",""],[1,"307","5","Tourism Area Infrastructure Improvement","Physical infrastructure in tourist areas will be improved, including roads, water supply, sanitation, and waste management.",""]],"195":[[1,"307","6","Tourism Data Research Programs","Research programs will be implemented to generate data on tourism inflow, expenditures, and private sector investment.",""]],"196":[[1,"310","1","Ex-FATA Ten-Year Development Programme","After merger of Ex-FATA with province of KPK, a ten-year (2018-2028) plan was initiated.",""],[1,"310","4","Targeted Investment in Priority Development Areas","The plan envisages priority development areas for targeted investment to generate revenues and overall socio-economic development.",""],[1,"311","7","Federal PSDP Financing for Special Area Development Plans","Federal government is facilitating development efforts in special areas/regions, through federal PSDP budget allocations which are provided to finance ADPs of AJ&K, GB and merged districts of KPK.",""],[1,"311","7","Regional Priority Sector Investment Planning","The respective area governments will formulate their development priorities in accordance with their need/demand.",""],[1,"311","8","Targeted Investment in Priority Sectors for AJ&K Development","priority sectors has been identified for targeted investment.",""],[1,"313","2","Merged Districts Priority Investment Programme","The priority investment areas identified include communication infrastructure, social sector development, tourism, industrial development & promotion of border trade, agriculture & livestock, mineral development, and energy and power.",""]],"197":[[1,"310","4","Capacity Building for Special Area Governments","The Plan intends to increase capacities of the governments of special areas for generating their own resources, strengthening institutions, creating effective partnership with non-governmental development partners, encouraging community driven development, enhancing the element of public-private partnership, and delegating more administrative & financial powers.",""],[1,"310","8","Local Government Institutional Capacity Building for Service Delivery","Capacity building of local government institutions for improvement in service delivery.",""],[1,"311","5","Public-Private Partnership Procedure Simplification","Facilitate PPP in development process through simplification of procedure.",""],[1,"313","4","Institutional Development and Infrastructure Upgrade Programme","To support institutional development, infrastructure upgrades are planned, alongside fiber optic connectivity for 8 District Headquarters (DHQs) and 25 Tehsil Headquarters (THQs).",""],[1,"314","14","Government Department and TEVTA Capacity Building","Capacity Building of Govt. Departments/TEVTA",""],[1,"314","14","Construction of Patwar Khanas","Construction of Patwar Khanas",""],[1,"314","14","Reform of Religious Institutes","Reforming religious institutes",""]],"198":[[1,"310","7","Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Development","To improve regional connectivity and coherence through development of disaster resilient infrastructure including roads, bridges energy, etc.",""],[1,"321","15","Crisis Management and Resilient Systems Strengthening","Strengthen crisis management and resilient system by developing effective strategies for natural disasters and public emergencies",""]],"199":[[1,"310","10","Health Facility Improvement and Nutrition Support","Improvement in health facilities to ensure healthy lives and wellbeing of all at all ages and reduction in prevalence of stunting through improved nutrition.",""],[1,"313","1","District-Level Diagnostic and Telehealth Services","diagnostic facilities and telehealth services will be established at the district level, to address the shortages in human resources and quality health services.",""],[1,"315","4","Health Facility Establishment and Upgrading","Establishment/up-gradation of health facilities",""],[1,"316","12","Medical College Establishment and Hospital Upgradation","Establishment of medical college, upgradation of PHQ, DHQ Skardu and Chillas.",""],[1,"316","12","Telemedicine and Diagnostic Services Introduction","Introduction of telemedicine and diagnostic services.",""],[1,"316","12","Disease Prevention and Early Diagnosis Services","Prevention, early identification through diagnostics, effective treatment.",""],[1,"317","7","Health Facility Improvement","Improve health facilities.",""]],"200":[[1,"310","11","ICT Development with Private Sector Participation","Development of ICT especially involving the private sector.",""],[1,"312","7","Broadband Expansion to Villages and Tourist Destinations","in order to capitalize on the CPEC fiber optic, broadband internet access will be extended to villages and key tourist destinations",""],[1,"312","7","E-commerce and E-learning Centers in Key Locations","the plan to establish e-commerce and e-learning centers in 50 key locations will directly benefit over 600,000 individuals and support 15,000 SMEs over the next five years",""],[1,"315","2","IT Park and Excellence Centers Establishment","Establishment of IT Park and Excellence Centers",""],[1,"316","2","Tehsil-Level Business Hubs and IT Centers","Establishment of business hubs and IT centers at tehsil level.",""],[1,"317","7","Employable Digital Skills Training for Youth","Provision of employable digital skills to youth",""]],"201":[[1,"311","2","Community-Based Responsible Tourism Promotion and Tourist Site Upgrading","Promotion of community based responsible tourism and development/upgradation of tourist sites and allied facilities.",""],[1,"312","1","Tourism Development Corridor","To promote tourism and livelihoods, a Tourism Development Corridor will be developed and integrated with the CPEC, contributing to 1,450 km road network across the region.",""],[1,"312","2","Village Guest House and Homestay Support Initiative","Special initiatives will support village guest houses and homestay enterprises in high- potential tourism sites",""],[1,"312","7","Adventure Tourism Center Construction in Hunza","projects such as the construction of adventure Tourism Center in Hunza",""],[1,"312","7","Hospitality Center Construction in Shiger","and a Hospitality Center in Shiger aim to boost high-value tourism services",""],[1,"313","7","Integrated Tourism Zones Development in Orakzai and Kurram","the development of integrated tourism zones in Orakzai and Kurram",""],[1,"313","7","Gomal-Zam Dam Tourism Promotion Initiative","promotion of Gomal-Zam Dam as a tourist destination",""],[1,"314","10","All-Weather Tourism and Economic Corridor Development","Development of all-weather Tourism/ Economic Corridor",""],[1,"314","10","Chairlift and Cable Car Installation","Establishment of Chairlift/ Cable Cars",""],[1,"315","14","Tourism and Adventure Sports Regulatory Framework","Formulation of regulatory framework for tracking, expedition, adventure sports.",""],[1,"315","14","Homestay and Tourism PPP Promotion","Initiatives of homestays and other Public-Private Partnership (PPP) projects will be actively encouraged.",""],[1,"317","5","Integrated Tourism Zones Development","Opening new avenues & development of integrated tourism zones and promote private sector investment.",""]],"202":[[1,"311","3","Affordable and Sustainable Electricity Supply Expansion","Provision of affordable, & sustainable electricity supply by exploring renewable/alternate energy sources/hydel power.",""],[1,"311","10","Neelum Valley Hydel Power Plant Development","projects such as the 35 MW Nagdar, 40 MW Dowarian, 22 MW Jagran-IV, and 3 MW Phullawai hydel power plants are planned for Neelum Valley to harness the region's hydropower potential",""],[1,"312","3","Priority Piped Gas Supply Expansion","To meet critical energy needs, piped gas supply will be provided to on a priority basis, with phased expansion to major areas.",""],[1,"312","6","Hydropower Project Prioritization","To address the energy shortage and harness the region water resources, hydropower projects will be prioritized.",""],[1,"314","6","Hydropower Project Construction","Construction of Hydropower projects",""],[1,"314","6","Supply Network Renovation","Renovation of Supply Network",""],[1,"314","6","New Grid Station Construction","Construction of New Grid Stations",""],[1,"315","12","Hydropower Development Projects","Hydro Power . 54 MW attabad, 40 MW Hanzel, 30MW Guwari, Thack Chillas, 26 Shagarthang .",""],[1,"315","12","Energy Sector Institutional Reforms and Power Policy","Institutional Reforms for energy sector/Power Policy)",""],[1,"315","12","Clean Development Mechanism for Clean Energy Generation","Conservation and generation of clean energy through Clean Development Mechanism (CDM)",""],[1,"317","15","Priority Dam Construction and Renewable Energy Promotion","Energy and Power Construction of priority dams and promotion of micro hydel power and solar energy",""]],"203":[[1,"311","9","Regional Transport Connectivity Infrastructure Programme","To operationalize these priorities, a number of major programs and projects have been identified for implementation.",""],[1,"311","9","Mansehra-Muzaffarabad Expressway","These include Mansehra-Muzaffarabad Expressway and Muzaffarabad- Mirpur-Mangla Kashmir Highway, aimed at enhancing regional integration.",""],[1,"311","9","Muzaffarabad-Mirpur-Mangla Kashmir Highway","These include Mansehra-Muzaffarabad Expressway and Muzaffarabad- Mirpur-Mangla Kashmir Highway, aimed at enhancing regional integration.",""],[1,"311","9","Rural Access Roads, Link Roads, and Bridges Construction","Additionally, access roads, link roads, and bridges will be constructed in remote and underserved areas to strengthen market connectivity and integrate physical infrastructure with China-Pakistan Economic Corridor (CPEC).",""],[1,"312","1","Leepa and Shaunter Tunnel Infrastructure Projects","Strategic infrastructure projects like Leepa tunnel and Shaunter tunnel aim to improve access to valleys and link AJ&K with GB, thereby boosting trade, tourism, and cross-regional economic activity.",""],[1,"312","5","Interregional Road Connectivity and Access Infrastructure Programme","To enhance interregional connectivity, several major road projects are planned.",""],[1,"313","3","Regional Road Connectivity Projects","In the domain of connectivity, several major projects have been planned to improve access and economic linkages.",""],[1,"314","4","Expressway and Highway Construction Programme","Construction of express ways/highways.",""],[1,"314","4","Road Rehabilitation and Upgradation Programme","Rehabilitation/ upgradation of roads.",""],[1,"315","8","Inter-Regional and Inter-Provincial Connectivity Roads Construction","Inter-regional and inter provincial connectivity roads . Construction of Gilgit Shounter Via AJK, Shadoor Road), Darial & Tangir and Shara-e-Nager",""],[1,"317","3","Communication Infrastructure Development and Road Rehabilitation","Communication Infrastructure · Construction/ Rehabilitation of Roads · Development /upgradation of communication networking.",""]],"204":[[1,"312","2","Targeted Employable Skills Development Programs","targeted programs to enhance employable skills in sectors such as tourism, handicrafts, and mining in underdeveloped districts and valleys",""],[1,"312","2","TVET Institution Upgrading Programme","TVET institutions will be upgraded, to increase market-oriented skills training opportunities",""],[1,"313","1","Designated TVET Authority","efforts would be made to develop human capital by establishing a designates TVET Authority.",""],[1,"313","1","District-Level Vocational Centers for Demand-Driven Skills","District-level vocational centers will be set up to deliver demand-driven skills, to foster local entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"313","4","Girls' Higher Secondary School Expansion","In the education sector, 25 new higher secondary schools for girls will be established across the tehsils, along with working women hostels in 25 tehsils.",""],[1,"313","4","Wana Education City Development","An education city in Wana is also planned.",""],[1,"313","6","Women's Technical Training Institutes","eight new technical training institutes will be established for women.",""],[1,"313","6","Scholarship and Internship Programme for Technical and Vocational Graduates","scholarship and internship programs will be launched for graduates of technical and vocational institutes.",""],[1,"315","4","School and College Construction and Facility Provision","Construction of Schools/collages buildings and provision of missing facilities.",""],[1,"315","4","Teacher Training and Student Support Programme","Teachers trainings and student support program",""],[1,"316","10","Premier Institutions for High-Skilled Market Capture","Premier institutions will be established to capture the highly skilled market",""],[1,"316","10","School Facility Upgrading for Early Childhood Education Centers","Provision of missing facilities at schools with Early Childhood Education (ECD) centers.",""],[1,"316","10","Technical and Vocational Education Authority Establishment","TVET authority and intuitional set up and intuitona stik up.",""],[1,"316","10","Technical and Vocational Training Institute Establishment","Establishment of Technical and vocational training institutes.",""],[1,"316","10","Campus Language Centers","Language centers within the campuses of KIU and Baltistan University.",""],[1,"316","10","Private Sector Skills Linkage for Women, Youth, and Persons with Disabilities","Private sector involvement in skill development/ market linkages for women, youth and person with disabilities.",""],[1,"317","7","Literacy and Primary Enrollment Expansion","Increase literacy rate and primary enrolment.",""],[1,"319","3","Youth Internship and On-the-Job Initiatives","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""]],"205":[[1,"310","1","Small Industrial Estate Development and Marble City Project","In industries sector, 03 Small industrial estates have been planned and work on Mohmand Marble City is in progress.",""],[1,"311","7","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Special Area Development","PPP in development process will be encouraged through simplifying the procedures and formulating transparent policies and regulations that incentivize private sector participation in development process of special areas.",""],[1,"312","3","Business Environment and Market Integration Reforms","Legal and regulatory reforms will be pursued to improve the ease of doing business and integrate local industries into regional and global markets.",""],[1,"312","3","LoC Area Rehabilitation and Socio-economic Upliftment Package","A multi-sector development package is also included for the rehabilitation of damaged infrastructure and socio-economic upliftment of the Line of Control (LoC) affected areas.",""],[1,"312","3","Agricultural Enterprise Development and Asset Creation Support","In the agriculture and food security domain, programs will support enterprise development, asset creation, especially in rural areas.",""],[1,"313","8","New Industrial Estates and Border Market Development","Industrial development will be promoted through the establishment of new industrial estates across eight merged districts, along with border markets, city centers, and custom stations in Bajaur, Mohmand, and South Waziristan.",""]],"206":[[1,"312","8","Geological Data Generation and Mineral Sector Investment Promotion","To unlock its value, efforts would be made to generate geological data, enhance skills in mineral exploration and processing, and promote investment through PPPs.",""],[1,"312","8","Mineral Exploration and Processing Skills Development","To unlock its value, efforts would be made to generate geological data, enhance skills in mineral exploration and processing, and promote investment through PPPs.",""],[1,"312","8","Public-Private Partnership Investment Promotion in Mining","To unlock its value, efforts would be made to generate geological data, enhance skills in mineral exploration and processing, and promote investment through PPPs.",""],[1,"313","8","Mineral Sector Geological Survey Programme","For the mineral sector, geological surveys will be undertaken to assess resource potential and guide future investments.",""],[1,"316","4","Mineral Exploration and Extraction for Export Facilitation","Mineral exploration, extraction of deposits to facilitate exports.",""]],"207":[[1,"313","5","Small and Medium Dam Construction Programme","several small & medium dams are planned, including the Jabba and Barra Dams in Khyber, Larazan Dam in Tank, Khan Meer Kalay Dam in Orakzai, and the Tank-Zam Dam",""],[1,"314","1","Olive Cultivation Project","The agriculture and livestock sectors will see transformation through projects like olive cultivation in Bajaur, Khyber, and Orakzai;",""],[1,"314","1","Saffron Cultivation Project","saffron cultivation in Orakzai;",""],[1,"314","1","Forest Survey and Classification Initiative","forest surveys and classification, rainwater retention and aquifer recharge systems in South Waziristan and Mohmand; and irrigation schemes across the merged districts.",""],[1,"314","1","Rainwater Retention and Aquifer Recharge Systems","forest surveys and classification, rainwater retention and aquifer recharge systems in South Waziristan and Mohmand; and irrigation schemes across the merged districts.",""],[1,"314","1","Irrigation Schemes for Merged Districts","and irrigation schemes across the merged districts.",""],[1,"314","8","Agricultural Infrastructure and Support Measures","Construction of canals, small dams and water channels · Agriculture research . Interest free loans for model farms · Crops/fruit development/food storage capacity . Animal health services · Reforestation",""],[1,"316","14","Cold Chain Technology Establishment","Agriculture . Establishment of cold chain technology.",""],[1,"317","17","Agricultural Storage Reservoirs and Irrigation Channels Construction","Construction of 130 storage reservoirs/check dams & 130 irrigation channels.",""]],"208":[[1,"313","6","Startup and Business Upgrade Loan Financing Windows","Financial inclusion will be supported through loan financing windows from Bank of Khyber and Akhuwat Foundation to assist start-ups and upgrade existing businesses.",""],[1,"313","6","Rescue 1122 Emergency Response Center","a Rescue 1122 center will be set up.",""],[1,"315","4","Social Protection Services for Poor and Marginalized Populations","Provision of Social Protection services to poor/marginalized population",""]],"209":[[1,"319","3","Implementation of National Security and Prevention Policies","The Plan also focuses on implementation of the National Action Plan (NAP), National Security Policy, National Prevention of Violent Extremism (NPVE) Policy.",""],[1,"319","3","Model Police Stations in ICT","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""],[1,"322","5","Violence Reduction and Access to Justice Initiative","Initiatives will be implemented to reduce violence, and exploitation of vulnerable segments and promote rule of law while ensuring equal access to justice and inclusive decision-making.",""],[1,"322","6","Police and Judicial Capacity Enhancement","sufficient funds will be allocated to enhance the capacity of police and judicial system.",""],[1,"323","1","Law Enforcement and Forensic Capacity Enhancement","Special attention will be given to enhance capacity of law enforcement agencies including police, FIA, NAB, prosecution and public defenders' system especially in the area of collection of forensic and other evidences.",""],[1,"323","4","Community-Focused Policing Reform","Effective community focused policing will be ensured through merit-based recruitment, postings, and transfers at all levels.",""],[1,"323","4","Criminal Database Development and Integration","Criminal databases will be established in coordination with National Database and Registration Authority (NADRA) at national and provincial levels.",""],[1,"327","6","FIA Capacity Building and Enforcement Strengthening","The Plan signifies the role of FIA and focuses on initiatives for capacity building, strengthening its role in upholding rule of law, and combating white-collar crimes, cybercrimes and terror financing.",""]],"210":[[1,"323","5","Public Finance Management Act Implementation","Therefore, the plan will focus on effective implementation of Public Finance Management Act.",""],[1,"323","5","Alignment of Public Financial Management Procedures with International Standards","Existing procedures and rules governing public financial management will be aligned with international standards.",""],[1,"323","5","Policy Audit by Auditor General of Pakistan","Audit of each policy will be conducted by the Auditor General of Pakistan.",""],[1,"323","6","Public Financial Management Reform Programme","Better Public Financial Management in accounting functions of the Federal, Provincial and District Governments will be ensured by reforming financial management system especially in the areas of accounting, reporting, efficient and effective government payment and receipt.",""],[1,"324","2","Financial Management Effectiveness Assessment Mechanism","A mechanism to assess effectiveness of financial management practices will be developed to promote performance and policy audits.",""],[1,"324","2","Parliamentary Oversight Strengthening for Public Spending","The roles of Public Account Committees and Parliamentary Standing Committees will be strengthened to enhance their oversight on public spending while ensuring transparency and accountability.",""],[1,"324","2","Financial Management Procedure Review and Capacity Development","Regular reviews and updates of financial management procedures will be institutionalized with investment in capacity development of human resources of financial management institutions.",""],[1,"328","2","Public Spending Implementation and Institutional Capacity-Building Strategy","A comprehensive strategy will be devised for effective implementation/utilization of public spending including PSDP and capacity building for institutional development of agencies involved in development processes, including Planning Commission and Provincial Planning and Development Boards/Departments.",""]],"211":[[1,"324","1","Pension Reform Programme","To reduce the burden pension expenditure of the government, pension reforms will be implemented.",""],[1,"324","2","Federal Contributory Pension Reform","The plan will consider contributory pension reforms at federal level imitating Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Punjab model to reduce burden on federal expenditure.",""]],"212":[[1,"326","4","National Statistics and Data Systems Strengthening","A systematic approach will be employed to address key gaps in economic and social statistics, including enhancing quality and coverage of MIS, national accounts, poverty estimation, monitoring and analysis of data.",""],[1,"326","4","Data Dissemination Improvement Measures","Measures will be undertaken to enhance dissemination of data and information at federal, provincial, ministerial, and institutional levels.",""],[1,"326","5","Quarterly GDP and Automated Inflation Measurement System","A system to issue Quarterly GDPs data and Automated Inflation measurement support system will be established.",""],[1,"326","5","National Data Centre for Integrated Statistical Management","A National Data Centre will manage both current and historical datasets to meet future needs.",""],[1,"326","5","Integrated Socio-Economic Data Linkage with NADRA","Integration of data, including local government vital events, health, education and other socio-economic indicators with NADRA will be pursued for forecasting organizational demands and effective decision making.",""],[1,"326","5","National Spatial Data Infrastructure Digital Mapping Initiative","Digital maps based on integrated datasets will be generated following National Spatial Data Infrastructure (NSDI) model to utilizes potential source of earning.",""],[1,"326","5","Open Government Data Publication Initiative","All relevant departments will publish current and historical data on their websites to facilitate accessibility for researchers and policymakers.",""],[1,"326","5","PBS Data Collection Projects","PBS will initiate new projects for collection of requisite data to address the data gap.",""]],"213":[[1,"321","6","Ease-of-Doing-Business Regulatory Streamlining","Effective economic governance by streamlining regulatory frameworks with an ease-of-doing-business regime",""],[1,"324","4","Board of Investment Regulatory Reform","Regulatory reforms in Board of Investment to enhance ease of doing business environment and promoting exports will be ensured.",""],[1,"329","2","Legal and Regulatory Regime Strengthening","During the Plan period, legal and regulatory regime will be strengthened to protect public properties and interests through formulation and application of the rules and regulations, strengthening of institutions integrity, separation of institutional power, consistent and coordinated regulations, transparency, predictability of policies and rule of law.",""],[1,"329","2","Business Environment and Legislative Reform Package","Efforts will be made to provide business friendly environment specially to promote private sector as an engine of growth by implementing legislative reforms pending on the issue.",""],[1,"329","2","One-Stop Shop Ease of Doing Business Reform","One-Stop Shop solutions will be further strengthened to promote ease of doing businesses.",""],[1,"329","2","Integrated Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","A comprehensive and integrated legal and regulatory framework including financial institutions, trade facilitation, revenue mobilization, fair competition, food, water and energy security, intellectual property, grievance redressal and consumer protection, will be formulated.",""],[1,"329","2","Regulatory Institution Autonomy Strengthening","The regulatory institutions will be further strengthened with administrative and financial autonomy.",""],[1,"330","1","Policy Impact Evaluation and Innovation Promotion","and evaluating policy impacts, and promoting innovation will be essential components.",""],[1,"330","1","Flexible Multi-Stakeholder Policy Implementation Framework","The plan will emphasize flexibility and collaboration with governmental agencies, stakeholders, and the private sector for successful policy implementation in response to evolving economic conditions and emerging market challenges.",""]],"214":[[1,"319","3","Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure Initiatives","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""],[1,"329","3","SBP Strategic Transformation for Financial Sector Development","State Bank of Pakistan (SBP) intends strategic transformation for economic growth while maintaining monetary stability.",""],[1,"329","3","Banking Sector Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanism","the SBP will actively pursue establishing institutional mechanisms for alternate dispute resolution within the banking sector.",""],[1,"329","3","Climate Risk Policy Measures for the Financial Sector","Recognizing vulnerabilities in financial sector, the SBP will proactively implement policy measures to address impact of climate change.",""],[1,"329","3","Digital Technology Adoption for Banking Efficiency and Inclusion","Emerging technologies will be adopted to enhance efficiency and promote financial inclusion and equality governance within organization and among regulated financial institutions.",""],[1,"330","2","Capital Market Reform Agenda","SECP's capital market reform agenda is focused on revamping primary market framework to encourage quality listing in a timely manner; implementing a state of the art on-boarding mechanism to expand the investor base; expanding investor education program through creation of market development fund; reviewing leverage products and bringing-in new products to enhance liquidity in the secondary market.",""],[1,"330","2","Five-Year Insurance Regulatory Reform Plan","SECP intends to launch a five-year Strategic Plan to improve regulatory framework, policyholder protection and increase insurance penetration in the country.",""]],"215":[[1,"329","4","Competition Commission Enforcement and Institutional Strengthening","A comprehensive approach will be adopted to further strengthen the Commission with necessary tools to enforce laws across diverse economic sectors.",""],[1,"329","4","Market Intelligence Unit for Competition Enforcement","Proactive enforcement through new Market Intelligence Unit (MIU) will be adopted to create advanced technological and data analytical capabilities while assessing market data to identify the collusive practices.",""],[1,"329","4","Competition Enforcement, Market Studies, and Regulatory Reform","Under competition enforcement, investigating and prosecuting anti-competitive practices, monitoring mergers, and prosecuting abuse by entities with significant market power will be pursued.",""],[1,"329","4","National Competition Policy Development and Advocacy","Market studies will be conducted which can lead in development of a National Competition Policy and engage in advocacy for pro-competition policies.",""],[1,"329","4","Competition Regulatory Framework Review and Reform","Review of regulatory framework and introduction of regulatory reforms will be initiated.",""]],"216":[[1,"319","3","Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi Project","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""]],"217":[[1,"319","3","Integrated Transit Trade Management System","It also includes the Development of Internship Policy and other on job initiatives for youth, e-governance initiatives, performance agreement of Ministries with PM establishment of Model Police Stations in ICT; Integrated Transit Trade Management Systems; Pakistan Raises Revenue initiatives; Financial Inclusion and Infrastructure initiatives; Competitive and Liveable City of Karachi (CLICK) project; Establishment of Public Private Partnership Authority(P3A); AGPR Online Billing Solution (Sehel) and Audit Management Information System (AMIS) etc.",""]],"218":[[1,"314","14","Vehicle Inspection and Certification System","Establishment of Vehicle inspection and certification system",""]],"219":[[1,"330","3","National Tariff Commission Trade Remedy and Tariff Rationalization Measures","National Tariff Commission (NTC) will further strengthen its role for effective tariff and trade measures with a focus on enhancing domestic industry competitiveness.","National Tariff Commission (NTC)"],[1,"330","3","Second National Tariff Policy 2025-29","The second National Tariff Policy (2025-29) will further help industries to enhance competitiveness, substitute imports and enable them to create surpluses for exports as well.",""],[1,"330","3","Implementation of Trade Remedy Laws Research","Ongoing research to ensure effective implementation of Trade Remedy Laws will be continued.",""],[1,"341","2","Second National Tariff Policy Implementation","Implementation of Second National Tariff Policy (2025-29) to support industries for enhancing competitiveness, substitute imports and enable exports",""]],"220":[[1,"330","4","E-Procurement System Implementation","The plan includes implementation of e- Procurement System (EPADS) as federal level as well as in provinces",""],[1,"330","4","Standardized Bidding Documents Development","the development of standardized bidding documents for different procurement categories",""],[1,"330","4","Procurement Regulatory Monitoring and Evaluation System","a Regulatory Monitoring & Evaluation system will be established",""],[1,"330","4","Public Procurement Regulatory Reforms","The plan will include introduction of regulations for improving government management, transparency, accountability, and the quality of public procurement",""],[1,"330","4","Public Asset Disposal and Bid Sanctions Mechanism","disposal of public assets, mechanisms for blacklisting and debarments of bidders, and implementation of a Procurement Monitoring and Evaluation Framework through EPADS will be initiated",""],[1,"338","19","Standardized Bidding Documents Development","Development of standardized bidding documents for different procurement categories",""],[1,"338","20","Regulatory Monitoring and Evaluation System for Public Procurement","Regulatory Monitoring & Evaluation system to ensure effective regulatory compliance and combat corrupt practices in public procurement",""],[1,"338","21","Public Procurement Streamlining Framework through EPADS","Establishment of framework to streamline and enhance the efficiency and integrity of public procurement processes through EPADS",""]],"221":[[1,"330","5","Intellectual Property Organization Strengthening","Intellectual Property Organization will be strengthened to support innovation, creativity and development of knowledge base.",""],[1,"331","1","Knowledge Sharing Sessions with Academia and R&D Organizations","knowledge sharing sessions with academia and research & development organizations will be conducted.",""],[1,"331","1","Digitization of Intellectual Property Applications","Applications related to copyright, patent, designs and geographical indications will be digitized.",""],[1,"331","1","Copyright Law Improvement through Stakeholder Consultation","Existing copyright law will be improved through consultations with artists, lawyers, musicians, and representatives from other creative industries.",""]],"222":[[1,"332","2","Independent Nuclear Regulatory Oversight and Capacity Strengthening","Pakistan Nuclear Regulatory Authority (PNRA) will keep on actively pursuing its role as an independent national nuclear regulator to achieve its mission of protection of the workers, public and the environment from harmful effects of ionizing radiation.",""],[1,"332","2","Regulatory Regime Enhancement and New Nuclear Regulations","PNRA will further enhance its regulatory regime to remain aligned with international standards through development of new regulations in emerging areas along with enhancement of regulatory guidance in diverse fields for effective implementation of regulations by its licensees.",""],[1,"332","2","Nuclear Safety Capacity Building and Self-Assessment Improvement","Continuous improvement through capacity building, action on findings of the internal self- assessments and international peer reviews will be focused.",""],[1,"332","2","Stakeholder Engagement and Public Trust Initiative","PNRA will maintain transparency by ensuring a meaningful engagement with its stakeholders along with pursuing activities to build public trust.",""],[1,"332","2","Public Awareness and Licensee Feedback Mechanism","Confidence in PNRA by its stakeholders will be further enhanced through better interaction, utilizing various measures for ease of doing business, intensifying public awareness program and acting on feedback received from the licensees, public, academia and the Government.",""],[1,"332","2","Nuclear Technology Research and Development Programme","PNRA will engage in R&D activities in emerging areas to overcome challenges related to regulation of new nuclear and radiation technologies.",""],[1,"332","2","Bilateral Nuclear Safety Technical Cooperation","PNRA will pursue technical cooperation through bilateral engagements in the field of nuclear safety for the next five years.",""],[1,"332","2","International Nuclear Safety Engagement and Expert Support","Efforts will made to further polish country image at multilateral platforms such as IAEA by actively providing its expert services in various activities of the agency.",""],[1,"341","7","R&D in Emerging Nuclear and Radiation Technologies","Engage in R&D activities in emerging areas to overcome challenges related to regulation of new nuclear and radiation technologies",""],[1,"341","8","Development of New Regulations in Emerging Areas","Enhance regulatory regime to remain aligned with international standards through development of new regulations in emerging areas",""],[1,"341","9","Bilateral Technical Cooperation on Nuclear Safety","Pursuing technical cooperation through bilateral engagements in the field of nuclear safety",""],[1,"341","10","Capacity Building for Compliance with National and International Obligations","Fulfilment of national and international obligations through capacity building, action on findings of the internal self-assessments and international peer reviews",""]],"223":[[1,"334","16","Community-Focused Policing Reform","Effective community focused policing through merit-based recruitment, postings, and transfers at all levels",""],[1,"334","18","Integrated National and Provincial Criminal Databases","Establishment of integrated National & Provincial Criminal Databases in coordination with NADRA","NADRA"]],"224":[[1,"334","19","Implementation of the National Action Plan and National Security Policy","Implementation of National Action Plan and National Security Policy in true sprit",""],[1,"334","23","Independent Prosecution System Strengthening","Improving/ strengthening independent prosecution system by providing forensic facilities.",""]],"225":[[1,"335","19","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Law Implementation","Implementation of Anti-Money Laundering (AML) and Counter-Terrorism Financing (CTF) Laws to curb white collar crimes",""],[1,"338","16","Anti-Money Laundering Training and Performance Monitoring Mechanism","Development and implementation of Anti Money Laundering Training Module, KPIs, Performance Measurement Mechanism and establishment of Anti Money Laundering Wing and its digitization",""]],"226":[[1,"340","1","Competitive Standards-Setting Process Reform","foster innovation and competition by ensuring standing setting processes open for competition",""],[1,"340","3","Financial Inclusion Strategy Alignment and Institutional Mechanism Adaptation","Transformation to align with the Financial Inclusion Strategy designed to achieve universal financial inclusion by addressing documentation issues of the economy and adaptation of institutional mechanism for alternative dispute resolution",""]]}});